window.TOPICS=[{"n":78,"t":"Adam et Ève","en":"Adam and Eve","sum":"Adam and Eve were a Material Son and Daughter of Jerusem who came about thirty-eight thousand years ago as biologic uplifters to Urantia, a world isolated by rebellion. They worked in the Garden of Eden for one hundred and seventeen years, but through Eve's impatience to hasten results and Adam's errors of judgment they turned aside from the divine plan and defaulted. They were reduced to mortal status yet cleared of the charge of rebellion, and through the violet race they made a great contribution to the biologic and cultural progress of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Sending the Biologic Uplifters","items":[{"x":"Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son, destined to serve as physical uplifters on the evolutionary worlds.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"After the inspection and recommendation of Tabamantia, Adam and Eve were sent to Urantia, a world retarded and isolated by rebellion.","r":["73:0.3"]},{"x":"They were members of the senior corps of Material Sons on Jerusem, an experienced pair who had led research on the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"The entire senior corps volunteered, and Adam and Eve, who had stayed loyal during the Lucifer rebellion, were chosen.","r":["74:1.3","74:1.4"]},{"x":"They arrived 37,848 years before A.D. 1934, in the season when the Garden was in full bloom.","r":["74:0.1"]}]},{"h":"The Culture of the Garden of Eden","items":[{"x":"The schools of Eden taught health, the golden rule, individual and group rights, play, and competition, aiming at socialization.","r":["74:7.2","74:7.3"]},{"x":"Adam discouraged set prayers and taught that effective prayer must be the personal longing of the soul.","r":["74:7.21"]},{"x":"Adam sought to awaken sex equality by teaching that woman contributes equally with man to new life.","r":["74:7.22"]},{"x":"Traditions such as the six days of creation and the rib story are later confusions and condensations of events from the Garden days.","r":["74:8.1","74:8.3"]},{"q":"« L’âge d’or » est un mythe, mais Éden était un fait, et la civilisation du Jardin fut effectivement ruinée.","r":"74:8.14"}]},{"h":"A Difficult Task and Impatience","items":[{"x":"They faced deep loneliness in a world of spiritual darkness, wholly unprepared to accept brotherhood.","r":["75:1.3","75:1.4"]},{"q":"they were not willing to settle down to the long, long endurance test.","r":"75:1.6"},{"x":"Caligastia often visited the Garden urging easier ways, but at first they firmly rejected every proposal of compromise.","r":["75:2.1"]},{"x":"Serapatatia sincerely wanted to help the world but never knew that he had become Caligastia's tool.","r":["75:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Default and Its Consequences","items":[{"x":"In her secret meeting with Cano, Eve broke the long-standing warning against mixing good and evil.","r":["75:4.4","75:4.5"]},{"q":"it constituted evil because it represented the wrong way to achieve righteous ends, because it departed from the right way, the divine plan.","r":"75:4.6"},{"x":"Realizing the failure, Adam in despair committed the same folly as Eve, and enraged inhabitants destroyed a Nodite settlement.","r":["75:5.2","75:5.3"]},{"x":"They left the Garden for the second garden, and their children who had reached twenty could choose the way to Jerusem.","r":["75:6.2","75:6.3"]},{"x":"Gabriel adjudged them in default but cleared them of the charge of rebellion against the universe government.","r":["75:7.1","75:7.2"]},{"q":"Ce qu’ils avaient fait était réellement mal, mais jamais ils ne furent coupables d’avoir outragé la vérité, ils ne s’étaient pas non plus engagés consciemment dans une rébellion contre la juste autorité du Père Universel et de son Fils Créateur.","r":"75:7.7"}]},{"h":"There Was No Fall of Man","items":[{"q":"Il n’y a pas eu de « chute de l’homme ».","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"The Adamic bestowal greatly improved mankind biologically, and Adam should not be regarded as the cause of a curse on the human race.","r":["75:8.2","75:8.3"]},{"x":"After their demotion to mortal status they sincerely repented, and Thought Adjusters came to indwell them.","r":["76:5.2"]},{"x":"In the second garden Adam left his life plasm, adding 1,570 superior men and women to the world.","r":["76:4.8"]},{"x":"Adam lived 530 years and, after death, awoke in a special resurrection and attained citizenship on Jerusem.","r":["76:5.5","76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"Never, in all your ascent to Paradise, will you gain anything by impatiently attempting to circumvent the established and divine plan by short cuts, personal inventions, or other devices","r":"75:8.5"}]}],"see":["Fils et Filles Matériels","Caligastia","Races","Urantia","Révélation","Rébellion de Lucifer"]},{"n":53,"t":"Adoration","en":"Worship","sum":"Worship is the act of recognizing and rejoicing in the intimate relationship with the Creator; it is the highest privilege and the first duty of all intelligent beings. Unlike prayer, which contains an element of self-interest, worship asks nothing and adores God for what he is. The worship impulse, beginning in primitive nature worship, was turned by the adjutant spirits toward the God of nature, and on Paradise it becomes the highest delight.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Worship","items":[{"q":"L’adoration est le privilège suprême et le premier devoir de toutes les intelligences créées.","r":"27:7.1"},{"x":"Worship is the conscious and joyous recognition of the intimate and personal relationships of the Creators with their creatures.","r":["27:7.1"]},{"x":"In the highest sense, worship is directed, directly or indirectly, to the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.1"]},{"x":"Worship is personal communion with that which is divinely real, the source of reality, not a vain monologue.","r":["196:3.22"]},{"x":"Worship is the act of the part identifying itself with the Whole, the finite with the Infinite, the son with the Father.","r":["143:7.8"]}]},{"h":"Worship and Prayer","items":[{"q":"Worship is for its own sake; prayer embodies a self- or creature-interest element","r":"5:3.3"},{"x":"True worship requests nothing and expects no reward; it is a natural response to the Father's lovable nature.","r":["5:3.3"]},{"x":"When self-interest enters worship, it turns into prayer.","r":["5:3.4"]},{"q":"La prière est un rappel du moi — une pensée sublime. L’adoration est l’oubli du moi — une superpensée.","r":"143:7.7"},{"x":"Prayer is spiritually sustaining, but worship is divinely creative; prayer enriches life, and worship illuminates destiny.","r":["143:7.5","102:4.5"]},{"x":"Modern religions have overemphasized prayer and neglected the more essential communion of worship.","r":["102:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Worship of Soul and Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Sincere worship is the mobilization of all the powers of the personality under the leadership of the evolving soul and the direction of the Adjuster.","r":["5:3.7"]},{"x":"The mortal mind consents to worship, the soul craves it, and the Adjuster conducts that worship to the Father.","r":["5:3.8"]},{"x":"The fragments of the Father are empowered to register the genuine adoration of their subjects before the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.2"]},{"x":"The Father's spirit speaks best when the human mind is in an attitude of true worship.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"q":"Le mental mortel consent à adorer ; l’âme immortelle souhaite ardemment l’adoration et en prend l’initiative ; la présence de l’Ajusteur divin dirige cette adoration pour le compte du mental mortel et de l’âme immortelle évoluante.","r":"5:3.8"}]},{"h":"Origin of the Worship Impulse","items":[{"x":"Primitive man, fearing the incomprehensible forces of nature, worshiped almost everything on earth and in the heavens.","r":["85:0.4"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship, the sixth adjutant spirit, constantly stimulated the worship urge in the primitive mind.","r":["85:7.1"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship is the mark of spiritual-ascension candidacy, separating beings capable of possessing souls from those who are not.","r":["36:5.11"]},{"x":"When the spirit of wisdom guides the worship impulse, man begins to turn from the objects of nature to the God of nature.","r":["85:7.3"]},{"q":"L’adoration est l’insigne de la candidature à l’ascension spirituelle.","r":"36:5.11"}]},{"h":"The Worshipful Life","items":[{"x":"Worship, or spiritual contemplation, must alternate with service, which keeps contact with material reality.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"q":"L’adoration est la technique consistant à se tourner vers l’Un pour recevoir l’inspiration permettant de servir la multitude.","r":"143:7.6"},{"x":"Worship is effortless attention, the true rest of the soul, a form of restful spiritual activity.","r":["143:7.7"]},{"x":"In time, thought leads to wisdom, and wisdom leads to worship.","r":["112:2.13"]},{"x":"On Paradise worship is the highest delight and a refreshing play, and all the arts are employed in worship.","r":["27:7.2","27:7.5"]},{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the ascender begins a new and more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]}]}],"see":["Prière","Père Universel","Ajusteur de Pensée","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Expérience religieuse","Service"]},{"n":71,"t":"Adversité et épreuves","en":"Adversity and Trials","sum":"The confusion and trials of Urantia signify not God's indifference but part of the divine plan to forge strong and noble characters between the anvils of necessity and the hammers of anguish. Virtues such as courage, altruism, hope, and faith can grow only in a world of hardship and uncertainty. Jesus corrected the superstition that suffering is God's punishment, and while he did not exempt believers from difficulty, he promised to go with them through all their trials.","sections":[{"h":"Why There Is Adversity","items":[{"x":"The uncertainties and vicissitudes of life are in no way contradictory to the universal sovereignty of God.","r":["3:5.5"]},{"q":"Le courage — la force de caractère — est-il désirable ? Alors, il faut que l’homme soit élevé dans un environnement qui l’oblige à s’attaquer à de dures épreuves et à réagir aux désappointements.","r":"3:5.6"},{"x":"Altruism requires inequality, hope requires insecurity, and faith requires a situation in which one must believe more than one knows.","r":["3:5.7","3:5.8","3:5.9"]},{"x":"Even the satisfaction of happiness is truly experienced only in a world open to the possibility of pain and distress.","r":["3:5.14"]},{"x":"The perfect beings of Havona know neither the sweetness of escaping the potential of pain nor saving faith.","r":["3:5.17"]}]},{"h":"The Anvil and Hammer That Forge Character","items":[{"x":"The Creators could make Urantia a paradise, but such an Eden would not produce strong and noble characters.","r":["23:2.12"]},{"q":"Vos anxiétés et vos tristesses, vos épreuves et vos désappointements, font tout aussi bien partie du plan divin sur votre sphère que la perfection exquise et l’adaptation infinie de toutes choses à leur but suprême sur les mondes de l’univers central et parfait.","r":"23:2.12"},{"q":"L’univers de votre origine se forge entre l’enclume de la justice et le marteau de la souffrance, mais ceux qui manient le marteau sont des enfants de miséricorde, la descendance spirituelle de l’Esprit Infini.","r":"9:1.8"},{"q":"On ne peut percevoir la vérité spirituelle avant d’en éprouver l’expérience, et beaucoup de vérités ne sont réellement ressenties que dans l’adversité.","r":"48:7.18"},{"x":"God sometimes disciplines us for our good, but he suffers with us in our fiery trials.","r":["2:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Suffering Is Not Punishment","items":[{"x":"Jesus declared superstitious the belief that prosperity is a sign of God's approval and adversity a sign of his displeasure.","r":["166:4.3"]},{"x":"Those killed by the falling tower of Siloam were not greater sinners but innocent victims of the accidents of time.","r":["166:4.4"]},{"x":"As the story of Job shows, material prosperity is no proof of God's favor, and the Father loves the poor just as much.","r":["148:6.2"]},{"x":"People suffer from the accidents of time, from imperfection, from the consequences of sin, and from the harvest of rebellion; suffering is not a visitation of divine judgment.","r":["148:6.11"]},{"x":"Even in suffering Job pierced the clouds by faith and found the God of comfort and salvation.","r":["148:6.11","148:6.10"]}]},{"h":"The Believer's Attitude Toward Trials","items":[{"q":"Je ne vous promets pas de vous délivrer des eaux de l’adversité, mais ce que je vous promets, c’est de les traverser toutes avec vous.","r":"159:3.13"},{"x":"Believing the gospel does not exempt one from accidents and calamities, but it keeps one unafraid when trouble comes.","r":["159:3.13"]},{"q":"Il sait comment supporter courageusement les souffrances inévitables et ne se plaint pas quand il doit affronter des épreuves inéluctables.","r":"156:5.20"},{"x":"In times of testing a person's soul is revealed, and the loyal who endure trials are entrusted with the work of the kingdom.","r":["165:6.2"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over the soul, the one who entrusts his soul to the indwelling spirit has a citadel of the spirit that does not fall.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"x":"True religion produces profound courage and confidence even in natural adversity and physical calamity.","r":["101:3.7","34:6.13"]}]},{"h":"The Way Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"Jesus met suffering with faith, courage, and the determination to do the Father's will, and thus conquered life and death.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Even before apparent defeat and the anguish of despair, Jesus stood calm and unafraid in the divine presence.","r":["196:0.5"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged a fear-ridden young man that suffering would give vigor, disappointment a spur, and obstacles a stimulus.","r":["130:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught the multitude gathered at Bethsaida for more than an hour on \"the mission of adversity and the spiritual value of disappointment.\"","r":["151:0.1"]},{"x":"The two hard years before his marriage were a time of real trial in Jesus' earth life.","r":["126:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Peur et inquiétude","Foi","Croissance","Joie et bonheur","Caractère de Jésus"]},{"n":33,"t":"Ajusteur de Pensée","en":"Thought Adjuster","sum":"The Thought Adjuster is a fragment of God that comes directly from the Universal Father and indwells the human mind. It is not a created being but divinity itself; it leads man from within to do the Father's will and seeks to become one with the evolving soul and go forward with it in the eternal career. At the center of the personal religion presented in The Urantia Book stands this indwelling spirit of the Father.","sections":[{"h":"A Divine Fragment from the Father","items":[{"x":"Though he dwells on Paradise, the Father is actually present in the human mind as the Mystery Monitor.","r":["107:0.1"]},{"q":"Ils ne sont pas des êtres créés, mais des entités de fragmentation constituant la présence factuelle du Dieu infini.","r":"107:1.2"},{"x":"Adjusters are limited in scope yet absolute in essence, and so they are called the \"qualified absolute fragments\" of the Father.","r":["107:4.2"]},{"x":"The Adjuster is not a personality, yet it is a true reality of the purest order in the universe, a divine presence.","r":["107:7.1"]},{"q":"No Adjuster has ever been disloyal to the Paradise Father","r":"107:4.3"}]},{"h":"When and How It Comes","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is assigned after the child makes its first moral choice, and on Urantia it arrives, on the average, just before the sixth birthday.","r":["108:2.1"]},{"x":"The preparation of the seven adjutant mind-spirits and the circuitizing of the Holy Spirit must come first before an Adjuster can enter the mind.","r":["108:2.2"]},{"x":"That a perfect Adjuster should volunteer to dwell in a mortal of animal origin is a marvel of divine condescension.","r":["108:6.1"]},{"q":"which came forth from God to find man and sonship him even in the days of the flesh.","r":"107:0.3"}]},{"h":"What the Adjuster Does","items":[{"x":"The basic mission of the Adjuster is to represent the Universal Father to the mortal creature, and indeed to be that Father.","r":["108:0.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster comes with a plan for the ideal life, but man is free to accept or reject that plan.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"x":"It undertakes the difficult work of an interpreter, receiving counsel from spiritual intelligences and conveying it to the material mind.","r":["108:5.1"]},{"q":"only occasionally do you catch an echo, a faint and distant echo, of the divine voice.","r":"110:3.1"},{"x":"Unless the mind's capacity is wholly destroyed, the Adjuster stays with a person through every calamity and illness.","r":["110:1.5"]}]},{"h":"A Life of Co-operation with the Adjuster","items":[{"q":"The great goal of human existence is to attune to the divinity of the indwelling Adjuster;","r":"110:3.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion greatly retard the Adjuster's work, as bodily poisons do.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"Confusion, discouragement, or ignorance alone does not prevent survival; only conscious resistance to the Adjuster's leading does.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"When clouds gather, faith should accept the fact of the Adjuster's presence and look to the light beyond.","r":["108:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Fusion and Eternal Destiny","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is the Father's love incarnate in the human soul, the essence of the finaliter personality foretasted in time.","r":["107:0.2"]},{"x":"Mastering the seven psychic circles is not fusion itself but the preparatory stage leading to fusion.","r":["110:6.1"]},{"q":"but fusion depends on yet other greater and more sublime spiritual achievements, upon the attainment of a final and complete attunement of the mortal will with the will of God as it is resident in the Thought Adjuster.","r":"110:7.1"},{"x":"The eternal union of the Adjuster with a perfected creature brings into being a unique creature that no other universe technique can produce.","r":["108:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Fusion avec l’Ajusteur","Âme","Personnalité","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Volonté de Dieu","Survie"]},{"n":35,"t":"Âme","en":"Soul","sum":"The soul is a morontia reality newly arising from the relationship between the material mind and the indwelling Thought Adjuster, the child born of human effort and the divine spirit together. During the life in the flesh it grows like an embryo; it then survives death and becomes the new vehicle of personality on the mansion worlds. The growth of the soul depends on moral choices and the decision to seek God, and personality identity survives in the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"How the Soul Comes into Being","items":[{"x":"When a mortal chooses to do the Father's will, the indwelling spirit becomes the father of a new reality and the material mind becomes its mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"x":"Three factors operate in making the soul: the human mind, the indwelling divine spirit, and the relationship between the two.","r":["111:2.4","111:2.5","111:2.6"]},{"q":"La réalité de cette relation unique n’est ni matérielle ni spirituelle, mais morontielle. C’est l’âme.","r":"111:2.7"},{"x":"The divine spirit arrives with the first moral activity of the human mind, and at that very moment the soul is born.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The morontia life of an ascending mortal actually begins at the moment the soul is conceived, when the Adjuster comes to indwell.","r":["48:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Nature of the Soul","items":[{"x":"The midway creatures called this soul the \"midmind,\" meaning that it lies between the material mind and the cosmic mind.","r":["111:2.8"]},{"x":"The soul is the part that lifts man above the animal level, characterized by moral choice and the urge to know God and be like him.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness itself is not the soul; moral self-consciousness, as true self-realization, forms the foundation of the soul.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The soul cannot be proved by material investigation or by purely spiritual tests, yet the morally awakened mortal knows its reality by experience.","r":["133:6.7"]},{"q":"Dès ses premiers débuts, l’âme est réelle ; elle a des qualités de survie cosmique.","r":"16:9.2"},{"x":"The morontia soul is the child both of the Father's Adjuster action and of the cosmic reaction of the Supreme Being.","r":["117:6.5"]}]},{"h":"The Growth of the Soul","items":[{"x":"Mind is the human soil on which the Adjuster, with the co-operation of the personality, evolves the morontia soul.","r":["111:1.1"]},{"q":"The material mind of mortal man is the cosmic loom that carries the morontia fabrics","r":"111:2.2"},{"x":"The soul can grow regardless of cultural level, but not without the decision to choose survival and to do the Father's will.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Mistakes and errors may delay the evolution of the soul, but they cannot prevent the soul evolution that began with the consent of the will.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"q":"L’âme de l’homme ne peut exister sans pensée morale et sans activité spirituelle. Une âme stagnante est une âme mourante.","r":"133:6.5"},{"x":"The more the soul is filled with truth, beauty, and goodness, the more indestructible the resulting being becomes.","r":["111:3.7"]}]},{"h":"The Soul and the Human Will","items":[{"x":"During life the deciding will resides in the material mind, but as the self grows, it becomes increasingly identified with the emerging morontia soul.","r":["111:3.2"]},{"q":"L’âme est ainsi l’embryon du futur véhicule morontiel de l’identité de la personnalité.","r":"111:3.2"},{"x":"By its own choice the mortal personality can transfer the seat of its identity from the transient material-intellect system to the morontia-soul system.","r":["112:5.4","112:2.20"]},{"q":"The faith-activated soul of man cannot stop short of the attainment of this goal of destiny;","r":"132:3.7"},{"x":"Whether a soul is saved or lost depends on whether moral consciousness gains survival value through eternal alliance with its immortal spirit endowment.","r":["133:6.6"]}]},{"h":"The Soul After Death","items":[{"q":"Cette entité nouvellement apparue est l’âme, et elle survit à la mort de votre corps physique aussi bien qu’à celle de votre mental matériel.","r":"112:5.12"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the seraphic guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the seraphim bestow the sleeping soul upon a new morontia form and unite it with the returning Adjuster.","r":["112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"x":"If a mortal does not survive, the spiritual values of his experience remain in the Adjuster, but his identity does not survive.","r":["16:9.3"]},{"x":"The soul in the body is embryonic; it is born into the morontia life and grows through the mansion worlds.","r":["66:4.9"]},{"x":"The immortal soul is at first morontial but rises to true spirit levels and usually fuses with the spirit of the Father who started it.","r":["111:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Human Ideas About the Soul","items":[{"x":"Primitive man associated the soul with blood, breath, shadows, and reflections in water, or believed it dwelt in various organs of the body.","r":["111:0.3"]},{"x":"Early man took the other self of dreams to be the soul, and this idea led on to belief in nature spirits.","r":["86:5.1"]},{"x":"Hindu teachers, in the concept of the atman, almost discerned the Adjuster, but they failed to distinguish the co-evolving soul.","r":["111:0.4"]}]}],"see":["Ajusteur de Pensée","Personnalité","Mental","Morontia","Survie","Fusion avec l’Ajusteur"]},{"n":60,"t":"Amour","en":"Love","sum":"\"God is love.\" In The Urantia Book love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures, and it embraces truth, beauty, and goodness. The Father's love individualizes each person as an irreplaceable child and dwells within man through the Adjuster. Love is the desire to do good to others; it cannot be held captive and becomes real only when bestowed upon one's fellows. Jesus gave the new commandment to love one another \"as I have loved you.\"","sections":[{"h":"God Is Love","items":[{"x":"Because God is love, his only personal attitude toward the affairs of the universe is always a reaction of divine affection.","r":["2:5.1"]},{"x":"The love of God is not induced by sacrifice or intercession; the Father himself loves us.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"q":"Dieu est amour, mais l’amour n’est pas Dieu.","r":"2:5.10"},{"x":"The love of God is a farseeing parental affection that functions in unity with wisdom and sometimes includes discipline for our good.","r":["2:5.3","2:5.10"]},{"x":"Love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures.","r":["2:5.12"]}]},{"h":"Manifestations of the Father's Love","items":[{"x":"The Father's love individualizes each personality as a unique child, eternally irreplaceable.","r":["12:7.9"]},{"x":"The greatest manifestation of divine love for mortals is the bestowal of the Adjusters, and its greatest revelation is the bestowal life of Michael.","r":["2:5.10"]},{"x":"The love and devotion an Adjuster gives to its subject is the most truly divine affection in all creation.","r":["110:0.2"]},{"x":"God is love and the Son is mercy; mercy is applied love, love in action.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"We love God because we discern that he truly loves us; the experience of loving is a response to the experience of being loved.","r":["2:5.8"]},{"q":"L’amour du Père nous suit maintenant et tout au long du cercle sans fin des âges éternels.","r":"2:5.9"}]},{"h":"What Love Is","items":[{"q":"L’amour est le désir de faire du bien aux autres.","r":"56:10.21"},{"x":"In its true sense, love, whether human or divine, connotes the mutual regard of whole personalities.","r":["112:2.7"]},{"q":"it cannot be created, manufactured, or purchased; it must grow.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Love is born only of thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments; one cannot love fellows by mere willpower.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"Love must continually readapt its concept of the highest good of the one loved, under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["180:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Circuit of Love","items":[{"x":"All true love is from God, and man receives the divine affection as he bestows that love upon his neighbors.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"q":"L’homme ne peut jamais saisir l’amour du Père pour l’emprisonner dans son cœur.","r":"117:6.10"},{"x":"The circuit of love proceeds from the Father, through sons to brothers, and thence to the Supreme.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"Love is the soil of religious growth; love is the essence of religion and the wellspring of superior civilization.","r":["100:0.2","102:6.3"]}]},{"h":"Love as Jesus Revealed It","items":[{"x":"Jesus revealed a God of love, and that love embraces truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["5:4.6"]},{"q":"L’amour est la plus grande de toutes les réalités spirituelles.","r":"143:1.4"},{"x":"Beyond the commandment to love one's neighbor as oneself, Jesus gave the new commandment: \"Love one another as I have loved you.\"","r":["180:1.1"]},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows, and the greatest love is to lay down one's life for one's friends.","r":["180:1.2","180:1.3"]},{"x":"To share the Master's love is to share his service; that love does not make a new world but makes the old world new.","r":["180:1.5"]},{"x":"Advanced mortals on worlds settled in light and life have learned that love is the greatest thing in the universe and know that God is love.","r":["56:10.20"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Miséricorde","Service","Fraternité des hommes","Bonté","Ajusteur de Pensée"]},{"n":21,"t":"Anciens des Jours","en":"Ancients of Days","sum":"Les Anciens des Jours sont vingt-et-un chefs suprêmes originaires de la Trinité du Paradis qui, par groupes de trois, gouvernent chacun des sept superunivers. Eux seuls rendent les verdicts exécutifs finals sur la vie et la mort éternelles des créatures volitives, et, grâce à la technique de la réflectivité, ils voient et entendent à la fois le Paradis, en haut, et les univers locaux, en bas. Ils sont le sommet du gouvernement superuniversel que les mortels rencontrent au cours de leur voyage d’ascension, après avoir été diplômés de l’univers local.","sections":[{"h":"Des chefs issus de la Trinité","items":[{"x":"Les Anciens des Jours sont le troisième des sept ordres de Personnalités Suprêmes de la Trinité ; leur nombre est fixe, et il n’en apparait plus de nouveaux.","r":["18:0.4","18:0.9"]},{"q":"Les Anciens des Jours sont tous fondamentalement identiques ; ils font ressortir le caractère conjugué et la nature unifiée de la Trinité.","r":"18:3.2"},{"x":"Les Sept Maitres Esprits diffèrent par leur nature, mais les Anciens des Jours, bien que possédant une individualité, sont des descendants uniformes et superparfaits de la Trinité.","r":["18:3.2"]},{"x":"Les vingt-et-un furent trinitisés en même temps, et la toute première inscription des archives de personnalité du Paradis est le récit de leur trinitisation.","r":["18:3.4"]},{"q":"Ils représentent l’inauguration d’archives concernant les personnalités dans l’univers des univers, d’où leur nom — Anciens des Jours.","r":"18:3.4"},{"x":"Les êtres d’origine trinitaire ne courent aucun risque d’échec ni de rébellion, et ces chefs ne se sont jamais écartés de la voie d’une conduite parfaite de la personnalité.","r":["18:0.11"]}]},{"h":"Le supergouvernement dirigé par trois","items":[{"q":"Chaque superunivers est régi par trois Anciens des Jours, chefs exécutifs conjoints du supergouvernement.","r":"15:10.3"},{"x":"Dans la haute administration, les trois agissent toujours ensemble ; bien qu’ils ne quittent jamais leur monde-siège, la position de celui-ci, foyer du système de réflectivité, permet à leur gouvernement de s’exercer sans entrave.","r":["18:3.5"]},{"x":"Tandis que les Maitres Esprits déterminent la nature d’un superunivers, les Anciens des Jours en déterminent l’administration, et assurent un gouvernement uniforme à des superunivers par ailleurs différents.","r":["18:3.3"]},{"x":"Ils sont assistés par les Perfecteurs de Sagesse, les Conseillers Divins et les Censeurs Universels, ainsi que par des Fils Trinitisés issus de mortels ascendants glorifiés.","r":["15:10.11","15:10.12"]},{"x":"Les observations et les recommandations recueillies par les chefs des secteurs majeurs et mineurs remontent degré par degré jusqu’à atteindre enfin les tribunaux des Anciens des Jours.","r":["15:13.6"]},{"q":"Et tous les décrets et jugements des Anciens des Jours sont caractérisés par la sagesse dans l’originalité et l’initiative dans l’individualité.","r":"18:3.9"}]},{"h":"Le jugement final de la vie et de la mort éternelles","items":[{"x":"Ils sont les plus puissants des chefs directs des créations spatiotemporelles, et eux seuls ont le pouvoir de prononcer la sentence finale d’extinction éternelle des créatures volitives.","r":["18:3.7"]},{"q":"Les Fils des univers locaux peuvent décréter la survie de l’homme mortel, mais seuls les Anciens des Jours peuvent prononcer un jugement exécutoire sur les questions de vie et de mort éternelles.","r":"15:12.2"},{"x":"Lorsque l’amour restaurateur des Fils Créateurs est définitivement rejeté, la sentence d’extinction est exécutée par des forces placées sous leur juridiction.","r":["2:3.6","2:3.3"]},{"q":"Il n’y a ni désaccord ni opinion minoritaire dans les décisions de ces tribunaux d’une excellence suprême.","r":"15:12.3"},{"x":"Il n’y a pas d’appel contre les verdicts d’un superunivers, car ils sont l’opinion unanime des Anciens des Jours et du Maitre Esprit qui préside ce superunivers.","r":["15:12.4"]},{"q":"Lorsque les trois Anciens des Jours fonctionnent, la Trinité du Paradis fonctionne.","r":"19:3.5"},{"x":"Eux et leurs associés d’origine trinitaire rendent les jugements justes de l’équité suprême dans les sept superunivers.","r":["10:6.17"]}]},{"h":"Le gouvernement réflectif qui voit et entend tout","items":[{"q":"the Ancients of Days from their position midway between the inhabited worlds and Paradise—between man and God—can instantly look both ways, hear both ways, and know both ways.","r":"28:4.1"},{"x":"Les seconaphins primaires servent de miroirs vivants, reflétant devant eux le mental et la voix de l’Esprit Infini, des Fils Créateurs et des armées angéliques.","r":["28:4.4","28:4.6","28:4.11"]},{"x":"Ils discernent la volonté du Père en harmonisant la voix de l’esprit venue d’en haut avec les voix des Micaëls venues d’en bas, et, comme cela exige les trois ensemble, un superunivers est toujours présidé par trois.","r":["28:4.10"]},{"x":"Les superunivers sont isolés les uns des autres, et toute communication personnelle directe avec les chefs d’un autre superunivers doit passer par les Messagers Solitaires.","r":["23:2.15","15:10.23"]}]},{"h":"Relation avec les univers locaux, et l’avenir","items":[{"x":"Un Fils Créateur s’engage envers la Trinité à ne pas assumer la pleine souveraineté avant que ses sept effusions en tant que créature n’aient été certifiées par les Anciens des Jours.","r":["119:0.3"]},{"x":"Ils ne certifient un Fils Créateur comme souverain d’univers qu’après qu’il a réellement vécu en tant que créature et acquis le point de vue de la créature.","r":["119:0.6"]},{"x":"À la requête de Micaël, ils autorisèrent la détention des personnalités impliquées dans la rébellion de Lucifer, et le sort final des archirebelles reste entre leurs mains.","r":["53:9.3","53:9.6"]},{"x":"Comme leurs prérogatives de gouvernement n’ont pas été acquises par l’expérience, ils seront un jour remplacés par l’Être Suprême, le souverain expérientiel, et deviendront ses vice-gérants.","r":["18:3.8"]},{"x":"Le voyage du mortel à la découverte de Dieu commence par le Fils Créateur et se poursuit, par les Anciens des Jours et le Maitre Esprit du superunivers, jusqu’au Père Universel.","r":["0:8.9"]}]}],"see":["Trinité du Paradis","Les sept superunivers","Dieu le Septuple","Être Suprême","Sept Maitres Esprits","Fils Créateur Micaël"]},{"n":96,"t":"Armées angéliques","en":"Angelic Hosts","sum":"The angelic hosts are ministering spirits deriving from the Infinite Spirit: the supernaphim of the central universe, the seconaphim of the superuniverses, and the seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes. They have no material bodies, yet they possess distinct individual personalities, and as associates of evolving will creatures they minister to man in daily life and through death and resurrection. Without ever invading the human will, the angels help mortals on their ascending journey with love and sympathy.","sections":[{"h":"Ministering Spirits of Time","items":[{"x":"The personalities of the Infinite Spirit comprise three orders: the angels, ministering spirits of time; the messenger hosts of space; and the higher spirits.","r":["38:0.1"]},{"x":"Supernaphim form the angelic corps of the central universe, seconaphim of the superuniverses, and seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes.","r":["38:0.2","28:0.1"]},{"x":"Angels are associates of evolving and ascending will creatures and co-workers with divine personalities, and all are highly individualized, unique personalities.","r":["26:1.1"]},{"x":"In this revelation the word \"angels\" refers chiefly to the seraphic offspring of the Universe Mother Spirit who are concerned with the mortal survival plan.","r":["38:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Origin and Nature of the Seraphim","items":[{"x":"Seraphim are created by the Universe Mother Spirit in projections of 41,472 at a time, and they are still being created, since Nebadon is still in the making.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"q":"Les anges n’ont pas de corps matériels, mais sont des êtres bien précis et distincts les uns des autres. Ils sont de nature et d’origine spirituelles.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"Angels are invisible to man, yet they perceive us as we are in the flesh and understand human emotions.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Seraphim are affectionate and sympathetic but not sex-emotional creatures, and they are much like what we will be on the mansion worlds.","r":["38:2.2"]},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit seeks to create uniformly perfect seraphim, but for unknown reasons the offspring are highly diverse.","r":["39:0.1"]},{"q":"Seraphim are still being periodically created","r":"38:1.3"}]},{"h":"The Angelic Orders","items":[{"x":"Local universe seraphim are divided into seven orders: supreme, superior, supervisor, and administrator seraphim, planetary helpers, transition ministers, and seraphim of the future.","r":["39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"x":"It is hard to say that any seraphim are inferior to other groups, and the higher orders are the more eager to be assigned to lowly service.","r":["39:0.9","39:0.11"]},{"x":"Cherubim and sanobim, of the same origin as seraphim, are the lowest angelic order; affectionate and almost human, they faithfully assist the seraphim.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]},{"x":"Cherubim are positive senior personalities and sanobim negative complemental ones, and the two are functionally united as one.","r":["38:7.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim may reach Paradise by several paths, such as elevation to Evening Stars or completion of specialized service.","r":["39:8.1","39:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Angels Beside Man","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Since Michael's bestowal, seraphim are assigned not by race but according to human intellect, spirituality, and destiny.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"q":"Les anges ne forcent pas le sanctuaire du mental humain. Ils ne manipulent pas la volonté des mortels et n’entrent pas non plus en contact direct avec les Ajusteurs intérieurs.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Angels are very near us and truly care for us; though they have no physical tears, they have spiritual emotions.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim work on our behalf under the orders of their superiors, regardless of our requests or whims.","r":["113:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Guides Through Death and Resurrection","items":[{"x":"Jesus said there is joy in the presence of the angels of heaven over one sinner who repents.","r":["167:7.5"]},{"q":"Les anges sont les fidèles guides célestes de l’âme des hommes durant la période inexplorée et imprécise qui intervient entre la mort physique et la vie nouvelle dans les demeures de l’esprit. »","r":"167:7.6"},{"x":"On first awakening on the mansion worlds we actually see for the first time the angelic companions who were always with us on earth.","r":["113:7.1"]},{"x":"On the morontia spheres the two attending seraphim, now open companions, aid our progress while they themselves learn and grow.","r":["113:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Seraphim in Planetary Government","items":[{"q":"LES Très Hauts gouvernent dans les royaumes des hommes au moyen de beaucoup de forces et d’agents célestes, mais principalement par le ministère des séraphins.","r":"114:0.1"},{"x":"At one noon roll call the planetary angels and guardians of Urantia numbered more than five hundred million pairs of seraphim.","r":["114:0.2"]},{"x":"When the Spirit of Truth was poured out, twelve corps of the master seraphim of planetary supervision came to Urantia with the first resident governor general.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.2"]},{"x":"It is through the ministry of angels that one world can keep in touch with other worlds.","r":["167:7.4"]}]}],"see":["Séraphins","Gardiens séraphiques","Esprit Infini","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Mondes des maisons","Médians"]},{"n":46,"t":"Ascension des mortels","en":"Mortal Ascension","sum":"The mortal ascension is the long road by which a human being of animal origin sets out from an evolutionary planet, passes through the mansion worlds and the morontia worlds of the local universe, the spirit training worlds of the superuniverse, and the central universe of Havona, and at last finds the Universal Father on Paradise and becomes a finaliter. The command \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect\" is both the starting point and the goal of this journey, and the way must be walked step by step in experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Call to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universes have embarked on the eternal adventure of reaching God the Father, the long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"Striving for the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and highest ambition of every creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Though man cannot be perfect in the infinite sense, he can fully attain the divine goal that God has set for him.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Cette recherche sublime du Dieu des univers est l’aventure suprême des habitants de tous les mondes du temps et de l’espace.","r":"1:0.6"}]},{"h":"An Outline of the Seven Stages","items":[{"x":"The ascending career is summed up in seven stages: planetary mortals, sleeping survivors, mansion world students, morontia progressors, superuniverse wards, Havona pilgrims, and Paradise arrivals.","r":["30:4.1","30:4.2","30:4.8"]},{"x":"For sleeping survivors the passing of time does not matter; one who has slept five thousand years awakens no differently from one who has rested five days.","r":["30:4.12"]},{"x":"Ascenders progress individually within a sphere, but between the stages of universe study they always move in classes.","r":["30:4.17"]},{"x":"Just before leaving the local universe they acquire true spirit identity, and from then on the ascender's status is forever settled.","r":["30:4.20","30:4.21"]}]},{"h":"Through the Local Universe and the Superuniverse","items":[{"x":"Passing from the mansion worlds through the spheres of the system, the constellation, and the universe headquarters, the ascender as a morontia progressor develops in intellect, spirit, and form.","r":["30:4.18","30:4.19"]},{"q":"Un tel avancement ne change pas le mental, la personnalité et le caractère ; la forme seule subit une modification.","r":"30:4.20"},{"x":"On the superuniverse training worlds the young spirits share what they have learned with others and master local universe and superuniverse administration.","r":["30:4.22","30:4.23","30:4.24"]},{"q":"Superuniverse wards have never been known to go astray.","r":"30:4.21"}]},{"h":"Havona and Paradise","items":[{"x":"The journey from superuniverse headquarters to Havona is always made alone, and the instruction of Havona is personal and individual.","r":["30:4.27"]},{"x":"The pilgrim arrives in Havona possessing only one perfection, perfection of purpose, and his faith has already been tested.","r":["26:4.13"]},{"q":"L’aptitude à comprendre est le passeport des mortels pour le Paradis. Le consentement à croire est la clef de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father on the third circle of Havona, with the help of the Father guides, becomes the passport to eternity.","r":["26:9.1","26:9.2"]},{"x":"Residence on Paradise means that God has been found, and Father-fused mortals are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"q":"On earth you were a creature of flesh and blood; through the local universe you were a morontia being; through the superuniverse you were an evolving spirit;","r":"30:4.26"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of the Journey and Beyond","items":[{"x":"Step by step, life by life, world by world, the ascending career is mastered and the goal of Deity is attained, and survival is completed in perfection.","r":["26:9.4"]},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded as spirits of the sixth stage, so a destiny of the unrevealed seventh stage still remains.","r":["31:3.3","31:3.5"]},{"x":"The long and tremendous training of the ascension must surely be designed to fit them for tests of greater trust and more sublime service.","r":["31:3.2","48:8.3"]},{"x":"The destinies of Adjuster-fused, Son-fused, and Spirit-fused mortals differ, but none is greater or lesser, for God loves all his sons alike.","r":["40:10.5","40:10.13"]},{"x":"Every facility and power is provided so that the Paradise goal of divine perfection may at last be attained.","r":["40:10.14"]},{"q":"La survie est achevée en perfection et la perfection est complète dans la suprématie de la divinité.","r":"26:9.4"}]}],"see":["Mondes des maisons","Morontia","Corps de la Finalité","Havona","Paradis","Quête de la perfection"]},{"n":2,"t":"Attributs de Dieu","en":"Attributes of God","sum":"Les attributs de Dieu montrent comment le Père infini se rapporte à sa création. Il est présent partout, tout-puissant et omniscient. Il se donne sans réserve sans être aucunement diminué, et il gouverne par ses Fils tout en se réservant la souveraineté finale. Tous ces attributs sont unifiés et coordonnés dans l’amour et la sagesse, la justice et la miséricorde.","sections":[{"h":"Créativité et omniprésence","items":[{"x":"La créativité n’est pas tant un attribut que la totalité de la nature agissante de Dieu, qui culmine dans la vérité de la paternité de Dieu.","r":["3:0.3"]},{"x":"Seul Dieu peut être en d’innombrables endroits à la fois ; il est présent dans toutes les parties de sa création et dans tous les cœurs.","r":["3:1.1","3:1.2"]},{"q":"Dieu est révélé dans tout le cosmos, mais le cosmos ne saurait jamais contenir ni englober l’infinité de Dieu dans son intégralité.","r":"3:1.2"},{"x":"Dieu n’est présent de manière pleinement discernable qu’au Paradis et dans l’univers central ; dans les créations extérieures, il limite sa présence directe par respect pour la souveraineté de ses créateurs coordonnés.","r":["3:1.6"]},{"x":"La présence effective du Père en l’homme dépend de la mesure dans laquelle son mental coopère avec l’Ajusteur intérieur.","r":["3:1.11","3:1.12"]}]},{"h":"Puissance infinie","items":[{"x":"La longue évolution des races, des planètes et des univers se déroule avec ordre selon le dessein éternel du Père, sous le contrôle des créateurs.","r":["3:2.2"]},{"x":"Considéré sous l’angle des phénomènes non spirituels, Dieu est énergie ; toute énergie physique procède de lui et est maintenue sous le contrôle gravitationnel du bas Paradis.","r":["3:2.3","3:2.4"]},{"q":"En dépit des apparences, le pouvoir de Dieu ne fonctionne pas comme une force aveugle dans l’univers.","r":"3:2.6"},{"x":"Les actes de Dieu ne paraissent parfois impitoyables qu’à cause de la vision finie ; tous visent le plus grand bien de tous les intéressés.","r":["3:2.8","3:2.10"]},{"x":"La puissance de Dieu n’est limitée que par sa nature (amour, vérité, beauté et bonté), par sa volonté (miséricorde) et par sa loi (la justice de la Trinité).","r":["3:2.12","3:2.13","3:2.14"]}]},{"h":"Connaissance universelle","items":[{"x":"Dieu est conscient des pensées de toute la création et il est la seule personnalité qui connaisse effectivement le nombre des étoiles et des planètes de l’espace.","r":["3:3.1","3:3.2"]},{"x":"Sa connaissance est complétée par le circuit de personnalité qui embrasse toutes les personnalités, par les Fils divins descendants et par les Ajusteurs de Pensée intérieurs.","r":["3:3.3"]},{"x":"Même si Dieu connaissait d’avance les actes de libre arbitre de ses enfants, cette prescience n’abolirait en rien leur liberté.","r":["3:3.4"]},{"q":"Une chose est certaine : Dieu n’est jamais pris au dépourvu.","r":"3:3.4"},{"x":"L’omnipotence n’implique pas le pouvoir de faire ce qui est contraire à la nature divine, et l’omniscience ne signifie pas connaitre l’inconnaissable.","r":["3:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Infinité non diminuée","items":[{"x":"Après s’être donné sans réserve à ses Fils et à sa création, le Père n’est en rien diminué dans son potentiel de pouvoir, de sagesse et d’amour.","r":["3:4.1","3:4.3"]},{"x":"Même si la création se poursuivait sans fin, le pouvoir de contrôle du Paradis suffirait, et l’Infini resterait rempli de la même force et de la même énergie.","r":["3:4.2"]},{"x":"L’homme ne peut concevoir pleinement l’infinité du Père, mais il peut réellement éprouver l’impact de son amour ; la qualité de cette expérience est illimitée, tandis que sa quantité dépend de la capacité spirituelle.","r":["3:4.6"]},{"q":"Therefore man's nearest and dearest approach to God is by and through love","r":"3:4.7"}]},{"h":"Suprématie et primauté","items":[{"x":"Hors de Havona, le Père exerce son pouvoir par ses Fils et leurs personnalités subordonnées, et il n’agit directement que lorsqu’un agent délégué manque à sa mission.","r":["3:5.1","3:5.2"]},{"x":"Dans le cœur des hommes, la volonté du Père peut ne pas toujours être faite, mais dans le cours et la destinée d’une planète, le plan divin prévaut.","r":["3:5.3"]},{"x":"L’adversité, l’inégalité, l’incertitude et la possibilité d’erreur sont des conditions de vie nécessaires pour développer des qualités telles que le courage, l’altruisme, l’espoir et la foi.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.9"]},{"x":"Le Père délègue librement l’autorité, mais se réserve la décision finale et le veto en ce qui concerne le bien-être et la destinée de la création.","r":["3:6.1"]},{"q":"La souveraineté de Dieu est illimitée, elle est le fait fondamental de toute création.","r":"3:6.2"}]},{"h":"Perfection, justice et miséricorde","items":[{"x":"Les plans et les desseins de la Source-Centre Première sont, comme lui-même, éternels, parfaits et immuables ; même s’ils semblent changer, le dessein sous-jacent ne change pas.","r":["2:2.1","2:2.3"]},{"x":"La justice du Père ne dépend pas de la conduite de ses créatures, et même lorsqu’il les laisse récolter les fruits de leurs méfaits, elle est toujours tempérée par la miséricorde.","r":["2:3.1","2:3.2"]},{"q":"Mercy is simply justice tempered by that wisdom which grows out of perfection of knowledge and the full recognition of the natural weaknesses and environmental handicaps of finite creatures.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"En raison de sa sagesse infinie, Dieu accorde en même temps justice et miséricorde, et il n’est jamais déchiré par des attitudes contradictoires envers ses enfants.","r":["2:4.3"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Personnalité de Dieu","Miséricorde","Justice","Amour","Volonté de Dieu"]},{"n":58,"t":"Beauté","en":"Beauty","sum":"Beauty, together with truth and goodness, is one of the three ways in which man comprehends divinity; it is the recognition of the harmonious unification of diverse realities. In the physical universe we see divine beauty, and its climax is the cosmic drama of man seeking God and God seeking man. Art and the appreciation of beauty become part of religion when they are linked with ethics and spiritual motivation, and Jesus valued the power of beauty to lead to worship.","sections":[{"h":"A Face of Divinity","items":[{"x":"Creatures can comprehend divinity as truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"x":"In the physical universe one sees divine beauty, in the intellectual world one discerns truth, and goodness is found in religious experience.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"x":"The Father enjoys the response of divine beauty that Havona presents and delights in providing the evolving universes with patterns of harmony.","r":["14:6.8"]},{"x":"Even beauty and truth would be divorced from the hope of survival were they not attributes of a loving Father.","r":["1:7.3"]}]},{"h":"What Beauty Is","items":[{"x":"Beauty, or art, is largely a matter of the unification of contrasts, and diversity is essential to the concept of beauty.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"x":"Beauty is the intellectual recognition of the harmonious synthesis of the diversities of phenomenal reality, derived from eternal oneness.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"q":"Discerner la beauté suprême, c’est découvrir et intégrer la réalité.","r":"2:7.8"},{"q":"Discerner la bonté divine dans la vérité éternelle, c’est la beauté ultime.","r":"2:7.8"},{"x":"Universal beauty is the recognition of the reflection of the Isle of Paradise in the material creation.","r":["56:10.17"]},{"q":"La beauté, le rythme et l’harmonie sont intellectuellement associés et spirituellement parents.","r":"44:7.2"}]},{"h":"The Climax of Universe Art","items":[{"x":"The climax of finite art is the drama of uniting the two poles of Creator and creature: man seeking God and God seeking man.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"q":"Le matérialisme, l’athéisme, est donc le comble de la laideur, l’apogée de l’antithèse finie du beau.","r":"56:10.4"},{"x":"The existence of beauty implies the presence of an appreciative creature mind.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"x":"Cosmologic thinking is accompanied by curiosity toward harmony, aesthetic appreciation, and ethical sensitivity leading to God-consciousness.","r":["56:10.6","56:10.7","56:10.8"]}]},{"h":"Art and Religion","items":[{"x":"The search for beauty becomes part of religion only when it enriches ethical and moral concepts.","r":["101:9.4"]},{"q":"L’art n’est religieux que s’il se diffuse avec un dessein dérivé de haute motivation spirituelle.","r":"101:9.4"},{"x":"The high mission of all art is to foreshadow higher reality and to crystallize the emotions of time into the thought of eternity.","r":["48:7.23"]},{"x":"Art arises from the attempt to escape the lack of beauty in the material environment; it is a gesture toward the morontia level.","r":["196:3.30"]},{"x":"If truth, beauty, and goodness are not unified in the experience of the artist or philosopher, the expression lacks a true soul.","r":["44:7.3"]},{"x":"The celestial artists of the morontia worlds portray in art the divine beauty of the Paradise Creators.","r":["44:8.6"]}]},{"h":"Beauty and Jesus","items":[{"x":"Viewing Flavius's art treasures, Jesus said there was no reason to condemn the appreciation of the beauty of things created by the Father and fashioned by man.","r":["142:4.2","142:4.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that beauty has great value in leading to the worship impulse, especially in children.","r":["167:6.5"]},{"x":"The spirit that Jesus and the Father send is not only the spirit of truth but also the spirit of idealistic beauty.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"The Hebrews based their religion on goodness and the Greeks on beauty, but the love Jesus revealed embraces truth, beauty, and goodness together.","r":["5:4.6","196:3.19"]},{"x":"The beauty of divine love, once fully admitted to the human heart, forever destroys the charm of sin and the power of evil.","r":["188:5.3"]},{"q":"Construisez ainsi, pour vous-même et en vous-même, des musées de beauté, de bonté et de grandeur artistique.","r":"160:4.12"}]}],"see":["Vérité","Bonté","Amour","Adoration","Philosophie","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":59,"t":"Bonté","en":"Goodness","sum":"Goodness, together with truth and beauty, is one of the three ways of comprehending divinity, but it is understood only in relation to personality. God's primal perfection consists in the perfection of the goodness inherent in his nature, and that goodness is fully revealed only in personal religious experience. For man, goodness is always relative and growing, more a quest than a possession until Paradise is attained. The goodness of God leads people to repentance.","sections":[{"h":"The Goodness of God","items":[{"q":"La perfection primordiale de Dieu ne consiste pas en une droiture présumée, mais plutôt en la perfection inhérente à la bonté de sa nature divine.","r":"2:2.5"},{"q":"La bonté de Dieu repose au fond du libre arbitre divin — la tendance universelle à aimer, à montrer de la miséricorde, à témoigner de la patience et à offrir le pardon.","r":"2:6.9"},{"x":"God is supremely great and good, and greatness and goodness are inseparably one in him.","r":["28:6.21"]},{"x":"The infinite goodness of the Father is beyond the finite mind's comprehension and is discerned only by contrast with relative imperfection.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"God the Supreme is truth, beauty, and goodness, for these concepts are the finite maximum of ideational experience.","r":["117:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Goodness in Personality and Religion","items":[{"x":"Truth and beauty may be conceived without personality, but divine goodness is understood only in relation to personality.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"The goodness of God is found only in the spiritual world of personal religious experience, and religion is essentially faith-trust in that goodness.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"q":"Man might fear a great God, but he trusts and loves only a good God.","r":"2:6.1"},{"x":"Goodness is the mind's recognition of the relative values of the levels of divine perfection, and it implies a moral mind that discriminates between good and evil.","r":["56:10.12"]},{"x":"Goodness embraces ethics, morality, and religion, the craving for experiential perfection.","r":["56:10.10"]}]},{"h":"Goodness Is Relative and Growing","items":[{"x":"Good and evil are words denoting relative levels of human comprehension of the observable universe.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"One should not take social custom or religious tradition as the standard of goodness but choose the good by the spiritual standards set by the indwelling spirit.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"Experience is good when it heightens the appreciation of beauty, strengthens the moral will, and enlarges the capacity to love and serve one's fellows.","r":["132:2.5"]},{"q":"Jusqu’à ce que vous atteigniez les niveaux du Paradis, la bonté sera toujours davantage une recherche qu’une possession, plus un but qu’une expérience d’aboutissement.","r":"132:2.8"},{"x":"As one ascends the universe scale, goodness increases and evil diminishes, and on Paradise goodness is no longer contrastive but perfect.","r":["132:2.6","132:2.9"]},{"q":"La bonté est vivante, relative, toujours en progrès ; elle est invariablement une expérience personnelle et perpétuellement liée au discernement de la vérité et de la beauté.","r":"132:2.7"}]},{"h":"Goodness and the Possibility of Evil","items":[{"x":"The possibility of evil is necessary to moral choosing, but actual evil need not exist.","r":["132:2.10"]},{"x":"The presence of good and evil in the world is proof of the reality of personality, with a moral will that chooses between them.","r":["132:2.8"]},{"x":"Spiritual evolution is an experience of increasingly choosing the good, with a corresponding decrease in the potential of evil.","r":["132:3.8"]},{"x":"No good deed is ever wholly lost; it remains forever effective in proportion to the divinity of its motivation.","r":["48:6.7"]}]},{"h":"How Goodness Leads Men","items":[{"q":"La bonté de Dieu conduit à la repentance ; la bienfaisance de Dieu conduit au service ; la miséricorde de Dieu conduit au salut ; alors que l’amour de Dieu conduit à l’adorer intelligemment de tout cœur.","r":"149:6.4"},{"x":"Goodness without graciousness commands respect but repels affection; only when it is gracious is it universally attractive.","r":["171:7.2"]},{"x":"Righteousness of conduct must be judged by motives, so the highest goodness is unconscious.","r":["170:3.9"]},{"x":"An isolated morality that overemphasizes goodness while excluding truth and neglecting beauty fails to hold many modern minds.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"All true goodness, whether personal morality, social fairness, or divine ministry, is equally true and beautiful.","r":["2:7.11"]}]}],"see":["Vérité","Beauté","Mal","Moralité","Amour","Père Universel"]},{"n":77,"t":"Caligastia","en":"Caligastia","sum":"Caligastia was the Planetary Prince who came to Urantia some five hundred thousand years ago, a Lanonandek Son of rich experience and a brilliant career, who joined the Lucifer rebellion and betrayed the world entrusted to him. His apostasy isolated Urantia from the universe circuits, sixty members of the planetary staff followed him, and the culture of Dalamatia collapsed. He later entrapped Adam and Eve, and after Jesus defeated him on Mount Hermon he lost the power to invade the minds of men.","sections":[{"h":"A Brilliant Planetary Prince","items":[{"x":"Caligastia was a secondary Lanonandek Son with rich experience in the administration of the local universe and of Satania.","r":["66:1.1"]},{"x":"Lucifer promoted him to his personal staff, and he had long sought appointment as a Planetary Prince.","r":["66:1.2","66:1.3"]},{"x":"He had a record of loyalty and devotion, but also a restless temperament and a tendency to oppose the established order.","r":["66:1.4"]},{"q":"Nul prince planétaire ne s’embarqua jamais pour une carrière de règne sur un monde avec une expérience préparatoire plus riche ni avec de plus belles perspectives que Caligastia en ce jour mémorable, il y a un demi-million d’années.","r":"66:1.5"},{"x":"He arrived about five hundred thousand years ago, when the Sangik races were appearing, and set up his headquarters in the Mesopotamian region.","r":["66:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Dalamatia and the One Hundred","items":[{"x":"His associate assistant, Daligastia, headed the staff, and one hundred volunteers chosen from Jerusem formed the corporeal staff.","r":["66:2.2","66:2.4"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers transplanted the life plasm of one hundred male and female descendants of Andon and Fonta into the material bodies of the staff.","r":["66:2.6","66:2.7"]},{"x":"The Dalamatian revelation, the first teaching of the staff, lasted more than three hundred thousand years until it was interrupted by secession.","r":["92:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Betrayal and Isolation","items":[{"x":"At Satan's visit in the three hundred thousandth year of his rule, Caligastia agreed to betray the planet once the rebellion was proclaimed.","r":["67:1.1","67:1.2"]},{"q":"De toutes les formes du mal, aucune n’a d’effet plus destructeur sur le statut de la personnalité que l’abus de confiance et la déloyauté envers des amis confiants.","r":"67:1.3"},{"x":"Daligastia proclaimed Caligastia \"God of Urantia,\" and at that moment the system circuits were cut and Urantia was isolated.","r":["67:2.3","67:2.4"]},{"x":"Van declared this tantamount to planetary rebellion and protested, and after a struggle of more than seven years the loyalists were vindicated.","r":["67:2.2","67:2.6"]},{"x":"Forty members of the staff refused to rebel; the sixty who rebelled chose Nod as their leader and were reduced to mortal status.","r":["67:3.2","67:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"Caligastia, avec un maximum d’intelligence et une vaste expérience des affaires de l’univers, s’égara — il embrassa le péché.","r":"67:3.9"},{"x":"Amadon, of lesser intellect, remained loyal to the end, showing that loyalty counts more than intelligence in spiritual choice.","r":["67:3.8","67:3.9"]},{"x":"His plan to rebuild society at once on his ideas of personal and group liberty failed, plunging the world into deeper confusion.","r":["67:5.3"]},{"x":"One hundred and sixty-two years after the rebellion, Dalamatia sank beneath the sea.","r":["67:5.4"]},{"x":"Afterward twelve Melchizedek receivers administered the planet, and Van established outposts of civilization throughout the world.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]}]},{"h":"From the Days of Adam to the Days of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Caligastia and Daligastia hindered the preparation of the Garden of Eden and confused its inhabitants with teachings of unbridled liberty.","r":["73:2.5","74:5.6"]},{"q":"Caligastia avait réussi à prendre Adam et Ève au piège, mais n’avait pas réalisé son dessein de les entrainer dans une rébellion ouverte contre le gouvernement de l’univers.","r":"75:7.7"},{"x":"Serapatatia, though well-meaning, never realized that he was playing into the hands of Caligastia and Daligastia.","r":["75:3.6"]},{"x":"Jesus met Caligastia alone on Mount Hermon and prevailed, after which Caligastia's apostasy was virtually settled.","r":["134:8.6","134:8.9","136:3.1"]},{"x":"Before leaving Urantia, Michael offered mercy to Caligastia and Daligastia, but they rejected his offer.","r":["53:8.6"]},{"q":"he has absolutely no power to enter the minds of men, neither can he draw near to their souls to tempt or corrupt them unless they really desire to be cursed with his wicked presence.","r":"53:8.6"},{"q":"Caligastia est resté relativement impuissant depuis la croix du Christ.","r":"53:8.9"}]}],"see":["Rébellion de Lucifer","Urantia","Adam et Ève","Médians","Machiventa Melchizédek","Civilisation"]},{"n":85,"t":"Caractère de Jésus","en":"Character of Jesus","sum":"In The Urantia Book's portrayal of the character of Jesus, the most distinctive feature is not so much flawlessness as symmetry, the exquisite and balanced unification of all his qualities. He was enthusiastic but never fanatical, courageous but never foolhardy, full of gladness yet humble. At the center stood a childlike trust in God and a deep love for people, and he asked his followers not so much to believe in him as to believe with him.","sections":[{"h":"Balance and Unity","items":[{"q":"Le trait exceptionnel de la personnalité du Maitre n’était pas tant sa perfection que son harmonie, son exquise unification équilibrée.","r":"100:7.1"},{"x":"An ordinary mortal cannot attain Jesus' perfection of character, but it is altogether possible to develop a strong and unified personality along the lines of his.","r":["100:7.1"]},{"x":"He was emotional but not flighty, sympathetic but not sentimental, pious but not sanctimonious.","r":["100:7.4"]},{"x":"His plans were marked by consecrated common sense, with nothing queer, erratic, or hysterical about them.","r":["100:7.3"]},{"x":"As a perfectly unified personality, Jesus still today unifies human experience and simplifies life.","r":["100:7.18"]},{"q":"Jésus était grand parce qu’il était bon et, cependant, il fraternisait avec les petits enfants.","r":"100:7.17"}]},{"h":"Sincerity and Courage","items":[{"x":"He was free from affectation and hypocrisy and lived as he taught, staying true to the truth even when his sincerity brought him suffering.","r":["100:7.2"]},{"x":"He was frank but always kind; he hated sin but loved the sinner, and in all his honesty he was fair.","r":["100:7.11"]},{"q":"His courage was magnificent, but he was never foolhardy. His watchword was, \"Fear not.\"","r":"100:7.15"},{"x":"Even when urged, he did not hurry, saying his hour had not yet come; when indignant at evil, his anger was never directed at the sinner.","r":["100:7.14"]},{"x":"He did not seek popular support and was not swayed by people's opinions; he was brave but never proud.","r":["161:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Gladness and Kindness","items":[{"q":"Cet homme de Galilée n’était pas un homme de douleurs ; il avait une âme joyeuse.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"He was not a blind optimist, but out of trust in God and confidence in man he always encouraged others to be of good cheer.","r":["100:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus was a child of joy and a man of rare humor, and at the same time a man acquainted with sorrow.","r":["129:4.4"]},{"x":"Graciousness is the aroma of friendliness from a love-saturated soul, and Jesus spread that gladness wherever he went.","r":["171:7.1","171:7.2"]},{"x":"He was always generous, repeating that it is more blessed to give than to receive, but he was never wasteful or extravagant.","r":["100:7.10"]}]},{"h":"His Way with People","items":[{"x":"Because Jesus truly understood people, he showed genuine sympathy, yet he never indulged in pity or fostered their self-pity.","r":["171:7.3"]},{"x":"He never hurried and comforted people \"as he passed by\"; they felt they were consulting with him rather than confessing to him.","r":["171:7.5"]},{"x":"He did not try to direct or manage people, and those who received his smile felt their power to solve their own problems increase.","r":["171:7.6"]},{"x":"Great things happened because people not only believed in him but he also believed greatly in them.","r":["171:7.8"]},{"q":"Il était littéralement vrai qu’il « circulait en faisant du bien ».","r":"171:7.9"},{"x":"The apostles remembered him as a loyal friend who treated all with equal kindness without flattery, and who loved even sinners and enemies.","r":["161:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Childlike Faith","items":[{"x":"Jesus' faith was not tradition or intellectual belief but wholly personal and spiritual, born of experience with the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["196:0.1","196:0.5"]},{"x":"He did not hold faith as a consolation in hardship but enjoyed it as the serenity and thrill of living in the Father's presence.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"q":"La confiance de Jésus en Dieu ressemblait beaucoup à celle d’un enfant en ses parents.","r":"196:0.11"},{"x":"His strong faith never turned into fanaticism and was always in harmony with balanced judgment about family love, social obligation, and economic necessity.","r":["196:0.6","196:0.7"]},{"x":"His sublime self-forgetfulness shows in his reply when called good teacher: \"Why do you call me good?\"","r":["196:0.9"]}]},{"h":"What It Means to Follow Him","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not ask his disciples to believe in him but to believe with him in the love of God.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"To follow Jesus means to share his faith and to take part in his spirit of unselfish service to men.","r":["196:1.3"]},{"x":"A great service of this revelation will be to bring back the living Jesus, the human Jesus buried in theological tradition.","r":["196:1.1","196:1.2"]}]}],"see":["Effusion de Jésus","Enseignements de Jésus","Foi","Amour","Joie et bonheur","Les douze apôtres"]},{"n":82,"t":"Civilisation","en":"Civilization","sum":"Civilization is a racial acquirement that mankind won through a long and arduous struggle, starting from a state close to the animal. Because it is not passed on automatically by heredity, each generation must hand it on anew through the home and education. The Urantia Book examines one by one the material, intellectual, and social factors that sustain civilization, yet it says that the power that truly lifts culture is spiritual idealism.","sections":[{"h":"Civilization, an Acquired Heritage","items":[{"q":"Civilization is a racial acquirement; it is not biologically inherent","r":"68:0.2"},{"x":"Scientific, philosophic, and religious achievements are not inherited; they are kept only by wisely conserving social inheritance and educating each generation anew.","r":["68:0.2"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution and cultural civilization do not necessarily go together, but culture cannot flourish without a background of adequate racial progress.","r":["81:5.1"]},{"x":"Even though the missions of Caligastia and Adam failed, evolution kept the races moving forward; evolution may be delayed but it cannot be stopped.","r":["81:0.1"]},{"x":"The slogan \"back to nature\" is an ignorant delusion based on belief in a golden age that never existed.","r":["68:1.7"]}]},{"h":"How Society Arose","items":[{"x":"Primitive man was not naturally brotherly; through bitter experience he learned that to survive he must unite, and so he cooperated reluctantly.","r":["68:1.1","68:1.4"]},{"x":"Civilization became man's insurance against violent death, and man pays the premium by submitting to society's mores.","r":["68:1.2","81:5.4"]},{"x":"Hunger, sex love, vanity, and fear of ghosts drew people together and bound them into society.","r":["68:2.4","68:2.6"]},{"q":"Presque toutes les valeurs durables de la civilisation ont leurs racines dans la famille.","r":"68:2.8"},{"x":"The one hundred of Dalamatia did not try to change the primitive races all at once but trained the best of the tribes and sent them back as emissaries of social uplift.","r":["66:6.3","66:6.4"]},{"x":"The chief purpose of the Material Sons and Daughters is to move evolving man from the hunting and herding stages to the agricultural stage.","r":["52:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Factors Sustaining Civilization","items":[{"x":"Factors such as the natural environment, capital goods, scientific knowledge, human resources, language, machines, and the coordination of experts sustain present civilization.","r":["81:6.2","81:6.3","81:6.29"]},{"q":"La culture ne se développe jamais sous le règne de la misère ; les loisirs sont essentiels au progrès de la civilisation.","r":"81:6.6"},{"x":"Science stabilizes philosophy by eliminating error and purifies religion by destroying superstition.","r":["81:6.10"]},{"x":"A common language promotes peace and insures culture, and international exchange in language, trade, art, science, and religion should be encouraged.","r":["81:6.18","81:6.19"]},{"x":"Science guided by wisdom can liberate mankind, but it becomes a calamity for nations lacking the wisdom to adjust the transitional problems of mechanization.","r":["81:6.22"]}]},{"h":"Ideals, Education, and Leadership","items":[{"x":"The basic institution for passing the torch of culture to the next generation is the home, followed by play, social life, and the school.","r":["81:6.23","81:6.24"]},{"q":"Les idéaux d’une génération creusent les chemins de la destinée pour sa postérité immédiate.","r":"81:6.26"},{"x":"Intelligence controls the machinery of civilization and wisdom directs it, but the energy that lifts culture from level to level is spiritual idealism.","r":["81:6.27"]},{"q":"At first life was a struggle for existence; now, for a standard of living; next it will be for quality of thinking","r":"81:6.28"},{"x":"High civilization is born when material wealth, intellectual greatness, moral worth, social cleverness, and cosmic insight are wisely coordinated.","r":["81:6.38"]},{"x":"Civilization is jeopardized only when able and wise leadership disappears, and such leadership has never exceeded one per cent of the population.","r":["81:6.37","81:6.42"]}]},{"h":"Duties and Dangers of Civilization","items":[{"x":"Cultural society is not a club of free memberships but a union of workers making a better world for their descendants.","r":["81:5.3"]},{"x":"Every right is linked with social obligation, and liberty that accepts collective regulation is the legitimate goal of social evolution.","r":["81:5.6","81:5.7"]},{"q":"La préservation du moi fait naitre la société, tandis que l’excès des jouissances égoïstes détruit la civilisation.","r":"68:2.2"},{"x":"Society is not a divine institution but a phenomenon of evolution, so it may be experimented with fearlessly, but great changes should not be attempted suddenly.","r":["81:6.39","81:6.40"]},{"x":"Modern civilization has grown intellectually and scientifically but has stagnated in ethical awareness, spiritual development, and the safeguarding of the home.","r":["81:6.25"]}]},{"h":"Civilization and Religion","items":[{"x":"Religion renders its highest social service when least entangled with secular institutions, and it should not directly engage in building a new order or preserving the old.","r":["99:0.1","99:0.2"]},{"x":"As civilization advances, the attitude of seeking first heavenly realities becomes all the more necessary, even amid efforts to solve material problems.","r":["195:5.1"]},{"x":"Modern culture must become spiritually baptized with a new revelation of Jesus' life.","r":["195:10.1"]}]}],"see":["Gouvernement et société","Mariage et famille","Races","Évolution","Science et religion","Adam et Ève"]},{"n":16,"t":"Constellations et systèmes locaux","en":"Constellations and Local Systems","sum":"Un univers local est divisé en cent constellations, et chaque constellation en cent systèmes locaux. La constellation, gouvernée par les Très Hauts de l’ordre des Vorondadeks, est une unité législative qui socialise les mortels ascendants dans des sièges tels qu’Édentia ; le système local, gouverné par un Souverain de Système de l’ordre des Lanonandeks, est une unité exécutive qui accueille sur Jérusem et sur les mondes des maisons les mortels qui viennent de survivre. Urantia appartient au système de Satania, dans la constellation de Norlatiadek, et reçoit des soins particuliers depuis la rébellion de Lucifer.","sections":[{"h":"Les divisions de l’univers local","items":[{"x":"Urantia est le 606e monde habité du système de Satania, dans Norlatiadek, l’une des cent constellations de Nébadon.","r":["43:0.1"]},{"x":"Un système comprend environ mille mondes habitables, et une constellation cent systèmes.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4"]},{"x":"Les constellations fonctionnent comme des unités législatives et les systèmes locaux comme des unités exécutives, tandis que le gouvernement de Salvington est l’autorité judiciaire et coordinatrice suprême.","r":["43:2.2"]},{"x":"Les chefs des constellations relient les systèmes locaux à l’administration universelle de Salvington et, par la réflectivité, aux Anciens des Jours sur Uversa.","r":["43:0.1"]}]},{"h":"Le gouvernement de la constellation et les Très Hauts","items":[{"x":"Une constellation est gouvernée par trois Très Hauts de l’ordre des Vorondadeks, celui qui préside étant appelé Père de la Constellation.","r":["43:3.2"]},{"q":"no disaffection of the Vorondadek Sons has ever occurred in Nebadon.","r":"43:3.1"},{"x":"L’assemblée législative de la constellation se compose de trois groupes : une chambre basse d’ascendeurs, une troisième chambre de séraphins et d’autres êtres, et une chambre haute des Fils divins.","r":["43:2.5","43:2.6","43:2.7"]},{"x":"Les Très Hauts s’occupent du bien-être des nations et des races plutôt que des individus ; ils règnent dans les royaumes des hommes plutôt que dans le cœur individuel.","r":["43:3.5","43:9.4"]},{"x":"Un observateur Vorondadek est stationné sur les mondes isolés par la rébellion, et c’est lui qui, en fait, « règne dans les royaumes des hommes ».","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"Le Fidèle des Jours d’Édentia se tient aux côtés des Pères de la Constellation en tant que représentant de la Trinité, mais il ne donne jamais de conseil sans qu’on le lui demande.","r":["43:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Édentia : le jardin de Dieu","items":[{"x":"Édentia, le siège de la constellation, est environ cent fois plus grande qu’Urantia, et soixante-dix sphères majeures et sept-cents satellites tournent autour d’elle.","r":["43:0.2"]},{"x":"La capitale de la constellation abonde en ornements vivants et s’appelle « les jardins de Dieu » ; la moitié de la superficie d’Édentia est consacrée aux jardins des Très Hauts.","r":["43:6.1","43:6.2"]},{"q":"there is nothing in all Edentia to make any living being afraid.","r":"43:6.5"},{"x":"En traversant les soixante-dix mondes, les mortels ascendants vivent avec les univitatias et apprennent l’éthique de groupe et la véritable socialisation de la personnalité morontielle.","r":["43:8.3","43:8.4"]},{"q":"Intellectuellement, socialement et spirituellement, lorsque deux créatures morales emploient la technique de l’association, elles font plus que doubler leur potentiel personnel d’aboutissement universel ; c’est plutôt au quadruple qu’elles portent leur réussite et leurs possibilités d’accomplissement.","r":"43:8.11"},{"x":"Le séjour dans la constellation marque le milieu du chemin qui mène de l’être semblable à l’animal à l’esprit ascendant ; c’est la période la plus uniforme et la plus stable de la carrière morontielle.","r":["43:9.2","43:9.3"]}]},{"h":"Le système local et Jérusem","items":[{"x":"Le chef exécutif d’un système local est le Souverain du Système, un Fils Lanonandek primaire ; l’actuel souverain de Satania est Lanaforge, le successeur de Lucifer.","r":["45:2.1","45:3.2"]},{"x":"L’histoire de Nébadon a connu trois cas de déloyauté parmi les Souverains de Systèmes, la rébellion de Lucifer dans Satania étant la dernière et la plus étendue.","r":["45:2.1"]},{"x":"Jérusem est entourée de sept mondes de culture de transition et de leurs satellites, et les sept mondes des maisons sont des satellites du premier monde de transition.","r":["45:0.1","45:0.2"]},{"q":"Les capitales des systèmes sont uniques en ce sens qu’elles sont les seuls mondes où l’on peut observer à peu près parfaitement les trois phases matérielle, morontielle et spirituelle de l’existence universelle.","r":"46:4.8"},{"x":"Sur Jérusem, il n’y a ni jour et nuit séparés ni saisons, et la lumière est filtrée uniformément par tout le ciel, et non par une seule source.","r":["46:1.4","46:1.5"]},{"q":"Un gouvernement représentatif est l’idéal divin de l’autonomie pour les êtres imparfaits.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"L’entrainement à l’ascension dans la capitale du système","items":[{"x":"Les mondes des maisons sont le lieu où les mortels qui n’ont pas fusionné avec leur Ajusteur au cours de la vie dans la chair reçoivent l’occasion de reprendre leur accomplissement spirituel interrompu.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"Les Fils et Filles Matériels, citoyens permanents de Jérusem, deviennent les parrains et les éducateurs immédiats des mortels ascendants.","r":["45:5.5","45:6.2"]},{"x":"Les ascendeurs qui n’ont pas eu d’expérience parentale doivent acquérir cette expérience essentielle dans les foyers des Fils Matériels sur Jérusem ou dans les pouponnières probatoires.","r":["45:6.4","45:6.6"]},{"x":"Aux élections de Jérusem, la valeur d’un vote varie selon le degré de sagesse morontielle, et l’on ne peut partir pour la constellation qu’après avoir atteint la personnalité mota.","r":["45:7.6","45:7.8"]},{"x":"Les assemblées tenues sur le monde des finalitaires donnent aux résidents des mondes des maisons l’assurance qu’eux aussi pourront achever le long voyage.","r":["45:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Des soins particuliers après la rébellion","items":[{"x":"Depuis la rébellion de Lucifer, les Très Hauts d’Édentia ont pris en charge certaines phases de l’autorité planétaire sur les mondes rebelles et l’exercent encore.","r":["43:3.7"]},{"x":"Lucifer et la plupart des personnalités qui l’ont suivi sont confinés sur les mondes-prisons qui entourent le monde du Père de Jérusem, solennel avertissement pour tout Nébadon.","r":["45:1.11"]},{"x":"Après le triomphe du Christ Micaël, Satan fut rejeté à l’unanimité par les Souverains de Systèmes lors d’un conclave sur Édentia.","r":["43:4.9"]},{"q":"Quand nulle porte n’est ouverte pour recevoir le mal, il n’existe aucune occasion d’entretenir le péché.","r":"43:4.9"},{"x":"Les vingt-quatre conseillers de Jérusem sont des personnes originaires d’Urantia qui représentent Micaël lors des appels nominaux de Satania et dans les plans d’ascension des mondes isolés.","r":["45:4.1","45:4.2"]}]}],"see":["Univers local de Nébadon","Mondes des maisons","Rébellion de Lucifer","Ascension des mortels","Fils et Filles Matériels","Melchizédeks"]},{"n":32,"t":"Corps de la Finalité","en":"Corps of the Finality","sum":"The Corps of the Finality is the presently known destination of the ascending mortals of time, who are mustered into it after finding God and attaining Paradise. Centered on glorified mortals, it also includes Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, adopted seraphim, Material Sons, and midway creatures, and its members now serve on worlds settled in light and life. Their ultimate destiny has not been revealed, but it is conjectured to concern the future universes of outer space.","sections":[{"h":"Composition of the Corps","items":[{"x":"The primary Corps of the Finality consists of Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, glorified mortals, adopted seraphim, and glorified Material Sons and midway creatures.","r":["31:0.1","31:0.8"]},{"x":"The corps is organized in companies of one thousand, of which mortals and seraphim make up 990, leaving only ten places for the other beings.","r":["31:1.3","31:3.1"]},{"x":"All are received as equals, yet that equality does not erase individuality or personal identity.","r":["31:0.9"]},{"x":"Gravity Messengers are personalized Adjusters who transcend time and space, and they share a deep affection with mortals who have fused with Adjusters.","r":["31:2.2","31:2.4"]},{"q":"Ils sont en vérité l’accumulation des âmes éprouvées et sincères du temps et de l’espace — le sel évolutionnaire de l’univers — et ils sont pour toujours à l’abri du mal et inaccessibles au péché.","r":"31:0.13"},{"x":"Evangels of light are attached temporarily without taking the oath, and the one vacancy beyond the 999 permanent members remains a mystery.","r":["31:7.1","31:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Who Enters","items":[{"x":"Of all the creatures of the grand universe, only those fused with the Father are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality and take the finaliter oath.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"x":"Spirit-fused mortals usually remain in local universe service and do not share the destiny of the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","r":["40:9.9"]},{"x":"Many guardian seraphim ascend with their mortal wards, take the same finaliter oath, and are mustered into the corps.","r":["31:4.1","40:1.1"]},{"x":"Children who die early, deprived of the experience of mortal life, become Paradise citizens but do not enter the Corps of the Finality.","r":["47:2.8"]},{"q":"Et tout mortel connaissant Dieu désire ardemment être un finalitaire.","r":"14:6.39"}]},{"h":"The Way to Paradise","items":[{"x":"Mortals ascend through the stages of spirit one by one and become spirits of the sixth stage when they take the oath of the Corps of the Finality.","r":["31:3.4"]},{"x":"The seventh jubilee celebrates entrance into the mortal Corps of the Finality and the beginning of eternal service.","r":["27:7.8"]},{"x":"In the finaliter receiving circle, the chief of the Transcendentalers administers the eternity oath of the Trinity.","r":["31:8.4"]},{"q":"Les mortels évolutionnaires naissent sur les planètes de l’espace, passent par les mondes morontiels, gravissent les univers spirituels, traversent les sphères de Havona, trouvent Dieu, atteignent le Paradis et sont enrôlés dans le Corps primaire de la Finalité pour y attendre leur prochaine affectation de service universel.","r":"31:10.20"}]},{"h":"Present Service and Organization","items":[{"x":"Finaliters are not assigned to their native superuniverse until they have served in the other six, and so they gain a sevenfold concept of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:0.10"]},{"q":"Il y a en permanence une ou plusieurs compagnies de finalitaires mortels en service sur Urantia.","r":"31:0.11"},{"x":"The finaliters are a self-governing body that chooses its own leaders, and their oath of allegiance is given to the Paradise Trinity alone.","r":["31:0.12"]},{"x":"The first transition world of Satania is the headquarters of more than one hundred thousand finaliter companies, and finaliters remain invisible until true spirit vision is attained.","r":["47:0.2","47:1.3"]},{"x":"The mortal Corps of the Finality serves in various roles on worlds settled in light and life, but it seems to have no settled duties as yet.","r":["30:4.32"]}]},{"h":"A Destiny Not Yet Finished","items":[{"x":"Finaliters have reached the present limits of creature perfection, but not yet the ultimate spirit status or the finality of creature service.","r":["31:3.6"]},{"q":"Why should the Gods be so concerned in so thoroughly training surviving mortals in the technique of universe management?","r":"31:3.8"},{"x":"In the finaliter circle on Jerusem stands a sealed and empty temple inscribed \"Not yet dedicated to the seventh stage of spirit.\"","r":["46:5.32"]},{"x":"Having found the Father, the finaliters may one day have to begin a new search for the superfinite Father.","r":["10:8.7"]}]},{"h":"Prospects Toward Outer Space","items":[{"x":"The seven corps of finality are supervised by the senior Master Architect, and Grandfanda is head of the council of supreme destiny.","r":["31:10.1","31:10.9"]},{"x":"It is conjectured that the finaliters will compensate for the experiential deficiency of the outer universes, which cannot share in the evolution of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:10.11","31:10.13"]},{"q":"Nous croyons que les mortels fusionnés avec leur Ajusteur, ainsi que leurs compagnons finalitaires, sont destinés à fonctionner, d’une façon ou d’une autre, dans l’administration des univers du premier niveau d’espace extérieur.","r":"112:7.17"},{"x":"Even if there were no unrevealed future destiny, the present assignments of the finaliters would fully justify the ascension plan.","r":["30:4.33"]}]}],"see":["Ascension des mortels","Fusion avec l’Ajusteur","Havona","Paradis","Être Suprême","Quête de la perfection"]},{"n":72,"t":"Croissance","en":"Growth","sum":"Growth is the process in which the actual and the potential combine and values are realized in experience; unlike perfect Havona, it is the hallmark of the evolving grand universe and the Supreme Being. Man's spiritual growth proceeds from an awakening to needs to the discernment of meanings and the discovery of values, and it always takes place unconsciously. Man cannot cause growth, but through devotion to supreme values and living faith he can supply its conditions.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Growth","items":[{"q":"L’association des actuels et des potentiels équivaut à la croissance, à la réalisation expérientielle des valeurs.","r":"100:3.6"},{"x":"Growth is not mere progress; progress is meaningful, but without growth it is relatively valueless.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Values are never static, and change that does not enlarge meanings and elevate values is potential evil.","r":["100:3.5"]},{"x":"The supreme value of human life lies in the growth of values, the progress of meanings, and the realization of their cosmic interrelatedness.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Growth of a part is not the same as maturity of the whole; to traverse the psychic circles, the whole personality must grow harmoniously.","r":["110:6.3"]}]},{"h":"The Growing Universe and the Supreme Being","items":[{"q":"La croissance est la marque distinctive de la Déité expérientielle : il n’y a pas eu de croissance de Havona ;","r":"116:0.3"},{"x":"Experiential growth implies a creature-Creator partnership, the association of God and man.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The Supreme Being is first a spirit personality derived from the Trinity and second a God of evolutionary growth.","r":["115:4.2"]},{"x":"The growth of the whole is the sum of the growth of all its parts, and its completion is an act of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:6.6"]},{"x":"Creative growth is endless, but along the way moments of satisfying goal attainment become preludes to new adventure.","r":["118:0.10"]}]},{"h":"Stages and Signs of Spiritual Growth","items":[{"q":"La croissance spirituelle est d’abord un éveil aux besoins, ensuite un discernement des significations et enfin une découverte des valeurs.","r":"100:2.2"},{"x":"True spiritual development shows itself in a life motivated by love, activated by unselfish ministry, and dominated by wholehearted worship.","r":["100:2.2"]},{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by sharing what one receives with one's fellows.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spiritual growth is mutually stimulated by intimate association with other religionists, and love is the soil of that growth.","r":["100:0.2"]},{"x":"Loyal persons are growing persons, and children are lastingly impressed by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Conditions That Favor Growth","items":[{"q":"L’homme ne peut provoquer la croissance, mais il peut lui fournir des conditions favorables.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Growth, whether physical, intellectual, or spiritual, is always unconscious; like love, it must grow.","r":["100:3.7","100:1.9"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, worshipful problem solving, and avoidance of selfishness favor growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"The innate drive toward growth is most surely fostered by an attitude of wholehearted devotion to supreme values.","r":["100:1.6"]},{"q":"Spiritual growth is greatest where all external pressures are at a minimum.","r":"103:5.11"}]},{"h":"Hindrances to Growth and the Teaching of Jesus","items":[{"q":"Certaines personnes sont trop affairées pour croitre et se trouvent alors en sérieux danger d’immobilisme spirituel.","r":"100:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught not the building of character but the growth of character, and he likened the kingdom of heaven to a mustard seed.","r":["140:8.27","151:4.2"]},{"x":"With a carpenter's analogy Jesus taught that the soul is a living growth, and mind and morals are the soil from which its higher expressions spring.","r":["156:5.2"]},{"x":"The true believer should ask whether he is becoming more skillful in showing goodness today than yesterday, this year than last.","r":["156:5.15"]},{"x":"The morontia life forever uproots animal vestiges such as procrastination and evasion, so that growth may continue.","r":["48:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Expérience","Être Suprême","Âme","Quête de la perfection","Adversité et épreuves","Religion personnelle"]},{"n":7,"t":"Dieu le Septuple","en":"God the Sevenfold","sum":"Dieu le Septuple est l’association septuple de Déité instituée par le Père Universel pour que les créatures finies puissent approcher la Déité. Elle s’étend du Fils Créateur de l’univers local au Père Universel en passant par les Anciens des Jours, les Sept Maitres Esprits, l’Être Suprême, l’Esprit Infini et le Fils Éternel, et les mortels ascendants découvrent la Déité expérientiellement dans cet ordre. Ses trois premiers niveaux sont aussi la source du pouvoir tout-puissant de l’Être Suprême.","sections":[{"h":"Sept marches vers la Déité","items":[{"x":"Pour compenser les limitations du statut et des concepts finis, le Père Universel a établi l’approche septuple de la Déité par les créatures évolutionnaires.","r":["0:8.1"]},{"x":"Les sept niveaux sont les Fils Créateurs Paradisiaques, les Anciens des Jours, les Sept Maitres Esprits, l’Être Suprême, Dieu l’Esprit, Dieu le Fils et Dieu le Père.","r":["0:8.2","0:8.8"]},{"q":"Dieu le Septuple signifie que la Déité du Paradis reconnait les barrières du temps dans les univers évolutionnaires de l’espace.","r":"106:1.3"},{"x":"La carrière expérientielle de la découverte de Dieu commence par la reconnaissance de la divinité du Fils Créateur de l’univers local et se poursuit, par les Anciens des Jours et les Maitres Esprits, jusqu’au Père du Paradis.","r":["0:8.9"]},{"x":"Dieu le Septuple est la Déité qui fonctionne effectivement pour les mortels évolutionnaires dans la carrière d’ascension au Paradis.","r":["0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Créateurs Suprêmes et Déités du Paradis","items":[{"x":"Des sept niveaux, les trois premiers sont les Créateurs Suprêmes et les trois derniers les Déités du Paradis, l’Être Suprême s’interposant toujours entre eux.","r":["116:2.4","116:2.12"]},{"x":"La Déité du Paradis a atténué et qualifié la personnalisation de la divinité hors du Paradis pour amener à l’existence les Créateurs Suprêmes, et ceux-ci portent la lumière de vie aux mondes évolutionnaires.","r":["116:2.3"]},{"x":"Les actes combinés des trois premiers niveaux n’égalent pas la Déité du Paradis ; ils constituent un nouveau potentiel de pouvoir de Déité expérientielle.","r":["116:2.13"]},{"q":"Dans l’association de Déité de Dieu le Septuple, les Fils Créateurs fournissent le mécanisme par lequel le mortel devient immortel et le fini atteint l’embrassement de l’infini.","r":"0:8.11"},{"x":"Le ministère de divinité du Septuple atteint vers l’intérieur, par le Fils Éternel, le Père du Paradis et, vers l’extérieur, par les Anciens des Jours, les Fils Créateurs.","r":["106:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Relation avec l’Être Suprême","items":[{"x":"Dieu le Suprême tient de la Trinité ses attributs de personnalité et d’esprit, mais son pouvoir s’actualise dans les actions des Fils Créateurs, des Anciens des Jours et des Maitres Esprits.","r":["0:8.10","116:2.2"]},{"x":"Dieu le Suprême ne se manifeste aux créatures évolutionnaires comme une personnalité de pouvoir que lorsque les trois premiers niveaux de Dieu le Septuple fonctionnent de manière coordonnée.","r":["116:2.14"]},{"q":"L’Être Suprême est la révélation maximum de la Déité aux sept superunivers pour le présent âge de l’univers.","r":"116:2.12"},{"x":"Dans l’expérience mortelle, l’Être Suprême est l’unificateur de Dieu le Septuple, le maximum de Déité que les créatures finies puissent effectivement comprendre.","r":["56:8.1"]},{"x":"Les divers aspects de la Déité septuple sont actuellement intégrés de diverses manières, mais tous sont destinés à être unifiés dans la Suprématie.","r":["106:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Les contrôleurs septuples et la fonction cosmique","items":[{"x":"Dieu le Septuple comprend non seulement les créateurs, mais aussi les contrôleurs septuples du grand univers, tels que les Maitres Contrôleurs Physiques, les Centres Suprêmes de Pouvoir et les Directeurs Suprêmes de Pouvoir.","r":["116:5.1","116:5.9"]},{"x":"Le conseil des Sept Maitres Esprits semble coordonner les vastes activités de Dieu le Septuple, et il contribue aussi au dernier niveau, l’union du Fils Créateur et de l’Esprit Créatif.","r":["17:8.3","17:8.8"]},{"q":"La fonction de Dieu le Septuple date de l’organisation des sept superunivers et va probablement s’étendre avec l’évolution future des créations de l’espace extérieur.","r":"0:8.12"},{"q":"Les Absolus sont coordonnés dans l’Ultime, conditionnés dans le Suprême et modifiés par l’espace-temps dans Dieu le Septuple.","r":"56:9.1"},{"x":"Par le ministère de Dieu le Septuple, l’imparfait est relié au parfait dans le décalage du temps, et la créature devient l’associée du Créateur dans sa propre évolution.","r":["106:1.2"]},{"x":"Le pouvoir qui nait des accomplissements de Dieu le Septuple est un pouvoir expérientiel, gagné et démontré, par contraste avec le pouvoir existentiel des Déités du Paradis.","r":["106:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Révélation en lumière et vie","items":[{"x":"L’évolution du temps et de l’espace commence sur des planètes présidées par l’union du Fils Créateur et de l’Esprit Créatif, première manifestation de Dieu le Septuple, et à mesure qu’un univers local est ancré, Dieu le Septuple se révèle plus clairement.","r":["56:7.2"]},{"x":"À mesure que les créations sont ancrées, les trois premières manifestations se retirent et une activité plus complète de Dieu le Suprême apparait, mais ce qui suit n’a pas encore été révélé.","r":["56:7.6"]},{"q":"Nous savons toutefois que, dans les univers du temps et de l’espace, Dieu le Septuple permet de s’approcher progressivement du Père Universel, et que cette approche évolutionnaire est unifiée expérientiellement en Dieu le Suprême.","r":"56:7.8"},{"x":"Les mondes de lumière et de vie saisissent successivement la réalité de Dieu le Septuple, depuis l’adoration du Fils Créateur jusqu’à l’adoration du Père du Paradis.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"Quel que soit le niveau de Déité atteint, l’ascendeur redécouvre chaque fois, sur un nouveau niveau d’expérience, le Père du Paradis de toutes les personnalités.","r":["56:9.10"]}]}],"see":["Être Suprême","Fils Créateur Micaël","Anciens des Jours","Sept Maitres Esprits","Trinité du Paradis","Ascension des mortels"]},{"n":9,"t":"Dieu l’Ultime","en":"God the Ultimate","sum":"Dieu l’Ultime est la deuxième Déité expérientielle, qui s’extériorise après l’Être Suprême ; c’est une personnalité-pouvoir transcendantale qui fonctionne sur le niveau absonite, lequel transcende le temps et l’espace du maitre univers. Il s’extériorise à partir de l’unification de la Trinité Ultime, qui sera composée des Créateurs Suprêmes, de l’Être Suprême et des Architectes du Maitre Univers, et sa pleine émergence signifie l’achèvement de la création du maitre univers. Il est l’objet de la quête suivante des finalitaires et des citoyens parachevés, une fois le grand univers ancré dans la lumière et la vie.","sections":[{"h":"Déité du niveau absonite","items":[{"q":"Dieu l’Ultime — Le Dieu en cours d’extériorisation du supertemps et de l’espace transcendé.","r":"0:2.17"},{"x":"Les réalités absonites sont des choses et des êtres extériorisés plutôt que créés, sans commencement ni fin et transcendant le temps et l’espace, et la fonction de la Déité à leur égard est l’Ultimité.","r":["0:1.12"]},{"q":"Le Suprême est l’unification de la Trinité comprise par les êtres finis. L’Ultime est l’unification de la Trinité du Paradis comprise par les êtres absonites.","r":"0:9.2"},{"x":"Parmi les sept natures de la Déité, la Suprématie est le moi évolutionnaire-expérientiel et l’Ultimité le moi transcendantal-expérientiel.","r":["118:0.5","118:0.7"]},{"x":"Dieu l’Ultime transcende le temps et l’espace et il est capable de s’associer fonctionnellement avec les Absolus, mais il est absonite.","r":["106:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Suprématie et Ultimité","items":[{"q":"Dieu le Septuple est indispensable à l’aboutissement évolutionnaire du Suprême, mais le Suprême est également indispensable à l’émergence finale de l’Ultime.","r":"118:0.9"},{"x":"Le Suprême et l’Ultime se complètent dans l’accomplissement de la destinée, et ils forment le pont expérientiel qui relie les commencements et les achèvements de toute croissance créatrice dans le maitre univers.","r":["118:0.9"]},{"x":"L’Ultimité et la Suprématie sont comparables, mais non identiques, et l’Ultimité n’est pas simplement un agrandissement de la Suprématie.","r":["106:8.15"]},{"x":"De même que l’Être Suprême évolue à partir des potentiels du grand univers, Dieu l’Ultime s’extériorise à partir des potentiels de divinité des domaines du maitre univers qui transcendent le temps et l’espace.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"x":"Lorsque Dieu le Suprême en viendra à gouverner directement les univers du temps et de l’espace, cette administration fonctionnera sous le supercontrôle de l’Ultimité, et Dieu l’Ultime commencera à apparaitre comme le Tout-Puissant transcendantal.","r":["118:2.4"]}]},{"h":"La Trinité Ultime","items":[{"x":"La Trinité Ultime est l’association de Déité des Créateurs Suprêmes, de Dieu le Suprême et des Architectes du Maitre Univers, et elle est actuellement en évolution.","r":["0:12.6","106:8.10"]},{"q":"Finalement et inévitablement, Dieu l’Ultime acquerra pouvoir et personnalité comme conséquence, au niveau de la Déité, de l’unification de cette Trinité Ultime expérientielle dans le cadre en expansion du maitre univers à peu près illimité.","r":"0:12.6"},{"x":"Lorsque l’âge présent de l’univers prendra fin et que le Suprême Tout-Puissant émergera, la première Trinité expérientielle fonctionnera pleinement et intégrera davantage l’évolution de la maitre création.","r":["106:3.2"]},{"x":"Cette Trinité comprend les Maitres-Fils Créateurs, de sorte que l’expérience effective des créatures est englobée dans son association.","r":["106:3.3"]},{"q":"L’extériorisation totale de l’Ultime implique le parachèvement de la création du maitre univers, et comporte la pleine émergence de cette Déité transcendantale.","r":"106:4.2"},{"x":"L’unification du maitre univers est l’acte d’extériorisation de l’Ultime, et l’on pense qu’elle reflète une certaine phase du supercontrôle absonite de la Trinité du Paradis.","r":["10:8.2"]}]},{"h":"L’Ultimité révélée dès maintenant","items":[{"x":"De même que le Suprême est spirituellement et personnellement présent dans Havona, l’Ultimité y existe dans un sens absonite et superpersonnel.","r":["106:4.3"]},{"x":"On sait que des Vice-Gérants Qualifiés de l’Ultime existent déjà, mais leur emplacement et leur fonction actuels n’ont pas été révélés.","r":["106:4.3","117:7.4"]},{"x":"Dieu l’Ultime laisse présager son supercontrôle transcendantal dans les stades ultérieurs des univers locaux ancrés dans la lumière et la vie.","r":["56:7.5"]},{"x":"Les mortels qui atteignent le septième stade de lumière et de vie, tout en apprenant à connaitre Dieu le Suprême, discernent vaguement le ministère omniprésent de Dieu l’Ultime.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"L’« extériorisation de la capacité de l’univers », qui transforme le potentiel indifférencié en plans d’univers définis, est l’activité de l’Ultimité et des agences transcendantales.","r":["118:4.6"]}]},{"h":"Le prochain but des finalitaires","items":[{"x":"Les ascendeurs trouvent Dieu le Suprême dans Havona et, après être devenus finalitaires, ils tentent de le connaitre en tant qu’Ultimité.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Lorsque la vérité, la beauté et la bonté de l’Être Suprême les ont pleinement pénétrées, les qualités absonites de la divinité ultime, au-delà de ce niveau conceptuel, s’ouvrent devant les créatures en progrès.","r":["115:3.19"]},{"x":"Dieu l’Ultime existe pour offrir une destinée de service ultime à toutes les créatures qui atteignent les niveaux absonites par le ministère de Dieu le Septuple.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"q":"Certainement, surement et inexorablement, l’énigme de la Déité émergente de Dieu l’Ultime mettra au défi les citoyens devenus parfaits des univers établis, exactement comme leurs ancêtres évolutionnaires, qui se débattaient, furent jadis mis au défi par la recherche de Dieu le Suprême.","r":"117:7.17"},{"x":"Pour les finalitaires qui ont atteint l’Ultimité, le chemin restant est la quête de l’Absolu, et ils savent qu’au bout de ce chemin ils trouveront le même Père du Paradis.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Dieu le Suprême et Dieu l’Ultime sont des Déités éternelles seulement dans le futur et non dans le passé : ils ont un commencement de personnalité, mais pas de fin.","r":["0:9.5"]}]}],"see":["Être Suprême","Trinité du Paradis","Les trois Absolus","Corps de la Finalité","Grand univers et maitre univers","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":89,"t":"Les douze apôtres","en":"Twelve Apostles","sum":"The twelve apostles were ordinary Galileans whom Jesus personally called, trained, and ordained to proclaim the gospel of the kingdom of heaven. They were not ignorant men but men of varied temperaments who had received synagogue schooling, and each, with his own strengths and weaknesses, was transformed by living with Jesus. That only one of them deserted him, even though Jesus repeatedly shattered their worldly expectations, testifies to the charm of his life.","sections":[{"h":"Calling and Training","items":[{"x":"Jesus chose the first six himself, and each of them recommended one more, making twelve.","r":["139:6.1","138:5.1"]},{"x":"The first six apostles went out two by two, preaching the gospel by personal contact, and learned that religion is a purely personal experience.","r":["138:1.1","138:2.1"]},{"x":"The monotonous period of alternating fishing and personal work was a severe test, but they endured it through loyalty to the Master.","r":["138:9.1"]},{"x":"On January 12, A.D. 27, Jesus ordained the twelve as public preachers of the gospel of the kingdom.","r":["140:0.1"]},{"x":"The so-called Sermon on the Mount was not the gospel itself but Jesus' ordination charge to the twelve.","r":["140:4.1"]}]},{"h":"Ordinary and Diverse Men","items":[{"q":"Ne commettez pas l’erreur de considérer les apôtres comme complètement ignorants et dépourvus d’instruction.","r":"139:0.3"},{"x":"\"Unlearned\" means they were laymen untrained in rabbinical lore and methods of scriptural interpretation.","r":["139:0.4"]},{"x":"The apostles learned about the kingdom of heaven from Jesus, and Jesus learned much about human nature from them.","r":["139:0.2"]},{"x":"All the apostles loved Jesus, but each was drawn by some trait of his character that especially appealed to him.","r":["139:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Four Chief Apostles","items":[{"x":"Andrew, the eldest, became chief of the apostolic corps and held that place to the end; not a great preacher, he was an effective personal worker.","r":["139:1.2","139:1.3","139:1.4"]},{"x":"Peter was impulsive and optimistic, a born leader and eloquent speaker, but his speech often ran ahead of his thinking.","r":["139:2.3","139:2.4"]},{"x":"James Zebedee had a fierce temper, but his ability to see a problem from many sides brought him closest to the real meaning of Jesus' teaching.","r":["139:3.2","139:3.4"]},{"x":"John, the youngest, served as Jesus' personal representative in many matters, but the phrase \"the disciple whom Jesus loved\" is not accurate.","r":["139:4.2","139:4.4"]},{"x":"Peter, James, and John were appointed by Andrew as personal aides to attend to Jesus at his side.","r":["139:4.3"]},{"q":"Andrew was a man of clear insight, logical thought, and firm decision","r":"139:1.10"}]},{"h":"The Other Apostles","items":[{"x":"Philip, with his \"show me,\" lacked imagination but was a faithful steward who did small things in a great way.","r":["139:5.2","139:5.3","139:5.4"]},{"x":"Nathaniel was an honest man \"in whom there is no guile\" and the philosopher of the twelve; his weakness was a pride that verged on prejudice.","r":["139:6.3","139:6.4"]},{"x":"Matthew, the former publican, handled the finances of the group and was most deeply grateful for the Master's forgiving nature.","r":["139:7.2","139:7.4"]},{"x":"Thomas was the real scientist of the group, with an analytic mind and unflinching courage, but he struggled with doubt all his life.","r":["139:8.2","139:8.4"]},{"x":"The Alpheus twins were ordinary men with neither strong nor weak points, yet through them many timid believers entered the kingdom.","r":["139:9.4","139:9.5"]},{"x":"Simon Zelotes led the hesitant into the kingdom by his inspiring loyalty, but he never fully shed his nationalistic thinking.","r":["139:11.3","139:11.4"]},{"q":"Ils étaient « les moindres de tous les apôtres » ; ils le savaient, et cela les mettait de bonne humeur.","r":"139:9.5"}]},{"h":"Judas Iscariot","items":[{"x":"Judas was the only Judean among the apostles and the best educated; he handled the treasury honestly and efficiently.","r":["139:12.2","139:12.3"]},{"q":"Judas ne se comprenait réellement pas lui-même ; il n’était pas franchement sincère envers lui-même.","r":"139:12.2"},{"x":"He never overcame his prejudice against his Galilean associates and inwardly criticized Jesus as timid.","r":["139:12.4"]},{"q":"Jésus se borna à regarder le traitre avec pitié.","r":"139:12.14"}]},{"h":"Ambassadors of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that, as citizens of another, heavenly kingdom, they must now live better lives than before.","r":["140:3.1"]},{"x":"He taught the apostles at length not so much what they should do as what they should be.","r":["140:10.1"]},{"q":"LE charme et la droiture de la vie terrestre de Jésus comportent un éloquent témoignage : bien qu’il n’eût cessé de briser les espoirs de ses apôtres et de mettre en pièces chacune de leurs ambitions d’élévation personnelle, il ne fut abandonné que par un seul d’entre eux.","r":"139:0.1"}]}],"see":["Enseignements de Jésus","Caractère de Jésus","Pentecôte","Résurrection de Jésus","Mort sur la croix","Royaume des cieux"]},{"n":84,"t":"Effusion de Jésus","en":"Bestowal of Jesus","sum":"The bestowal of Jesus is the event in which Michael, Creator Son of Nebadon, in his seventh and final bestowal, was born on Urantia as a mortal infant and lived a human life to its end. Through this bestowal Michael completed his universe sovereignty by experience and ended the Lucifer rebellion; above all, he revealed God to man and showed God a man made perfect. The Urantia Book stresses that the supreme purpose of the bestowal was to enhance the revelation of God.","sections":[{"h":"Seven Bestowals and Sovereignty Earned by Experience","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son must live the life of his creatures in their likeness, and this is part of the price paid for universe sovereignty.","r":["120:0.1"]},{"x":"After six bestowals, as a Melchizedek, a Lanonandek, an Adam, a seraphim, a mortal, and a morontia mortal, Michael became a mortal of flesh and blood on Urantia in his seventh.","r":["119:8.4","120:0.2"]},{"q":"Micaël naquit créateur, il fut éduqué comme administrateur, formé comme directeur exécutif, mais il lui fallut gagner sa souveraineté par expérience.","r":"119:8.2"},{"x":"In each bestowal Michael subjected himself to a different will of the Paradise Deities, and on Urantia he submitted wholly to the will of the Universal Father.","r":["120:0.4","120:1.2"]},{"x":"The sum of the seven bestowals became Nebadon's new revelation of the Supreme Being and also contributed to expanding the sovereignty of the Supreme.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"The Eternal Son shares creature experience through the incarnations of the Paradise Sons, and so in Michael he actually came to mortal man.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Immanuel's Charge","items":[{"x":"Unlike his earlier bestowals, Michael had to appear on Urantia not as a fully grown being but as a helpless infant.","r":["120:1.1"]},{"x":"Michael was to lay aside all extraplanetary help and live his mortal life relying only on the Paradise Father.","r":["120:1.3"]},{"q":"Throughout your Urantia bestowal you need be concerned with but one thing, the unbroken communion between you and your Paradise Father","r":"120:1.4"},{"x":"Immanuel advised him to be chiefly a teacher, first liberating man's spiritual nature, enlightening his mind, and freeing him from age-old fears.","r":["120:2.5"]},{"x":"He was also counseled not to become involved in economic and political matters, not to form an organized cult, and to leave no writings or portraits.","r":["120:3.4","120:3.6","120:3.7"]},{"x":"Since a bestowal Son leaves no human offspring on a planet, Jesus would not enter the marriage relation.","r":["120:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purposes of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"One goal of the bestowal was, as the Son of Man, to formally terminate the Lucifer rebellion in Satania and be recognized as the Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["120:2.2","120:2.3"]},{"x":"His life was intended less as an example for the people of Urantia than as an inspiration for all generations in all of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]},{"x":"He revealed the Father to the creatures of flesh and at the same time showed God a new revelation of man.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"He was charged to pour out the Spirit of Truth at the end of his bestowal, so that all normal mortals would have immediate access to the ministry of the Adjusters.","r":["120:2.6"]},{"q":"Ne perdez jamais de vue le fait que le but spirituel suprême de l’effusion de Micaël était de rehausser la révélation de Dieu.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"His life of self-forgetful service forever silenced those who had charged the Creators with selfishly holding on to power.","r":["120:4.1"]}]},{"h":"God and Man","items":[{"q":"He was not God in association with man but, rather, God incarnate in man.","r":"120:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus did not gradually become God, nor did he become man at some moment; he was always God and man, and what grew was his awareness of that fact.","r":["120:4.2","120:4.3"]},{"x":"A bestowal in which a Paradise Son appears in the world by natural processes is the most fascinating of miracles even to local universe citizens.","r":["120:4.5","120:4.6"]}]},{"h":"A Full Human Life","items":[{"x":"Jesus passed through every stage of human life from infancy to death and personally experienced a wide range of emotions, from joy to deep sorrow.","r":["129:4.4","129:4.5"]},{"x":"He did not set a detailed example for all to copy but lived a truly human life so that each person could live his own life in his own time.","r":["129:4.7"]},{"x":"His life fully revealed God to man and offered God a perfected human personality, and it was wholly accepted by the Father.","r":["129:4.6"]},{"q":"He came on earth the fullness of God to be manifest to man; he had now become well-nigh the perfection of man awaiting the occasion to become manifest to God.","r":"129:4.8"},{"x":"At his baptism in the Jordan he was a perfected mortal at the height of mind mastery, and his Adjuster stood by him as a Personalized Adjuster instead of fusing.","r":["136:2.2","136:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Completion of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Having completed the Urantia bestowal, Michael was recognized by the Ancients of Days and the Universal Father as the settled ruler of Nebadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where the Creator Son completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"En Jésus, l’univers a produit un homme mortel en qui l’esprit d’amour a vaincu les handicaps matériels du temps et triomphé du fait de son origine physique.","r":"195:10.2"}]}],"see":["Fils Créateur Micaël","Caractère de Jésus","Enseignements de Jésus","Mort sur la croix","Résurrection de Jésus","Rébellion de Lucifer"]},{"n":17,"t":"Énergie et matière","en":"Energy and Matter","sum":"L’énergie est la base de toute existence, une réalité éternelle mais non infinie qui sort du Paradis et retourne au Paradis. De la puissance d’espace, en passant par la force primordiale et l’énergie émergente, jusqu’au pouvoir d’univers et à la matière, elle est transmuée par les organisateurs de force et les directeurs de pouvoir, et la lumière, la chaleur, l’électricité et la matière ne font qu’un quant à l’origine et à la destinée. Pourtant, l’univers n’est pas mécanique ; il s’inscrit dans un ordre où le mental domine la matière et où l’esprit gouverne le mental.","sections":[{"h":"L’énergie issue du Paradis","items":[{"x":"L’énergie est la base de toute existence, et l’énergie pure est contrôlée par le Père Universel ; le flux d’énergie qui sort du Paradis n’a jamais cessé.","r":["42:0.1"]},{"q":"Le fondement de l’univers est matériel, mais l’essence de la vie est esprit.","r":"42:1.1"},{"x":"Considéré sous l’angle des phénomènes non spirituels, Dieu est énergie, et toute énergie physique procède de lui.","r":["3:2.3"]},{"x":"La création de l’énergie et le don de la vie sont des prérogatives du Père et de ses personnalités créatrices ; si avancé qu’il soit, un savant ne pourra jamais créer un atome ni ajouter la vie à la matière.","r":["42:1.4","42:1.5"]},{"q":"Energy is eternal but not infinite","r":"42:1.8"},{"x":"La force-énergie est impérissable et indestructible ; elle peut être transmuée sans fin, mais jamais anéantie.","r":["42:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Les stades de la transmutation","items":[{"x":"La puissance d’espace (absoluta) est la libre présence spatiale de l’Absolu Non Qualifié, qui ne réagit qu’à l’emprise personnelle du Père Universel.","r":["42:2.3","42:2.5"]},{"x":"Les organisateurs de force du Paradis transforment la puissance d’espace en force primordiale (segregata) et la transmuent ensuite en énergie puissante et en énergie gravitationnelle (ultimata).","r":["42:2.7","42:2.10","42:2.13"]},{"x":"Lorsque l’énergie atteint le stade où elle réagit à la gravité du Paradis, les directeurs de pouvoir prennent le relai et manient le pouvoir d’univers (gravita).","r":["42:2.12","42:2.14"]},{"x":"L’énergie de Havona n’est pas double, mais trine (triata), et l’énergie du Paradis, la monota, ne se distingue de l’esprit du Paradis que par le nom.","r":["42:2.16","42:2.19","42:2.20"]},{"x":"La force cosmique, l’énergie émergente et le pouvoir d’univers se distinguent par leur manière de réagir à la gravité du Paradis et à la gravité linéaire.","r":["0:6.5","0:6.6","0:6.7"]}]},{"h":"La structure de la matière","items":[{"q":"La lumière, la chaleur, l’électricité, le magnétisme, la chimie, l’énergie et la matière sont — quant à leur origine, leur nature et leur destinée — une seule et même chose au même titre que d’autres réalités matérielles non encore découvertes sur Urantia.","r":"42:4.1"},{"x":"L’unité primaire de l’existence matérielle est l’ultimaton, et exactement cent ultimatons constituent un électron.","r":["42:3.3","42:6.5"]},{"x":"L’univers local a une structure décimale, de sorte que les atomes n’existent que sous cent formes, ayant d’un à cent électrons orbitaux.","r":["42:7.4"]},{"x":"Le noyau atomique est maintenu par le mésotron, cent-quatre-vingts fois plus lourd que l’électron, qui fait la navette avec les charges entre protons et neutrons.","r":["42:8.3","42:8.4"]},{"x":"L’espace n’est pas vide ; même l’espace le plus vide connu dans Nébadon contient environ cent ultimatons par pouce cube.","r":["42:4.6"]},{"x":"La récurrence des propriétés des éléments de sept en sept est une marque de naissance de leur origine spirituelle septuple, laissée sur le monde matériel.","r":["42:9.2","42:9.3"]}]},{"h":"Le circuit et l’équilibre de l’énergie","items":[{"x":"Bien qu’elle subisse les transmutations du temps, la matière oscille toujours dans le circuit de l’éternité, toujours sensible à la source d’où elle est sortie.","r":["42:4.2"]},{"x":"Les soleils flamboyants transforment la matière en énergie, tandis que l’espace froid et les mondes obscurs ralentissent l’énergie jusqu’à la reconvertir en matière.","r":["42:4.9"]},{"x":"L’intégrité de la matière est assurée par le fait que l’énergie n’est absorbée ou émise que par unités quantiques.","r":["42:4.13"]},{"x":"Il n’y a pas d’éther ; la lumière et l’énergie sont des flux de particules qui se déplacent en ligne droite et ne paraissent ondulatoires qu’en raison de la résistance de l’espace.","r":["42:5.14","42:5.16"]},{"q":"L’énergie physique est l’unique réalité qui soit fidèle et constante dans sa soumission à la loi universelle.","r":"12:8.3"},{"x":"Les directeurs de pouvoir et les organisateurs de force, qui sont vivants, dirigent intelligemment les métamorphoses sans fin de la formation, de la désagrégation et de la reformation des univers.","r":["15:8.10"]}]},{"h":"Le mental et le mécanisme de l’univers","items":[{"x":"L’univers n’est ni mécanique ni magique ; il est une création du mental et un mécanisme de la loi.","r":["42:11.1"]},{"x":"L’univers des univers est planifié, fabriqué et dirigé par le mental, mais son mécanisme est si parfait que les méthodes de la science ne peuvent discerner la trace du mental infini.","r":["42:11.2"]},{"x":"Les énergies non spirituelles sont réunies à nouveau dans des systèmes vivants de mental, tels que le mental d’esprit pré-adjuvat, le mental d’esprit adjuvat, le mental morontiel et le mental cosmique.","r":["42:10.2","42:10.6"]},{"q":"Le mental est toujours créateur.","r":"42:12.9"},{"q":"L’esprit est l’architecte, le mental est le constructeur, le corps est le bâtiment matériel.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"Le mental domine la matière et répond au supercontrôle de l’esprit, et seul le mental qui suit librement la conduite de l’esprit peut survivre au-delà de l’existence mortelle.","r":["42:12.15"]},{"x":"Au Paradis, les énergies physiques, mentales et spirituelles sont coordonnées entre elles ; dans Havona, elles sont coordonnées ; et sur les niveaux absolus, l’esprit est nettement dominant.","r":["42:12.13"]}]}],"see":["Gravité","Paradis","Mental cosmique","Les trois Absolus","Temps et espace","Réalité"]},{"n":86,"t":"Enseignements de Jésus","en":"Teachings of Jesus","sum":"The teachings of Jesus are rooted in the simple gospel that God is the Father of all men and that men, recognizing by faith that they are his sons, become brothers to one another. The kingdom of heaven is not a political realm but a spiritual experience that begins within each person, and faith opens its door. Jesus gave the new commandment to love not merely as one loves oneself but as he loved, and he called people out of the religion of tradition and authority into the religion of the spirit that knows God directly.","sections":[{"h":"The Heart of the Gospel","items":[{"q":"God is your Father, and religion—my gospel—is nothing more nor less than the believing recognition of the truth that you are his son.","r":"141:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught a new concept of God, not as a judge keeping a ledger of sins but as a Father who loves each person.","r":["141:4.1"]},{"x":"The kingdom of heaven is built on the truths of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, and this teaching frees man from age-old animal fears.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel if it were presented in terms of family relationships rather than of a kingdom.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"His gospel delivered man from the superstition that he is a child of the devil and lifted him to the dignity of a faith son of God.","r":["194:2.1"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"Jesus said the kingdom of heaven had nothing to do with earthly kingdoms or temporal governments, but the idea of a temporal king rooted deep in the Jewish mind was not easily removed.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"q":"Ses derniers mots, au sujet du royaume, étaient toujours : « Le royaume est en vous. »","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom; once inside, one must grow through the steps of righteousness.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in the measure that a person forgives his fellows.","r":["170:3.3","170:3.4"]},{"x":"The kingdom is an evolutionary experience that begins on earth and advances through successive stages of life to Paradise.","r":["142:7.3"]}]},{"h":"Love and the New Commandment","items":[{"x":"Brotherly love is loving one's neighbor as oneself, but fatherly love is loving people as Jesus loved them.","r":["140:5.1"]},{"x":"Disciples should strive to see people as God sees them and so begin to show fatherly affection.","r":["140:5.3"]},{"q":"Aimez-vous les uns les autres comme je vous ai aimés.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but meant to bring the new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"x":"\"Resist not evil\" did not mean condoning sin but forgiving rather than retaliating against personal insults.","r":["141:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Jesus said not to patch new teaching onto the old but to be born again like little children and make a fresh start.","r":["140:6.2"]},{"x":"The righteousness he required is not buying favor through alms, prayer, and fasting, but the desire to do the Father's will in love, mercy, and truth.","r":["140:6.3"]},{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God within and to make that a fact of personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"q":"The religion of the mind ties you hopelessly to the past; the religion of the spirit consists in progressive revelation","r":"155:6.4"},{"x":"Jesus did not teach that all should think alike; believers are united in their diversity by the motive and goal of doing the Father's will.","r":["141:5.1","141:5.3"]},{"q":"Je suis venu dans le monde pour proclamer la liberté spirituelle afin que les mortels aient le pouvoir de vivre des vies individuelles originales et libres devant Dieu.","r":"141:5.1"}]},{"h":"Ways of Spreading the Teaching","items":[{"x":"Always respect human personality, and never sweep people into the kingdom by overpowering them with logic, eloquence, fear, or sentiment.","r":["159:3.2"]},{"x":"The gospel restores self-respect to those who have lost it and restrains those who have too much.","r":["159:3.3"]},{"x":"The teaching to trust God is not passive fatalism; what Jesus opposed was not forethought but worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.2","140:8.3"]},{"x":"His teaching was not the talk of a meek mystic but dynamic; he not only meant well but actually did good.","r":["141:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of Jesus","items":[{"q":"On peut prêcher une religion à propos de Jésus, mais obligatoirement, on doit vivre la religion de Jésus.","r":"196:2.1"},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom rests on Jesus' own religious experience, while Christianity rests mainly on Paul's.","r":["196:2.1"]},{"x":"As the Messiah of the kingdom became the Redeemer of the church, Jesus' teachings were transplanted from Jewish to gentile soil.","r":["170:5.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth restates Jesus' message anew for each generation, helping it remember and understand his teachings.","r":["194:2.1","194:2.5"]}]}],"see":["Royaume des cieux","Filiation avec Dieu","Fraternité des hommes","Paraboles","Caractère de Jésus","Foi"]},{"n":39,"t":"Esprit de Vérité","en":"Spirit of Truth","sum":"The Spirit of Truth is the Creator Son's own spirit, the Comforter, which he pours out upon all flesh after completing his bestowal career. On Urantia it was poured out at Pentecost as the spirit of Michael, preparing every normal mind to receive an Adjuster. This spirit teaches truth not as law or creed but as living conviction; it creates consciousness not of itself but of Michael, and it shows forth anew the life of Jesus in the lives of believers.","sections":[{"h":"The Bestowal Spirit of the Creator Son","items":[{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the first is the bestowal spirit of the Creator Son, the Spirit of Truth, the Comforter.","r":["34:4.2","15:9.12"]},{"q":"Ce Consolateur effusé est la force spirituelle qui attire toujours tous les chercheurs de vérité vers Celui qui personnifie la vérité dans l’univers local.","r":"34:4.5"},{"x":"This spirit proceeds from the personality of the Son but is functionally focalized in the Divine Minister, so it works without hindrance wherever the Son may be.","r":["34:4.6","34:4.7"]},{"x":"In a sense the Spirit of Truth is the spirit of both the Universal Father and the Creator Son, and it is commonly regarded as the spirit of the Universe Son.","r":["194:2.3","194:2.16"]},{"x":"On Avonal bestowal worlds it comes as the joint spirit of the bestowal Avonal and the Creator Son, but after Michael's final bestowal it becomes more literally the spirit of Michael.","r":["52:5.6","20:6.8","20:6.9"]}]},{"h":"The Promise and Pentecost","items":[{"x":"Before departing, Jesus promised that, if the Father permitted, he would pour out the Spirit of Truth upon all flesh and send it as another teacher.","r":["180:4.1","180:4.2"]},{"q":"Je vous enverrai très prochainement mon esprit, qui est exactement semblable à moi, à l’exception de ce corps matériel.","r":"180:4.5"},{"x":"Not only the one hundred and twenty in the upper chamber but every honest person in the world received this teacher according to his love of truth and his capacity for spiritual understanding.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the spirit was independent of forms, ceremonies, and sacred places; prayer did not bring the spirit, but it determined the capacity of the vessel that received it.","r":["194:3.10","194:3.20"]},{"x":"At that time the \"baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception and recognition of the gift of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"q":"since Pentecost, man is still searching for God, but there shines out over the world the spectacle of God also seeking for man and sending his spirit to dwell within him when he has found him.","r":"194:3.13"}]},{"h":"The Work of the Spirit of Truth","items":[{"q":"Bien entendu, la première mission de cet esprit consiste à entretenir et à personnaliser la vérité, car c’est la compréhension de la vérité qui constitue la forme la plus élevée de la liberté humaine.","r":"194:2.2"},{"x":"It also destroys the believer's feeling of orphanhood and helps him remember and understand the Master's words and reinterpret his life on earth.","r":["194:2.2","194:2.5"]},{"x":"Living within men, the Spirit of Truth restates the message of Jesus for each new generation in terms suited to its time.","r":["194:2.1"]},{"x":"This spirit teaches the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy, revealing the Father's spirit nature and the Son's moral character.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"Le Fils Créateur, dans la chair, a révélé Dieu aux hommes ; l’Esprit de Vérité, dans le cœur, révèle le Fils Créateur aux hommes.","r":"194:3.1"},{"x":"This spirit creates no consciousness of itself, only consciousness of Michael, so its evidence is found in deepening communion with Michael.","r":["194:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or the law of truth but the conviction of its true meaning on spirit levels, a spirit that grows and unfolds of itself.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"q":"La vérité statique est une vérité morte, et seule la vérité morte peut être considérée comme une théorie.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Without the insight of the Spirit of Truth the golden rule is only a rule of ethics; its true meaning appears when the spirit of the Son interprets the law of conduct to the spirit of the Father.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.8"]},{"x":"Love must pass through ever-new interpretations, readjusting itself under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth toward the highest good of the one loved.","r":["180:5.10"]},{"x":"The bestowed Spirit of Truth responds unerringly to truth, the living relationship in which all beings are attuned toward God.","r":["56:10.13","2:7.6"]}]},{"h":"Preparation and Guidance for the Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Until a bestowal Son releases the Spirit of Truth, not every normal mind is automatically prepared to receive an Adjuster.","r":["34:5.4","20:5.3","194:2.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is poured out upon all flesh, but its function and power depend almost entirely on the degree to which a person personally receives it.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"x":"Spiritual philosophy, the wisdom of spirit realities, is the endowment of the Spirit of Truth given by the bestowal Sons.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"Even when the ascender leaves his local universe, he is not wholly beyond the ministry of the Spirit of Truth, which points the way in every crisis of the ascent.","r":["117:5.9"]},{"q":"for in every dark hour, at every crossroad in the forward struggle, the Spirit of Truth will always speak, saying, \"This is the way.\"","r":"34:7.8"}]}],"see":["Fils Créateur Micaël","Pentecôte","Saint-Esprit","Vérité","Effusion de Jésus","Ajusteur de Pensée"]},{"n":5,"t":"Esprit Infini","en":"Infinite Spirit","sum":"L’Esprit Infini est la troisième personne de la Déité, l’Acteur Conjoint et le Créateur Conjoint, venu à l’existence au moment où le Père et le Fils ont conçu une action commune. En tant qu’exécutif de l’association du Père et du Fils, il est la source du mental, le manipulateur de l’énergie et l’esprit omniprésent qui dispense à toutes les créatures l’amour du Père et la miséricorde du Fils. Ses nombreux enfants spirituels forment l’échelle vivante par laquelle les mortels montent au Paradis.","sections":[{"h":"Le Dieu d’Action","items":[{"x":"Au moment même où le Père et le Fils ont conçu ensemble une action infinie, l’exécution d’un plan-pensée absolu, l’Esprit Infini est apparu dans une existence complète.","r":["8:0.3"]},{"x":"Cet ordre d’origine n’est qu’une explication destinée à aider la compréhension humaine ; tous trois existent depuis l’éternité, sans commencement ni fin.","r":["8:0.4"]},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini a promis une allégeance éternelle au Père et reconnu sa dépendance éternelle envers le Fils, et c’est ainsi que la Trinité du Paradis est venue à l’existence.","r":["8:1.2","8:1.3"]},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini a été éternisé avec la naissance de l’univers central de Havona, et par cet acte créateur conjoint il est devenu l’éternel Créateur Conjoint.","r":["8:1.7"]},{"q":"En bref, l’Esprit Infini témoigne que, puisqu’il est éternel, l’univers central l’est aussi.","r":"8:1.9"}]},{"h":"Nature et position","items":[{"x":"Il est connu sous de nombreux noms, entre autres l’Esprit Universel, le Créateur Conjoint, le Mental Infini, l’Esprit des Esprits et l’Acteur Conjoint, et sur Urantia on le confond parfois avec le mental cosmique.","r":["8:2.2"]},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini partage la perfection, la droiture et l’amour du Père, mais il penche vers la miséricorde du Fils Éternel et devient le ministre de miséricorde des Déités du Paradis.","r":["8:2.6"]},{"x":"Après la personnalisation de la Source Troisième, le Père ne participe plus personnellement à la création de l’univers ; il confie au Fils tout ce qu’il peut, et le Fils, à son tour, au Créateur Conjoint.","r":["8:3.2"]},{"q":"Le Fils Éternel est l’unique voie d’approche vers le Père Universel, et l’Esprit Infini est le seul moyen d’atteindre le Fils Éternel.","r":"8:3.7"},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini est la première Déité du Paradis qu’atteignent les pèlerins ascendants au centre de toutes choses.","r":["8:3.8"]}]},{"h":"L’Esprit tutélaire","items":[{"q":"God is love, the Son is mercy, the Spirit is ministry","r":"8:4.2"},{"x":"Dans l’univers local, par l’intermédiaire de l’Esprit-Mère, sa Fille Créative, il s’unit au Fils Créateur pour favoriser l’ascension spirituelle des créatures matérielles.","r":["8:4.4"]},{"x":"L’Esprit ne descend pas dans la chair, mais il se soumet volontiers à une série d’atténuations de la divinité jusqu’à se tenir enfin à nos côtés, sous la forme des anges, pour nous guider sur notre chemin terrestre.","r":["8:4.5"]},{"x":"Notre univers est façonné entre l’enclume de la justice et le marteau de la souffrance, mais ceux qui manient le marteau sont les êtres de miséricorde, les enfants de l’Esprit Infini.","r":["9:1.8"]},{"x":"Les personnalités spirituelles de l’Esprit Infini forment l’échelle vivante par laquelle l’homme mortel monte du chaos à la gloire.","r":["9:8.25"]}]},{"h":"L’Esprit omniprésent de Dieu","items":[{"x":"L’attribut le plus remarquable de l’Esprit Infini est l’omniprésence ; il partage l’omniscience du Père, mais n’est omnipotent que dans le domaine du mental.","r":["8:5.1","9:1.5"]},{"x":"Le Saint-Esprit est le circuit spirituel distinctif que la Fille Créative de l’Esprit Infini étend sur chaque univers local, tandis que l’Esprit Infini lui-même est présent partout.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"q":"Il y a de nombreuses influences spirituelles, mais elles ne font qu’un.","r":"8:5.4"},{"x":"Bien que d’origines différentes, l’Ajusteur, l’esprit du Fils Éternel et la présence de l’Esprit Infini coopèrent parfaitement dans le mental et l’âme de l’homme, et œuvrent comme un seul esprit.","r":["8:5.4","9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Manipulateur de l’énergie et mental absolu","items":[{"x":"Le Créateur Conjoint n’est pas l’énergie elle-même, mais le manipulateur de l’énergie ; il possède le pouvoir d’antigravité, que l’on n’observe ni chez le Père ni chez le Fils.","r":["9:3.2","9:3.5"]},{"q":"Le Paradis est l’archétype de l’infinité ; le Dieu d’Action est l’animateur de cet archétype.","r":"9:3.8"},{"x":"Le mental des créatures a sa seule origine dans la Source Troisième, et pas même un fragment du Père ne peut habiter l’homme avant que l’Esprit Infini n’ait préparé la voie du mental.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"Le fait que la source du mental soit divine ne rend pas divin tout phénomène mental ; l’intellect humain s’enracine dans des origines animales.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"x":"De même que le Père attire toute personnalité et le Fils tout esprit, l’Acteur Conjoint attire tout mental par le circuit de gravité mentale.","r":["9:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Une vraie personnalité","items":[{"x":"L’Esprit Infini est une présence universelle, un pouvoir et le mental universel, et davantage encore ; mais il est en même temps une personnalité vraie et divine.","r":["8:6.1"]},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini possède une volonté aussi bien qu’un mental ; son amour et ses chagrins sont réels, et il réagit à l’univers en tant que personne.","r":["8:6.3","8:6.4"]},{"q":"therefore \"Grieve not the Spirit of God.\"","r":"8:6.4"},{"x":"Dans l’Esprit Infini, le Père et le Fils sont mutuellement présents, toujours dans une perfection non qualifiée.","r":["8:6.7"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Fils Éternel","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Mental cosmique","Sept Maitres Esprits","Saint-Esprit"]},{"n":23,"t":"Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","en":"Local Universe Mother Spirit","sum":"L’Esprit-Mère de l’univers local est la Fille Créative individualisée par l’Esprit Infini pour chaque univers local, la compagne coordonnée qui construit l’univers, fait naitre la vie et gouverne avec le Fils Créateur. Dans Nébadon, on l’appelle la Divine Ministre, et, par le souffle de vie, les sept esprits-mentaux adjuvats et le Saint-Esprit, elle dispense le mental et l’esprit à toutes les créatures. De même que Micaël agit en père, elle remplit le rôle d’une mère, ne contraignant jamais, mais conduisant doucement les hommes sur le chemin de la filiation.","sections":[{"h":"La Fille de l’Esprit Infini dans l’univers local","items":[{"x":"Lorsqu’un Fils Créateur est personnalisé, l’Esprit Infini individualise une représentation nouvelle et unique de lui-même pour l’accompagner dans l’espace en tant que compagne.","r":["34:0.1","17:6.3"]},{"x":"Les Esprits-Mères d’Univers reçoivent une formation prépersonnelle sur les mondes de Havona, où elles apprennent à coopérer avec les Fils du Paradis sous la volonté du Père.","r":["14:6.32"]},{"q":"She volunteered to accompany Michael on the occasion of his liberation from Paradise obligations","r":"33:3.2"},{"x":"L’Esprit-Mère de Nébadon est la 611 121e du sixième groupe des Esprits Suprêmes, et elle a créé et gouverné cet univers avec Micaël.","r":["33:3.2"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’un Fils Créateur part pour l’espace, la proclamation par le Père Universel de l’union éternelle des deux est l’un des évènements les plus émouvants du Paradis.","r":["17:6.5"]}]},{"h":"La personnalisation et les stades de sa carrière","items":[{"x":"Lorsque Micaël proclame la création de la vie, une « éruption primaire » se produit au Paradis, et à cet instant l’Esprit Créatif devient un être personnel, la Divine Ministre.","r":["34:1.1","17:6.7"]},{"x":"L’Esprit-Mère personnalisée acquiert une nature personnelle teintée de la nature du Maitre Esprit qui préside ce superunivers.","r":["34:1.3"]},{"x":"Au stade de la création physique, le Fils de l’Univers fournit le modèle, et l’Esprit de l’Univers matérialise ces créations d’énergie en substance physique.","r":["34:0.3"]},{"x":"Lorsque Micaël revint de sa septième effusion, l’Esprit-Mère lui promit sa subordination, et Micaël l’établit comme cogouvernante.","r":["33:3.5","33:3.6","17:6.8"]},{"q":"the Son published to the worlds the fact of the Spirit's equality with him in all endowments of personality and attributes of divine character.","r":"33:3.6"},{"x":"Cette « Proclamation d’Égalité » est le modèle transcendant pour l’organisation de la famille et du gouvernement, et le haut idéal du foyer humain et du mariage librement consenti.","r":["33:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Mère de la vie et des personnalités spirituelles","items":[{"x":"Lorsque les Porteurs de Vie ont préparé les corps physiques, l’Esprit de l’Univers apporte « le souffle de vie », qui active les modèles sans vie et leur confère le pouvoir de se reproduire.","r":["34:2.5","36:6.3"]},{"x":"Micaël et l’Esprit-Mère sont littéralement le père-fils et la mère-esprit de toutes les créatures natives de Nébadon.","r":["37:0.1"]},{"q":"Such a Divine Minister is in reality the mother of spirits and spirit personalities, the ever-present and all-wise adviser of the Creator Son","r":"33:3.3"},{"x":"Les séraphins furent créés comme la première reproduction spirituelle solitaire de l’Esprit-Mère, et son activité créatrice ne cesse jamais à mesure que Nébadon grandit.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’une rébellion survient, seul le Fils peut agir en sauveur, mais l’Esprit le soutient toujours en tout ce qu’il endure.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Le ministère du mental et de l’esprit","items":[{"q":"Elle est partout présente d’une manière égale et diffuse dans tout son univers. Elle est donc tout aussi littéralement et personnellement présente sur un monde que sur tous les autres.","r":"34:3.3"},{"x":"Les sept esprits-mentaux adjuvats sont créés par la Divine Ministre et s’appellent les esprits de sagesse, d’adoration, de conseil, de connaissance, de courage, d’entendement et d’intuition.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"Dès qu’un mental atteint le niveau où il reçoit les adjuvats d’adoration et de sagesse, il est inclus dans le circuit spirituel de la Divine Ministre, le ministère du Saint-Esprit.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"L’Esprit-Mère ne quitte jamais Salvington, et, comme elle y est fixée, l’Esprit de Vérité fonctionne indépendamment du lieu où se trouve Micaël.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"q":"L’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers agit comme centre et foyer universels de l’Esprit de Vérité aussi bien que de sa propre influence personnelle, le Saint-Esprit.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"La présence conjointe du Saint-Esprit, de l’Esprit de Vérité et de l’Ajusteur dans un même mortel est une symétrie de dotation spirituelle qui apporte la conscience de la filiation avec Dieu.","r":["34:5.7"]}]},{"h":"L’Esprit à l’œuvre dans l’homme","items":[{"q":"From the heights of eternal glory the divine Spirit descends, by a long series of steps, to meet you as you are and where you are","r":"34:6.3"},{"x":"Le ministère du Saint-Esprit est en partie indépendant de l’attitude de l’homme, mais plus l’homme suit pleinement la conduite divine, plus ce ministère devient efficace pour sanctifier la vie intérieure.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"L’Esprit ne contraint jamais, il ne fait que guider.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"Entre la nature animale et les élans spirituels, les esprits conjugués aident l’homme, tout au long de sa vie, à soumettre de plus en plus la chair à la conduite de l’esprit.","r":["34:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Fils Créateur Micaël","Esprit Infini","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Saint-Esprit","Esprit de Vérité","Séraphins"]},{"n":38,"t":"Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","en":"Adjutant Mind-Spirits","sum":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits are circuits of mind ministry created by the local universe Mother Spirit and named the spirits of intuition, understanding, courage, knowledge, counsel, worship, and wisdom. More like circuits than independent personalities, they act on animal and human minds that can learn by experience, conditioning evolution so that it proceeds purposefully rather than by accident. When the adjutants of worship and wisdom begin to function, mind crosses the threshold of spiritual ministry and is prepared to receive the circuit of the Holy Spirit and the Thought Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Mind Circuits of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"x":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits were created by the Divine Minister of the local universe; alike in character but diverse in power, they can hardly be regarded as personalities apart from their mother.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the third is the intelligence-ministry circuit of the seven adjutant mind-spirits.","r":["34:4.4"]},{"q":"Les sept esprits-mentaux adjuvats accompagnent toujours les Porteurs de Vie sur une nouvelle planète, mais il ne faudrait pas les considérer comme des entités.","r":"36:5.4"},{"x":"They are in fact a level of consciousness of the Divine Minister and are always subordinate to the action and presence of their creative mother.","r":["36:5.4"]},{"x":"The adjutants grow in function through experience, yet they never become personal beings.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"This ministry emanates from the local universe headquarters, but the actual direction of the lower levels of mind function is centered at the system capitals.","r":["65:7.1"]},{"x":"In the early stages of evolution the mortal races climb the grades of intelligence as they progressively make contact with the seven adjutant mind-spirits of the Mother Spirit.","r":["194:2.12","194:2.18"]}]},{"h":"The Names and Functions of the Seven Adjutants","items":[{"x":"The spirit of intuition gives quick perception, reflex instincts, and the sense of direction, and it is the only adjutant that makes extensive contact with the mechanical levels of mind.","r":["36:5.6","34:4.12"]},{"x":"The spirit of understanding is the gift of spontaneously associating and co-ordinating ideas, shown in quick reasoning and prompt decision.","r":["36:5.7"]},{"q":"L’esprit de courage — le don de fidélité. Chez les êtres personnels, il est la base de la formation du caractère, la racine intellectuelle de la vigueur morale et de la bravoure spirituelle.","r":"36:5.8"},{"x":"The spirit of knowledge is the mother of the curiosity that leads to adventure and discovery, and the spirit of counsel is the urge to social co-operation that brings harmony with one's fellows.","r":["36:5.9","36:5.10"]},{"q":"L’adoration est l’insigne de la candidature à l’ascension spirituelle.","r":"36:5.11"},{"q":"Cet adjuvat est le plus élevé des sept ; c’est l’esprit qui coordonne et articule le travail de tous les autres.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"When knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the presence of the adjutant of wisdom, it becomes wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]}]},{"h":"A Ministry That Guides Evolution","items":[{"x":"Because the presence of the adjutant mind-spirits conditions organic evolution, evolution is purposeful rather than accidental.","r":["36:5.1"]},{"x":"The adjutants do not contact purely mechanical responses; they begin to minister the moment the capacity to learn by experience appears.","r":["65:7.5","65:7.6"]},{"x":"They are not concerned with physical evolution, yet they mesh with it so perfectly that man sees in mind phenomena only the workings of nature.","r":["65:7.2"]},{"x":"Because of Urantia's unique life pattern, the lower adjutants had greater difficulty in making contact here than almost anywhere else in Nebadon.","r":["65:7.3","65:7.4"]},{"x":"Since the functioning of the first five adjutants in the animal stage is essential to human intellect, animals are indispensable to the intellectual evolution of man as well.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"The central focus at Life Carrier headquarters registers the function of the first five adjutants, but the quantitative activity of worship and wisdom is registered in the presence of the Mother Spirit on Salvington.","r":["36:5.3"]},{"x":"The work of the Mother Spirit is done chiefly through the seven adjutants, the spirits of promise, always leading mankind toward higher thoughts and ideals.","r":["34:5.2"]}]},{"h":"The Threshold of Spiritual Ministry","items":[{"q":"Les adjuvats opèrent exclusivement dans l’évolution du mental qui expérimente jusqu’au niveau de la sixième phase, l’esprit d’adoration.","r":"65:7.7"},{"x":"When mind becomes able to receive the adjutants of worship and wisdom, the mortal first experiences the ministry of spirit joined with mind.","r":["34:5.3"]},{"x":"Creature mind before it recognizes and worships divinity is the exclusive domain of the adjutants, but as soon as spiritual response appears, it becomes supermind.","r":["36:5.15"]},{"x":"The adjutants are not directly concerned with the highly spiritual functions of the Holy Spirit, but in evolutionary man they prepare the way ahead of the appearance of that spirit.","r":["36:5.16"]},{"q":"And it requires the co-ordinate function of all seven adjutants to thus qualify the human mind for the reception of an Adjuster.","r":"108:2.2"},{"x":"All genuinely religious reactions of man are sponsored by the adjutant of worship and censored by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Mental","Saint-Esprit","Porteurs de Vie","Évolution","Ajusteur de Pensée"]},{"n":8,"t":"Être Suprême","en":"Supreme Being","sum":"L’Être Suprême est la Déité expérientielle qui évolue dans le temps et l’espace. Il tient sa personnalité spirituelle de la Trinité du Paradis et son pouvoir tout-puissant des trois premiers niveaux de Dieu le Septuple, et ces deux aspects s’unifient dans le Mental Suprême. En tant que surâme du grand univers et somme de la réalité finie, il enregistre l’expérience de chaque créature et de chaque créateur, et il s’actualise d’un pas de plus chaque fois que l’homme fait la volonté de Dieu.","sections":[{"h":"Déité expérientielle en évolution","items":[{"x":"Le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit sont des Déités existentielles, tandis que Dieu le Suprême, Dieu l’Ultime et Dieu l’Absolu sont des Déités expérientielles qui s’actualisent dans l’évolution post-havonienne des univers.","r":["0:7.1","0:7.5"]},{"q":"WITH God the Father, sonship is the great relationship. With God the Supreme, achievement is the prerequisite to status","r":"115:0.1"},{"x":"Havona ne croit pas, il est simplement, tandis que la croissance est la marque du grand univers et le signe de la Déité expérientielle.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"L’Être Suprême fonctionne comme une personnalité spirituelle dans l’univers central et comme Dieu le Tout-Puissant, une personnalité de pouvoir, dans le grand univers.","r":["116:0.5"]},{"x":"La destinée du Suprême est la perfection, mais son expérience présente comporte des éléments de croissance et d’inachèvement.","r":["116:0.4"]}]},{"h":"Origines : la Trinité et Dieu le Septuple","items":[{"x":"La personnalité spirituelle du Suprême provient de la Trinité du Paradis, et sa croissance dérive des deux triunités d’actualité et de potentialité.","r":["115:4.2","115:4.7"]},{"x":"Le pouvoir du Tout-Puissant repose sur les succès de divinité de Dieu le Septuple, et l’Acteur Conjoint confère le mental de Suprématie, qui joint le pouvoir et la personnalité spirituelle.","r":["115:4.7"]},{"x":"L’Être Suprême dépend absolument de la Trinité du Paradis pour la réalité de sa nature personnelle et spirituelle.","r":["115:5.1"]},{"x":"Dieu le Suprême n’est pas seulement développé par les créateurs et dérivé de la Trinité ; il est aussi un être volitif qui participe lui-même à sa propre actualisation.","r":["117:3.7"]},{"q":"Ce que la Trinité est pour Dieu le Suprême, l’Ajusteur de Pensée l’est pour l’homme en évolution.","r":"117:3.10"}]},{"h":"Surâme du grand univers","items":[{"q":"Le Suprême est la beauté de l’harmonie physique, la vérité de la signification intellectuelle et la bonté de la valeur spirituelle.","r":"117:1.1"},{"x":"Dans l’Être Suprême, le Créateur et la créature sont unifiés en une seule Déité, dont la volonté est quelque chose de plus grand que la volonté du créateur ou celle de la créature.","r":["117:1.5"]},{"x":"Il est la synthèse finie de l’expérience des créateurs qui descendent pour révéler Dieu et des créatures qui montent à la recherche de Dieu.","r":["117:1.2"]},{"x":"La personnalité d’un non-survivant est absorbée dans la surâme de la création et retourne au Suprême comme une goutte d’eau retourne à la mer.","r":["117:4.2","117:4.4"]},{"x":"L’homme ne perd pas son identité personnelle dans l’unification avec le Suprême, et les échos de toutes ses expériences deviennent une partie de l’expérience du Suprême.","r":["117:5.5"]},{"x":"Le grand univers est un organisme vivant magnifiquement réactif, imprégné de circuits d’intelligence et de canaux d’énergie.","r":["116:7.1"]}]},{"h":"L’interdépendance de l’homme et du Suprême","items":[{"x":"Dans la mesure où nous faisons la volonté de Dieu, où que ce soit, le potentiel tout-puissant du Suprême devient d’un pas plus actuel.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"x":"La créature ne peut évoluer sans le Suprême, et l’évolution du Suprême ne peut s’achever sans la pleine évolution de toutes les créatures.","r":["117:4.9"]},{"x":"Cette relation de l’homme et du Suprême est le fondement de la moralité cosmique, qui reconnait une obligation expérientielle envers la Déité expérientielle.","r":["117:4.8"]},{"q":"Dieu est si confiant, si aimant, qu’il remet une fraction de sa divine nature aux mains des êtres humains eux-mêmes pour qu’ils la gardent en sureté et réalisent leur moi.","r":"117:4.3"},{"x":"Tandis que nous cherchons le Père, le Suprême cherche lui aussi, en nous et avec nous, le Créateur Paradisiaque de toutes choses.","r":["117:4.6"]}]},{"h":"Le chemin pour trouver le Suprême","items":[{"x":"De même que Dieu est le Père divin, le Suprême est la Mère divine, en qui nous sommes nourris tout au long de nos carrières dans l’univers.","r":["117:6.2"]},{"q":"Man can discover the Father in his heart, but he will have to search for the Supreme in the hearts of all other men","r":"117:6.23"},{"x":"Chaque individu peut trouver le Père, mais le Suprême ne sera pas trouvé individuellement avant un avenir lointain, lorsque toutes les créatures ensemble atteindront la maturité cosmique et le trouveront.","r":["117:6.16","117:6.21"]},{"x":"L’amour du Père ne devient réel que lorsqu’il est dispensé à nos semblables, et l’affection fraternelle qui s’écoule ainsi est l’essence de l’amour du Suprême.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"L’homme ne découvre pas le Suprême soudainement, comme frappe un tremblement de terre, mais lentement et patiemment, comme une rivière use le sol.","r":["117:6.25"]},{"q":"Comprendre plus que le Suprême, c’est être plus que fini !","r":"117:6.19"},{"x":"Le mortel qui connait Dieu n’est jamais seul ; le Père l’accompagne tout au long du chemin, et le sentier même qu’il parcourt est la présence du Suprême.","r":["117:6.27"]}]},{"h":"L’avenir du Suprême","items":[{"x":"Quand le grand univers sera ancré dans la lumière et la vie, la personnalité spirituelle et le pouvoir tout-puissant seront unifiés dans le Mental Suprême, et l’Être Suprême sera factualisé en tant qu’actualité achevée.","r":["117:0.2","117:7.14"]},{"x":"On croit que le Suprême deviendra alors le souverain effectif du grand univers et que les distinctions entre les sept superunivers disparaitront graduellement.","r":["117:7.15"]},{"x":"Les citoyens de l’univers parachevé affronteront alors un nouveau défi : la quête de Dieu l’Ultime.","r":["117:7.17"]}]}],"see":["Dieu le Septuple","Trinité du Paradis","Dieu l’Ultime","Volonté de Dieu","Lumière et vie","Évolution"]},{"n":94,"t":"Évolution","en":"Evolution","sum":"In The Urantia Book evolution is not a chance process but the divine technique by which the universes of time and space progressively grow. Life implanted by the Life Carriers advanced, under the ministry of the physical controllers and the adjutant mind-spirits, from the protoplasm of the seas to human beings with will, and society, religion, and government have followed the same evolutionary path. All this growth is bound up with the evolution of the Supreme Being and moves at last toward the age of light and life.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolving Universe","items":[{"q":"Ces univers du temps et de l’espace sont tous évolutionnaires.","r":"32:0.2"},{"x":"Unlike Havona, which was created perfect, growth is the characteristic of the grand universe and the mark of experiential Deity.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The confusion and inequality of Urantia show that this world is the work of subabsolute Creators who are not yet perfect.","r":["116:0.2"]},{"x":"Continuing evolution corrects nature, increasing the share of Paradise perfection and decreasing that of evil, error, and disharmony.","r":["4:2.4"]},{"x":"We evolve in God the Supreme, and he also evolves in us.","r":["31:10.12"]}]},{"h":"Plan, Not Chance","items":[{"q":"L’évolution cosmique n’est pas toujours compréhensible (prévisible), mais elle est strictement non accidentelle.","r":"49:1.1"},{"x":"Urantia was a life-experiment world, but the establishment of life was not an experiment in the sense of the haphazard or accidental.","r":["65:4.1","65:4.2"]},{"x":"Features of human existence such as cells that heal their own wounds show that life was intelligently planned.","r":["65:4.3"]},{"q":"La physique et la chimie, seules, ne peuvent expliquer comment l’être humain a évolué en partant du protoplasme primordial des mers primitives.","r":"65:6.8"},{"x":"In every living thing dwells an innate, unsatisfied longing for greater perfection.","r":["65:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Life","items":[{"x":"Material life arises from the cooperation of a threefold creativity: the physical controllers, the Seven Master Spirits, and the Life Carriers.","r":["65:0.1"]},{"x":"The development of life passes through three stages: physical energy, the mind ministry of the adjutant spirits, and spiritual endowment completed by the Adjuster bestowal.","r":["65:0.2","65:0.5"]},{"x":"The primitive ancestors of mankind were the mud of the warm bays and lagoons of ancient inland seas, and the transition from plant to animal occurred 450,000,000 years ago.","r":["65:2.1","58:6.1"]},{"x":"New species appear suddenly as fully developed new orders, not by the accumulation of small variations.","r":["58:6.3"]},{"x":"About a million years ago the immediate ancestors of mankind came from a lemur type of mammal through three successive sudden mutations.","r":["62:0.1"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers complete their work when beings with will appear, and thereafter they cannot interfere with will.","r":["36:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Mind and Spirit","items":[{"x":"As life rises higher, the adjutant mind-spirits act one by one, and mind becomes ever more coordinating, creative, and integrating.","r":["65:6.7","62:6.3"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution finally reached the dignity of human will, and Urantia was recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago.","r":["62:7.7"]},{"q":"Dans les laboratoires évolutionnaires cosmiques, le mental domine toujours la matière, et l’esprit est toujours en corrélation avec le mental.","r":"65:8.5"},{"x":"Spiritual progress depends on mental expansion and is slowed by intellectual retardation, yet the soul can evolve regardless of the cultural level of the mind.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Evolution seems long because creatures make their own lifespan the measure of time.","r":["65:8.2","65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Society and Religion","items":[{"x":"Like marriage, industry, and religion, civil government is a product of gradual evolution.","r":["70:5.1"]},{"x":"Early evolution is marked by the survival of the fittest, but later civilization advances better through intelligent cooperation and spiritual brotherhood.","r":["71:5.3"]},{"x":"Until the Planetary Prince arrives, religion is wholly an evolutionary process; thereafter evolution and revelation advance religion together.","r":["52:2.3"]},{"x":"Attempts to overturn the mores by revolution are fatal to civilization, for the mores are the thread of continuity that has held civilization together.","r":["68:4.6"]},{"q":"Il est possible de retarder l’évolution, mais non de l’arrêter.","r":"81:0.1"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of Evolution","items":[{"x":"The march of the universes has a great and glorious purpose, and none of the struggles of mortals is in vain.","r":["32:5.1"]},{"q":"Les évènements du temps et les luttes de l’existence matérielle ne sont que l’échafaudage provisoire qui assure la communication avec l’autre côté, avec la terre promise de la réalité spirituelle et de l’existence céleste.","r":"32:5.2"},{"x":"The final attainment of an evolutionary world is the age of light and life, and the achievements of settled worlds alone justify the creation of man.","r":["55:0.1","55:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Porteurs de Vie","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Être Suprême","Lumière et vie","Urantia","Civilisation"]},{"n":99,"t":"Expérience","en":"Experience","sum":"In The Urantia Book experience is the way the evolutionary universe lives and the source of its growth. Paradise and Havona are existentially perfect, but the creatures of time and space and the Supreme Being become perfect through experience. Even a Creator Son earned his sovereignty by experience, and the Adjuster too accumulates experience together with man. Above all, the personal religious experience of knowing God remains true and valid even when theology and philosophy waver, and it transforms people and leads them to service.","sections":[{"h":"What Is Experience?","items":[{"q":"C’est simplement l’effet réciproque entre un moi actif et interrogateur, et toute autre réalité active et extérieure.","r":"102:4.2"},{"x":"The mass of experience is determined by depth of concept and totality of recognition of external reality, and its fact is found in other things, minds, and spirits.","r":["102:4.2"]},{"x":"Man experiences matter in his mind and spiritual reality in his soul, but it is the mind that is conscious of this experience.","r":["103:6.6"]},{"q":"Without experience, no evolutionary creature could even exist","r":"106:9.2"}]},{"h":"Existential and Experiential Perfection","items":[{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The Father has achieved existential expression in the Son and the Spirit and is now achieving experiential expression as God the Supreme, Ultimate, and Absolute.","r":["0:7.6"]},{"x":"The perfection of the creatures of time, though mixed with grace, is a true personal possession gained through personal effort and actual living.","r":["32:3.9"]},{"x":"The experiential nature of evolutionary personalities is the natural complement of the ever-perfect nature of the Paradise-Havona creatures.","r":["32:3.12"]},{"x":"The experience of every evolving creature personality is a phase of the experience of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:1.1"]}]},{"h":"The Good Fortune of Starting at the Bottom","items":[{"x":"Animal evolutionary origin is no stigma on any personality; there is greater honor for those who have climbed the ladder of life from the very bottom.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"It would have been easy for the Father to make all mortals perfect from the start, but that would deprive them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"q":"an experience to be had only by those who are so fortunate as to begin at the very bottom of living existence.","r":"32:3.11"},{"x":"The mortal career, the evolution of the soul, is not so much a probation as an education.","r":["111:3.5"]}]},{"h":"The Experience of Divine Beings","items":[{"x":"Michael was born a creator, yet his sovereignty had to be earned through the experience of seven bestowals.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"x":"All the human experiences Jesus passed through became the eternal possession of the Universe Sovereign, making him an experienced sovereign.","r":["127:6.13"]},{"x":"Virgin Adjusters too must gain experience while the mortal creature grows, rehearsing in advance the techniques of the next stage of life.","r":["109:0.1"]},{"x":"A Personalized Adjuster possesses as an eternal endowment all the experience gained while indwelling various mortal minds.","r":["109:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Religious Experience","items":[{"q":"L’expérience religieuse est la réalisation de la conscience d’avoir trouvé Dieu.","r":"102:3.4"},{"q":"Ce sont vos pensées, et non vos sentiments, qui vous conduisent vers Dieu.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion may be accompanied by feeling but is not itself the experience of feeling, and the conditions that induce mystic experience rather show its dangers.","r":["101:5.9","100:5.10"]},{"x":"Though theology and philosophy may be distorted, the spiritual experience of personal religion remains true and valid.","r":["103:9.1"]},{"x":"The experience of God-consciousness is the same in every generation, but philosophic concepts and theologic definitions of God must change with knowledge.","r":["5:5.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience results in a certain consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["101:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Experience","items":[{"q":"L’EXPÉRIENCE d’une vie religieuse dynamique transforme un individu médiocre en une personnalité douée d’un pouvoir idéaliste.","r":"100:0.1"},{"x":"One who has found God is impelled by overflowing goodness to serve his fellows; true religion leads to increased social service.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"x":"The senses reveal the existence of things and the mind their meaning, but spiritual experience reveals the true values of life.","r":["100:4.4"]},{"x":"Faith always triumphs over doubt, for experience is superior to theory, and spiritual reality to isolated facts.","r":["102:6.7"]},{"x":"The Adjuster restores only the memories and experiences needed for the universe career; many memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain.","r":["112:5.22"]}]}],"see":["Expérience religieuse","Être Suprême","Croissance","Réalité","Foi","Quête de la perfection"]},{"n":54,"t":"Expérience religieuse","en":"Religious Experience","sum":"Religious experience is the personal experience of living knowledge of God and supreme values under the guidance of the indwelling spirit. It is neither a reasoned system of belief nor a mystic ecstasy; it sprouts from moral consciousness and grows through faith and insight. However erroneous one's theology, the experience itself can be genuine, and its certainty cannot be refuted. Religious experience culminates in a certain consciousness of God and assurance of survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Religious Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is neither a philosophic system proved by reason nor a mystic ecstasy enjoyed by a favored few.","r":["101:1.1"]},{"q":"Ce sont vos pensées, et non vos sentiments, qui vous conduisent vers Dieu.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion is not the search for new facts but the discovery of new spiritual meanings in facts already known.","r":["101:1.4"]},{"x":"The religious tendency is innate and universal; it is fostered by the spirit of worship and censored by the spirit of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1","103:0.2"]},{"x":"The experience of realizing spiritual values is superideational and hard to express in human language; it is called God-consciousness.","r":["103:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Where Experience Begins","items":[{"x":"Every person early experiences conflict between selfish and altruistic urges, and in its resolution may first experience God-consciousness.","r":["103:2.4"]},{"x":"When a moral being makes an unselfish choice against the urge to be selfish, that is primitive religious experience.","r":["103:2.8"]},{"x":"It is right to identify altruistic desire with an influence outside oneself, with God, for it comes from the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["103:2.10"]},{"x":"Religious \"birth\" is usually gradual, though there is a day of spirit rebirth; those who grow without crisis and those who pass through crisis should not disparage one another.","r":["103:2.1","103:2.2"]},{"q":"Quand un être moral choisit d’être altruiste en face d’une incitation à l’égoïsme, il fait une expérience religieuse primitive.","r":"103:2.8"}]},{"h":"Conversion and Mysticism","items":[{"x":"Religious growth moves from stagnation to adjustment, from insecurity to faith, and from the bondage of fear to the liberty of sonship.","r":["100:5.2"]},{"x":"God-consciousness may grow gradually or arrive in a dramatic moment, as with Paul on the Damascus road.","r":["100:5.3"]},{"q":"Mais l’émotion seule est une fausse conversion ; il faut avoir la foi aussi bien que la sensation.","r":"100:5.5"},{"x":"Rather than seeking conversion, living faith, sincere worship, and unselfish prayer are a better way of approach to the Adjuster.","r":["100:5.7"]},{"x":"Trances and visions should not be sought as religious experience, and Jesus never resorted to such methods.","r":["100:5.8","100:5.11"]}]},{"h":"Experience and Theology","items":[{"x":"Religion begins with the quest for values, and systems of interpretive belief come later, so people agree more readily on values than on creeds.","r":["103:1.4"]},{"q":"Quelles que soient les illusions et les erreurs de votre théologie, votre religion peut être tout à fait authentique et éternellement vraie.","r":"103:9.2"},{"q":"Quand la théologie domine la religion, la religion meurt ; elle devient une doctrine au lieu d’être une vie.","r":"103:9.6"},{"x":"Knowing the varied religious experiences of others keeps one's own religion from becoming selfish and narrow.","r":["103:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Fruits and Certainty of Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is a living love and a life of service; it takes nothing away from a person and adds new meaning to all of life.","r":["100:6.5"]},{"x":"A remarkable trait of the religious life is a peace that passes all understanding, unshaken by any disappointment.","r":["100:6.6"]},{"x":"Religion rests on the Adjuster-derived postulate that God is knowable and attainable.","r":["103:9.8"]},{"x":"The reality of religious experience is proportional to its spiritual content; its certainties are unassailable and its devotion beyond question.","r":["103:9.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience culminates in a sure consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of the believer.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"q":"Mais la vraie religion est un amour vivant, une vie de service.","r":"100:6.5"}]}],"see":["Religion personnelle","Foi","Adoration","Ajusteur de Pensée","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Philosophie"]},{"n":47,"t":"Filiation avec Dieu","en":"Sonship with God","sum":"Sonship with God is the family relationship between the heavenly Father and the individual that becomes real when a person accepts God as Father by faith. At the center of the gospel of the kingdom that Jesus proclaimed stand the fatherhood of God and the sonship of man that follows from it. This sonship is not earned by deeds but received as a gift, and the indwelling Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit bear witness to this fact with the human spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Sonship Received by Faith","items":[{"x":"By accepting the status of sonship and believing in its reality, a person makes sonship with God an eternal reality.","r":["40:6.4"]},{"q":"En ayant foi dans la paternité de Dieu, vous pouvez entrer dans le royaume des cieux et devenir ainsi les fils de Dieu.","r":"142:1.3"},{"q":"Si vous recevez Dieu en tant que Père, alors, en vérité, vous êtes vraiment les fils de Dieu.","r":"142:5.2"},{"x":"Salvation is the gift of the Father, and those who receive it by faith partake of the divine nature and become sons or daughters of God.","r":["150:5.3"]},{"x":"The first condition for entering the kingdom is the faith and sincerity of coming as a little child and receiving the bestowal of sonship as a gift.","r":["170:2.21"]}]},{"h":"Why Mortals Are Sons","items":[{"x":"It is a solemn and sublime fact that lowly and material man is a faith child of the Most High.","r":["40:6.2"]},{"x":"Because the Creator Son became man and our elder brother, we who are his brothers are sons of the same Father.","r":["40:6.5"]},{"x":"We are sons because the spirit of the Son has been poured out upon all races, because we have received personality from the Father, and because a fragment of the Father indwells us.","r":["40:6.6","40:6.7","40:6.8"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster are present together, mortals are qualified for the conscious realization of sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"x":"The spirit bears witness not \"to\" our spirits but \"with\" our spirits that we are children of God.","r":["34:6.12"]},{"q":"he is your elder brother in fact","r":"40:6.5"}]},{"h":"From Servant to Free Son","items":[{"x":"The subjects of a kingdom hear the laws of a ruler, but one who discovers sonship by faith sees himself as the privileged son of a loving Father.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are a noble slave; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are a free child of God.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"As a good earthly father does not keep his children in anxiety, so the heavenly Father does not leave his faith children in doubt.","r":["142:5.2"]},{"q":"whosoever has been born of the spirit has in himself the power to overcome all doubt, and this is the victory that overcomes all uncertainty, even your faith.","r":"142:5.3"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Sonship","items":[{"x":"Righteousness is not the condition of salvation but the natural fruit of the spirit-born life of sonship.","r":["150:5.5"]},{"q":"La réalisation de la filiation est incompatible avec le désir de pécher.","r":"150:5.5"},{"x":"The evidence to the world of being born of the spirit is that believers sincerely love one another.","r":["142:5.4"]},{"x":"When we accept by living faith that our ideals come from a superhuman source, belief in sonship becomes effective and brotherhood becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]},{"x":"Religion is the experience that leads from the bondage of primitive fear to the liberty of faith that realizes sonship with God.","r":["101:0.1"]},{"q":"and the evidence to all the world that you have been born of the spirit is that you sincerely love one another.\"","r":"142:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Center of the Gospel Jesus Proclaimed","items":[{"x":"By proclaiming that every mortal creature is a child of a loving Father, a son of God, Jesus raised the concept of the Father to a sublime experience.","r":["196:0.2"]},{"x":"Jesus told his disciples first to make known that God is Father and man his son, and only then to discuss doctrine.","r":["141:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel in family terms: the fatherhood of God, the brotherhood of man, and sonship with God.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom is the fact of the fatherhood of God joined with the truth of the sonship-brotherhood of men.","r":["194:0.4"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth came to lead believers into a growing consciousness of eternal and ascending sonship with God.","r":["194:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Fraternité des hommes","Royaume des cieux","Foi","Esprit de Vérité","Ajusteur de Pensée"]},{"n":25,"t":"Fils Avonals","en":"Avonal Sons","sum":"Les Fils Avonals, ou Fils Magistraux, sont le deuxième ordre de Fils du Paradis, issus du Fils Éternel et de l’Esprit Infini. Sur les mondes évolutionnaires, ils servent de juges des dispensations, de magistrats qui élèvent un âge planétaire d’un degré, et de Fils d’effusion nés de femme qui vivent en mortels. Par ces « Christs mineurs », pleinement soutenus par le pouvoir du Fils Créateur, presque tous les mondes habités reçoivent l’Esprit de Vérité et les Ajusteurs de Pensée ; Urantia, pourtant, n’a jamais reçu de mission magistrale.","sections":[{"h":"Le deuxième ordre de Fils du Paradis","items":[{"x":"Chaque fois qu’un concept absolu du Fils Éternel s’unit à un nouvel idéal de service aimant de l’Esprit Infini, un nouveau Fils Magistral du Paradis apparait.","r":["20:2.1","20:1.11"]},{"x":"On estime les Fils Magistraux du grand univers à environ un milliard ; ils sont dirigés par le conseil suprême du Paradis et, une fois affectés à un univers local, servent sous le Fils Créateur.","r":["20:2.2"]},{"q":"since each Avonal Son has an exclusive personality, since no two are alike","r":"20:2.3"},{"q":"Et ces « Christs mineurs » sont aussi efficaces et tout-puissants dans leurs effusions planétaires que le Fils Créateur et Maitre le fut sur Urantia.","r":"35:0.1"},{"x":"Tandis que les Fils Créateurs révèlent le caractère du Père, les Avonals, Fils de l’effusion miséricordieuse, révèlent la nature du Fils Éternel avec sa compassion infinie.","r":["20:10.3","20:10.4"]}]},{"h":"Juges des dispensations","items":[{"x":"Les Avonals sont les magistrats des royaumes qui réveillent les survivants endormis, mettent fin à une dispensation et réaffectent les ministres planétaires aux tâches du nouvel âge.","r":["20:3.1"]},{"q":"though they may render judgments extinguishing the identity of personal creatures, they do not execute such sentences.","r":"20:3.2"},{"x":"Lors des visites « techniques », faites uniquement pour le jugement dispensationnel, ils ne s’incarnent pas, mais viennent en êtres spirituels invisibles pour les créatures matérielles.","r":["20:3.3","52:4.3"]},{"x":"L’appel nominal qui clôt une dispensation est proclamé par l’archange qui accompagne l’Avonal, et les gardiens séraphiques des dormeurs répondent à cette « voix de l’archange ».","r":["37:3.6"]},{"x":"Même sur les mondes ancrés dans la lumière et la vie, leurs actes judiciaires continuent, mais ils deviennent alors formels et ne modifient pas le cours des évènements planétaires.","r":["55:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Missions magistrales","items":[{"x":"La paix mondiale, une fois disparus les conflits raciaux et les hostilités nationales, est le signe qu’une planète est assez mûre pour recevoir un Fils Magistral.","r":["52:3.12"]},{"x":"Lors de la première mission magistrale, l’Avonal s’incarne sans naitre, en adulte pleinement développé de la race, et il apparait comme quelqu’un que les hommes peuvent voir et toucher.","r":["20:4.1","20:2.6"]},{"q":"Each new dispensation extends the horizon of revealed religion","r":"52:4.4"},{"x":"Peu après la première visite d’un Fils Magistral, l’humanité parvient à la libération économique, le travail quotidien nécessaire à la subsistance tombant à environ deux heures et demie.","r":["52:4.5"]},{"x":"Si une mission magistrale ne prépare pas le monde à recevoir un Fils d’effusion, un deuxième Fils Magistral, ou d’autres, viennent et font progresser l’humanité d’un âge à la fois.","r":["52:4.9"]}]},{"h":"Missions d’effusion","items":[{"x":"Chaque Avonal s’effuse au moins une fois sur une race mortelle, et, sur chaque planète, un seul Fils d’effusion apparait, né de femme.","r":["20:2.7","20:5.4"]},{"q":"But a bestowed Avonal does declare, \"Whosoever has seen me has seen the Eternal Son of God.\"","r":"20:6.5"},{"x":"Un Fils Magistral s’effuse toujours en étant soumis non à la volonté du Père, mais à la volonté du Fils Éternel du Paradis.","r":["20:6.5"]},{"x":"Les Fils d’effusion doivent mourir, mais une mort violente n’est pas exigée par le plan divin, et la plupart des mondes les traitent avec plus d’égards.","r":["20:6.6","20:6.7"]},{"q":"Jamais ils ne manquent d’atteindre le but de leur mission d’effusion.","r":"20:5.7"},{"x":"Lorsqu’un Avonal qui a achevé son effusion et le Fils Créateur envoient ensemble l’Esprit de Vérité, les créatures volitives normales de ce monde reçoivent des Ajusteurs de Pensée.","r":["52:5.6","20:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Les auxiliaires, et Urantia","items":[{"x":"Dans les missions planétaires, les Avonals sont aidés par des Melchizédeks et des archanges, et dans les missions d’effusion ils sont accompagnés de Brillantes Étoiles du Soir et d’une suite d’effusion de 144 membres.","r":["20:2.9","39:1.4"]},{"x":"Habituellement, après sept missions, un Avonal cède l’occasion à d’autres Fils et se joint à l’administration de l’univers dans les hauts conseils du Fils Créateur.","r":["20:2.8"]},{"q":"Urantia n’a encore jamais reçu un Fils Avonal en mission magistrale.","r":"20:4.4"},{"x":"Le Fils d’effusion d’Urantia n’était pas un Avonal, mais Micaël lui-même, bien que n’importe quel Fils d’effusion eût été tout aussi capable d’opérer la réhabilitation spirituelle.","r":["49:5.26","20:5.6"]},{"x":"Comme le monde de l’effusion de Micaël est le pupille du Maitre Fils, seul le temps révèlera quand un Fils Magistral viendra sur Urantia.","r":["20:4.5"]}]}],"see":["Fils Créateur Micaël","Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité","Melchizédeks","Fils Éternel","Esprit de Vérité","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":22,"t":"Fils Créateur Micaël","en":"Creator Son Michael","sum":"Un Fils Créateur est un Fils primaire du Paradis, né conjointement du Père Universel et du Fils Éternel, qui conçoit, crée et gouverne un univers local. Le créateur de notre univers de Nébadon est Micaël, qui a acquis sa souveraineté expérientiellement en s’effusant sept fois à la ressemblance de ses créatures ; sa dernière effusion fut la vie qu’il vécut sur Urantia en tant que Jésus de Nazareth. Pour nous, il est Dieu à toutes fins pratiques, et la voie par laquelle le Père est révélé.","sections":[{"h":"Origine et nature","items":[{"x":"Un Fils Créateur est un être de double origine, qui nait en un éclair lorsque le concept absolu de personnalité du Père et l’idée spirituelle absolue du Fils Éternel s’unissent parfaitement.","r":["21:0.1","21:1.1"]},{"q":"But each Creator Son is different from every other","r":"21:0.1"},{"x":"Micaël de Nébadon est la 611 121e personnalisation d’un concept originel d’identité infinie, et il présente des caractéristiques plus proches de celles du Fils Éternel.","r":["33:1.1","33:2.1"]},{"x":"Micaël n’est pas membre de la Trinité du Paradis, mais, dans son univers, il possède tous les attributs et pouvoirs divins qu’aurait le Fils Éternel s’il était présent.","r":["33:1.2","33:1.3"]},{"q":"À toutes fins pratiques, le Fils Souverain est Dieu pour notre univers et tous ses mondes habités.","r":"33:1.4"}]},{"h":"Créateur d’un univers local","items":[{"x":"Avant de choisir son emplacement dans l’espace, un Fils Créateur passe de longues périodes à observer les créations de ses frères ainés dans le même superunivers et à s’en instruire.","r":["21:2.1"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’il quitte le Paradis, il est accompagné d’une Fille Créative de l’Esprit Infini, qui se personnalise plus tard en tant qu’Esprit-Mère de l’univers local.","r":["21:2.2","21:2.9"]},{"x":"Les nouvelles modifications d’énergie-matière exigent le consentement de l’Esprit Infini, et les nouveaux modèles de créatures celui du Fils Éternel, tandis que la personnalité n’est conférée que par le Père.","r":["21:2.4","21:2.5","21:2.6"]},{"x":"Comme les créateurs diffèrent, les formes de vie des univers locaux qu’ils conçoivent sont chaque fois originales.","r":["21:2.10"]},{"x":"En l’absence de Micaël, Gabriel, la Radieuse Étoile du Matin, dirige l’univers, et l’Esprit-Mère supervise à la place de sa présence spirituelle.","r":["21:2.11","33:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Sept effusions et la souveraineté","items":[{"x":"Un Fils Créateur pourrait revendiquer la souveraineté dès le commencement, mais il s’engage envers la Trinité à ne pas assumer la souveraineté suprême avant d’avoir accompli sept effusions.","r":["21:3.2","21:3.12"]},{"q":"but they all could, they are truly freewill Sons.","r":"21:3.3"},{"x":"Par ses sept effusions, il pénètre sept niveaux de vie des créatures, révélant un à un la volonté septuple de la Déité, telle qu’elle est personnalisée dans les Sept Maitres Esprits.","r":["21:3.17","21:3.18","119:8.4"]},{"q":"These divine Sons are innately just, but they become understandingly merciful as a result of these successive bestowal experiences","r":"119:0.4"},{"x":"Ayant achevé ses effusions, un Fils Créateur devient un Maitre Fils, et l’ajout de l’expérience de créature à sa nature produit un changement permanent.","r":["21:4.6"]},{"q":"Micaël naquit créateur, il fut éduqué comme administrateur, formé comme directeur exécutif, mais il lui fallut gagner sa souveraineté par expérience.","r":"119:8.2"}]},{"h":"L’effusion sur Urantia","items":[{"x":"Après six effusions, Micaël descendit sur Urantia dans la similitude de la chair mortelle, la plus humble des créatures volitives.","r":["120:0.2"]},{"x":"La dernière effusion allait au-delà de l’acquisition de la souveraineté ; c’était un plan pour la révélation suprême de la soumission à la volonté du Père Universel.","r":["120:0.7","120:0.8"]},{"q":"Jésus fut Dieu et homme, toujours et pour l’éternité.","r":"120:4.3"},{"q":"Ne perdez jamais de vue le fait que le but spirituel suprême de l’effusion de Micaël était de rehausser la révélation de Dieu.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"Parce que sa mort sur Urantia achevait sa carrière d’effusion, il put dire en vérité : « Tout est accompli. »","r":["21:4.5"]},{"x":"Ainsi, cette petite planète, la demeure mortelle du souverain Christ Micaël, est devenue le sanctuaire sentimental de tout Nébadon.","r":["119:8.8"]}]},{"h":"Le gouvernement et la destinée du Maitre Fils","items":[{"x":"Après l’effusion sur Urantia, Micaël fut reconnu par les Anciens des Jours et par le Père Universel comme souverain établi de Nébadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"Lorsque l’Esprit-Mère se subordonna à lui, Micaël devint le dépositaire personnel de la divinité, avec tout pouvoir au ciel et sur la terre.","r":["33:2.3","33:2.4"]},{"x":"Le Maitre Fils répand l’Esprit de Vérité « sur toute chair » et communique ainsi sans cesse avec les mondes où il a séjourné.","r":["21:5.10"]},{"x":"La somme des sept effusions est une nouvelle révélation de l’Être Suprême pour Nébadon, et elle a aussi accru la souveraineté de Dieu le Suprême en évolution.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"On croit que les Micaëls sont destinés à devenir, dans l’éternité, littéralement « le chemin, la vérité et la vie ».","r":["21:6.4"]}]}],"see":["Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Univers local de Nébadon","Esprit de Vérité","Fils Avonals","Être Suprême","Anciens des Jours"]},{"n":31,"t":"Fils et Filles Matériels","en":"Material Sons and Daughters","sum":"The Material Sons and Daughters are an order of sex-endowed Sons produced by the Creator Son for each local system; sent to the evolutionary worlds as Adam and Eve, they are charged with the biologic uplift of the races. Being material, they are visible to mortals and form the last link between the invisible Planetary Prince and human beings. The Adam and Eve of Urantia defaulted in their mission, yet their contribution greatly improved mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Nature","items":[{"x":"The Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son; the Universe Mother Spirit takes no part in their production.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"For each system the Creator Son makes only the original pair, fashioned to the life pattern of that system, and all the rest are their descendants.","r":["51:1.2"]},{"x":"They stand eight to ten feet tall and shine with a violet radiance; Adam and Eve are equal yet complementary and usually work as a pair.","r":["51:1.3"]},{"x":"With a dual constitution that takes in both material food and cosmic energy, they are cut off from their life source if they rebel and in the end meet material death.","r":["51:1.4"]},{"q":"Ces Fils Matériels sont le chainon physique et ultime dans la chaine des personnalités qui descend de la divinité et de la perfection vers l’humanité et l’existence matérielle.","r":"45:5.3"}]},{"h":"Life on Jerusem, the System Capital","items":[{"x":"Each family of Material Sons and Daughters lives in the Adamic domain of one thousand centers on Jerusem, and their numbers increase by natural reproduction.","r":["45:5.2","45:5.4"]},{"x":"The Adamites of Jerusem experiment with self-government through elections and representative government, and they handle most of the routine affairs of the capital sphere.","r":["45:5.5","45:5.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks maintain a faculty at each system headquarters for the education and spiritual training of young Material Sons and Daughters.","r":["45:5.7"]},{"x":"While living on the system capital, Material Sons have no Thought Adjusters, but through service they gain capacity for Adjuster indwelling and the ascending career.","r":["51:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Mission of a Planetary Adam","items":[{"x":"When an evolutionary world reaches the peak of its physical evolution, a volunteer pair is chosen, dematerialized, and carried to that world by seraphim.","r":["51:2.1","51:2.2"]},{"x":"On arrival they are rematerialized under the direction of the Life Carriers, and they remain in the unconsciousness of seraphic sleep throughout the process.","r":["51:2.4"]},{"q":"Le principal rôle du couple importé consiste à se multiplier et à rehausser les enfants du temps.","r":"51:3.3"},{"x":"Adam and Eve do not mate directly with the evolutionary races; their children voluntarily unite with superior men and women brought to the garden.","r":["51:5.3"]},{"x":"With the added strain of the violet race, more progress is made in one hundred thousand years than in the previous million.","r":["51:5.6"]},{"x":"The garden schools teach practical arts, economics, and civil government, and with the schools of the Planetary Prince they set the pace of civilization.","r":["51:6.2","51:6.4"]}]},{"h":"The Link Between God and Man","items":[{"x":"Unlike the other planetary Sons, Material Sons are visible to mortals, understandable to them, and can actually associate with them.","r":["51:1.7"]},{"q":"Chez ces immortels Fils et Filles Matériels, nous rencontrons le dernier chainon indispensable qui relie Dieu à l’homme, qui jette un pont sur l’abime presque infini entre le Créateur éternel et les plus humbles personnalités finies du temps.","r":"51:6.5"},{"x":"They can see the invisible Planetary Prince and his staff, and so they can interpret him to mortals.","r":["51:6.5"]},{"x":"On the ascending path mortals come to recognize seven fathers, the second of whom is the Planetary Adam, the father of the realm.","r":["51:6.6","51:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Adam and Eve of Urantia","items":[{"x":"The Adam and Eve who came to Urantia were number 14,311 of the senior corps on Jerusem and had been heads of the laboratory dealing with the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"They were overcome by the subtle counterplans of Caligastia and violated their covenant, but they did not join the Lucifer rebellion.","r":["51:3.4"]},{"q":"Il n’y a pas eu de « chute de l’homme ».","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"Though the divine plan miscarried, the Adamic bestowal left the peoples of Urantia biologically far better than before.","r":["75:8.1","75:8.3"]},{"x":"Adam and Eve awoke again on the mansion worlds in a special resurrection and returned to Jerusem as ascending citizens.","r":["76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"Ce sont les peuples qui font une civilisation ; la civilisation ne fait pas les peuples.","r":"76:6.4"}]},{"h":"Ascending Material Sons","items":[{"q":"Et il est bien vrai que les Adams Planétaires — les Fils et Filles Matériels des mondes évolutionnaires — sont des Fils descendants qui, de leurs sphères d’origine, les capitales des systèmes locaux, descendent vers les mondes habités.","r":"40:2.1"},{"x":"An Adam and Eve who succeed in their mission may, once the world is settled in light and life, retire from administration and register as perfected Material Sons.","r":["40:2.2"]},{"x":"Material Sons whose planetary assignment is long delayed may also be released from citizenship status and advance toward Paradise with the ascending pilgrims.","r":["31:5.1"]},{"x":"Material Sons are rare in the finaliter companies but are always chosen as leaders, and an Edenic pair sometimes works together as one personality.","r":["31:5.3"]}]}],"see":["Adam et Ève","Races","Corps de la Finalité","Porteurs de Vie","Médians","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":4,"t":"Fils Éternel","en":"Eternal Son","sum":"Le Fils Éternel est la Source-Centre Deuxième, l’expression parfaite du premier concept personnel et absolu du Père Universel. Il est la Parole divine vivante, la révélation finale de l’esprit et de la personnalité du Père, et l’administrateur spirituel qui maintient toute réalité spirituelle dans le circuit de gravité spirituelle. Étendant l’amour du Père sous forme de miséricorde, il se rapproche des créatures par les effusions des Fils du Paradis.","sections":[{"h":"Identité et nature","items":[{"x":"Le Fils Éternel est l’expression complète du premier concept personnel et absolu du Père ; chaque fois que le Père s’exprime personnellement, il le fait par le Fils.","r":["6:0.1"]},{"x":"L’expression « première pensée » n’est qu’une concession aux mentaux liés au temps ; le Fils n’a pas de commencement et il est coéternel avec le Père.","r":["6:0.2","6:0.4"]},{"q":"La Source-Centre Première est l’Absolu Volitif. La Source-Centre Deuxième est l’Absolu de Personnalité.","r":"6:1.2"},{"x":"Le Père n’agit jamais personnellement comme créateur, sinon conjointement avec le Fils ou avec l’action coordonnée du Fils.","r":["6:1.3"]},{"x":"Sur Urantia, on a confondu le Fils Originel avec le Fils d’effusion, Micaël de Nébadon, mais le titre de « Fils Éternel » appartient au seul Fils Originel.","r":["6:1.5","6:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Ministre de la miséricorde","items":[{"x":"Le Fils est aussi immuable et infiniment digne de confiance que le Père, et il nous semble plus personnel, étant d’un degré plus proche de nous.","r":["6:2.1"]},{"q":"De même que Dieu est amour, le Fils est miséricorde.","r":"6:3.1"},{"x":"Le Fils n’est pas un intercesseur qui implore la miséricorde du Père ; toute miséricorde que montre le Fils est une révélation directe de l’amour du Père.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"La miséricorde est de l’amour appliqué ; par analogie, l’amour de Dieu ressemble davantage à l’amour d’un père, tandis que l’amour du Fils Éternel ressemble davantage à l’affection d’une mère.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"Le Père aime ses enfants de l’univers comme un père, tandis que le Fils Éternel considère chaque créature à la fois en père et en frère.","r":["6:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Le circuit de gravité spirituelle","items":[{"x":"Le Fils n’est omnipotent que dans le domaine spirituel ; il n’agit pas personnellement dans les domaines physiques, ni dans l’aide mentale autrement que par l’Acteur Conjoint.","r":["6:4.2","6:5.1"]},{"x":"La gravité spirituelle est exempte de délai temporel, l’espace ne la diminue pas, et elle ne décroit pas selon le carré de la distance.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"Les réalités spirituelles réagissent à la gravité spirituelle selon leur valeur qualitative, et cette réaction est aussi sure et prévisible que la réaction de la matière à la gravité.","r":["7:1.3","7:1.8"]},{"q":"Le péché et la rébellion peuvent interférer avec les opérations des circuits d’un univers local, mais rien ne peut suspendre la gravité d’esprit du Fils Éternel.","r":"7:1.7"},{"q":"Le circuit de gravité d’esprit tire littéralement l’âme des hommes vers le Paradis.","r":"7:3.2"}]},{"h":"La prière et la relation avec l’individu","items":[{"x":"L’esprit du Fils Éternel nous entoure, mais il ne nous habite pas et ne devient pas une partie de nous comme le fait le Moniteur de Mystère.","r":["6:4.6"]},{"x":"Le contenu spirituel d’une prière sincère est transmis instantanément par le circuit de gravité spirituelle à toutes les personnalités divines concernées.","r":["7:3.3"]},{"x":"Les requêtes purement matérielles et égocentriques ne peuvent entrer dans le circuit spirituel et tombent mortes.","r":["7:3.6"]},{"q":"C’est la pensée motivante, le contenu spirituel, qui valide la supplique d’un mortel. Les paroles sont sans valeurs.","r":"7:3.7"}]},{"h":"L’effusion et le plan de perfection","items":[{"x":"Le Fils a accepté sans réserve le plan d’accomplissement progressif du Père, et il a lui-même proposé le plan d’effusion, qui consiste à envoyer les Fils de Dieu sur les mondes évolutionnaires.","r":["7:4.4","7:4.5"]},{"x":"Le Fils Éternel est le dépositaire personnel et le gardien divin du plan d’ascension des créatures que le Père lui a confié.","r":["7:4.7"]},{"x":"La personnalité du Fils ne pouvant être fragmentée, il participe à l’expérience des créatures par les incarnations des Fils du Paradis.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]},{"x":"Le Fils Éternel s’est effusé sept fois sur les sept circuits de Havona, fait qui est un encouragement éternel pour chaque pèlerin qui traverse Havona.","r":["7:5.5","7:5.9"]},{"q":"Il est littéralement vrai que quiconque a vu un Fils du Paradis a vu le Fils Éternel de Dieu.","r":"7:5.11"}]},{"h":"Révélation suprême du Père","items":[{"x":"Le Fils Éternel est la révélation complète et finale de l’esprit et de la personnalité du Père, et toute connaissance du Père vient du Fils et de ses Fils.","r":["7:7.1"]},{"x":"Le Père ne se rapproche de nous en tant que personnalité que par les Fils divins du Fils Éternel, et c’est par cette voie vivante que nous aussi montons vers le Père.","r":["7:7.4"]},{"x":"Les pèlerins qui traversent les circuits de Havona peuvent atteindre le Fils bien avant d’être préparés à discerner le Père.","r":["7:7.5"]},{"x":"La personnalité du Fils ne brille pas avec éclat pour le mental matériel ou morontiel ; ce n’est qu’au début de l’ascension spirituelle qu’elle devient de plus en plus réelle.","r":["6:8.5","6:8.6"]},{"q":"Au même sens que Dieu est le Père Universel, le Fils est la Mère Universelle.","r":"6:8.1"}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Esprit Infini","Trinité du Paradis","Fils Créateur Micaël","Prière","Miséricorde"]},{"n":26,"t":"Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité","en":"Trinity Teacher Sons","sum":"Les Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité, ou Daynals, sont des Fils issus directement de la Trinité du Paradis qui, avec les Fils Créateurs et les Fils Magistraux, forment le troisième ordre de Fils du Paradis. Ils ne gouvernent ni ne jugent ; ils sont les éducateurs des univers, voués à l’illumination morale et à l’éveil spirituel des mortels comme des êtres spirituels. Sur les mondes évolutionnaires, ils accomplissent la dernière mission divine, ouvrant un âge spirituel qui conduit une planète à l’ère de lumière et de vie.","sections":[{"h":"Des Fils d’origine trinitaire","items":[{"x":"Ces Fils furent amenés à l’existence par la Trinité du Paradis ; on les appelle Daynals dans Havona, Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité dans Orvonton et Fils Spirituels du Paradis sur Salvington.","r":["20:7.1"]},{"q":"Ces êtres forment le seul groupe des Fils de Dieu qui vous soit révélé et qui soit issu de la Trinité du Paradis.","r":"19:1.3"},{"x":"D’origine trinitaire, mais au service du ministère de la filiation divine, ils ont un double statut d’êtres de liaison entre les personnalités d’origine trinitaire et celles de double origine.","r":["19:1.1"]},{"x":"Contrairement aux Fils stationnaires de la Trinité, dont le nombre est fixe, les Fils Instructeurs ne cessent d’augmenter ; leur nombre rapporté est d’un peu plus de vingt-et-un milliards, sans compter d’importantes réserves au Paradis.","r":["19:1.2","20:7.2"]},{"x":"Ils partagent les natures conjuguées des trois Déités, mais, dans Havona, ils semblent refléter davantage le Père, dans les superunivers le Fils Éternel, et dans les créations locales l’Esprit Infini.","r":["20:7.4"]},{"q":"Dans tous les univers, ils sont la personnification du service et la discrétion de la sagesse.","r":"20:7.4"}]},{"h":"Des Fils qui enseignent au lieu de gouverner","items":[{"x":"Ils ne sont ni créateurs ni sauveteurs, ni juges ni chefs, et ne font donc pas organiquement partie des gouvernements locaux ou superuniversels.","r":["20:7.3"]},{"q":"Ils sont les éducateurs universels, et se consacrent à l’éveil spirituel et à la gouverne morale de tous les royaumes.","r":"20:7.3"},{"x":"Ils sont envoyés directement aux sièges des superunivers sans formation préalable dans l’univers central, et, n’ayant pas de pouvoir propre d’attraction spirituelle, ils utilisent l’influence spirituelle des Fils Créateurs et des Fils Magistraux.","r":["20:7.5"]},{"x":"Ils commencent leur ministère dans les systèmes locaux, progressent à travers les constellations jusqu’à l’œuvre la plus élevée de la création locale, et se soucient également d’éduquer les mortels et les êtres natifs de l’univers local, tels que les séraphins.","r":["20:8.1","20:8.2"]},{"x":"Ils forment le corps enseignant chargé des épreuves et des examens de qualification pour les stades inférieurs du service de l’univers, et ils dirigent des cours de formation depuis les écoles planétaires jusqu’aux hauts collèges de sagesse de Salvington.","r":["20:8.3"]},{"x":"Le système éducatif de Nébadon est administré conjointement par les Fils Instructeurs et le corps enseignant des Melchizédeks, et l’univers entier est décrit comme une vaste école.","r":["37:6.1","37:6.2"]},{"x":"Ils adoptent comme apprentis des fils trinitisés par des créatures, les forment et peuvent les proposer pour l’étreinte de la Trinité.","r":["22:8.3","22:8.4"]}]},{"h":"L’ouverture d’un âge spirituel sur une planète","items":[{"x":"Ils n’ont rien à voir avec la fin des dispensations ni avec le jugement des morts ; ils se consacrent entièrement à faire poindre sur une planète évolutionnaire l’aube de l’ère des réalités spirituelles.","r":["20:9.2"]},{"q":"Ils rendent manifestes les contreparties spirituelles de la connaissance matérielle et de la sagesse temporelle.","r":"20:9.2"},{"x":"Un Fils Instructeur planétaire est assisté de soixante-dix Fils primaires, de douze Fils secondaires et de trois de l’ordre suprême, et le corps demeure au moins mille ans du temps planétaire.","r":["52:7.2","20:9.3"]},{"q":"Cette mission est une contribution de la Trinité aux efforts antérieurs de toutes les personnalités divines qui ont apporté leur ministère à un monde habité.","r":"52:7.2"},{"x":"Comme ils ne se matérialisent pas pour devenir visibles aux mortels, les Brillantes Étoiles du Soir servent de liaison entre le corps invisible des Fils Instructeurs et les mortels du monde.","r":["20:9.3","37:2.9"]},{"x":"Au cours de cet âge, beaucoup de mortels sont transférés d’entre les vivants, et, à mesure que la fusion avec l’Ajusteur se multiplie, la mort naturelle devient de moins en moins fréquente.","r":["52:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Urantia et l’avenir de lumière et de vie","items":[{"x":"N’ayant jamais connu d’âge spirituel, Urantia n’est pas familiarisée avec ces Fils, mais des Fils Instructeurs visitent dès maintenant le monde pour préparer leur futur séjour.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"Ils apparaitront lorsque les habitants de ce monde se seront relativement libérés des chaines de l’animalisme et des entraves du matérialisme.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"Nul ne sait si le second avènement promis par Jésus aura lieu avant ou après l’apparition d’un Fils Magistral ou des Fils Instructeurs.","r":["52:7.1"]},{"x":"À la fin de l’une de leurs missions répétées, le Prince Planétaire est élevé au statut de Souverain Planétaire, et le Souverain du Système proclame l’ouverture de l’ère de lumière et de vie.","r":["52:7.10"]},{"q":"sooner or later the grace of God and the ministry of angels will usher in the day of the advent of the Trinity Teacher Sons;","r":"52:7.14"},{"x":"On croit sur Uversa que les Fils Instructeurs, longtemps associés à la vie des mortels évolutionnaires, seront éternellement unis au Corps de la Finalité lorsque le superunivers sera ancré dans la lumière et la vie.","r":["20:9.5"]}]},{"h":"La coopération des trois Fils du Paradis","items":[{"x":"Les Fils Créateurs révèlent le caractère du Père, les Avonals la miséricorde du Fils Éternel, et les Daynals la personnalité enseignante de l’Esprit Infini ; ensemble, ils réalisent la souveraineté de Dieu le Suprême.","r":["20:10.4"]},{"q":"Chez les Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité, l’amour, la miséricorde et le ministère des trois Déités du Paradis sont coordonnés sur les niveaux de valeurs les plus élevés de l’espace-temps et présentés aux univers comme la vérité vivante, la divine bonté et la vraie beauté spirituelle.","r":"20:10.3"},{"x":"Les Fils Instructeurs sont les personnalités coordinatrices suprêmes d’origine trinitaire ; dans le vaste univers, il y a toujours un grand danger de points de vue étroits et de concepts fragmentaires de la réalité.","r":["19:1.4"]},{"q":"Ils sont les maitres exaltés de toutes les personnalités d’esprit, et même les instructeurs loyaux et éprouvés des Fils de Dieu eux-mêmes.","r":"20:8.4"}]}],"see":["Trinité du Paradis","Fils Avonals","Fils Créateur Micaël","Lumière et vie","Melchizédeks","Corps de la Finalité"]},{"n":51,"t":"Foi","en":"Faith","sum":"Faith is a living trust in God and in spiritual values, distinct from belief, which merely accepts a doctrine as true. Belief becomes faith only when it actually guides and shapes life, and faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the God of experiential certainty. Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God and the key to Havona, and Jesus lived out its highest example.","sections":[{"h":"Belief and Faith","items":[{"x":"Accepting a teaching as true is only belief; belief becomes faith when it actually dominates the mode of living.","r":["101:8.1"]},{"q":"La croyance attache, la foi affranchit.","r":"101:8.2"},{"x":"Beliefs may become group possessions, but faith must always be personal.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"x":"Faith is a God-knowing and man-serving life, a living experience concerned with spiritual meanings and supreme values.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"q":"Belief may not be able to resist doubt and withstand fear, but faith is always triumphant over doubting","r":"102:6.7"},{"q":"Le fait d’accepter un enseignement comme vrai n’est pas la foi, c’est une simple croyance.","r":"101:8.1"}]},{"h":"Faith and Certainty","items":[{"x":"Faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the saving God of certainty in personal religious experience.","r":["102:6.4"]},{"q":"On peut arriver à des convictions sur Dieu par de sages raisonnements, mais on n’apprend individuellement à connaitre Dieu que par la foi, par l’expérience personnelle.","r":"102:6.5"},{"x":"In science God is a possibility and in philosophy a probability, but in religion he is a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]},{"x":"God is not revealed by miracles or material proofs; he is known by trusting him.","r":["102:1.5"]},{"x":"The more one knows of science, the less sure one becomes; the more religion one has, the more certain one is.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Marks of True Faith","items":[{"x":"True faith trusts in the goodness of God even amid bitter disappointment and defeat, and it generates profound courage in the face of calamity.","r":["101:3.6","101:3.7"]},{"x":"Faith maintains an inexplicable poise and serenity in the midst of illness and suffering, abuse and injustice.","r":["101:3.8","101:3.9"]},{"x":"True faith worships God in every circumstance and declares, \"Though he slay me, yet will I serve him.\"","r":["101:3.16"]},{"x":"Faith does not violate intellectual honesty, foster intolerance and persecution, or turn away from scientific discoveries.","r":["101:8.3","101:8.4"]},{"x":"Faith vitalizes religion and moves the religionist to live the golden rule heroically.","r":["101:8.4"]},{"q":"La foi vivifie la religion et oblige le religioniste à vivre héroïquement la règle d’or.","r":"101:8.4"}]},{"h":"Faith and Salvation","items":[{"x":"Faith links moral consciousness with the spiritual concept of enduring reality, making religion a technique of salvation.","r":["101:9.9"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Faith releases the divine spark that lives within man, the potential of eternal survival.","r":["132:3.6"]},{"x":"The Adjuster's success in achieving survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"Le consentement à croire est la clef de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"}]},{"h":"The Faith of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not use faith as a consolation in suffering or a comfort in despair; he enjoyed serenity in an unquestioning trust in God.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus' great contribution was less a new idea of God than the human demonstration of a new and higher type of living faith.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus asks people not so much to believe in him as to believe with him, to believe as he believed.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom.","r":["170:3.2"]}]}],"see":["Expérience religieuse","Religion personnelle","Vérité","Royaume des cieux","Survie","Caractère de Jésus"]},{"n":48,"t":"Fraternité des hommes","en":"Brotherhood of Man","sum":"The brotherhood of man is the universal relationship that follows from the fact that every personality is a child of the same heavenly Father. Because God loves each individual and that love reaches all, people are bound together as brothers. Jesus taught the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man as the center of the gospel, and its realization depends not on law or force but on mutual understanding and love, and on the spiritual transformation of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Brotherhood Flowing from Fatherhood","items":[{"x":"God loves each person as an individual child, yet because that love reaches all, a universal brotherhood arises.","r":["12:7.8","12:7.10"]},{"x":"Brotherhood is a relationship of the whole, not of the parts: the good of each helps all, and the evil of each adds to the suffering of all.","r":["12:7.11"]},{"q":"Après tout, la fraternité des hommes est basée sur la reconnaissance de la paternité de Dieu.","r":"52:6.7"},{"x":"When the belief that we are sons of God becomes effective, the feeling of brotherhood, an altruistic conviction, also becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]}]},{"h":"The Brotherhood Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus taught a new and greater brotherhood beyond the family of blood, the brotherhood of the sons of God.","r":["140:8.14"]},{"x":"Jesus named two laws of the heavenly family, loving the Father and loving one's brother as oneself, and said that brotherly love shows itself in unselfish service.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"q":"Aimez-vous les uns les autres comme je vous ai aimés.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"Jesus also used such expressions as the family of God, the fellowship of believers, and the brotherhood of man to refer to the kingdom.","r":["170:2.24"]},{"x":"The religion Jesus founded consists in the personal experience of doing the will of God and serving the human brotherhood.","r":["196:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Spiritual Brotherhood and Social Brotherhood","items":[{"q":"Le royaume des cieux n’est ni un ordre social, ni un ordre économique ; il est une fraternité exclusivement spirituelle d’individus connaissant Dieu.","r":"99:3.2"},{"x":"Since the kingdom of heaven is a spiritual brotherhood of spirit-born sons, it can be proclaimed only by the power of the spirit, not by physical force.","r":["178:1.2"]},{"x":"Jesus showed the way to the immediate attainment of spiritual brotherhood, but social brotherhood depends on many personal and planetary changes.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"x":"Religious brotherhood cannot be realized unless all religions give up their claims of ecclesiastical authority and spiritual sovereignty.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"La révélation religieuse est essentielle pour que se réalise la fraternité sur Urantia.","r":"52:6.2"}]},{"h":"The Way to Brotherhood","items":[{"x":"Social contact through travel, commerce, and exchange, and intellectual cross-fertilization through acquaintance with one another's thought, hasten brotherhood.","r":["52:6.3","52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ignorance breeds suspicion, and suspicion cannot coexist with sympathy and love.","r":["52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ethical awakening, political wisdom, and above all spiritual insight are needed for the realization of brotherhood.","r":["52:6.5","52:6.6","52:6.7"]},{"x":"The quickest way to brotherhood is spiritual pressure from above, enlarging the soul's capacity to understand and love one another.","r":["52:6.7"]},{"x":"On an isolated world like Urantia, religious revelation is essential for realizing brotherhood.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"q":"L’ignorance engendre la suspicion, et la suspicion est incompatible avec l’attitude essentielle de sympathie et d’amour.","r":"52:6.4"}]},{"h":"The Contagion of Love and Future Civilization","items":[{"x":"No one can love his fellows by willpower alone; love is born of a thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"q":"Il est moins important d’aimer tous les hommes aujourd’hui que d’apprendre chaque jour à en aimer un de plus.","r":"100:4.6"},{"x":"If every person became a focus of love, that love would encompass all civilization, and the brotherhood of man would be realized.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"The secret of a better civilization lies in Jesus' teachings about brotherhood, the good will of love and mutual trust.","r":["194:3.12"]},{"x":"The progress of civilization leads to the social achievement of the brotherhood of man and the personal status of God-consciousness.","r":["71:4.15"]},{"x":"The hope of modern Christianity lies in learning anew the living gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["195:10.21"]}]}],"see":["Filiation avec Dieu","Père Universel","Royaume des cieux","Amour","Service","Civilisation"]},{"n":34,"t":"Fusion avec l’Ajusteur","en":"Adjuster Fusion","sum":"Adjuster fusion is the event in which the evolving immortal soul becomes eternally one with the indwelling Thought Adjuster. It usually takes place on the mansion worlds after death, but rarely it is achieved by translation during the life in the flesh. Fusion announces to the universe the mortal's final choice to do the Father's will; by it the ascender's eternal career is assured, and the way opens to the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","sections":[{"h":"What Fusion Is","items":[{"q":"Et cette fusion constitue le mystère qui fait que Dieu et l’homme sont un, le mystère de l’évolution de la créature finie, mais cela est éternellement vrai.","r":"112:7.2"},{"x":"Since the Adjuster is an immortal spirit, union with it confers eternal life on the soul of the fused mortal.","r":["40:7.1"]},{"x":"In fusion the Adjuster and the soul share all of each other's experiences and values and actually become one being.","r":["110:7.4","110:7.5"]},{"x":"The fused being is one personality, and no universe intelligence can distinguish the human and the Adjuster separately.","r":["112:7.8"]},{"x":"The fused Adjuster keeps its existential divine nature yet is transformed to the level of finite experience and inseparably linked with the ascending personality.","r":["107:2.7"]}]},{"h":"When It Occurs","items":[{"x":"Fusion usually occurs during the sojourn in the local system, and sometimes it is delayed until the ascender reaches the constellation or the local universe capital.","r":["112:7.3"]},{"x":"Fusion that is actually effective is often not achieved until the sojourn on the fifth or sixth mansion world.","r":["47:8.3"]},{"x":"When the seven cosmic circles are attained and the final choice of the will is added, fusion may occur during the life in the flesh, and the body is instantly consumed.","r":["110:7.2"]},{"x":"In the case of most Urantians, the Adjuster must wait patiently for the deliverance of death.","r":["110:7.6"]},{"q":"La mort physique naturelle n’est pas inévitable pour les humains.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, fusion translations steadily increase, and by the fourth stage more than half of all mortals are translated from among the living.","r":["55:2.2","55:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Fusion","items":[{"q":"La fusion avec l’Ajusteur ne se produit jamais avant que les décrets du superunivers aient confirmé que la nature humaine a porté son choix d’une manière définitive et irrévocable sur la carrière éternelle.","r":"112:7.5"},{"x":"Until fusion an ascender may at any time forsake the Father's will, but fusion announces that he has chosen the Father's will without reservation.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster of one who has made the supreme decision foresees the time of fusion and regards the union as an already existing fact.","r":["109:2.4"]},{"x":"When Adjuster fusion proclaims the final choice to the universe, the eternal destiny of the human being is assured.","r":["5:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Scene of Fusion","items":[{"q":"and then, in the presence of such a survivor's morontia associates, these messengers of confirmation speak: \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":"47:8.4"},{"x":"The new being is presented under a new name, spends forty days in spiritual retirement, and chooses a route to Havona.","r":["47:8.5"]},{"x":"On settled worlds the candidate for fusion departs in a flash of life before family and friends gathered in the temple.","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"q":"the human beings who might witness such a spectacle would only observe the translating mortal disappear \"in chariots of fire.\"","r":"110:7.2"},{"x":"Those fused during the life in the flesh do not pass through death but go to the higher morontia spheres by direct Adjuster transit.","r":["49:6.18","49:6.19"]}]},{"h":"When Fusion Does Not Take Place","items":[{"x":"Mortals are divided into three groups according to their relation to the Adjuster: temporary indwelling, nonfusion, and fusion-potential types.","r":["40:5.4","40:5.5","40:5.7"]},{"x":"Mortals of primitive ages may survive through the ministry of Adjusters, yet they do not become eternally united with them.","r":["40:5.9","40:5.10"]},{"x":"Mortals of the nonfusion type are also indwelt by Adjusters throughout life, but if they survive, their souls fuse with spirit.","r":["40:5.13","40:5.14"]},{"x":"The few whose survival is recognized but who never become one with their Adjusters go, after the verdict of the courts of inquiry, on the path of fusion with the Son.","r":["40:8.1","40:8.3"]},{"q":"In the fusion experience there is no overlapping","r":"40:9.1"}]},{"h":"Results of Fusion","items":[{"q":"Quand la fusion avec l’Ajusteur a été effectuée, la carrière éternelle de la personnalité ne court plus aucun danger dans l’avenir.","r":"112:7.4"},{"x":"Fusion confers on the personality actualities that were only potential: fixation of divinity qualities, past-eternity experience and memory, and immortality.","r":["112:7.1"]},{"x":"In matters of personality the human leads in the fused ascender, whose headquarters is Ascendington rather than Divinington.","r":["112:7.12"]},{"x":"The number of a fused Adjuster is stricken from the superuniverse records, and its destiny becomes the same as that of the ascending mortal: the Corps of the Finality.","r":["112:7.11","112:7.13"]},{"x":"Through fusion the Universal Father fulfills his promise to give himself to his material creatures.","r":["112:7.14"]},{"x":"Adjuster-fused mortals are the only human order that passes through the Havona circuits and finds God on Paradise.","r":["40:7.5"]}]}],"see":["Ajusteur de Pensée","Âme","Corps de la Finalité","Mondes des maisons","Survie","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":28,"t":"Gardiens séraphiques","en":"Guardian Seraphim","sum":"Les gardiens séraphiques sont les séraphins qui veillent sur des mortels individuels. Lorsqu’une personne atteint le troisième cercle, prend la décision suprême de devenir semblable à Dieu ou entre dans le corps de réserve de la destinée, un gardien personnel, un gardien de la destinée, lui est affecté. Ils agissent par les circonstances extérieures sans envahir la volonté humaine ; après la mort, ils détiennent les valeurs de survie de l’âme, aident à la repersonnalisation sur les mondes des maisons et accompagnent l’ascendeur dans la carrière ascendante. Pour les séraphins, cette affectation est la voie la plus sure vers le Paradis.","sections":[{"h":"Comment les anges gardiens sont affectés","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Depuis l’effusion de Micaël, les séraphins sont affectés non selon la race, mais selon l’intelligence, la spiritualité et la destinée des êtres humains.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"x":"Les personnes ordinaires sont prises en charge par des gardiens séraphiques selon le cercle atteint : par groupes de mille au septième cercle, de cinq-cents au sixième, de cent au cinquième et de dix au quatrième.","r":["113:1.6","113:1.7"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’un mortel atteint le troisième cercle, un ange personnel (en réalité deux) se consacre entièrement à lui.","r":["113:1.8"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’une personne est inscrite dans le corps de réserve de la destinée ou prend la décision suprême, véritables fiançailles avec l’Ajusteur, un gardien personnel lui est aussitôt affecté, quel que soit son cercle.","r":["113:1.5"]},{"x":"Pour les réservistes choisis comme gardiens de la destinée planétaire, le chef des séraphins planétaires désigne des gardiens personnels de la destinée.","r":["114:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Les gardiens de la destinée","items":[{"x":"Les séraphins ne sont appelés gardiens de la destinée qu’après que l’être humain a pris la décision suprême, est entré dans le troisième cercle ou a été incorporé au corps de réserve de la destinée.","r":["113:2.1"]},{"x":"Le premier mortel d’Urantia à recevoir un gardien personnel fut Rantowoc, un sage de la race rouge, il y a très longtemps.","r":["113:2.2"]},{"x":"Les affectations sont toujours faites parmi les volontaires de séraphins expérimentés et éprouvés, et plus de cent séraphins se sont portés candidats pour la garde d’une seule personne.","r":["113:2.3","113:2.7"]},{"x":"L’un des membres du couple est toujours en service, tandis que son complément tient le rôle d’ange archiviste de la personne, et les archives sont tenues par les chérubins et sanobins associés.","r":["113:2.7","113:2.9"]},{"x":"Les séraphins désirent également servir un Fils incarné et être affectés comme gardiens de la destinée, ce dernier service étant le passeport le plus sûr pour le Paradis.","r":["39:1.6"]},{"x":"Les anges éprouvent une affection durable pour leurs associés humains, mais ils ont du mal à comprendre les peurs animales qui dominent même la foi humaine.","r":["113:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Aider du dehors, et non du dedans","items":[{"x":"Le gardien coordonne personnellement les multiples influences impersonnelles de l’Esprit Infini et les met en corrélation avec la présence spirituelle du Père et du Fils.","r":["113:3.1","113:3.2"]},{"q":"Les serviteurs angéliques ont le don de conjuguer l’amour du Père et la miséricorde du Fils dans leur ministère auprès des hommes.","r":"113:3.3"},{"x":"Alors que l’Ajusteur agit du dedans, par l’âme, les séraphins agissent du dehors vers le dedans, par l’environnement social, éthique et moral des êtres humains.","r":["113:4.1"]},{"q":"The Adjuster is the essence of man's eternal nature; the seraphim is the teacher of man's evolving nature","r":"113:4.2"},{"x":"Accepter la conduite séraphique ne rend pas la vie facile ; on rencontre au contraire les collines escarpées des choix moraux et du progrès spirituel.","r":["113:4.3"]},{"x":"L’élan de prière des personnes conscientes de Dieu naît souvent de l’influence séraphique, et le gardien est le plus actif quand l’Ajusteur l’est le moins.","r":["113:4.4","113:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Un ministère qui respecte la volonté humaine","items":[{"q":"Les anges ne forcent pas le sanctuaire du mental humain. Ils ne manipulent pas la volonté des mortels et n’entrent pas non plus en contact direct avec les Ajusteurs intérieurs.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Les séraphins n’ont ni larmes physiques, ni corps, ni ailes, mais ils éprouvent des émotions spirituelles quelque peu semblables aux sentiments humains.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"Ils ne répondent pas directement aux prières, mais agissent sur l’ordre de leurs supérieurs, et ils fonctionnent donc indépendamment des caprices et des humeurs humaines.","r":["113:5.3"]},{"q":"Les séraphins ne sont ni des suzerains ni des directeurs, mais simplement des gardiens.","r":"113:5.4"},{"x":"Lorsqu’une personne trace sa propre route, les anges l’aident à en tirer le meilleur parti possible, n’intervenant qu’en cas d’urgence, et alors généralement sur l’ordre de leurs supérieurs.","r":["113:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Après la mort et dans la carrière ascendante","items":[{"x":"À la mort, le gardien conserve les archives de la personne, les spécifications de son identité et la réalité morontielle de l’âme, et il attend le réveil de son pupille sur le premier monde des maisons.","r":["113:6.1","113:6.2"]},{"q":"L’Ajusteur vous identifiera. L’ange gardien vous repersonnalisera et vous présentera de nouveau au fidèle Moniteur de vos jours terrestres.","r":"113:6.6"},{"x":"Ceux des cercles inférieurs qui n’avaient pas de gardien personnel sont rassemblés par des gardiens de groupe dans les salles de résurrection des sphères des maisons à la fin d’une dispensation.","r":["113:6.7"]},{"x":"Chaque mortel acquiert un gardien permanent avant de quitter les mondes des maisons, et ce gardien reste jusqu’à ce que l’ascendeur soit enseconaphiné pour le départ vers Havona.","r":["113:7.4"]},{"q":"Pour les séraphins, la manière la plus sure d’arriver jusqu’aux Déités du Paradis consiste à guider avec succès une âme d’origine évolutionnaire jusqu’aux portes du Paradis.","r":"113:7.7"},{"x":"Seuls des couples de gardiens de la destinée atteignent l’unité spirituelle et entrent dans le Corps de la Finalité primaire, ou mortel, devenant les compagnons éternels des êtres humains.","r":["113:7.8"]}]}],"see":["Séraphins","Armées angéliques","Ajusteur de Pensée","Mondes des maisons","Mort","Survie"]},{"n":83,"t":"Gouvernement et société","en":"Government and Society","sum":"Government was not designed by anyone; it is an institution that evolved through trial and error in efforts to adjust human antagonisms and keep the peace. The Urantia Book traces its development from the council of elders to modern representative government and names the separation of executive, legislative, and judicial functions as the only sacred feature of government. It teaches that a state can never rise above the moral values of its citizens, and that true world peace will come when a government of all mankind is established.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolutionary Origin of Government","items":[{"x":"Once man had partly solved the problem of making a living, he faced the task of regulating human relations, and private property made government necessary.","r":["70:0.1"]},{"q":"Le gouvernement est un développement inconscient ; il évolue par tâtonnements.","r":"70:0.3"},{"q":"La guerre est l’état naturel et l’héritage de l’homme en évolution ; la paix est l’étalon social mesurant le développement de la civilisation.","r":"70:1.1"},{"x":"Peace groups widened from the family to the clan, the tribe, and the nation, and then to the territorial state, now embracing many nations beyond ties of blood.","r":["70:4.1"]},{"x":"The first organ of government was the council of elders, which already contained the seeds of executive, legislative, and judicial functions.","r":["70:5.2","70:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Rights, Justice, and the Gifts of Society","items":[{"x":"Nature confers no rights on man, and the supreme gift of society to man is security.","r":["70:9.1"]},{"x":"Natural justice is a man-made theory; the only justice nature gives is the unfailing conformity of results to causes.","r":["70:10.1","70:10.2"]},{"x":"Liberty is a gift of civilization made possible by the enforcement of law; for one person to be absolutely free, another must be a slave.","r":["134:6.1"]},{"x":"The chief task of government is to define what is right, regulate class differences fairly, and enforce equality of opportunity under the rule of law.","r":["81:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Representative Government and the Separation of Powers","items":[{"x":"Universe administrators have learned by experience that evolutionary peoples are best governed by representative government with three balanced branches.","r":["70:12.1","70:12.2"]},{"q":"Le seul caractère sacré de tout gouvernement humain est la division de l’État en trois domaines, ceux des fonctions exécutive, législative et judiciaire.","r":"71:8.1"},{"x":"Mortals must create their own government and constitution and choose the ablest and most worthy as their leaders and judges.","r":["70:12.5"]},{"q":"Bien que la démocratie soit un idéal, elle est un produit de la civilisation et non de l’évolution.","r":"71:2.1"},{"x":"Democracy carries dangers such as the glorification of mediocrity, the choice of ignorant rulers, and enslavement to public opinion.","r":["71:2.2","71:2.6"]},{"x":"Educating public opinion is the only safe way to accelerate civilization, and voting is the right method even when doing the wrong thing.","r":["71:2.7","71:2.8"]}]},{"h":"The Ideal State","items":[{"x":"What the state does matters more than its form of government, and no state can rise above the moral values of its citizens.","r":["71:3.1"]},{"x":"The ideal state is moved by three impulses: the love loyalty born of realizing brotherhood, wise patriotism, and cosmic insight.","r":["71:3.3","71:3.6"]},{"q":"Le meilleur État est celui qui coordonne le plus en gouvernant le moins.","r":"71:3.9"},{"x":"In advanced states political service is honored as the highest devotion of the citizen, and public office is regarded as an honor, not a burden.","r":["71:3.10","71:3.12"]},{"x":"An enduring state is founded on culture, ruled by ideals, and motivated by service, and its education aims at wisdom and spiritual values.","r":["71:7.1","71:7.2"]},{"x":"An economy of profit motivation alone is doomed unless supplemented by service motives, yet it must not be abolished suddenly before higher motives are established.","r":["71:6.1","71:6.3"]},{"x":"A continental nation on a neighboring planet, with a federation of one hundred states and a three-branch representative government, has a society more advanced than Urantia's.","r":["72:2.1","72:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Sovereignty and World Peace","items":[{"x":"Relative sovereignty exists on only two levels, the spiritual free will of the individual and the collective sovereignty of mankind as a whole; all groups between are temporary.","r":["134:5.2"]},{"q":"La souveraineté globale empêchera les guerres globales — rien d’autre ne peut le faire.","r":"134:6.4"},{"x":"Even if all weapons were abolished, nations clinging to the illusion of national sovereignty would fight with fists and stones.","r":["134:6.6"]},{"x":"The Most Highs rule in the kingdoms of men to bring about the greatest good for all men, not for any chosen people.","r":["134:5.3","134:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Believer and the State","items":[{"x":"Sonship in the kingdom should make believers better citizens of earthly nations, and believers bear a twofold duty to God and to man.","r":["178:1.4","178:1.5"]},{"x":"Believers must not worship temporal rulers nor try to extend the spiritual kingdom by temporal power.","r":["178:1.6"]},{"x":"The persistent spread of the gospel will in time separate politics from religion and bring intellectual and religious liberty to all peoples.","r":["178:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Civilisation","Mariage et famille","Fraternité des hommes","Justice","Service","Royaume des cieux"]},{"n":13,"t":"Grand univers et maitre univers","en":"Grand and Master Universe","sum":"Le maitre univers est la totalité de la création, constituée de six niveaux d’espace elliptiques et concentriques centrés sur le Paradis : Havona, les sept superunivers et les quatre niveaux d’espace extérieur. La partie actuellement organisée et habitée, Havona et les sept superunivers, s’appelle le grand univers. De vastes créations futures prennent dès maintenant forme dans l’espace extérieur, et les ascendeurs du grand univers parachevé semblent destinés à y servir dans les temps à venir.","sections":[{"h":"Grand univers et maitre univers","items":[{"x":"L’univers central et divin, avec les sept superunivers qui l’entourent, s’appelle le grand univers : c’est la création actuellement organisée et habitée.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"Le maitre univers comprend, outre le grand univers, les univers de l’espace extérieur, encore inhabités et en cours d’organisation.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"Urantia appartient à l’univers local de Nébadon, Nébadon au septième superunivers, Orvonton, et les sept superunivers tournent autour de l’univers central de Havona.","r":["0:0.5","12:1.12"]},{"x":"Le grand univers a un potentiel évolutionnaire d’environ sept-mille milliards de planètes habitées, mais ses bords irréguliers sont encore inachevés.","r":["12:1.13"]},{"q":"To created beings the master universe might appear to be almost infinite, but it is far from finished","r":"12:0.3"}]},{"h":"Six niveaux d’espace","items":[{"x":"Le maitre univers n’est ni un plan infini ni un cercle sans fin ; il fonctionne comme une seule unité d’espace coordonnée, avec des dimensions et des limites définies.","r":["12:1.1"]},{"x":"En partant du Paradis vers l’extérieur se trouvent Havona, les sept superunivers et quatre niveaux d’espace extérieur, disposés en ellipses concentriques.","r":["12:1.3","12:1.9"]},{"q":"The Paradise-Havona System, the eternal universe encircling the eternal Isle, constitutes the perfect and eternal nucleus of the master universe","r":"12:1.11"},{"x":"Entre les niveaux d’espace se trouvent des zones de calme relatif, et les niveaux successifs tournent alternativement en sens opposés, ce qui équilibre les tensions de gravité.","r":["11:7.7","12:4.15"]},{"q":"The central universe is the creation of eternity; the seven superuniverses are the creations of time","r":"12:1.16"},{"x":"Les quatre niveaux d’espace extérieur sont destinés à extérioriser-évoluer l’ultimité de la création.","r":["12:1.16"]}]},{"h":"Les créations futures de l’espace extérieur","items":[{"x":"Le premier niveau d’espace extérieur est une vaste zone d’activité énergétique qui commence à environ cinq-cent-mille années-lumière au-delà de la périphérie du grand univers et s’étend sur plus de vingt-cinq millions d’années-lumière.","r":["12:1.14"]},{"x":"L’espace situé au-delà des sept superunivers est considéré comme étant en grande partie le domaine de l’Absolu Non Qualifié, et ses énergies sont transmuées par les organisateurs de force du Paradis.","r":["12:2.1","12:2.4"]},{"x":"L’énergie et la matière de l’espace extérieur représentent déjà de nombreuses fois la masse totale des sept superunivers, mais aucun être matériel ni aucun ange connus n’y vivent.","r":["12:2.4","12:2.5"]},{"x":"Environ quatre-vingt-quinze pour cent de la gravité absolue du Paradis sont actuellement occupés à maintenir des systèmes matériels au-delà des frontières des univers actuellement organisés.","r":["12:3.8"]},{"x":"La gravité spirituelle opère presque entièrement dans le grand univers, de sorte que les univers extérieurs semblent encore non spirituels, tandis qu’environ quinze pour cent de la gravité mentale agissent hors du grand univers.","r":["12:3.9","12:3.10"]},{"q":"Une plus grande création future est en cours de formation.","r":"12:2.5"}]},{"h":"L’espace et le temps en expansion","items":[{"x":"La création physique de tout l’espace pénétré se dilate actuellement de manière uniforme vers l’extérieur, selon le cycle de respiration de l’espace d’environ deux milliards d’années.","r":["12:4.12"]},{"x":"Les vitesses apparentes de récession des univers lointains ne sont pas réelles, mais proviennent de plusieurs facteurs d’erreur, tels que les angles d’observation et les distorsions de temps-espace.","r":["12:4.14"]},{"x":"L’espace prend naissance au Paradis, mais il n’est pas infini, et le temps et l’espace ne sont inséparables que dans les créations spatiotemporelles des sept superunivers.","r":["12:5.2","12:5.3"]},{"q":"Il n’y a absolument rien de stationnaire dans le maitre univers excepté le centre même de Havona, l’éternelle Ile du Paradis, le centre de gravité.","r":"12:4.1"}]},{"h":"La sollicitude qui embrasse le tout","items":[{"x":"Les besoins de tout le maitre univers dépendent des Absolus pour le potentiel, de l’Ultime pour la direction, du Suprême pour la coordination évolutionnaire et des Architectes du Maitre Univers pour l’administration initiale.","r":["12:6.8","12:6.12"]},{"x":"Les Architectes absonites dressent les plans, les Créateurs Suprêmes les font exister et l’Être Suprême en achève la plénitude.","r":["106:3.1"]},{"x":"La miséricorde est l’attitude de Dieu envers l’individu et l’équité son attitude envers le tout, et la volonté de Dieu finit par prévaloir dans tout l’univers des univers.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"x":"Le temps et l’espace sont un mécanisme cosmique qui permet aux créatures finies d’exister dans le cosmos avec l’Infini.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"On croit que les nouvelles créations de l’espace extérieur seront le futur champ d’activité des Corps de la Finalité en voie de rassemblement.","r":["12:2.6"]},{"x":"Dans les âges futurs, les sept superunivers semblent destinés à devenir les écoles intermédiaires des êtres de l’espace extérieur, et Havona leur école de perfectionnement.","r":["14:6.41"]},{"q":"À ce moment futur de l’éternité, le maitre univers paraitra encore jeune ; en vérité, il sera toujours jeune en face des possibilités illimitées de l’éternité sans fin.","r":"106:7.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Les sept superunivers","Paradis","Dieu l’Ultime","Corps de la Finalité","Temps et espace"]},{"n":18,"t":"Gravité","en":"Gravity","sum":"La gravité est l’emprise toute-puissante par laquelle la présence physique du Paradis tient les mondes de tout l’espace. Il y a dans l’univers quatre circuits absolus : la gravité de personnalité du Père, la gravité spirituelle du Fils, la gravité mentale de l’Acteur Conjoint et la gravité cosmique de l’Ile du Paradis, et ils opèrent indépendamment du temps et de l’espace. La matière est tenue par la gravité du Paradis et par la gravité linéaire, mais plus un mental humain devient spirituel, moins il réagit à la gravité matérielle et plus il est attiré vers le Paradis par la gravité spirituelle.","sections":[{"h":"L’emprise toute-puissante du Paradis","items":[{"q":"La gravité est l’emprise toute-puissante de la présence physique du Paradis.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"Le centre de la gravité matérielle absolue est l’Ile du Paradis, complétée et équilibrée par les corps obscurs de gravité qui encerclent Havona et par les réservoirs d’espace situés au-dessus et au-dessous.","r":["11:8.2"]},{"x":"Le Contrôleur Universel est potentiellement présent dans les circuits de gravité de l’Ile du Paradis, et cette présence atteint toutes les parties de l’univers au même degré, selon la masse.","r":["3:1.7"]},{"x":"Comme les lignes de gravité venues des extrémités de la création convergent vers la demeure du Père, un chaos universel s’ensuivrait instantanément s’il quittait ce lieu.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"x":"Chaque nouvel univers exige un nouvel ajustement de la gravité, mais le pouvoir de contrôle du Paradis suffit même pour un univers infini.","r":["3:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Les quatre circuits absolus","items":[{"x":"Il y a dans l’univers quatre circuits absolus : la gravité de personnalité du Père, la gravité spirituelle du Fils, la gravité mentale de l’Acteur Conjoint et la gravité cosmique de l’Ile du Paradis, et le Père agit par chacun d’eux.","r":["12:3.1","12:3.5"]},{"q":"Ce sont des circuits absolus de présence, et à l’instar de Dieu ils sont indépendants du temps et de l’espace.","r":"12:3.6"},{"x":"Toute gravité est mise en circuit dans l’Ile du Paradis, tout mental dans l’Acteur Conjoint, tout esprit dans le Fils Éternel et toute personnalité dans la présence personnelle du Père.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"De même que le Père attire toute personnalité et le Fils toute réalité spirituelle, l’Acteur Conjoint exerce un pouvoir d’attraction sur tout mental.","r":["9:6.2"]},{"x":"L’action de la gravité de personnalité est toujours un acte volitif du Père Universel, et la réalité qui réagit à son circuit ne peut être mesurée.","r":["9:6.4","12:3.12"]}]},{"h":"Les stades de la gravité physique","items":[{"x":"La gravité absolue est la gravité du Paradis, tandis que la gravité locale ou linéaire appartient au stade électrique de l’énergie et de la matière.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"L’énergie réagit à la gravité du Paradis en trois stades : prégravité (force), gravité (énergie) et postgravité (pouvoir d’univers).","r":["11:8.4","11:8.5","11:8.7"]},{"x":"La gravité linéaire devient pleinement opérante lorsqu’apparait l’organisation atomique de la matière, tandis que les ultimatons non combinés ne réagissent qu’à la gravité circulaire du Paradis.","r":["42:6.2","42:6.3"]},{"q":"La gravité est le seul contrôle de l’énergie-matière.","r":"0:6.11"},{"x":"La gravité linéaire est la force de cohésion à courte portée du grand univers, et l’expression « en raison inverse du carré de la distance » n’est qu’une approximation grossière, à cause de l’influence de l’espace.","r":["42:11.5"]},{"x":"Le zéro absolu théorique n’est jamais réellement atteint en raison de la présence et de l’action de la gravité.","r":["42:4.6"]}]},{"h":"Équilibre et antigravité","items":[{"q":"L’espace ne répond pas à la gravité, mais il agit sur la gravité comme un équilibrant.","r":"11:8.3"},{"x":"L’Esprit Infini possède le pouvoir d’antigravité, que l’on n’observe ni chez le Père ni chez le Fils, et il peut le transmettre à des personnalités supérieures.","r":["9:3.2"]},{"x":"La disposition des niveaux d’espace, qui tournent alternativement en sens opposés, empêche les pressions de gravité de s’accumuler jusqu’à des points destructeurs.","r":["11:7.9"]},{"x":"Les corps obscurs de gravité de Havona, dont les ceintures intérieure et extérieure tournent en sens opposés, stabilisent parfaitement l’univers central.","r":["14:1.15"]},{"x":"Les univers actuellement organisés n’utilisent qu’environ cinq pour cent de la gravité absolue du Paradis ; le reste est occupé à maintenir les systèmes matériels de l’espace extérieur.","r":["12:3.8"]}]},{"h":"La gravité spirituelle et l’ascension","items":[{"x":"La gravité spirituelle est exempte de délai temporel, l’espace ne la diminue pas, et la masse matérielle ne la ralentit pas.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"Les réalités spirituelles réagissent à la gravité spirituelle selon leur valeur qualitative, tout comme la matière réagit à la gravité physique selon sa quantité.","r":["7:1.3"]},{"q":"À mesure que le mental d’une personnalité de l’univers devient plus spirituel — plus semblable à Dieu — il répond moins à la gravité matérielle.","r":"12:8.5"},{"x":"L’action de la gravité physique est la mesure quantitative de l’énergie non spirituelle, et l’action de la gravité spirituelle est la mesure qualitative de l’énergie vivante de la divinité.","r":["12:8.5"]},{"x":"Dans le temps et l’espace, la spiritualité se mesure en raison inverse de la réaction à la gravité linéaire.","r":["42:11.4"]},{"q":"Le circuit de gravité d’esprit tire littéralement l’âme des hommes vers le Paradis.","r":"7:3.2"}]}],"see":["Paradis","Énergie et matière","Fils Éternel","Esprit Infini","Les trois Absolus","Père Universel"]},{"n":12,"t":"Havona","en":"Havona","sum":"Havona est l’univers central éternel d’un milliard de mondes parfaits qui entoure l’Ile du Paradis. N’étant pas un produit de l’évolution, mais un univers créé parfait dès l’origine, il est le modèle de tous les univers, et les mondes de ses sept circuits sont l’ultime terrain d’entrainement que traversent les pèlerins ascendants des univers du temps avant d’entrer au Paradis. Dans sa perfection, sans gouvernement et sans péché, Havona donne satisfaction au Père et aux créateurs, et un émerveillement sans fin aux ascendeurs.","sections":[{"h":"L’univers central éternel et parfait","items":[{"x":"Havona est l’univers parfait et divin situé au centre de toute la création, autour duquel tourbillonnent les vastes créations du temps et de l’espace.","r":["14:0.1"]},{"q":"C’est un univers entièrement créé et parfait ; il ne s’est pas développé par évolution.","r":"14:0.2"},{"x":"Les Fils Créateurs aspirent à reproduire dans le temps et dans l’espace la perfection divine de cet univers modèle.","r":["14:0.2"]},{"x":"Havona n’est ni exactement fini ni absolu ; il sert de tampon entre le Paradis absolu et les créations finies.","r":["105:7.2"]},{"x":"Havona est éternel, mais il n’est pas statique au sens d’une absence de croissance ; dans le présent âge, il connait certains changements progressifs en coordination avec les superunivers en évolution.","r":["105:7.2","106:0.18"]}]},{"h":"Circuits et structure","items":[{"x":"Le milliard de mondes de Havona est disposé en sept circuits concentriques entourant les trois circuits des satellites du Paradis.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"Chaque circuit est imprégné par un Esprit de Circuit, expression spécialisée de l’Esprit Infini, qui coordonne les affaires célestes de ce circuit.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"À l’extérieur se trouvent les énormes corps obscurs de gravité, qui ne réfléchissent ni n’absorbent la lumière et tournent en sens opposés, dissimulant et stabilisant Havona.","r":["14:1.14","14:1.15"]},{"x":"Un jour Paradis-Havona équivaut à près de mille années d’Urantia et sert de temps étalon aux sept superunivers.","r":["14:1.12","14:1.13"]},{"x":"La matière de Havona est organisée en un système énergétique triple, fondamentalement différent du système énergétique double des superunivers.","r":["14:2.2","14:2.6"]},{"q":"If a Urantia mortal could be transported to Havona, he would there be deaf, blind, and utterly lacking in all other sense reactions","r":"14:2.4"}]},{"h":"Des mondes parfaits sans gouvernement","items":[{"q":"Quant au gouvernement de l’univers central, il n’y en a pas.","r":"14:3.1"},{"x":"Chaque sphère de Havona est dirigée par un Éternel des Jours d’origine trinitaire, et elle est développée selon ses propres plans avec une telle originalité qu’il n’y en a pas deux semblables.","r":["14:3.3","14:5.6"]},{"x":"Dans Havona, aucune créature, native ou pèlerine, n’a jamais péché, et aucune âme ascendante n’y est jamais entrée avant son heure.","r":["14:2.9"]},{"x":"La décrépitude et la mort ne font pas partie du cycle de vie de Havona ; les êtres vivants inférieurs changent de forme, mais ne se désintègrent jamais.","r":["14:4.9"]},{"x":"Les natifs de Havona sont des descendants de la Trinité du Paradis sans parents créatures, et, par leur nature même, ils vivent la volonté de Dieu.","r":["14:4.10","14:4.13"]}]},{"h":"L’ultime terrain d’entrainement des ascendeurs","items":[{"x":"Les pèlerins du temps arrivent sur les mondes d’accueil du septième circuit et progressent vers l’intérieur, planète par planète et circuit par circuit, jusqu’à atteindre enfin le Paradis.","r":["14:3.4"]},{"x":"Le pèlerin arrive dans Havona en ne possédant qu’une seule perfection, la perfection de dessein, éprouvée et confirmée.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"q":"L’aptitude à comprendre est le passeport des mortels pour le Paradis. Le consentement à croire est la clef de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"En progressant vers l’intérieur à travers les circuits, le pèlerin atteint successivement l’identité d’un Maitre Esprit, de l’Être Suprême, de l’Esprit Infini, du Fils Éternel et du Père Universel.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"L’expression « cercles de progrès » appliquée au mental humain dérive de cette disposition en circuits de l’univers central.","r":["14:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Un émerveillement sans fin","items":[{"x":"La vie dans l’univers central est si riche et si pleine qu’elle transcende les concepts humains de ce que des êtres créés peuvent éprouver.","r":["14:5.2"]},{"q":"La monotonie ne fait pas partie de la carrière de Havona.","r":"14:5.9"},{"x":"Chacun du milliard de mondes est une véritable université de surprises, et à chaque circuit franchi le pèlerin rencontre des changements insoupçonnés.","r":["14:5.9"]},{"x":"Le gout de l’aventure et la curiosité, souvent réprimés sur terre, sont des dons divins destinés à être pleinement satisfaits au cours des longs âges à venir.","r":["14:5.10","14:5.11"]}]},{"h":"Le dessein de l’univers central","items":[{"x":"Le Père tire de la perfection de Havona une suprême satisfaction parentale et se réjouit de l’adoration de créatures parfaites.","r":["14:6.6"]},{"x":"Havona est le terrain d’entrainement où les Fils Créateurs se préparent à la création d’univers, et chaque Fils Créateur cherche à amener son propre univers à ce niveau de perfection.","r":["14:6.27"]},{"x":"Havona est une révélation de la nature spirituelle parfaite de l’Être Suprême et une préfiguration de son unification future.","r":["14:6.23","14:6.24"]},{"q":"Le Paradis est le foyer, et Havona l’atelier et le terrain de jeu des finalitaires.","r":"14:6.39"},{"x":"Dans les âges futurs également, Havona semble avoir un potentiel illimité en tant qu’univers d’entrainement pour des êtres absonites.","r":["14:6.41"]}]}],"see":["Paradis","Les sept superunivers","Être Suprême","Ascension des mortels","Corps de la Finalité","Grand univers et maitre univers"]},{"n":70,"t":"Joie et bonheur","en":"Joy and Happiness","sum":"True happiness comes from the inner life rather than from wealth or environment, and it is achieved when the selfish desires and the unselfish urges of the indwelling spirit are reconciled in one will. The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and joy is experienced not alone but in sharing love and service. Jesus was not a man of sorrows but a man of gladness, and his peace is the joy and satisfaction of one who does the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"Where Happiness Comes From","items":[{"q":"Le bonheur et la joie prennent origine dans la vie intérieure. On ne peut ressentir tout seul une joie réelle. Une vie solitaire est fatale pour le bonheur.","r":"111:4.7"},{"x":"Happiness is the sum of techniques for gratifying natural urges in better ways, and it does not depend greatly on environment.","r":["140:4.10"]},{"x":"Human happiness is achieved when the desires of the self and the unselfish urges of the higher self, the divine spirit, are coordinated in one will.","r":["103:5.5"]},{"x":"Health, mental efficiency, and happiness arise from the unification of body, mind, and spirit.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"q":"L’effort ne produit pas toujours de la joie, mais il n’est pas de bonheur sans effort intelligent.","r":"48:7.10"}]},{"h":"Spiritual Growth and Lasting Joy","items":[{"x":"The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and spiritual growth yields lasting joy and a peace that passes understanding.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"x":"The Adjuster respects the value of selfish motives but gives weight to the unselfish urges that lead to happiness and the joys of the kingdom of heaven.","r":["103:2.7"]},{"x":"One born of the spirit is released from the bondage of self-denial and translated into the joyous kingdom of the spirit.","r":["143:2.8"]},{"q":"Science yields knowledge; religion yields happiness; philosophy yields unity","r":"101:2.8"},{"x":"There is an inherent joy in freewill existence independent of all external influences, and the angels of the joy of existence strive to demonstrate it.","r":["28:5.16"]}]},{"h":"Happiness as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"The sermon on the beatitudes opened on the keynote of happiness, and its faith and love strengthen character and create happiness.","r":["140:5.6"]},{"x":"A child's happiness is immediate pleasure, but an adult sows seeds of self-denial for greater happiness.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Those who humbly seek God do not wait for distant rewards but experience the happiness of the kingdom in their hearts now.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Asked why some are happier than others, Jesus answered that much depends on willingness to be led by the Father's indwelling spirit.","r":["149:5.1","149:5.2"]},{"x":"Much sorrow comes from thwarted ambition and wounded pride, so after doing one's best one should accept one's lot and exercise ingenuity.","r":["149:5.3"]},{"q":"Seek not, then, for false peace and transient joy but rather for the assurance of faith and the sureties of divine sonship","r":"149:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Joy of Love and Service","items":[{"x":"The new commandment was meant not as a burden but as a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"q":"If you would share the Master's joy, you must share his love.","r":"180:1.5"},{"x":"Jesus showed a fear-ridden young man the paths of service and the highways of happiness that lead to the joy of loving activity.","r":["130:6.2"]},{"x":"Loving service rendered with full affection becomes not a sacrifice but supreme joy.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"After Pentecost the believers broke bread together with gladness and singleness of heart, enjoying the spiritual joy of the brotherhood's fellowship.","r":["194:4.3","190:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, a Man of Gladness","items":[{"q":"Cet homme de Galilée n’était pas un homme de douleurs ; il avait une âme joyeuse.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is neither stoic resignation nor vague optimism but the joy and satisfaction of one who has fully learned how to do the will of God.","r":["181:1.7","181:1.8"]},{"x":"The religion of Jesus does not flee from this life but ennobles present living with the joy and peace of a spiritual state of being.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Morontia life is about half work and half play, and it enjoys the humor of realizing how trivial many past worries were.","r":["48:4.1","48:4.6"]},{"x":"Jesus regarded this world not as a vale of tears but as a vale of soul making, where eternal spirits are born.","r":["149:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Peur et inquiétude","Service","Amour","Croissance","Royaume des cieux","Religion personnelle"]},{"n":62,"t":"Justice","en":"Justice","sum":"Justice is the application of law; it is not the personal attitude of any one Deity but a collective function of the Paradise Trinity. The Ancients of Days and the Trinity-origin Sons render its verdicts, the personalities of the Infinite Spirit supply the evidence, and justice is always tempered by mercy. Man's idea of justice evolved from blood vengeance to the courts of the state, and Jesus taught that justice should be left to the group while the individual shows mercy.","sections":[{"h":"A Collective Function of the Trinity","items":[{"x":"Law issues from the Father, its administration belongs to the Son, its revelation and interpretation to the Spirit, and justice, the application of law, to the Trinity.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"La justice n’est jamais une attitude personnelle, elle est toujours une fonction plurale.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Evidence for fairness is presented by personalities of the Infinite Spirit, and verdicts are rendered by the stationary Sons of the Trinity.","r":["10:6.3","10:6.4"]},{"x":"The Ancients of Days render the decisions of supreme equity in the seven superuniverses, but in perfect Havona this function exists only in theory.","r":["10:6.17"]},{"x":"The Supreme Trinity Personalities represent justice throughout the grand universe and function as the executive judgment of the Trinity.","r":["18:0.10"]}]},{"h":"The Justice and Fairness of God","items":[{"q":"The justice of the Universal Father cannot be influenced by the acts and performances of his creatures","r":"2:3.1"},{"x":"It is futile to plead with God to escape the just results of natural law and spiritual mandates, for one reaps what one sows.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy guides God's attitude toward the individual, while fairness guides his attitude toward the whole.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"q":"La justice est l’idée collective de la droiture ; la miséricorde en est l’expression personnelle.","r":"10:6.18"},{"x":"When fully understood, the righteous justice of the Trinity and the merciful love of the Father coincide as one.","r":["10:6.18","2:4.4"]}]},{"h":"The Execution of Justice and Its Delay","items":[{"x":"The final result for a being wholly identified with sin is annihilation, but its execution is delayed until the appointed processes of justice are fulfilled.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.3"]},{"x":"Between identification with sin and the execution of the sentence there must be time enough to satisfy all concerned, even the sinner himself.","r":["54:3.2","54:3.3"]},{"q":"Il existe, dans l’univers, une loi fondamentale de justice, que la miséricorde est impuissante à tourner.","r":"146:2.5"},{"x":"The seraphic advocate of the courts is the mortal's defender, representing the element of mercy inherent in justice, the fairness that knows motives and tendencies.","r":["39:1.8"]},{"x":"At the adjudication of survival the Memory of Mercy is read, and justice prevails only when mercy has been exhausted.","r":["28:6.6","28:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Justice as It Evolved in Human Society","items":[{"q":"La justice naturelle est une théorie élaborée par les hommes ; elle n’est pas une réalité.","r":"70:10.1"},{"x":"Man's idea of justice is getting his rights; though latent in the spirit-endowed mind, it grew by evolution.","r":["70:10.2"]},{"x":"Primitive society substituted trial by ordeal and blood vengeance for justice, ignoring motive and judging only by the injury inflicted.","r":["70:10.3","70:10.5","70:10.9"]},{"x":"The true administration of justice begins when vengeance is taken from the individual and the kin and given to the state.","r":["70:10.13"]},{"x":"It gradually became clear that the certainty and swiftness of punishment deter crime more than its severity.","r":["70:10.15"]}]},{"h":"Justice as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"q":"Civil government is founded on justice, even as true religion is founded on mercy.","r":"132:4.8"},{"x":"A magistrate's duty is not only to punish the guilty but to acquit the innocent, so that injustice befalls not even the humblest citizen.","r":["132:4.8"]},{"x":"The individual should show mercy, but fixing punishment should be left to groups and their representatives who know all the circumstances.","r":["133:1.2","159:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus possessed a firm sense of justice, but it was always tempered by mercy, and he recognized society's right to punish criminals.","r":["140:8.12","140:8.4"]},{"q":"Ayez la foi — ayez confiance dans le triomphe final de la justice divine et de la bonté éternelle.","r":"140:8.8"}]}],"see":["Miséricorde","Trinité du Paradis","Anciens des Jours","Gouvernement et société","Péché","Bonté"]},{"n":41,"t":"Libre arbitre","en":"Free Will","sum":"Free will is the power of choice that the Universal Father gives together with personality. God himself is the original personality with absolute free will, and man shares that will on a relative and finite level. Especially in matters of eternal survival the mortal's choice holds a sovereignty that no being can invade, so free will becomes the key by which man builds his own destiny.","sections":[{"h":"The Free Will of God","items":[{"x":"God is not an automatic force bound by law but the original personality possessed of free will.","r":["12:7.6"]},{"x":"God's free will is conditioned only by his own divine nature and perfect attributes.","r":["4:4.3"]},{"x":"He shares personality and goodness with his creatures, but infinity of will belongs to God alone.","r":["4:4.4"]},{"x":"Even though God foreknows the acts of his children, that foreknowledge does not abrogate their freedom.","r":["3:3.4","118:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of Choice Given to Personality","items":[{"x":"The two marks that distinguish creature personality are self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5","16:8.6"]},{"x":"Man's relative free will relates to such higher functions as moral decision, spiritual choice, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.13","16:8.14"]},{"x":"The bestowal of personality adds to a living organism the prerogatives of self-determination and self-evolution.","r":["118:7.6"]},{"q":"L’homme mortel est doté du libre arbitre, du pouvoir de choisir ; bien que ce choix ne soit pas absolu, il est néanmoins relativement final sur le niveau fini et en ce qui concerne la destinée de la personnalité qui choisit.","r":"118:6.4"},{"q":"L’homme est vraiment l’architecte de sa propre destinée éternelle.","r":"103:5.10"}]},{"h":"A Will That No One Invades","items":[{"x":"God has decreed that in matters of eternal survival no being or force can interfere with the free will of a mortal.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure;","r":"5:6.12"},{"x":"The Adjuster brings a plan for the ideal life but never arbitrarily moves man's choices; it always respects his will.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"q":"No human being will ever be spiritualized by a divine Monitor against his will;","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Angels, too, do not invade the sanctity of the human mind or manipulate the will, and they have no authority to curtail the prerogatives of choice.","r":["113:5.1"]},{"x":"Even a rebel like Caligastia could not force a normal person to do anything against that person's will.","r":["66:8.6"]}]},{"h":"True Liberty and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"True liberty is the reward of evolutionary progress; false liberty is a subtle deception born of the errors of time.","r":["54:1.2"]},{"q":"La vraie liberté est le fruit de la maitrise de soi ; la fausse liberté est la prétention de s’affirmer soi-même.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty without self-mastery is an illusion, and license masquerading as liberty is the forerunner of bondage.","r":["54:1.5"]},{"x":"The Lucifer rebellion paraded as liberty, but in reality it threatened to rob creatures of their freewill participation.","r":["54:2.3"]},{"x":"Sin arises from an immaturity that, dazzled by freedom of the will, fails to grasp the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Responsibility of Choice and Destiny","items":[{"x":"Energy systems have no choice, but man, by the choices of his free will, has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"The power of choice is both the greatest opportunity and the supreme responsibility, and the Adjuster, the Father, and the Supreme Being depend on its faithfulness.","r":["112:5.5"]},{"x":"On the lower levels the range of choice is narrow, but as one ascends the universe, choice becomes ever freer.","r":["118:7.8"]},{"x":"Choosing the will of God is not the surrender of will but its consecration, enlargement, and perfection.","r":["111:5.5"]},{"q":"the portal of eternity opens only in response to the freewill choice of the freewill sons of the God of free will.","r":"5:6.12"}]}],"see":["Personnalité","Volonté de Dieu","Survie","Ajusteur de Pensée","Péché","Rébellion de Lucifer"]},{"n":93,"t":"Lumière et vie","en":"Light and Life","sum":"Light and life is the final evolutionary attainment of the worlds of time and space, the age in which a planet at last becomes settled after the successive ministries of the divine Sons. In this age the planet flourishes under one language, religion, and philosophy, war and poverty disappear, and many mortals fuse with their Adjusters without passing through death and are translated to the morontia career. This settledness begins with the planet and widens through seven stages to the system, constellation, local universe, and superuniverse.","sections":[{"h":"The Final Goal of Evolutionary Worlds","items":[{"q":"L’ÂGE de lumière et de vie est l’aboutissement évolutionnaire final d’un monde du temps et de l’espace.","r":"55:0.1"},{"x":"An inhabited world passes through the ages of the Planetary Prince, Adam, the Magisterial Son, and the bestowal Son, and is prepared for this age by the ministry of the Trinity Teacher Sons.","r":["55:0.1","52:7.2"]},{"x":"This age begins when the Teacher Sons complete their final mission and continues on that world without end.","r":["55:0.2","55:0.3"]},{"x":"Light and life unfolds in seven stages: planet, system, constellation, local universe, minor sector, major sector, and superuniverse.","r":["55:0.4","55:0.11"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Temple and the New Rule","items":[{"x":"The appearance of the morontia temple at the planetary capital is the certificate that the world has entered light and life.","r":["55:1.1"]},{"x":"At the center of the temple is the shrine of the bestowal Son, flanked by the seats of the Planetary Sovereign and the chief of finaliters.","r":["55:1.2"]},{"x":"The temple is said to \"come down from heaven,\" but in fact it is built on the spot by the morontia power supervisors from designs made at the system capital.","r":["55:1.3"]},{"x":"In this age the Planetary Prince is elevated to Planetary Sovereign, and finaliters who have reached Paradise return to take part in planetary affairs.","r":["55:7.1","55:4.1"]},{"x":"The visible actual rulers are the Material Son and Daughter, and this arrangement has given renown throughout the universe to the idea of king and queen.","r":["55:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Translation Without Death","items":[{"q":"La mort physique naturelle n’est pas inévitable pour les humains.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"Most citizens living in the final era of light and life do not die but are translated directly from the life in the flesh to the morontia existence.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"When fusion is near, the candidate withdraws from duties and, in the morontia temple with family and friends gathered, is translated in a \"flash of life.\"","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"x":"Those who come from such worlds are far better prepared to continue the ascent than those from disordered worlds like Urantia.","r":["55:2.10"]}]},{"h":"Life on a Settled World","items":[{"x":"The world attains one language, one religion, and normally one race, yet it is not perfect, for it still has hospitals, accidents, and senility.","r":["55:3.1"]},{"x":"One first-stage world collected a tenth of its income and spent it on truth, beauty, goodness, and disaster relief.","r":["55:3.2","55:3.6"]},{"x":"Most public offices, education, and judicial work were shared by men and women, and the highest honor was the order of \"supreme service.\"","r":["55:3.8","55:3.9"]},{"q":"La guerre est désormais une histoire du passé ; il n’y a plus d’armées ni de forces de police.","r":"55:5.4"},{"x":"As self-control replaces law, government gradually shrinks, and its extent is in inverse proportion to the morality and spirituality of the citizens.","r":["55:5.4"]},{"x":"Poverty and social inequality all but vanish, and economic life becomes ethical.","r":["55:5.2","55:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Still Mortal","items":[{"q":"Cette grande évolution n’est pas le ciel, mais un avant-gout sublime des mondes divins que l’on rencontrera dans l’ascension vers le Paradis.","r":"55:6.2"},{"x":"Society grows more peaceful, and people become more altruistic and fraternal without losing independence or family love.","r":["55:6.1"]},{"x":"Even on such worlds there is still abundant potential evil to stimulate choice between truth and error, good and evil.","r":["55:3.10"]},{"x":"Communion with the Adjusters deepens from age to age, and the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective.","r":["55:6.4"]},{"q":"Même si la progression éternelle des créatures n’avait pas de futur, les réalisations évolutionnaires superbes des races humaines sur les mondes bien établis d’accomplissements perfectionnés justifieraient amplement la création de l’homme sur les planètes du temps et de l’espace.","r":"55:6.9"}]},{"h":"Urantia and Light and Life","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"q":"Nul monde évolutionnaire ne peut espérer progresser au-delà du premier stade d’ancrage dans la lumière sans s’être rallié à un seul langage, une seule religion, une seule philosophie.","r":"55:3.22"},{"x":"When Urantia reaches that age, Machiventa Melchizedek will assume the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even on an isolated world personal attainment is not thwarted; Jesus of Nazareth personally achieved the status of light and life on Urantia.","r":["55:11.7"]}]}],"see":["Urantia","Fusion avec l’Ajusteur","Corps de la Finalité","Fils et Filles Matériels","Évolution","Être Suprême"]},{"n":79,"t":"Machiventa Melchizédek","en":"Machiventa Melchizedek","sum":"Machiventa Melchizedek was a Melchizedek who incarnated as an emergency Son at Salem in Palestine 1,973 years before the birth of Jesus, at a time when the truth of the one God was dying out after Adam's failure. For ninety-four years he taught the covenant that God's favor is received by faith alone in El Elyon, the Most High, and through Abraham he ensured that this truth would be carried on. He prepared the way for Michael's bestowal and is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","sections":[{"h":"Incarnation of an Emergency Son","items":[{"x":"For thousands of years after the failure of Adam's mission, revealed truth was in danger of extinction, and by about 3000 B.C. the concept of God had grown very dim.","r":["93:1.1"]},{"x":"Machiventa volunteered from among the twelve planetary receivers and made an emergency Son incarnation, one of only six in the history of Nebadon.","r":["93:1.3"]},{"q":"C’est 1 973 ans avant la naissance de Jésus que Machiventa s’effusa sur les races humaines d’Urantia.","r":"93:2.1"},{"x":"He appeared in the tent of the herder Amdon, ate material food for the first time, and that night began to reveal the truth of God's reality.","r":["93:2.1","93:2.2","93:2.3"]},{"x":"He received a Thought Adjuster but never married and could leave no offspring; his body was of the type of the one hundred staff members.","r":["93:2.6","93:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Salem Teachings","items":[{"x":"He founded a school at Salem modeled on the training system of the Sethite priests and was known as \"priest of El Elyon\" and \"the sage of Salem.\"","r":["93:2.4","93:3.1"]},{"q":"Je crois en El Elyon, le Dieu Très Haut, le seul Père Universel et Créateur de toutes choses.","r":"93:4.2"},{"x":"The Salem creed was to believe in the Most High, accept the covenant that he grants favor for faith rather than sacrifice, and keep the seven commandments.","r":["93:4.3","93:4.4","93:4.5"]},{"q":"Tu ne douteras pas que la foi soit la seule condition requise pour le salut éternel.","r":"93:4.8"},{"x":"He permitted no sacrifices at Salem and offered the sacrament of bread and wine in place of blood offerings.","r":["93:4.14"]},{"x":"The three concentric circles symbolized the Paradise Trinity, but most understood them as the three kingdoms of men, angels, and God.","r":["93:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Covenant with Abraham","items":[{"x":"The Melchizedek receivers had long observed Abraham's ancestors, and the family of Terah met their expectations.","r":["93:5.3","93:5.4"]},{"x":"Abraham, who harbored ambitions to become king, won the battle of Siddim despite Melchizedek's dissuasion and then paid him tithes.","r":["93:5.9","93:5.13"]},{"q":"God agrees to do everything; man only agrees to believe God's promises and follow his instructions.","r":"93:6.4"},{"x":"Melchizedek again brought the news that salvation comes by faith, but the Semitic tribes went back to the system of blood sacrifice.","r":["93:6.4"]},{"x":"The covenant was completed after Abraham publicly renounced his personal ambitions, and more than one hundred thousand people were enrolled in the Salem brotherhood.","r":["93:6.7","93:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purpose and Spread of the Mission","items":[{"q":"Il vint accomplir deux tâches : garder vivante sur terre la vérité du Dieu unique et préparer le chemin pour l’effusion ultérieure en tant que mortel d’un Fils Paradisiaque de ce Père Universel.","r":"93:4.15"},{"x":"He taught that another Son of God would come, born of a woman.","r":["93:3.7"]},{"x":"Salem missionaries went beyond Egypt, Mesopotamia, and Asia Minor, reaching Europe and the British Isles.","r":["93:7.1","93:7.2"]},{"x":"Michael appeared on earth and confirmed everything that Melchizedek had taught about the Paradise Father.","r":["93:3.8"]},{"x":"Because Melchizedek's teachings had been lost, few recognized Michael when he came in the flesh.","r":["93:9.10"]}]},{"h":"Departure and Later Career","items":[{"x":"When people began to regard him superstitiously as a demigod, he left suddenly, soon after the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah.","r":["93:8.1"]},{"x":"His disappearance left Abraham with a grief he never overcame for the rest of his life.","r":["93:9.1","93:9.2"]},{"x":"What the Old Testament describes as conversations between Abraham and God were actually conferences between Abraham and Melchizedek.","r":["93:9.7"]},{"x":"For nineteen centuries he worked with the prophets to preserve the truth of Salem, and he is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["93:10.4","93:10.7"]},{"q":"This is the story of Machiventa Melchizedek, one of the most unique of all characters ever to become connected with the history of Urantia","r":"93:10.11"}]}],"see":["Melchizédeks","Révélation","Foi","Urantia","Effusion de Jésus","Adam et Ève"]},{"n":67,"t":"Mal","en":"Evil","sum":"Evil is not created by God; it is the shadow cast when immature creatures in an imperfect finite world reject the light or choose wrongly. Evil is the unintended transgression of the Father's will and so differs from sin; when deliberately embraced, it becomes sin. Potential evil is necessary for free will and moral choice, but actual evil need not be experienced, and God brings ultimate good even out of the evil of time.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Evil","items":[{"x":"God is so positively good that there is no room for negative evil in him, and he does not create evil.","r":["130:1.5","54:0.2"]},{"q":"Le mal est l’inévitable obscurité qui suit de près le rejet malavisé de la lumière.","r":"130:1.5"},{"q":"« Le mal est la transgression inconsciente ou involontaire de la loi divine, de la volonté du Père.","r":"148:4.3"},{"x":"Evil is a partial realization of, or maladjustment to, universe reality and indicates a deficiency of wisdom.","r":["67:1.4","67:1.5"]},{"x":"Evil is the misapplication of plans and the maladjustment of techniques, producing universe disharmony and planetary confusion.","r":["75:4.3"]}]},{"h":"A Relative Shadow","items":[{"q":"Le mal est un concept de relativité. Il nait de l’observation des imperfections qui apparaissent dans l’ombre projetée par un univers fini de choses et d’êtres quand ce cosmos obscurcit la lumière vivante de l’expression universelle des réalités éternelles de l’Un Infini.","r":"130:4.13"},{"x":"Evil arises from observing the imperfections in the shadow cast when a finite universe obscures the living light of the Infinite.","r":["130:4.13"]},{"x":"Error is the inevitable shadow of incompleteness cast upon the ascending path toward Paradise perfection, not an actual universe quality.","r":["130:4.11"]},{"x":"For relative good to appear, contrast with comparative evil, an imperfection that is not sin, is always necessary.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"Ascending the universe scale, goodness increases and evil decreases, but the possibility of experiencing evil remains until final spirit levels are attained.","r":["132:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Free Will and Potential Evil","items":[{"x":"For evolving man to be free he must be able to err; the only world without the possibility of error is one without free intelligence.","r":["3:5.15"]},{"x":"By giving the power to choose between truth and error, the Father created potential negation, but evil actually exists only when creatures choose it.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"q":"La possibilité du mal est nécessaire au choix moral, mais l’actualisation du mal ne l’est pas.","r":"132:2.10"},{"x":"The finite mind's imperfect comprehension of the infinite is itself potential evil; when it is not corrected and error grows, it becomes actual evil.","r":["130:4.14"]},{"x":"Evil deliberately chosen becomes sin, and the persistent pursuit of sin and error becomes iniquity.","r":["54:0.2","130:1.6"]}]},{"h":"How Evil Appears","items":[{"q":"evil always results when purely personal evaluations are elevated to the levels of absolutes.","r":"100:1.1"},{"q":"Le mal est une créativité partielle qui tend vers la désintégration et, en fin de compte, vers la destruction.","r":"111:4.11"},{"x":"All inner conflict is evil because it inhibits the creative function; it is a kind of civil war within the personality.","r":["111:4.11"]},{"x":"Suffering is latent in evil, but much suffering has come from sin and iniquity, and the Father does not send suffering as punishment.","r":["148:5.3"]},{"x":"Man should not blame God for the results of his own choices but should overcome earthly suffering through intelligent effort.","r":["148:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom That Permits Evil","items":[{"x":"For creatures to be truly free, the possibility of evil and sin is unavoidable, and the rulers do not deprive any being of freedom.","r":["54:3.1"]},{"x":"The Father allows good and evil to grow together, like wheat and tares, until the end of life.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousandfold the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]},{"x":"As wisdom grows through ascension, one better understands how ultimate good arises out of time-limited evil.","r":["54:6.10"]},{"x":"Even man's experience of evil is part of God's unending self-realization in the children of time.","r":["2:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Péché","Libre arbitre","Bonté","Rébellion de Lucifer","Adversité et épreuves","Sagesse"]},{"n":81,"t":"Mariage et famille","en":"Marriage and Family","sum":"Marriage is human society's institutional response to the biologic fact of bisexuality, and the home is the crowning fruit of that long evolutionary struggle. The Urantia Book says that marriage is not a sacrament but an essentially human institution, yet it teaches that pair marriage and the good home are the roots of civilization's stability and of morality, and the place where the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man are first learned.","sections":[{"h":"The Origin and Social Meaning of Marriage","items":[{"x":"Marriage is not the mating instinct itself but the institutional reaction society developed to regulate that instinct.","r":["82:1.1","82:3.1"]},{"q":"Le mariage a donné le foyer à l’humanité, et le foyer est la gloire qui couronne toute la longue et opiniâtre lutte évolutionnaire.","r":"82:0.1"},{"x":"Marriage always has an outer domain regulated by mores and law and a private, personal domain between man and woman.","r":["82:3.2"]},{"x":"Marriage has always been bound up with property and religion: property stabilized marriage, and religion moralized it.","r":["82:4.1"]},{"x":"Material necessity founded marriage, sex appetite embellished it, religion sanctioned it, and love later came to justify it.","r":["84:0.1"]},{"x":"Intelligently adjusting the strong sex urge to social regulation is the supreme test of the reality of civilization, and it always demands self-control.","r":["82:1.10"]}]},{"h":"Monogamy and Pair Marriage","items":[{"x":"Monogamy is not natural to evolving man at first, but it has great cultural value and is unquestionably best for the children.","r":["83:6.1","83:6.2"]},{"q":"La monogamie a toujours été le but idéaliste de l’évolution sexuelle humaine ; elle l’est encore et le sera toujours.","r":"83:6.6"},{"x":"The ideal of pair marriage entails self-denial, so it often fails when the partners lack rugged self-control.","r":["83:6.6"]},{"x":"Monogamy fosters delicate sentiments, refinement of moral character, and spiritual growth, and is best for the happiness of parents and the welfare of children.","r":["83:6.7","83:6.8"]},{"x":"Society should not ignore the plight of those who fail to obtain mates but should always treat them with kindness and consideration.","r":["83:6.4","83:6.5"]}]},{"h":"A Human Institution, Not a Sacrament","items":[{"q":"Marriage which culminates in the home is indeed man's most exalted institution, but it is essentially human","r":"83:8.1"},{"x":"Comparing the union of husband and wife to the relation of the Adjuster and man, or to a divine union, is an unfortunate analogy that has caused great confusion.","r":["83:8.2","83:8.3"]},{"x":"The very fact that marriage can be dissolved shows that God is not a party to the union.","r":["83:8.4"]},{"x":"Yet there is an ideal of marriage on the high spheres, embodied supremely by the Material Sons and Daughters; ideal mortal marriage is humanly sacred.","r":["83:8.5"]},{"x":"The marriage ideals of youth should not be crushed, but they should be balanced by learning the realities of home life beforehand, with a degree of disillusionment.","r":["83:8.6","83:8.7"]}]},{"h":"The Home, Chief Civilizing Agency","items":[{"x":"Religious, social, and educational institutions are needed, but since children learn most essentials of life from home and neighborhood, the home is the chief civilizing agency.","r":["82:0.2","82:0.3"]},{"q":"Le mariage est la mère de toutes les institutions humaines, car il conduit directement à la fondation et à l’entretien du foyer, qui est la base structurelle de la société.","r":"84:6.8"},{"q":"Si les familles sont bonnes, la société est également bonne.","r":"84:7.1"},{"x":"Man and woman can never fully understand each other, but they complement each other effectively, and their differences continue into the morontia and spirit careers.","r":["84:6.3","84:6.6","84:6.7"]},{"x":"Marriage is now passing beyond the stage that regarded the wife as property into a new era that respects personality.","r":["84:7.3","84:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Parents, Children, and the Spiritual Meaning of the Home","items":[{"x":"Bearing children is not a parental right but the supreme responsibility of human existence; civilization places duties on parents and rights on children.","r":["84:7.25","84:7.26"]},{"x":"The home is the basic unit of brotherhood, where parents and children together learn the patience, altruism, tolerance, and forbearance that brotherhood requires.","r":["84:7.28"]},{"x":"Society would be greatly improved by returning to the practice of the family council, as among the Andites, where family affairs were discussed freely and fraternally.","r":["84:7.29"]},{"q":"La vie de famille est le berceau de la vraie moralité, l’ancêtre de la fidélité consciente au devoir.","r":"84:7.30"},{"x":"Jesus said the gospel of the kingdom would be better received when understood in family terms, as the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that the true family rests on seven facts: existence, safety and pleasure, education, discipline, companionship, love and mercy, and provision for the future.","r":["142:7.5","142:7.11"]},{"x":"After Joseph's death the young Jesus made the support of the family his first duty and acted as a father to his brothers and sisters.","r":["126:3.2","126:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Threats to the Home","items":[{"x":"The greatest threat to family life is the modern pleasure mania that pursues self-gratification.","r":["84:8.1"]},{"q":"Les plaisirs physiques ne peuvent satisfaire la soif de l’âme ; la poursuite malavisée du plaisir n’augmente pas l’amour du foyer et des enfants.","r":"84:8.4"},{"x":"Wholesome play and recreation have value, but pleasure that brings the breakup of marriage and the home is self-destructive.","r":["84:8.5","84:8.6"]},{"x":"Attempts to shift parental responsibility to the state or the church would be suicidal to the welfare and progress of civilization.","r":["84:7.27"]}]}],"see":["Civilisation","Moralité","Fraternité des hommes","Amour","Fils et Filles Matériels","Gouvernement et société"]},{"n":29,"t":"Médians","en":"Midwayers","sum":"Les médians, ou créatures médianes, sont des êtres natifs de la planète qui existent sur un niveau situé à mi-chemin entre les mortels et les anges. Sur Urantia, les médians primaires sont issus de l’état-major corporel du Prince Caligastia, et les médians secondaires des enfants uniques d’Adamson et de Ratta. Beaucoup se sont égarés lors de la rébellion, mais les loyaux, en tant que Médians Unis, assistent les séraphins et gardent la mémoire de la planète ; lorsque viendra l’âge de lumière et de vie, ils entreprendront la carrière du Paradis en tant que fils ascendants de Dieu.","sections":[{"h":"Des êtres entre l’homme et l’ange","items":[{"x":"On les appelle créatures médianes parce qu’ils fonctionnent sur un niveau de vie situé entre les mortels et les ordres angéliques, et ils apparaissent sur la plupart des planètes habitées et sur toutes les planètes décimales.","r":["77:0.1","38:9.2"]},{"x":"Ils ne sont pas un accident de l’évolution, mais une partie essentielle d’un plan préétabli par les architectes de l’univers et conçu par les Porteurs de Vie.","r":["38:9.5"]},{"x":"Ils relèvent d’une triple classification : fils ascendants par leur origine, citoyens pratiquement permanents en fait, et comptés parmi les esprits tutélaires du temps par leur fonction.","r":["38:9.1"]},{"q":"Midwayers are not men, neither are they angels, but secondary midwayers are, in nature, nearer man than angel","r":"77:8.4"},{"q":"Le vide entre le monde matériel et le monde spirituel est parfaitement comblé par la série d’associations : homme mortel, médian secondaire, médian primaire, chérubin morontiel, chérubin de phase médiane et séraphin.","r":"38:9.9"}]},{"h":"L’origine des médians primaires","items":[{"q":"It was immediately discovered that a creature of this order, midway between the mortal and angelic levels, would be of great service in carrying on the affairs of the Prince's headquarters,","r":"77:1.3"},{"x":"La permission fut accordée aux couples de l’état-major corporel du Prince Caligastia, et les cinquante premiers naquirent, suivis avec le temps par le corps originel de cinquante-mille.","r":["77:1.3","77:1.4"]},{"x":"En tant que corps de renseignement de l’administration du Prince, ils étudièrent les races du monde et contribuèrent à influencer les sociétés humaines éloignées du siège.","r":["77:1.6"]},{"x":"Lors de la rébellion planétaire, 40 119 des cinquante-mille originels se joignirent à la sécession de Caligastia.","r":["77:7.1"]},{"x":"Les médians primaires loyaux entrèrent au service des administrateurs provisoires Melchizédeks, et leur chef, le premier 1-2-3, tint bon aux côtés de Van et d’Amadon le jour de la rébellion.","r":["77:1.7","77:9.5"]}]},{"h":"L’origine des médians secondaires","items":[{"x":"Les médians secondaires sont issus des enfants d’Adamson, fils ainé d’Adam et Ève, et de Ratta, dernière descendante de lignée pure de l’état-major du Prince.","r":["77:5.1","77:5.5"]},{"x":"Seize enfants uniques d’Adamson, formant huit couples, produisirent chacun un médian secondaire tous les soixante-dix jours, jusqu’à ce qu’ils soient 1 984 au total.","r":["77:6.2","77:6.4"]},{"q":"Un tel phénomène n’avait jamais été possible sur terre avant cette époque et ne s’est jamais reproduit depuis lors.","r":"77:6.2"},{"x":"Après la mort d’Adamson, les médians secondaires restèrent à la dérive sans organisation, et 873 d’entre eux, qui ne voulurent pas suivre le gouvernement de Micaël, furent internés lors du jugement de la Pentecôte.","r":["77:6.6","77:7.2"]},{"x":"Avant la Pentecôte, les médians rebelles pouvaient influencer le mental de mortels inférieurs, mais, depuis l’effusion de l’Esprit de Vérité, aucun esprit déloyal ne peut envahir le mental humain.","r":["77:7.5","77:7.8"]}]},{"h":"Le service des Médians Unis","items":[{"x":"À présent, les deux ordres d’Urantia fonctionnent comme un seul groupe de 10 992 membres, gouverné alternativement par le doyen de chaque ordre.","r":["77:8.1"]},{"x":"Ce sont des êtres non matériels qui ne dorment ni ne se reproduisent, mais ils peuvent apprécier l’humour humain et suivre l’adoration humaine.","r":["77:8.3"]},{"x":"Organisés en messagers médians, sentinelles planétaires, personnalités de contact et auxiliaires du progrès, ils servent avec les séraphins planétaires.","r":["77:8.5","77:8.7","77:8.8"]},{"x":"Les médians secondaires peuvent établir un contact physique avec les choses matérielles, et bien des phénomènes littéraux attribués aux anges furent leur œuvre.","r":["77:8.11","77:8.12"]},{"x":"Aujourd’hui, leur tâche principale est d’être les associés non reconnus des hommes et des femmes qui forment le corps de réserve de la destinée.","r":["77:8.13"]},{"q":"Leur détermination ressort de la devise de leur ordre : « Ce que les Médians Unis entreprennent, les Médians Unis l’accomplissent. »","r":"77:9.3"}]},{"h":"Citoyens permanents de la planète et leur destinée","items":[{"q":"The seraphim come and go, but the midway creatures remain","r":"77:9.2"},{"x":"Ils se sont engagés à ne pas quitter la planète avant d’en être relevés par les autorités de l’univers, et ils y demeurent jusqu’à l’âge de lumière et de vie.","r":["77:9.4"]},{"q":"Les générations d’hommes oublient, mais le corps des médians se souvient, et cette mémoire est le trésor des traditions sur votre monde habité.","r":"77:9.9"},{"x":"La civilisation d’Urantia est le produit conjoint des mortels et des médians, et l’écart entre les deux niveaux culturels ne sera pas comblé avant l’âge de lumière et de vie.","r":["77:9.8"]},{"x":"Lorsque la planète atteindra la lumière et la vie, les deux groupes seront relevés du service planétaire, inscrits comme fils ascendants de Dieu, et commenceront l’ascension du Paradis avec leurs frères terrestres.","r":["40:3.1","38:9.13"]},{"x":"Tous les médians secondaires finissent par fusionner avec des Ajusteurs et sont incorporés au Corps de la Finalité mortel.","r":["31:6.2"]}]}],"see":["Caligastia","Adam et Ève","Rébellion de Lucifer","Séraphins","Urantia","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":24,"t":"Melchizédeks","en":"Melchizedeks","sum":"Les Fils Melchizédeks sont l’ordre premier-né de l’univers local, amené à l’existence conjointement par le Fils Créateur, l’Esprit-Mère et le Père Melchizédek. Situés à mi-chemin entre la plus haute Divinité et la plus humble vie de créature, ils peuvent servir les races évolutionnaires sans s’incarner, et ils œuvrent comme éducateurs de l’univers, comme modèle d’autonomie et comme Fils de secours, les premiers à agir lors de toute crise. Les mortels ascendants reçoivent leur enseignement tout au long du chemin, depuis les mondes des maisons jusqu’à l’Université Melchizédek de Salvington.","sections":[{"h":"Les Fils premiers-nés de l’univers local","items":[{"x":"D’une nouvelle union créatrice du Fils Créateur et de l’Esprit Créatif vint d’abord le Père Melchizédek, et, en coopération avec les deux créateurs, il amena à l’existence l’ordre tout entier.","r":["35:1.1","20:1.10"]},{"x":"Les Melchizédeks de Nébadon furent tous créés en l’espace de mille ans du temps standard ; ils forment un ordre qui ne se reproduit pas et compte plus de dix millions de membres.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.9"]},{"q":"These Sons are naturally at the mid-point of the great personality descent","r":"35:2.1"},{"x":"Ils deviennent ainsi les intermédiaires naturels entre l’existence divine supérieure et la vie matérielle, les amis, les éducateurs et les conseillers de tous les êtres intelligents.","r":["35:2.1"]},{"x":"Le Père Melchizédek, premier associé exécutif de Gabriel, préside les commissions de secours et fait fonction de chef exécutif de Nébadon en l’absence de Gabriel.","r":["35:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Un ordre autonome et digne de confiance","items":[{"x":"Les Melchizédeks sont un ordre autonome qui élit ses propres chefs administratifs, première tentative d’autodétermination de la part des êtres de l’univers local.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.2"]},{"q":"not once throughout all the superuniverse of Orvonton have these Melchizedek Sons ever betrayed their trust.","r":"35:2.2"},{"x":"Ils patrouillent l’univers de leur propre initiative et font rapport au Fils Créateur indépendamment des organismes réguliers ; ils fonctionnent aussi comme tribunaux consultatifs de révision qui se déplacent de monde en monde.","r":["35:2.3","35:2.4"]},{"q":"La sagesse des Melchizédeks est à peu près parfaite, mais leur jugement n’est pas infaillible.","r":"35:2.8"},{"x":"Lors de la rébellion de Lucifer, tous les Melchizédeks restèrent loyaux envers Micaël, et sur Panoptia toute la population, sous leur direction, se rangea aux côtés de Micaël.","r":["53:7.4","53:7.1"]}]},{"h":"Éducateurs de l’univers","items":[{"x":"La sphère Melchizédek, monde pilote du circuit de Salvington, et les mondes qui lui sont associés s’appellent l’Université Melchizédek, et chaque mortel ascendant passe par sa formation.","r":["35:3.1"]},{"q":"Pour un ascendeur, ce monde est probablement le lieu le plus intéressant de tout Nébadon.","r":"35:3.11"},{"x":"L’éducation progressive des mortels ascendants dans la carrière morontielle est dirigée sous la supervision générale des Melchizédeks, en association avec les Fils Instructeurs de la Trinité.","r":["35:4.1"]},{"x":"Les Melchizédeks dirigent le grand corps enseignant des mondes des maisons et aident les âmes à y poursuivre les accomplissements qu’elles n’ont pas atteints au cours de la vie dans la chair.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"Sur Jérusem, ils dirigent plus de trente centres éducatifs, formant les mortels ascendants dans des écoles d’administration pour qu’ils assument le gouvernement représentatif.","r":["45:7.3","45:7.4"]},{"q":"Un gouvernement représentatif est l’idéal divin de l’autonomie pour les êtres imparfaits.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"Fils de secours","items":[{"q":"Dans toutes les circonstances de temps et de lieu où le besoin d’une aide spéciale se fait sentir, on rencontre un ou plusieurs Fils Melchizédeks.","r":"35:4.2"},{"x":"Ils sont les premiers à agir dans toute situation critique ; ils servent parfois de gardiens temporaires de planètes égarées ou d’administrateurs provisoires de gouvernements planétaires défaillants.","r":["35:4.4"]},{"x":"Sept fois dans Nébadon, un Melchizédek a servi un monde évolutionnaire dans la similitude de la chair mortelle, Melchizédek de Salem, au temps d’Abraham, étant l’un d’eux.","r":["35:4.4","35:4.5"]},{"x":"Lorsqu’un Fils Avonal part pour une effusion, douze Melchizédeks l’accompagnent en tant que parrains, et ils assistent aussi les Avonals dans leurs missions magistrales.","r":["35:2.6"]},{"x":"Les Melchizédeks coopèrent avec les Porteurs de Vie à l’examen des plans de vie des nouveaux mondes, et le chef des Melchizédeks représente souvent le Fils Créateur.","r":["36:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Urantia et les Melchizédeks","items":[{"x":"Après la rébellion du Prince Planétaire, Urantia fut longtemps administrée par un conseil de douze administrateurs provisoires Melchizédeks.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]},{"x":"Les administrateurs provisoires Melchizédeks avertirent Adam et Ève des dangers du prince rebelle, et environ sept ans après l’arrivée d’Adam ils lui remirent l’administration du monde.","r":["51:3.4","74:5.1"]},{"x":"Lors de sa première effusion, Micaël apparut comme un Fils Melchizédek inconnu et participa au service de secours de cet ordre.","r":["119:1.3","119:1.6"]},{"q":"By universal consent he has become chief of Melchizedeks","r":"119:1.5"},{"x":"On croit que les Melchizédeks sont destinés à rester dans leur univers d’origine et à prendre une part de plus en plus importante au gouvernement et à l’administration de l’univers local.","r":["55:10.11"]}]}],"see":["Machiventa Melchizédek","Fils Créateur Micaël","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Fils Avonals","Mondes des maisons","Univers local de Nébadon"]},{"n":37,"t":"Mental","en":"Mind","sum":"Mind is the gift of intelligence that originates in the Third Source and Center, the Infinite Spirit, and is bestowed upon creatures through the Seven Master Spirits and the local universe Mother Spirit. Mind deals with meanings between energy and spirit; it dominates matter while responding to the leading of spirit. In man, mind is the arena in which he makes his own decisions and chooses God or forsakes him, so the way the mind is used determines eternal survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Mind: The Third Source and Center","items":[{"x":"Creature mind has its origin only in the Third Source and Center, who is the bestower of mind.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"The Conjoint Actor exerts a gravity pull upon all mind, and every true intellectual value and divine thought is drawn into the absolute mind circuit.","r":["9:6.1","9:6.2"]},{"x":"The mind of man is an individualized circuit, an impersonal part, of the cosmic mind bestowed on the local universe by the Creative Daughter of the Infinite Spirit.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"q":"Le Créateur Conjoint est la source du mental, mais le mental n’est pas le Créateur Conjoint.","r":"9:5.5"},{"x":"Mind is absolute on Paradise, subabsolute in Havona, and finite in Orvonton, yet all levels are overspread by the mind-gravity of the Conjoint Actor.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"Levels of Mind and the Cosmic Mind","items":[{"x":"Preadjutant-spirit mind is mechanical, nonexperiencing mind, ministered by the Master Physical Controllers.","r":["42:10.3"]},{"x":"Adjutant-spirit mind is the teachable level ministered by the Mother Spirit through the seven adjutant mind-spirits, and here mind first becomes experiencing.","r":["42:10.4"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is the expanding consciousness of personalities in the ascending career, functioning differentially according to the 570 levels of morontia life.","r":["42:10.5"]},{"x":"The Seven Master Spirits are the sevenfold source of cosmic mind, each distributing mind to one superuniverse, and Nebadon is pervaded by its Orvonton-type modification.","r":["9:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic mind responds unerringly to three levels of reality, causation (science), duty (morality), and worship (religion), and this underlies reflective thinking.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Energy is thing, mind is meaning, and spirit is value; mind establishes relationships between energy and spirit in time and space.","r":["9:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Mind at Work Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"Le mental transmue les valeurs de l’esprit en significations de l’intellect. La volition a le pouvoir de faire fructifier les significations du mental à la fois dans les domaines matériel et spirituel.","r":"9:4.6"},{"q":"L’esprit est l’architecte, le mental est le constructeur, le corps est le bâtiment matériel.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"Mind is ever creative; the liaison of the cosmic mind and the adjutant mind-spirits fashions a body suited to evolving man.","r":["42:12.9","42:12.11"]},{"x":"The universe is planned, made, and managed by mind, but lower minds cannot discern the creative spirit-mind hidden within the universe mechanism.","r":["42:11.2","42:11.8"]},{"q":"Le mental domine universellement la matière, de même qu’à son tour il répond au supercontrôle ultime de l’esprit.","r":"42:12.15"}]},{"h":"The Human Mind: Animal Roots and Moral Insight","items":[{"x":"Human intellect is rooted in the material origin of the animal races, so not all phenomena of mind should be regarded as divine.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"q":"Le mental a vraiment une origine divine et surement une destinée divine, mais votre mental humain n’est pas encore de dignité divine.","r":"9:5.6"},{"x":"Man defiles his mind with insincerity and unrighteousness, animal fear and needless anxiety, and so he should be humble before his immature intellect.","r":["9:5.7"]},{"x":"Only personality knows what it is doing before it does it, and man can exercise scientific, moral, and spiritual insight in advance of experiment.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"To sharpen this inherent cosmic insight is the purpose of education, to ennoble it is the purpose of religion, and to unify it is the purpose of personality.","r":["16:6.11"]}]},{"h":"Mind as the Arena of Choice","items":[{"q":"Le mental matériel est le cadre dans lequel les personnalités humaines vivent, sont conscientes d’elles-mêmes, prennent des décisions, choisissent ou abandonnent Dieu, se rendent éternelles ou se détruisent elles-mêmes.","r":"111:1.3"},{"x":"Mind is a temporary intellectual system lent for the material lifetime, and the way it is used accepts or rejects the potential of eternal existence.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Not what the mind comprehends but what it desires to comprehend, and what it seeks to be like, brings about survival and identification with spirit.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Mind is a cosmic instrument that, according to the will, can sound the discords of destruction or the exquisite melodies of identification with God.","r":["111:1.6"]},{"q":"Le mental est votre navire, l’Ajusteur est votre pilote, la volonté humaine est le capitaine.","r":"111:1.9"},{"x":"Even a personal mind has no survival qualities unless it is identified with spirit; when it lacks the capacity to worship and to crave survival, it is not immortal.","r":["36:5.17"]}]}],"see":["Mental cosmique","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Esprit Infini","Personnalité","Libre arbitre","Âme"]},{"n":19,"t":"Mental cosmique","en":"Cosmic Mind","sum":"Le mental cosmique est le mental septuplement diversifié du temps et de l’espace, que chacun des Sept Maitres Esprits dispense à l’un des sept superunivers. Il est la manifestation, sur les niveaux finis, du mental absolu de l’Esprit Infini ; il atteint les mortels de l’univers local par l’intermédiaire de l’Esprit-Mère et des esprits-mentaux adjuvats, et il dote chaque créature volitive de trois réponses à la réalité : la causalité, le devoir et l’adoration. C’est là que se trouve le fondement de la science, de la philosophie et de la religion, et d’un caractère fort.","sections":[{"h":"Un mental septuplement diversifié","items":[{"x":"Le mental cosmique est le mental septuplement diversifié du temps et de l’espace ; chacun des Sept Maitres Esprits en dispense une phase à un superunivers.","r":["42:10.6"]},{"x":"Les Maitres Esprits sont la source septuple du mental cosmique et le potentiel intellectuel du grand univers, et le mental cosmique est une manifestation subabsolue du mental de la Source-Centre Troisième.","r":["16:6.1"]},{"x":"Le don du mental aux sept superunivers procède des Sept Maitres Esprits, et Nébadon est imprégné par la modification nébadonienne du type orvontonien de mental cosmique.","r":["9:4.3"]},{"q":"Le mental infini ignore le temps, le mental ultime transcende le temps, le mental cosmique est conditionné par le temps.","r":"9:4.4"},{"x":"Le mental cosmique fonctionne différemment dans chacun des sept superunivers, mais il est coordonné dans l’Être Suprême par une technique d’association inconnue.","r":["116:1.4"]},{"x":"Au Paradis, le mental est absolu ; dans Havona, absonite ; et dans Orvonton, fini.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"Par l’Esprit Infini et l’univers local","items":[{"x":"C’est dans le fonctionnement universel du mental cosmique des Maitres Esprits du Paradis que l’on discerne le mieux, dans la création finie, la présence mentale de Dieu.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"Pourtant, le mental de l’ordre humain est un don des filles de l’Acteur Conjoint, les Divines Ministres des univers locaux.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"Les Urantiens vivent sous l’influence de l’Esprit Créatif de Nébadon plutôt que sous l’influence directe d’un Maitre Esprit, mais les Maitres Esprits dominent les réactions fondamentales de tout mental de créature.","r":["16:6.2","16:5.3"]},{"x":"Le mental humain est un circuit individualisé et une partie impersonnelle du mental cosmique conféré à l’univers local par la Fille Créative.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"x":"Le mental cosmique s’étend du ministère primitif des esprits adjuvats jusqu’au mental des plus hauts administrateurs de l’univers, et il est unifié sous la supervision des Sept Maitres Esprits.","r":["56:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Trois réponses à la réalité","items":[{"x":"Dans toute association du mental cosmique avec la personnalité existe une « réponse à la réalité » qui préserve les créatures volitives de devenir les victimes impuissantes des postulats a priori de la science, de la philosophie et de la religion.","r":["16:6.4"]},{"x":"Le mental cosmique répond infailliblement sur trois niveaux de réalité : la causalité (discernement mathématique), le devoir (discernement judiciaire) et l’adoration (discernement spirituel).","r":["16:6.5","16:6.6","16:6.7"]},{"q":"C’est la perspicacité la plus élevée du mental cosmique, la forme révérencielle et adoratrice de la discrimination cosmique.","r":"16:6.8"},{"x":"Lorsque ces trois intuitions sont unifiées dans la personnalité, elles produisent un caractère fort, qui allie une science factuelle, une philosophie morale et une authentique expérience religieuse.","r":["16:6.10"]},{"q":"Le but de l’éducation est de développer et d’aiguiser ces dotations innées du mental humain ; le but de la civilisation, de les exprimer ; le but de l’expérience de la vie, de les réaliser ; le but de la religion, de les ennoblir ; et le but de la personnalité, de les unifier.","r":"16:6.11"},{"x":"Pourtant, trop peu de gens sur Urantia prennent plaisir à cultiver une pensée cosmique aussi courageuse et indépendante.","r":["16:6.9"]}]},{"h":"Mentaux apparentés et personnalité morale","items":[{"q":"Non seulement les esprits apparentés sont attirés les uns vers les autres, mais un mental apparenté à un autre est aussi très fraternel et enclin à coopérer avec lui.","r":"16:6.3"},{"x":"De même que les nébuleuses prennent naissance dans les énergies cosmiques de l’espace, les moi intellectuels prennent naissance dans le mental cosmique.","r":["111:1.2"]},{"x":"Seule une personnalité sait ce qu’elle fait avant de le faire, car elle possède une clairvoyance antérieure à l’expérience.","r":["16:7.3"]},{"x":"La vertu est la droiture en conformité avec le cosmos, et l’on ne connait pas la vertu en la nommant, mais en la vivant.","r":["16:7.6"]},{"x":"La moralité ne peut progresser par la loi ou par la force ; elle doit se répandre par la contagion du contact avec ceux qui exhalent un parfum moral.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"q":"La vertu suprême consiste donc à choisir de tout cœur de faire la volonté du Père qui est aux cieux.","r":"16:7.10"}]},{"h":"Le mental cosmique dans l’ascension","items":[{"x":"La conquête du premier cercle cosmique met fin à l’influence exclusive des esprits-mentaux adjuvats, et le mental se rapproche de plus en plus du mental cosmique et des dotations supra-adjuvates de l’Esprit Créatif.","r":["110:6.21"]},{"x":"Au stade morontiel, le mortel ascendant reçoit la modification nébadonienne du mental cosmique conféré par le Maitre Esprit d’Orvonton.","r":["112:6.4"]},{"x":"En quittant l’univers local et en atteignant les niveaux spirituels, l’ascendeur est accordé au ministère direct du mental cosmique d’Orvonton.","r":["112:6.10"]},{"x":"Chaque fois qu’un mental en évolution s’accorde aux circuits du mental cosmique, l’actualité du Suprême devient d’un pas plus réelle dans l’univers.","r":["117:0.3"]},{"q":"Est-il donc étrange que le mental cosmique soit de façon inhérente consciemment conscient de sa propre source, le mental infini de l’Esprit Infini, et soit en même temps conscient de la réalité physique des vastes univers, de la réalité spirituelle du Fils Éternel et de la réalité de personnalité du Père Universel ?","r":"16:9.15"}]}],"see":["Sept Maitres Esprits","Esprit Infini","Mental","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Être Suprême"]},{"n":88,"t":"Miracles","en":"Miracles","sum":"In the wilderness Jesus decided not to win people's attention and allegiance by miracles and wonders, and he kept that decision to the end. Yet because one with unlimited creator prerogatives was on earth, filled with divine mercy and human sympathy, extraordinary events such as healings sometimes followed apart from his will. The Urantia Book shows that many events that seemed miraculous were in fact natural occurrences, and it explains that even genuine miracles did not break natural law but involved the elimination of the time factor.","sections":[{"h":"The Decision Not to Work Miracles","items":[{"x":"During the forty days in the wilderness Jesus resolved not to use universe power to satisfy the Jewish craving for signs.","r":["136:8.1"]},{"q":"Il refusa de devenir un simple faiseur de prodiges.","r":"136:8.2"},{"x":"Wonder-working only stirs the material mind to outward allegiance; it neither reveals God nor saves men.","r":["136:8.2"]},{"q":"Jesus chose to establish the kingdom of heaven in the hearts of mankind by natural, ordinary, difficult, and trying methods","r":"136:8.6"},{"x":"He did not break this decision even when the Pharisees demanded proof or when he was taunted at Calvary to come down from the cross.","r":["136:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Wine at Cana","items":[{"x":"At the wedding feast at Cana others expected a miracle, but the most surprised of all was Jesus himself, who had resolved not to work one.","r":["137:4.12"]},{"q":"Mais ce ne fut en aucun sens un miracle. Nulle loi de la nature ne fut modifiée, abrogée, ou même transcendée.","r":"137:4.13"},{"x":"The agents of the Creator made wine by the ordinary natural processes, only independently of time.","r":["137:4.13"]},{"x":"It would not have happened had it been contrary to the Father's will, since Jesus had already committed all things to the Father's will.","r":["137:4.14"]}]},{"h":"Events That Were Not Miracles","items":[{"x":"The great catch of fish was no miracle; Jesus, a skilled fisherman who knew the habits of fish, simply told them where the school was.","r":["145:1.3"]},{"x":"The healing of Peter's mother-in-law's fever was not a miracle either, but a miracle-seeking generation counted all such coincidences as miracles.","r":["145:2.16","145:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged the apostles not to attribute ordinary physical events to spiritual causes but to seek the true causes of all phenomena.","r":["164:3.6"]},{"x":"The rabbis regarded blindness from birth as the result of sin, but Jesus rejected such superstitious explanations.","r":["164:3.2","164:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Sundown Healing and Genuine Miracles","items":[{"x":"At Capernaum, when Jesus said he wished his children to be made whole if it was not contrary to the Father's will, 683 persons were healed in a moment.","r":["145:3.9","145:3.10"]},{"x":"Jesus himself was the most surprised by this healing, having momentarily forgotten the warning that he could not limit the time element of creator prerogatives.","r":["145:3.11"]},{"q":"Les guérisons miraculeuses, qui accompagnèrent de temps à autre la mission de Jésus sur terre, ne faisaient pas partie de son plan pour proclamer le royaume.","r":"145:3.15"},{"x":"The cleansing of the leper was the first so-called miracle Jesus performed intentionally.","r":["146:4.5"]},{"q":"Ce fut le premier et unique miracle de la nature que Jésus accomplit après l’avoir sciemment projeté.","r":"152:2.10"},{"x":"When Jesus thanked the Father at the raising of Lazarus, the celestial hosts acted, and Lazarus came to life in twelve seconds of earth time.","r":["168:2.2","168:2.3"]}]},{"h":"What the Miracles Left Behind","items":[{"x":"Of the five thousand fed by the miracle, only about five hundred continued to follow Jesus.","r":["152:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said he would not turn from his mission of revealing the Father to satisfy the curiosity of wonder-seekers.","r":["145:5.6"]},{"x":"The fame of his healings brought prejudice-raising publicity and unsought notoriety, causing Jesus much trouble.","r":["145:3.12","145:3.15"]},{"x":"The resurrection of Lazarus strengthened the faith of believers, but the religious leaders hastened their decision to destroy Jesus.","r":["168:3.1","168:3.4"]}]},{"h":"The Greatest Miracle","items":[{"x":"To local universe citizens there are few miracles, and the most intriguing of them are the incarnational bestowals of the Paradise Sons.","r":["120:4.5"]},{"q":"Jesus of Nazareth was a miraculous person.","r":"120:4.5"},{"x":"Even in all these extraordinary experiences the Father chose to reveal himself in normal, natural, and dependable ways.","r":["120:4.6"]}]}],"see":["Effusion de Jésus","Caractère de Jésus","Foi","Miséricorde","Enseignements de Jésus","Ajusteur de Pensée"]},{"n":61,"t":"Miséricorde","en":"Mercy","sum":"Mercy is justice tempered by wisdom that fully knows the weaknesses and handicaps of creatures. God is merciful by nature and needs no one to persuade him; the Eternal Son is mercy itself, and the Infinite Spirit ministers that mercy throughout the universe. Mercy does not violate justice but applies it with understanding, and man learns true mercy by passing through justice, fairness, patience, and kindness.","sections":[{"h":"Justice Tempered by Wisdom","items":[{"q":"Mercy is simply justice tempered by that wisdom which grows out of perfection of knowledge and the full recognition of the natural weaknesses and environmental handicaps of finite creatures.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"Even divine justice, which lets wrongdoing reap its results, is always tempered by mercy, in proportions determined by infinite wisdom.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy is not a contravention of justice but an understanding interpretation of supreme justice as fittingly applied to evolving finite creatures.","r":["2:4.5"]},{"x":"When eternal justice and divine mercy work together, what man calls fairness emerges in human experience.","r":["2:4.4","10:6.3"]},{"x":"God is not torn between justice and mercy; in his omniscience he fully satisfies both demands at once.","r":["2:4.3","2:6.6"]}]},{"h":"Mercy Flowing from the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"Le besoin des créatures est entièrement suffisant pour que le Père donne libre cours à sa tendre miséricorde et à sa grâce salvatrice.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"Mercy is the natural offspring of goodness and love; a loving father cannot withhold mercy from his children.","r":["2:4.4"]},{"x":"It is an error to think that the Eternal Son pleads with the Father for mercy; all the Son's mercy is a direct revelation of the Father's love.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"God harbors no feelings of wrath or vengeance; such attitudes are inconsistent with the Father's merciful character.","r":["4:3.2","2:6.7"]},{"x":"Even a rebel who turns to righteousness is received in mercy, and God remembers his transgressions no more.","r":["2:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Son Is Mercy, the Spirit Ministers","items":[{"q":"Dieu est amour, le Fils est miséricorde. La miséricorde est l’amour appliqué, l’amour du Père en action dans la personne de son Fils Éternel.","r":"6:3.5"},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit inclines toward the Son's attribute of mercy and becomes the mercy minister of the Paradise Deities throughout the grand universe.","r":["8:2.6","8:4.7"]},{"q":"L’univers de votre origine se forge entre l’enclume de la justice et le marteau de la souffrance, mais ceux qui manient le marteau sont des enfants de miséricorde, la descendance spirituelle de l’Esprit Infini.","r":"9:1.8"},{"x":"Justice is the collective attitude of the Trinity, and mercy is the personal expression of that righteousness.","r":["10:6.2","10:6.18"]},{"x":"Creator Sons are inherently merciful, yet through their bestowal experiences they acquire understanding mercy in a new way.","r":["119:0.4"]},{"x":"Our superuniverse of Orvonton is a demonstration of love and mercy, noted for justice tempered by mercy and power conditioned by patience.","r":["15:14.2"]}]},{"h":"The Record and Limits of Mercy","items":[{"x":"The Memory of Mercy is a living record of the mercy ministry extended to an individual, read as testimony at the adjudication of survival.","r":["28:6.5","28:6.6"]},{"q":"Car la miséricorde n’est pas destinée à être imposée à ceux qui la méprisent ; la miséricorde n’est pas un don à fouler aux pieds par les rebelles persistants du temps.","r":"28:6.7"},{"x":"Yet for one sincere of purpose and honest of heart, the credit of mercy is always far greater than he could ever exhaust.","r":["28:6.7"]},{"x":"When endless mercy and patience are exhausted, justice prevails, and what mercy cannot rehabilitate justice will eventually annihilate.","r":["21:5.7","2:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Mercy as Man Learns It","items":[{"x":"Mercy is a quality of growth: one can be truly merciful only after first becoming just, fair, patient, and kind.","r":["28:6.8"]},{"q":"Il peut y avoir patronage, condescendance ou charité — et même pitié — mais pas miséricorde.","r":"28:6.8"},{"q":"Le ministère de la miséricorde est toujours une affaire individuelle, tandis que la justice et ses châtiments sont la fonction de groupes administratifs de la société, du gouvernement ou de l’univers.","r":"133:1.2"},{"x":"The mercy Jesus spoke of is not passive pity but active and dynamic, the supreme fatherly loving-kindness.","r":["140:5.17"]},{"x":"Disciples are saviors, not judges of men, so they must first show their brothers the mercy they themselves would desire.","r":["140:3.17","140:3.16"]},{"x":"The rule of the kingdom is that mercy determines judgment and love determines conduct, not the reckoning of giving and receiving.","r":["140:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Justice","Amour","Pardon","Fils Éternel","Esprit Infini","Bonté"]},{"n":44,"t":"Mondes des maisons","en":"Mansion Worlds","sum":"The mansion worlds are the seven transition worlds surrounding Jerusem, the capital of the local system, and they correspond to the \"many mansions in my Father's house\" of which Jesus spoke. After death the surviving mortal awakens in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world, makes up the deficiencies left unfinished on earth, and, passing through the seven worlds in turn, becomes less and less mortal and more and more morontial. This is the first school of the ascension, linking the material life with the spirit life.","sections":[{"h":"What the Seven Mansion Worlds Are","items":[{"x":"The \"many mansions\" of which Jesus spoke refer especially to the seven satellites of the first transition world surrounding Jerusem.","r":["47:0.1"]},{"x":"The mansion worlds are in the charge of the morontia supervisors and the Melchizedeks, and each world has an acting governor and headquarters for many groups of ministers.","r":["47:0.4"]},{"x":"When a system is settled in light and life, the mansion worlds one by one cease to serve as training spheres and are taken over by the finaliters.","r":["47:0.3"]},{"x":"The seven worlds are in fact demortalizing spheres: on the first one is still largely human, but by graduation one has become nearly morontial.","r":["47:9.5"]}]},{"h":"Awakening on the First Mansion World","items":[{"x":"At the center of the first mansion world stand the resurrection halls, the temple of personality assembly, where guardian seraphim, Adjusters, and archangels work together.","r":["47:3.2"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivor is resurrected when the morontia soul kept by the seraphim and the spirit-mind held by the Adjuster are reunited.","r":["47:3.3"]},{"q":"Vous commencez là-bas exactement au point où vous en étiez en partant d’ici.","r":"47:3.7"},{"x":"The resurrected one is granted ten days of liberty to explore the new home and look up loved ones who have gone before.","r":["47:3.6"]},{"x":"Morontia companions are assigned to the ascenders as their friendly associates and guides.","r":["47:3.11","47:3.12"]},{"q":"Sur les mondes des maisons, les survivants mortels ressuscités reprennent le fil de leur vie exactement au point où ils l’ont laissée quand ils ont été surpris par la mort.","r":"47:3.1"}]},{"h":"Worlds That Correct Deficiencies","items":[{"x":"The experience of the first mansion world is almost wholly devoted to correcting the defects of character and deficiencies of experience left from the life in the flesh.","r":["47:3.8"]},{"x":"No ascender can escape the experience of rearing children, and fathers must pass through it as surely as mothers.","r":["47:1.6"]},{"q":"Les enfants ont besoin d’un père aussi bien que d’une mère, et les pères ont autant besoin de l’expérience parentale que les mères.","r":"47:1.6"},{"x":"The second mansion world is devoted to removing intellectual conflicts and healing every kind of mental disharmony.","r":["47:4.8"]},{"x":"Whereas the first two worlds give negative training to make up deficiencies, truly progressive morontia culture begins on the third world.","r":["47:5.3"]}]},{"h":"From World to World","items":[{"x":"With each move to a new world one goes to sleep and awakens in a new morontia body, but at these times the Adjuster does not leave.","r":["47:4.4"]},{"x":"Memories of survival value are kept throughout the ascending career because the Adjuster has made counterparts of them.","r":["47:4.5"]},{"x":"In the morontia body one still eats, drinks, and rests, but the food is completely utilized and leaves no residue.","r":["47:4.6"]},{"x":"On the fourth world ascenders first learn true social life, based not on selfish conquest but on mutual appreciation and unselfish service.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"q":"Une véritable naissance de la conscience cosmique a lieu sur maisonnia numéro cinq.","r":"47:7.5"},{"x":"Fusion with the Adjuster is often actually effected on the fifth or sixth world, followed by the declaration, \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":["47:8.3","47:8.4"]},{"q":"Lors de chaque avance d’un monde des maisons à un autre, vous acquérez un corps morontiel nouvellement formé et convenablement approprié.","r":"47:4.4"}]},{"h":"Citizens of Jerusem","items":[{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the remnants of unfortunate heredity and unwholesome environment are cleansed away, and differences of world origin disappear.","r":["47:9.1"]},{"x":"On the seventh world ascenders visit the Father's world and begin a more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]},{"x":"The graduates are sent off in classes from the sea of glass and welcomed as citizens of Jerusem.","r":["47:9.4","47:10.1"]},{"x":"Those who pass through all the mansion worlds experience the adjustment sleep and the resurrection awakening seven times, after which consciousness is never again broken.","r":["47:10.5"]},{"q":"Mortal death is a technique of escape from the material life in the flesh","r":"47:10.7"}]}],"see":["Morontia","Mort","Survie","Ascension des mortels","Fusion avec l’Ajusteur","Constellations et systèmes locaux"]},{"n":65,"t":"Moralité","en":"Morality","sum":"Morality is the capacity unique to human personality to discern right from wrong and to judge the worth not only of means but of ends, and it distinguishes man from the animal. It evolved from self-conscious reason and grows not by law or force but by personal choice and influence. Morality is a prerequisite of religion but not the whole of religious experience, and the highest moral choice is the choice to do the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"The Moral Nature of Personality","items":[{"q":"L’intelligence seule ne peut expliquer la nature morale. La moralité, la vertu, est innée dans la personnalité humaine.","r":"16:7.1"},{"x":"Man can exercise moral insight before exploration or experiment, and only personality knows what it is doing before it does it.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"Intellect only selects means, but a moral being discerns the value of the ends themselves.","r":["16:7.4"]},{"x":"One who cannot discern the goal of his strivings lives on the animal level and has failed to use the advantages of personality.","r":["16:7.5"]},{"x":"A child's first moral choice appears with the seventh adjutant mind-spirit, and only after it is registered is an Adjuster assigned.","r":["108:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Virtue and Moral Choice","items":[{"q":"La vertu est droiture — la conformité avec le cosmos. Nommer des vertus, ce n’est pas les définir, mais les vivre, c’est les connaitre.","r":"16:7.6"},{"x":"Choosing between good and evil is influenced not only by moral keenness but also by ignorance, immaturity, and delusion, so a sense of proportion and the art of measurement are needed.","r":["16:7.7","16:7.8"]},{"x":"Moral conduct is the highest performance of intellect: choosing higher ends and choosing moral means suited to those ends.","r":["16:7.10"]},{"q":"Le choix moral le plus élevé est celui de la plus haute valeur possible, et toujours — dans chaque sphère et dans toutes les sphères — c’est le choix de faire la volonté de Dieu.","r":"39:4.14"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Morality","items":[{"x":"Morality arose from self-conscious reason; it transcends the animal but is wholly evolutionary.","r":["5:5.1"]},{"x":"Through the long and wasteful struggle to placate ghosts, man became conscious of relative right and wrong, and thus ethics was born.","r":["86:6.7","68:4.3"]},{"x":"Early feelings of duty grew out of emotional fear, but the urge to unselfish service comes from the indwelling divine spirit.","r":["103:5.1"]},{"q":"Conscience is not a divine voice speaking to the human soul.","r":"92:2.6"},{"x":"Static ethics and traditional morality are only slightly above the animal level; ethics becomes truly human when it is dynamic and progressive.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Morality and Religion","items":[{"q":"La conduite morale précède toujours la religion évolutionnaire, et elle fait même partie de la religion révélée, mais elle n’est jamais la totalité de l’expérience religieuse.","r":"5:5.4"},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion draws them by a loving desire to be like God.","r":["5:4.1"]},{"x":"As religion evolves, ethics becomes the philosophy of morals, and morality becomes the discipline of self by the standards of supreme spiritual ideals.","r":["92:7.5"]},{"x":"A religion that stresses an isolated morality apart from truth and beauty fails to win the loyalty of modern people.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus did not put ethics in the place of religion; he taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]}]},{"h":"How Morality Grows and Spreads","items":[{"q":"On ne peut jamais faire progresser la moralité par la loi ou par la force.","r":"16:7.9"},{"x":"Morality is a matter of the personality's free will and must spread by the contagion of contact with morally fragrant persons.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus interpreted the golden rule on the levels of the flesh, feelings, mind, brotherly love, morality, and spirit, teaching at the highest to treat people as God would treat them.","r":["147:4.3","147:4.8","147:4.9"]},{"x":"Primitive man's neighbor was only those near him, but Jesus extended the neighbor to all mankind and even to enemies, and the human heart knows this is right.","r":["103:5.2"]},{"x":"In the ages of philosophy and brotherhood people become truly moral beings and learn to live by the golden rule.","r":["50:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Bonté","Libre arbitre","Volonté de Dieu","Expérience religieuse","Sagesse","Péché"]},{"n":45,"t":"Morontia","en":"Morontia","sum":"Morontia is the vast intermediate level lying between the material and the spiritual. Since God does not change a mortal of animal origin into a perfect spirit in a single step, the surviving human passes through the many morontia worlds of the local universe and, by hundreds of gradual transformations, reaches the threshold of spirit. The morontia life actually begins on earth when the soul is conceived, and its philosophic insight is called mota.","sections":[{"h":"A Level Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"La chaine du tissu morontiel est spirituelle, sa trame est matérielle.","r":"0:5.12"},{"x":"Morontia is a broad level of reality that may be personal or impersonal, and may consist of living or nonliving energies.","r":["0:5.12"]},{"x":"The morontia worlds are architectural spheres furnished with one hundred physical elements plus one hundred organizations of energy known as morontia materials.","r":["48:1.3"]},{"x":"Like the \"better and more enduring substance\" of which Paul spoke, morontia material is real and literal.","r":["48:1.7"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is a dual mind in which material and spiritual minds co-operate, governed by a single will.","r":["110:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Why a Morontia Stage Is Needed","items":[{"x":"The Gods do not transform creatures of animal origin into perfect spirits at once by some mysterious magic.","r":["48:0.1"]},{"x":"The belief that the single step of death instantly transforms the mortal mind into a perfected spirit is ignorant superstition.","r":["48:0.2"]},{"x":"A morontia transition always intervenes between mortal state and spirit status, and its purpose is similar in all local creations.","r":["48:0.3"]},{"x":"The morontia career is the transition life between evolutionary material existence and the higher spirit attainment.","r":["47:10.7"]},{"q":"Ces croyances ne sont que des superstitions ignorantes et des fables plaisantes.","r":"48:0.2"}]},{"h":"Morontia Bodies and Gradual Transformation","items":[{"x":"The morontia power supervisors provide 570 successive morontia bodies during the morontia career in Nebadon.","r":["48:1.5"]},{"x":"In mortal life the spirit indwells almost as something separate, but in the morontia life the spirit becomes an actual part of the personality.","r":["48:1.6"]},{"x":"Early morontia life resembles the material worlds, but on the constellation and Salvington it reaches increasingly spiritual levels.","r":["48:1.4"]},{"x":"The body that the risen Jesus bore was also a morontia body: no blood circulated in it and it did not take material food, yet it was real.","r":["190:0.3"]}]},{"h":"Those Who Help the Morontia Life","items":[{"x":"Morontia companions are offspring of the local universe Mother Spirit, friendly associates, guides, and interpreters for the ascenders.","r":["48:3.1","48:3.5","48:3.12"]},{"x":"The mansion world teachers are cherubim and sanobim left behind by their seraphim, and they conduct the schools of thinking, feeling, and doing.","r":["48:5.1","48:5.6"]},{"q":"Il n’existe ni routes royales, ni raccourcis, ni sentiers faciles pour atteindre le Paradis.","r":"48:5.7"},{"x":"The morontia career seeks to eradicate forever such animal vestiges as procrastination, insincerity, and the avoidance of problems.","r":["48:5.8"]},{"x":"Transition seraphim help with the choice of a course, yet they respect the ascender's freewill choices as long as no harm results.","r":["48:6.5","48:6.6"]},{"q":"No act of good is ever wholly lost","r":"48:6.7"}]},{"h":"Mota and the Morontia Progressors","items":[{"x":"Mota is an insight superior to philosophy; as two eyes are to one, it gives stereoscopic depth to meanings and values.","r":["48:6.28"]},{"x":"On the first mansion world mota concepts are taught side by side with the corresponding statements of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"q":"Une âme en évolution n’est pas rendue divine par ce qu’elle fait, mais par ce qu’elle s’efforce de faire.","r":"48:7.24"},{"x":"The morontia life actually begins on earth at the moment the Adjuster comes to indwell and the soul is conceived.","r":["48:6.2"]},{"x":"After graduating from the mansion worlds and until attaining spirit status, the ascender is called a morontia progressor.","r":["48:8.1"]},{"x":"The purpose of this long training is not merely eternal ease but preparation for the transcendent service of future ages.","r":["48:8.3"]},{"q":"Mota is more than a superior philosophy","r":"48:6.28"}]}],"see":["Mondes des maisons","Âme","Ascension des mortels","Mort","Résurrection de Jésus","Philosophie"]},{"n":43,"t":"Mort","en":"Death","sum":"In The Urantia Book death is not an end but a doorway from the material life to the morontia life. For primitive man death was the supreme shock and the greatest fear, and it gave rise to the development of religion; revelation, however, shows that there are three kinds of death, spiritual, intellectual, and physical, and that the surviving soul sleeps and then awakens again on the mansion worlds. On advanced worlds even natural death becomes increasingly rare.","sections":[{"h":"Primitive Man and the Fear of Death","items":[{"q":"La mort était pour les hommes en évolution le choc suprême, la plus troublante combinaison de hasard et de mystère.","r":"86:3.1"},{"x":"Not the sanctity of life but the fear inspired by the shock of death fostered early religion.","r":["86:3.1"]},{"x":"Fearing the ghosts released by death, primitive peoples destroyed the dead person's house and took a different road home from the funeral.","r":["87:1.1","87:1.3","87:1.5"]},{"x":"The concept of a future life, derived from dreams, began to soften the fear of death bound up with the instinct of self-preservation.","r":["86:4.2"]},{"x":"The basic belief of primitive religion was survival after death.","r":["92:6.1"]}]},{"h":"The Three Kinds of Death","items":[{"x":"In relation to personality survival there are three kinds of death: spiritual (soul) death, intellectual (mind) death, and physical (body and mind) death.","r":["112:3.1"]},{"x":"One who has finally rejected survival is, from the universe point of view, already dead, even while the body lives.","r":["112:3.2"]},{"x":"When the mind circuits that make volitional action possible are irretrievably destroyed, the Adjuster departs, and this too is death.","r":["112:3.3"]},{"x":"In physical death the Adjuster remains until the mind ceases to function, then departs for Divinington when the life pulsations of the brain stop.","r":["112:3.4"]}]},{"h":"What Happens After Death","items":[{"x":"The body returns to the elements, but two nonmaterial factors continue: the Adjuster and the morontia soul.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"q":"Upon death the Thought Adjuster temporarily loses personality, but not identity; the human subject temporarily loses identity, but not personality;","r":"112:3.7"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the surviving soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"Those who go to the mansion worlds cannot send messages back to their loved ones on earth; such communication is forbidden.","r":["112:3.7"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the morontia form, the returning Adjuster, and the conserved soul are united, and identity is reassembled.","r":["112:5.16","112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"q":"on the mansion worlds both reunite in eternal manifestation.","r":"112:3.7"}]},{"h":"The Eye of Faith on Death","items":[{"x":"The spirit of adventure and the dread of monotony were placed in man to suggest that death is only the beginning of an endless career of adventure.","r":["14:5.10"]},{"x":"Life after death is not essentially different from mortal existence, and every good thing done now enhances the future life.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"True religion does not foster spiritual sloth through the vain hope of gaining noble virtues merely by passing through the portals of death.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that believers should live as if pursuing their careers with natural death always in prospect.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"q":"and which even now makes certain their resurrection from the bonds of natural death.","r":"190:0.2"},{"q":"La mort n’a rien ajouté aux possessions intellectuelles ni à la dotation spirituelle, mais elle a ajouté au statut expérientiel la conscience de la survie.","r":"48:7.25"}]},{"h":"Worlds Where Death Fades Away","items":[{"q":"La mort physique naturelle n’est pas inévitable pour les humains.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, many fuse with their Adjusters and are translated alive into the morontia state.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"On such worlds a \"funeral\" becomes an occasion not of weeping but of joy, deep satisfaction, and inexpressible hope.","r":["55:2.5"]},{"x":"Less advanced mortals would be helped if they too learned to view natural death with such cheerfulness and lightness of heart.","r":["55:2.6"]},{"x":"Yet even on long-settled worlds there is no system in which natural death as a way of leaving the flesh has wholly disappeared.","r":["55:2.8"]}]}],"see":["Survie","Mondes des maisons","Morontia","Âme","Peur et inquiétude","Lumière et vie"]},{"n":90,"t":"Mort sur la croix","en":"Death on the Cross","sum":"Jesus died on the cross at Golgotha on a Friday in A.D. 30. The Urantia Book makes clear that this death was not an atoning sacrifice to appease the wrath of God or pay mankind's debt; it was not required by the Father but planned and carried out by man. The true meaning of the cross lies not in the fact of his death but in the manner and spirit in which he met it, the supreme expression of a love that forgave even enemies, and so the cross became the eternal symbol of unselfish service.","sections":[{"h":"From the Arrest to Golgotha","items":[{"x":"When he was arrested, Jesus knew his work in the flesh was finished and took little interest in the details of the so-called trials.","r":["186:2.1"]},{"x":"He did not answer false testimony, but he always answered the question whether he was the Son of God.","r":["186:2.2"]},{"x":"Convinced that it was the Father's will for him to follow the natural course of events like an ordinary man, he did not try to change the outcome by his eloquence.","r":["186:2.3"]},{"x":"He was crucified at about half past nine on Friday morning, and the unseen hosts of the universe watched in silence as the Creator underwent a creature's death.","r":["187:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Hours on the Cross","items":[{"q":"Jesus' only words, as they nailed him to the crossbeam, were, \"Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do.\"","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Though thirsty, Jesus refused the drugged wine offered to deaden his suffering.","r":["187:2.3"]},{"x":"Unlike the brigand who mocked him, the other brigand turned wholeheartedly in his last hours and found salvation.","r":["187:4.1","187:4.2"]},{"x":"As a sandstorm darkened the sky, Jesus cried, \"It is finished,\" commended his spirit to the Father, and breathed his last.","r":["187:5.1","187:5.5"]},{"x":"A Roman centurion who saw him die confessed that he truly was a Son of God.","r":["187:5.5"]},{"q":"Jésus mourut royalement — comme il avait vécu.","r":"187:5.6"}]},{"h":"Not an Atoning Sacrifice","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to provide a way of approach to an offended God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"His death was neither a ransom to buy man back from fallen rulers nor a sacrifice to pay mankind's debt to God.","r":["188:4.3"]},{"x":"The whole idea of ransom and atonement is incompatible with the concept of God as a loving Father, which Jesus taught and showed.","r":["188:4.8"]},{"x":"Sin is not passed from parents to children; it is conscious rebellion committed by individual will creatures.","r":["188:4.5"]},{"x":"Even a sovereign of justice would not be satisfied with the childish scheme of substituting an innocent person for the guilty.","r":["188:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Who Killed Him","items":[{"q":"Ce fut l’homme, et non Dieu, qui projeta et mit à exécution la mort de Jésus sur la croix.","r":"186:5.2"},{"x":"There is no direct connection between his death and the Jewish Passover sacrificial system.","r":["186:5.1"]},{"x":"The experience required by the bestowal was already complete at his baptism; the manner of his later life and death was his personal ministry for his creatures.","r":["186:5.3"]},{"x":"The gospel of realizing sonship with God by faith does not depend on his death and was illuminated even more by his life than by his death.","r":["186:5.4"]},{"x":"The Father loved mankind just as much before Jesus lived and died as after.","r":["186:5.6"]}]},{"h":"The True Meaning of the Cross","items":[{"q":"En ce qui concerne l’enrichissement de l’expérience humaine et l’élargissement de la voie du salut, relativement à la mort de Jésus, la grande chose n’est pas le fait de sa mort, mais plutôt le comportement superbe et l’esprit incomparable avec lesquels il fit face à la mort.","r":"188:4.12"},{"q":"Elle place définitivement toutes les relations entre Dieu et l’homme sur la base de la famille.","r":"188:5.1"},{"x":"Divine love does not merely forgive wrongs; it absorbs and actually destroys them, so the forgiveness of love transcends the forgiveness of mercy.","r":["188:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus bore the cross of mortal existence for more than twenty-five years, and Golgotha was the final expression of that love.","r":["188:5.4"]},{"q":"Il n’est guère approprié de parler de Jésus comme d’un sacrificateur, d’un payeur de rançon ou d’un rédempteur, mais il est entièrement correct de l’appeler un sauveur.","r":"188:4.7"},{"x":"He lived and died not for this world alone but for the whole universe, and his death illuminated the certainty of survival after the death of the flesh.","r":["188:4.6"]}]},{"h":"The Symbol of Service","items":[{"x":"His love that laid down his life for his enemies was greater than any love then known on earth.","r":["188:5.7"]},{"x":"The cross is not a symbol of substitution appeasing wrath but of unselfish service, in which the good bestow themselves on the evil to save them by love.","r":["188:5.9"]},{"x":"Creatures on many worlds, looking upon Jesus on the cross, have not given up the struggle of faith but have pressed on once more.","r":["188:5.5"]},{"x":"On the cross there was nothing the Father required, only what Jesus willingly gave and refused to avoid.","r":["188:5.11"]},{"x":"His death was not meant to reconcile man to God but to awaken man to the Father's eternal love and the Son's mercy.","r":["188:5.13"]}]}],"see":["Effusion de Jésus","Résurrection de Jésus","Amour","Pardon","Mort","Service"]},{"n":87,"t":"Paraboles","en":"Parables","sum":"The parable is the storytelling method of teaching that Jesus first used with the multitude by the Sea of Galilee and that thereafter became almost his only method of public instruction. He taught that parables should not be interpreted as allegories with a hidden meaning in every detail but received as true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth. A parable appeals at once to minds of different levels, plants new truth while avoiding prejudice and controversy, and leaves each person to find its meaning in his own soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Beginning of Teaching by Parables","items":[{"x":"Jesus first used this method when, from a boat by the sea, he told the parable of the sower to a crowd of nearly a thousand.","r":["151:1.1","151:1.2"]},{"x":"It was intended that those sincerely wishing to enter the kingdom would grasp the meaning, while those seeking to entrap him would see and not understand.","r":["151:1.4"]},{"x":"From then on Jesus taught the public almost entirely in parables and explained their meaning more fully to the apostles in the evening.","r":["151:4.7"]},{"x":"Parables appealing to nature were the best reply to the charge that his work was done by the power of the devil, and they gave his enemies less to seize upon.","r":["151:3.14"]}]},{"h":"Parables, Not Allegories","items":[{"x":"Peter and Nathaniel disagreed while interpreting the parable of the sower as an allegory with a hidden meaning in every detail.","r":["151:2.1","151:2.4"]},{"x":"Thomas recalled the Master's teaching that illustrations should use true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth.","r":["151:2.5"]},{"q":"Well done, Thomas; you have discerned the true meaning of parables","r":"151:2.7"},{"x":"Jesus said that private flights of imagination may be profitable, but offering them as public teaching is a mistake.","r":["151:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus advised avoiding fables and allegories and using parables freely, especially those drawn from nature.","r":["151:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Value of Parables","items":[{"q":"La parabole fait simultanément appel à des niveaux extrêmement différents du mental et de l’esprit.","r":"151:3.6"},{"q":"La parabole part des choses connues pour aboutir au discernement de l’inconnu.","r":"151:3.7"},{"x":"The parable plants new truth in the mind while bypassing prejudice and arousing a minimum of antagonism.","r":["151:3.8"]},{"x":"Parables avoid direct conflict with tradition and authority and recall the teaching whenever the familiar scene is seen again.","r":["151:3.10","151:3.11"]},{"x":"Hearing the same story, each person can interpret a parable according to his own intellectual and spiritual level.","r":["151:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Parables of the Growing Seed","items":[{"x":"The parable of the sower reviewed the ministry up to then and foreshadowed the varied success later messengers would meet.","r":["151:3.13"]},{"x":"Appealing only to emotion or intellect bears no fruit; true change of character comes from appealing to the spirit that lives within man.","r":["152:6.3"]},{"x":"The parable of the seed that grows by itself into the full ear shows that the kingdom grows quietly beyond human understanding.","r":["151:3.15"]},{"x":"The parables of the mustard seed and the leaven tell how the kingdom, small in its beginnings, grows great and spreads like leaven through the whole lump.","r":["151:4.2","151:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Parables Portraying the Father's Love","items":[{"q":"But I have come to show you that, while you are seeking to find God, God is likewise seeking to find you.","r":"169:1.2"},{"q":"the Father accepts you even before you have repented","r":"169:1.3"},{"x":"The father of the prodigal saw his son returning afar off, ran to meet him, and ordered a feast before the son had finished his confession.","r":["169:1.9","169:1.10"]},{"x":"The three stories of the lost sheep, the lost coin, and the lost son show respectively the Father seeking the lost, the thoroughness of the search, and complete restoration.","r":["169:1.15"]},{"x":"The parable of the prodigal son and the story of the good Samaritan were Jesus' favorite ways of teaching the Father's love and human neighborliness.","r":["169:1.16"]}]},{"h":"Neighborliness, Humility, and Faithfulness","items":[{"x":"To the trick question \"Who is my neighbor?\" Jesus answered with the story of the good Samaritan, letting the lawyer answer for himself.","r":["164:1.2","164:1.3","164:1.4"]},{"x":"The parable of the Pharisee and the publican teaches that salvation cannot be bought by works but is a free gift to all who have faith.","r":["167:5.1"]},{"x":"The parables of the talents and the pounds show that ability is the measure of opportunity and that equal faithfulness receives equal reward.","r":["171:8.10","171:8.13"]},{"q":"Let every man find out the meaning for himself and in his own soul.","r":"167:2.4"}]}],"see":["Enseignements de Jésus","Royaume des cieux","Amour","Pardon","Miséricorde","Les douze apôtres"]},{"n":11,"t":"Paradis","en":"Paradise","sum":"Le Paradis est le centre éternel de l’univers des univers et l’Ile éternelle où demeurent le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit. À la fois demeure spirituelle et sphère matérielle composée d’absolutum, il est la source de toute énergie physique et de toute gravité, et l’absolu de tous les modèles. Il existe hors du temps et n’a pas d’emplacement dans l’espace, et il est la destination que tout mortel connaissant Dieu est appelé à atteindre au terme de la longue ascension.","sections":[{"h":"La demeure de la Déité","items":[{"x":"Le Paradis est le centre éternel de l’univers des univers, où demeurent le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit avec leurs coordonnés, et il est le corps organisé le plus gigantesque du maitre univers.","r":["11:0.1"]},{"x":"Le Paradis est à la fois une demeure spirituelle et une sphère matérielle ; il existe depuis l’éternité, et il n’y a ni archives ni traditions concernant son origine.","r":["11:0.1","11:0.2"]},{"x":"La présence personnelle du Père est au centre du Paradis supérieur, entourée de la présence du Fils Éternel et enveloppée dans la gloire de l’Esprit Infini.","r":["11:1.1"]},{"x":"Que l’on suive les lignes de gravité, les lignes de gravité spirituelle, les circuits mentaux ou le circuit de personnalité, on arrive finalement à la résidence centrale du Père.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"q":"Le fait que si peu de créatures de l’univers aient trouvé Dieu au Paradis ne contredit ni la réalité de son existence ni la présence effective de sa personne spirituelle au centre de toutes choses.","r":"11:1.3"}]},{"h":"La nature de l’Ile éternelle","items":[{"x":"Le Paradis n’est pas sphérique, mais un ellipsoïde aplati dont le diamètre nord-sud est d’un sixième plus long que le diamètre est-ouest, et il fournit l’étalon de direction absolue dans le maitre univers.","r":["11:2.2","11:2.3"]},{"x":"L’Ile se divise en Paradis supérieur, périphérique et inférieur ; la Trinité semble présider au plan supérieur, personnel, et l’Absolu Non Qualifié au plan inférieur, impersonnel.","r":["11:2.4","11:2.8"]},{"x":"Le Paradis est composé d’une organisation homogène de puissance d’espace que l’on ne trouve nulle part ailleurs dans l’univers, et que les Melchizédeks appellent absolutum.","r":["11:2.9"]},{"q":"Le Paradis existe sans le temps et n’a pas d’emplacement dans l’espace.","r":"11:2.10"},{"x":"En gros, l’espace semble prendre naissance juste au-dessous du bas Paradis, et le temps juste au-dessus du Paradis supérieur.","r":["11:2.11"]}]},{"h":"Le Paradis supérieur et périphérique","items":[{"x":"Le Paradis supérieur comprend l’aire de la présence de la Déité, la Sphère Très Sainte, consacrée à l’adoration et à la trinitisation, et l’Aire Sainte, consacrée à la résidence.","r":["11:3.1"]},{"x":"Les sept zones concentriques de l’Aire Sainte sont appelées « les demeures du Père au Paradis », et la deuxième zone est réservée aux ascendeurs des sept superunivers.","r":["11:3.3"]},{"x":"L’espace résidentiel prévu pour les ascendeurs occupe moins d’un pour cent de la terre sainte qui leur est assignée, ce qui laisse amplement de place pour des êtres encore à venir.","r":["11:3.4"]},{"x":"Le Paradis périphérique est le lieu d’atterrissage des voyageurs de l’espace, et il abrite de vastes aires d’exposition historique et prophétique des univers locaux.","r":["11:4.1","11:4.3"]},{"q":"You must wait, and ascend while you wait","r":"11:4.5"}]},{"h":"Le bas Paradis et l’espace","items":[{"x":"Toute énergie physique et tous les circuits de force cosmique prennent naissance au bas Paradis, où ne demeure aucune personnalité.","r":["11:5.1"]},{"x":"La zone intérieure du centre de force du bas Paradis bat comme un cœur gigantesque et envoie des courants jusqu’aux confins les plus extérieurs de l’espace physique.","r":["11:5.5"]},{"x":"On croit que la zone extérieure est le foyer central de la présence spatiale de l’Absolu Non Qualifié, dont les émanations sortent et rentrent alternativement selon des cycles d’un peu plus d’un milliard d’années.","r":["11:5.7","11:5.8"]},{"x":"Tout l’espace se dilate et se contracte alternativement, un cycle d’expansion et de contraction durant un peu plus de deux milliards d’années du temps d’Urantia.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.5"]},{"x":"L’espace ne touche pas le Paradis ; le Paradis est le noyau immobile des zones de repos situées entre l’espace pénétré et l’espace non pénétré.","r":["11:7.1","11:7.2"]}]},{"h":"L’absolu de la gravité et des modèles","items":[{"q":"La gravité est l’emprise toute-puissante de la présence physique du Paradis.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"La gravité absolue est la gravité du Paradis, tandis que la gravité locale ou linéaire appartient au stade électrique de l’énergie matérialisée.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"Le Paradis est la source absolue et le point focal éternel de toute énergie-matière dans l’univers des univers.","r":["11:8.9"]},{"x":"Le système Paradis-Havona est le noyau éternel du maitre univers, autour duquel les sept superunivers et l’espace extérieur tournent tous sur des orbites établies.","r":["12:1.11"]},{"x":"Le Paradis n’est ni créateur ni Déité ; il est l’absolu des modèles, et Havona est le déploiement effectif de ses potentiels.","r":["11:9.4","11:9.5","0:4.13"]},{"x":"Lorsque le Père a exprimé son moi spirituel dans le Fils Éternel, il a simultanément révélé, sous la forme du Paradis, le potentiel infini de son moi non personnel.","r":["11:9.3"]}]},{"h":"La destination de la destinée","items":[{"x":"Pour toutes les personnalités spirituelles, le Paradis est le royaume de l’origine première et le but de la destinée finale.","r":["11:9.1"]},{"x":"Le Paradis est le centre géographique de l’infinité, mais il ne fait partie d’aucune création universelle, pas même de Havona ; il est une existence éternelle et exclusive.","r":["11:9.2"]},{"q":"Le Paradis est le centre de toute la création, la source de toutes les énergies et le lieu d’origine primitif de toutes les personnalités.","r":"11:9.7"},{"x":"Le pèlerin qui tombe dans le dernier sommeil du temps sur le premier circuit de Havona s’éveille au Paradis, et c’est seulement alors qu’il devient un véritable enfant du Paradis.","r":["26:11.6"]},{"x":"Un ordre et une harmonie perceptibles règnent au Paradis, et des directeurs de conduite instruisent les nouveaux venus pour qu’ils puissent y vivre sans confusion.","r":["27:4.2","27:4.3"]},{"x":"La demeure de Dieu est le modèle de tous les mondes-sièges de l’univers, et l’univers central de sa résidence est le modèle des idéaux et de la destinée de tous les univers.","r":["11:9.6"]},{"q":"Tout mortel connaissant Dieu et ayant épousé la carrière d’accomplissement de la volonté du Père s’est déjà engagé sur la longue, longue route du Paradis, route de recherche de la divinité et d’aboutissement à la perfection.","r":"11:9.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Gravité","Les trois Absolus","Père Universel","Grand univers et maitre univers","Ascension des mortels"]},{"n":68,"t":"Pardon","en":"Forgiveness","sum":"God's forgiveness flows naturally from his infinite understanding; it is given before man asks and requires no intermediary or sacrifice. Yet this forgiveness becomes real in personal religious experience only when one forgives one's fellows. Jesus taught to forgive even seventy times seven, and he said that inability to forgive others is a mark of immaturity that has not attained understanding and love.","sections":[{"h":"Forgiveness in the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"Puisque Dieu sait tout ce qui concerne ses enfants, il lui est facile de pardonner.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"At the bottom of God's goodness lies the universal tendency to love, show mercy, manifest patience, and minister forgiveness.","r":["2:6.9"]},{"x":"The Father is not a personality divided between justice and mercy, and he requires no mediator in order to forgive.","r":["2:6.6"]},{"x":"Divine forgiveness is an inevitable consequence inherent in God's infinite understanding, his full knowledge of his children's errors and choices.","r":["174:1.3"]},{"x":"The understanding love of wise parents usually prevents the very estrangement that would call for repentance and forgiveness.","r":["174:1.2"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Receive Forgiveness","items":[{"x":"Divine forgiveness is the renewal of severed relations of loyalty; it need not be sought, only recognized and accepted.","r":["89:10.6"]},{"q":"The Father in heaven has forgiven you even before you have thought to ask him","r":"146:2.4"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is in fact unconditioned, but in experience it becomes real only when one forgives one's fellows.","r":["146:2.4","170:3.4"]},{"x":"In forgiving his brother, a person creates in his soul the capacity to receive God's forgiveness of his own misdeeds.","r":["170:2.23"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into God's family, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that forgiveness of sin is received by faith in God, without penance or sacrifice.","r":["138:8.2","150:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Forgive One Another","items":[{"q":"the Father in heaven forgives you your sins; therefore should you learn to forgive one another.","r":"159:1.3"},{"x":"When Peter asked whether seven times was enough, Jesus answered to forgive even seventy times seven.","r":["159:1.4"]},{"x":"With the parable of the steward forgiven a great debt by the king who would not forgive his fellow's small debt, he taught the duty of the forgiven.","r":["159:1.4","159:1.5"]},{"x":"The better one understands a neighbor, the easier it is to forgive; when one loves a brother, one has already forgiven him.","r":["2:4.2","174:1.4"]},{"q":"Un homme ne pardonne pas véritablement à ses semblables, à moins de les aimer comme lui-même.","r":"170:3.5"}]},{"h":"The Immaturity That Cannot Forgive","items":[{"q":"« Votre inaptitude ou votre répugnance à pardonner à vos semblables donne la mesure de votre immaturité, et dénote que vous n’avez pas atteint le niveau adulte de sympathie, de compréhension et d’amour.","r":"174:1.5"},{"x":"People hold grudges and nurse vengefulness in proportion to their ignorance of others' inner nature and longings.","r":["174:1.5"]},{"x":"All sin can be forgiven, but it is doubtful that a confirmed iniquitous person would ever truly sorrow or accept forgiveness.","r":["67:1.6"]},{"x":"Those who knowingly and maliciously attribute the works of God to the forces of evil can hardly obtain forgiveness.","r":["153:4.3","165:3.6"]},{"x":"The Father is not an indulgent parent who overlooks everything; he does not condone his children's self-destructive conduct.","r":["147:5.9"]}]},{"h":"Forgiveness in History and the Example of Jesus","items":[{"x":"In primitive religion confession and forgiveness were a meaningless ritual that forgave in advance even the sins of the following week.","r":["89:2.5"]},{"x":"Hosea preached forgiveness through repentance, not sacrifice, and revived the gospel of love and divine mercy.","r":["97:4.5"]},{"x":"Before Jesus, a God who forgives repentant sinners was known, but a God who goes out first to seek the lost sheep was new.","r":["159:5.16"]},{"q":"Jesus' only words, as they nailed him to the crossbeam, were, \"Father, forgive them, for they know not what they do.\"","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Peter, who had denied the Master, fully believed he was forgiven only after the risen Jesus received him again.","r":["184:2.13","139:2.10"]}]}],"see":["Miséricorde","Péché","Amour","Fraternité des hommes","Enseignements de Jésus","Filiation avec Dieu"]},{"n":66,"t":"Péché","en":"Sin","sum":"Sin is not mere imperfection or mistake but the attitude of a personality that knowingly and deliberately resists the Father's will and divine reality: deliberate disloyalty to God. The moral responsibility for sin is wholly personal and is not inherited, and no one loses survival because of another's sin. All sin can be forgiven, but a personality that has become wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and eventually reaches extinction.","sections":[{"h":"What Sin Is","items":[{"q":"« Le péché est la transgression consciente, connue et délibérée, de la loi divine, de la volonté du Père.","r":"148:4.4"},{"x":"Error is the misunderstanding of reality, evil a partial maladjustment to reality, and sin a purposeful resistance to divine reality.","r":["67:1.4"]},{"x":"Error reveals a lack of intellectual keenness, evil a deficiency of wisdom, sin spiritual poverty, and iniquity failing personality control.","r":["67:1.5"]},{"x":"Good is the carrying out of the divine plan; sin is a deliberate rebellion against the divine will.","r":["75:4.3"]},{"q":"Il faut redéfinir le péché comme une déloyauté délibérée envers la Déité.","r":"89:10.2"}]},{"h":"Imperfection Is Not Sin","items":[{"x":"The natural evil tendencies and imperfections of a person before rebirth are neither sin nor iniquity but only the starting point of the ascending journey.","r":["148:4.6"]},{"x":"Finiteness in itself is neither evil nor sinful; evil and sin arise when the finite is misused and distorted.","r":["111:6.3"]},{"x":"A sense of guilt is only the awareness of having violated a moral code and does not necessarily mean sin; there is true sin only in conscious disloyalty to God.","r":["89:10.3"]},{"x":"The capacity to feel guilt is not a badge of human degradation but a mark of a being with potential greatness.","r":["89:10.4"]},{"x":"Sin reveals the immaturity of one dazzled by the liberty of the will who fails to realize the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of and Responsibility for Sin","items":[{"x":"The effects of sin are never local, but sin is fatal to survival only when it becomes the whole attitude of mind and soul.","r":["67:7.4"]},{"q":"Sin is wholly personal as to moral guilt or spiritual consequences","r":"67:7.7"},{"x":"No being's sin can prevent another's survival; eternal survival is jeopardized only by one's own choosing.","r":["67:7.5"]},{"q":"La nature animale — la tendance à la malfaisance — peut être héréditaire, mais le péché ne se transmet pas de parent à enfant.","r":"188:4.5"},{"x":"Repeated sin becomes habit, and the habitual sinner can easily slip into iniquity and become a wholehearted rebel against the universe.","r":["67:1.6"]}]},{"h":"God and Sin","items":[{"x":"God loves the sinner as an eternal personality reality, but sin is neither a person nor a spiritual reality, so only justice takes cognizance of it.","r":["2:6.8"]},{"q":"L’amour de Dieu sauve le pécheur. La loi de Dieu détruit le péché.","r":"2:6.8"},{"x":"A being wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and self-destroying, and once the sentence of extinction is executed, it becomes as if it had never been.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.4"]},{"q":"Le péché est une expérience de la conscience des créatures ; il ne fait pas partie de la conscience de Dieu.","r":"174:1.4"}]},{"h":"The Evolution and Correction of the Idea of Sin","items":[{"x":"For primitive man sin was the violation of a ghost-sanctioned taboo, and death was regarded as its penalty.","r":["89:2.2","70:11.4"]},{"x":"Primitive sin was an act, not a thought, and ceremonial; it gave rise to the belief in a fall from a perfect beginning.","r":["89:2.3"]},{"x":"Sacrifice for personal sin gradually developed into the doctrine of atoning sacrifice for the sins of the race.","r":["89:4.5"]},{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to appease the wrath of God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"Confession of sin does not remove its temporal consequences, but it is essential to religious growth and spiritual progress.","r":["89:10.5","156:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Pardon","Libre arbitre","Justice","Rébellion de Lucifer","Moralité"]},{"n":92,"t":"Pentecôte","en":"Pentecost","sum":"Pentecost is the day, after Jesus' departure, when the Spirit of Truth was poured out upon the one hundred and twenty believers in the upper chamber in Jerusalem and upon all the sincere throughout the world. The apostles, who had been hiding in fear, came out endowed with new power and boldly preached the gospel, and that day more than two thousand were baptized. The Urantia Book explains that Pentecost was not an outburst of emotion but a spiritual event that freed the religion of Jesus from the fetters of nation, race, and sex, and from dependence on physical force.","sections":[{"h":"What Happened That Day","items":[{"x":"The one hundred and twenty believers at prayer sensed a strange presence in the room and became conscious of a new and profound feeling of spiritual joy, security, and confidence.","r":["194:0.1"]},{"x":"Peter declared this to be the coming of the Spirit of Truth the Master had promised and proposed that they go to the temple to proclaim the good news.","r":["194:0.2"]},{"x":"The apostles, who had hidden for forty days, appeared boldly in the temple crowded for the feast of Pentecost.","r":["194:1.1"]},{"x":"Peter's fervent appeal, made where the Master had last taught, won more than two thousand souls.","r":["194:1.2"]},{"x":"That evening the new believers were baptized in the Master's name at the pool of Siloam, and for a time the believers remained a sect within Judaism.","r":["194:1.4","194:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit Poured Out on All","items":[{"q":"Do not overlook the fact that the Spirit of Truth was bestowed upon all sincere believers","r":"194:3.6"},{"x":"The gift of the spirit came not only to the apostles but to all the men and women in the upper chamber and to the honest of heart throughout the world.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"At the same hour the spirit came wherever there were true believers, in Philadelphia, Alexandria, and elsewhere.","r":["194:3.17"]},{"x":"Jesus' mother and brother were present but received no greater gift than the others; Pentecost ended belief in holy families and special priesthoods.","r":["194:3.15"]},{"x":"The spirit came upon those quietly sitting in prayer, apart from any form, ceremony, or sacred place.","r":["194:3.10"]}]},{"h":"A Spiritual Event, Not an Emotional One","items":[{"x":"Later Pentecost was confused with uncontrolled emotionalism, but the chief mission of the outpoured spirit was to teach the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"Prayer did not bring the spirit on the day of Pentecost","r":"194:3.20"},{"x":"Prayer does not move God to give more liberally, but it had much to do with determining each believer's capacity of receptivity.","r":["194:3.20"]},{"x":"\"Baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception of the gift of the Spirit of Truth and the acknowledgment of its new power.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"x":"The apostles lost themselves and found the spirit; it was not an emotional experience but a response to their dedication of themselves to God.","r":["194:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Religion Freed from Fetters","items":[{"q":"Le jour de la Pentecôte, la religion de Jésus rompit toutes les restrictions nationales et entraves raciales.","r":"194:3.5"},{"x":"That many peoples received the apostles' preaching showed that the gospel must not be identified with any race, culture, or language.","r":["194:3.9"]},{"x":"After Pentecost, in the brotherhood of the kingdom, woman stood before God equal with man.","r":["194:3.14"]},{"x":"Pentecost freed the Master's religion from all dependence on physical force, equipping it with the spiritual weapons of forgiveness, good will, and love.","r":["194:3.11"]},{"q":"Seule une approche spirituelle peut unifier l’humanité, et l’Esprit de Vérité est une influence mondiale universelle.","r":"194:3.18"}]},{"h":"God Seeking Man","items":[{"q":"Up to Pentecost, religion had revealed only man seeking for God","r":"194:3.13"},{"x":"Since Pentecost there shines out the spectacle of God also seeking man and, when he has found him, sending his spirit to dwell within him.","r":["194:3.13"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the Spirit of Truth prepared the minds of all normal people for the subsequent universal bestowal of the Adjusters.","r":["194:2.3"]},{"x":"Thereafter man has threefold guidance: the Adjuster, spirit of the Father; the Spirit of Truth, spirit of the Son; and the Holy Spirit, spirit of the Spirit.","r":["194:2.11"]},{"x":"Within less than a month after the spirit came, the apostles made more spiritual progress than in their four years with Jesus.","r":["194:2.9"]}]},{"h":"The New Message and the Beginning of the Church","items":[{"x":"Their message shifted from the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man to the proclamation of the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:4.4"]},{"q":"L’évangile du royaume, le message de Jésus, venait d’être changé subitement en évangile du Seigneur Jésus-Christ.","r":"194:4.5"},{"x":"Calling one another brothers and sisters, the believers formed a fellowship of worship and life, breaking bread, praying, and caring for the poor.","r":["194:4.3","194:4.7"]},{"x":"Stephen's martyrdom led to the formal organization of the early church, and the persecution that followed scattered teachers to the ends of the empire.","r":["194:4.12","194:4.13"]},{"x":"Jesus' earth life becomes the anchor of time, and the Spirit of Truth the source that makes the religion he lived grow forever.","r":["194:3.8"]}]}],"see":["Esprit de Vérité","Résurrection de Jésus","Les douze apôtres","Religion institutionnelle","Ajusteur de Pensée","Saint-Esprit"]},{"n":1,"t":"Père Universel","en":"Universal Father","sum":"Le Père Universel est Dieu, la Source-Centre Première de toutes choses et de tous les êtres. Il est le Créateur, le Contrôleur et le Soutien infini ; bien qu’il soit un esprit invisible, il est une vraie personnalité qui aime toutes ses créatures comme un père. Parce que son fragment, l’Ajusteur de Pensée, habite l’homme, chacun peut se lancer dans l’aventure éternelle de trouver le Père et de devenir semblable à lui.","sections":[{"h":"Source-Centre Première","items":[{"x":"Le Père est le Dieu de toute la création, la Source-Centre Première de toutes choses et de tous les êtres, que l’on doit concevoir d’abord comme Créateur, ensuite comme Contrôleur et enfin comme Soutien infini.","r":["1:0.1"]},{"x":"Le Père a créé personnellement le Paradis et l’univers central, tandis que les univers du temps et de l’espace sont l’œuvre des Fils Créateurs ; Nébadon est la création de son Fils Micaël.","r":["1:2.9"]},{"x":"Le Père agit physiquement par la gravité de l’Ile du Paradis, mentalement dans l’Esprit Infini et spirituellement dans le Fils Éternel, et pourtant il garde un contact direct avec ses créatures.","r":["1:2.10"]},{"q":"Dieu n’est semblable ni à un homme ni à une machine.","r":"1:2.1"},{"x":"Pour Dieu, il n’y a pas de passé, de présent et de futur séparés ; tout le temps est présent, et aucun évènement de l’univers ne le prend jamais par surprise.","r":["2:1.5"]}]},{"h":"Le nom et la réalité","items":[{"x":"La Source-Centre Première n’a jamais révélé de nom pour elle-même ; le nom de « Père » est né de la relation personnelle que ses créatures entretiennent avec lui.","r":["1:1.1"]},{"x":"Le nom sous lequel on l’appelle importe peu ; ce qui importe, c’est le désir de le connaitre et de lui ressembler.","r":["1:1.6"]},{"x":"Dieu est une réalité transcendante, infiniment plus grande que toute réalité idéalisée, que toute loi de la nature personnifiée ou que le « plus haut produit de l’homme ».","r":["1:2.2"]},{"x":"L’existence de Dieu ne peut se prouver par l’expérimentation scientifique ni par la logique pure ; elle ne se réalise que dans le domaine de l’expérience humaine.","r":["1:2.7"]},{"q":"Those who know God have experienced the fact of his presence","r":"1:2.8"}]},{"h":"Esprit invisible, vraie personnalité","items":[{"q":"« Dieu est esprit. » Il est une présence spirituelle universelle.","r":"1:3.1"},{"x":"Le Père est invisible non parce qu’il se cache, mais parce que les êtres matériels ne pourraient préserver leur existence devant son éclat spirituel ; on peut pourtant le discerner avec l’œil de la foi.","r":["1:3.3"]},{"x":"Son infinité ne doit pas masquer sa personnalité ; le Père est le sommet de la personnalité divine, l’origine et la destinée de toute personnalité.","r":["1:5.1"]},{"x":"Dans l’univers local, le Père se révèle dans les personnalités des Fils Créateurs, de sorte que celui qui a vu le Fils a vu le Père.","r":["1:5.5","3:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Le Père aimant","items":[{"q":"Dieu n’aime pas comme un père, mais en tant que père.","r":"2:6.4"},{"x":"L’amour du Père n’a pas été gagné par le sacrifice ou l’intercession de ses Fils ; il aime personnellement ses enfants depuis le commencement.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"x":"Les prophètes hébreux ont proclamé Dieu comme le Père d’Israël, mais Jésus l’a révélé comme le Père de chaque être humain.","r":["2:6.4"]},{"x":"Le Père participe personnellement à la lutte de chaque âme qui s’efforce vers la perfection : il souffre de nos afflictions et triomphe de nos victoires.","r":["1:5.15","1:5.16"]},{"x":"Dieu le Père aime l’humanité, Dieu le Fils sert l’humanité, et Dieu l’Esprit inspire à ses enfants de monter à la recherche du Père.","r":["3:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Le chemin vers le Père","items":[{"x":"Le Père n’exige ni culte formel ni service servile ; la consécration sans réserve à faire la volonté du Père est le seul don vraiment personnel que l’homme puisse offrir.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"\"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect.\"","r":"1:0.3"},{"x":"L’homme ne peut approcher directement le Père, non parce qu’il est lointain, mais à cause de la finitude de la créature ; et le chemin est ouvert à tous.","r":["5:1.1","5:1.8"]},{"q":"Quelle erreur de rêver d’un Dieu lointain dans le ciel, alors que l’esprit du Père Universel vit dans votre propre mental !","r":"5:2.3"},{"x":"Si différent que soit leur statut intellectuel et social, tous les hommes ont reçu la même présence divine, de sorte que la possibilité de progrès spirituel est égale pour tous.","r":["5:1.4","5:1.5"]},{"x":"Quel que soit le temps nécessaire, l’ascendeur fusionné avec l’Ajusteur se tiendra un jour devant le centre divin et verra le Père face à face.","r":["5:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Attributs de Dieu","Personnalité de Dieu","Trinité du Paradis","Ajusteur de Pensée","Filiation avec Dieu","Adoration"]},{"n":36,"t":"Personnalité","en":"Personality","sum":"Personality is the unique gift that the Universal Father exclusively bestows upon living energy systems of matter, mind, and spirit. It is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul; it is the one changeless reality amid ever-changing experience, and it unifies all other factors. Personality shows itself in self-consciousness and relative free will; every personality is linked to the Father by his personality circuit and survives death with the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Father's Gift","items":[{"x":"God the Father is the bestower and conservator of every personality, and the destiny of all finite personalities who choose the divine will.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"q":"Nulle personnalité n’est séparée de Dieu le Père, et nulle n’existe sinon pour Dieu le Père.","r":"5:6.4"},{"x":"Personality does not arise of itself; the impersonal never becomes personal without a direct act of the Father.","r":["0:5.4","5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is not attained by degrees; it is either present or absent.","r":["5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is bestowed directly by the Universal Father, or by the Conjoint Actor acting for him, and may be given to living energy systems endowed with mind or spirit.","r":["112:0.3","112:0.4"]}]},{"h":"What Personality Is","items":[{"q":"Personality is the one changeless reality in an otherwise ever-changing creature experience;","r":"0:5.11"},{"x":"Human personality is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul, and it unifies all the other factors of individuality.","r":["0:5.11"]},{"x":"Personality is one of the unsolved mysteries of the universe; its components are known, but its real nature is not fully understood.","r":["5:6.2"]},{"x":"Personality has no identity of its own, yet it can unify the identity of a living energy system.","r":["112:0.7"]},{"x":"In the human system personality unifies all activities and imparts the qualities of identity and creativity.","r":["112:1.19"]}]},{"h":"Unique and Changeless","items":[{"x":"Personalities may be similar but never the same; even those of the same series and type are not identical.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"x":"Because of personality we can recognize a being as the very one we knew before, however much its form or spiritual status has changed.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"q":"they are associable but nontotalable.","r":"112:0.12"},{"x":"Adjusters are alike in nature when they come from the Father, but personality is diverse, original, and exclusive.","r":["16:8.3"]},{"x":"Through all the stages of evolution there is in each person a changeless part, the personality that endures amid change.","r":["112:0.1"]}]},{"h":"Self-Consciousness and Free Will","items":[{"x":"Creature personality is distinguished by two phenomena: self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness is awareness of one's own personality reality, and it includes the ability to recognize the reality of other personalities.","r":["16:8.6"]},{"x":"Human free will relates to seven domains, among them moral decisions, spiritual choices, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.8","16:8.14"]},{"q":"Elle peut faire un don à Dieu — la consécration du libre arbitre à faire la volonté de Dieu.","r":"112:0.10"},{"x":"Having provided for the growth of the soul, the Father steps aside; in the matter of eternal survival he has decreed the absolute sovereignty of the mortal will.","r":["5:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Personality Circuit and Relationships","items":[{"x":"All personalities are circuited in the personal presence of the Universal Father, and the Father is personally conscious of every personality.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.11"]},{"x":"This personality circuit exists apart from the mission of the Thought Adjusters, and personalities not indwelt by Adjusters are also embraced in it.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.12"]},{"x":"Personality responds directly to the presence of other personality and is characterized by a morality that recognizes the relativity of its relations with others.","r":["112:0.11","112:0.13"]},{"q":"La personnalité agit difficilement dans l’isolement.","r":"112:1.16"},{"x":"Because we are conscious of God as Creator Father, we become conscious of men as creature brothers.","r":["16:9.14"]}]},{"h":"Survival and Destiny of Personality","items":[{"x":"The material self has a temporal identity and the Adjuster an eternal identity, and together they produce the surviving identity of the immortal soul.","r":["5:6.7"]},{"q":"L’identité de la personnalité survit dans et par la survie de l’âme.","r":"16:9.3"},{"x":"Human personality is eternal yet conditional as to identity; it must choose for itself whether to stand where destiny is fulfilled.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"Relationships between personalities are not scaffolding; mortal memories of personal relations have cosmic value and persist on the mansion worlds.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"The fact that God became man has forever changed all the meanings and values of human personality.","r":["112:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Âme","Mental","Libre arbitre","Survie","Personnalité de Dieu"]},{"n":3,"t":"Personnalité de Dieu","en":"Personality of God","sum":"Le Père Universel est infini, et pourtant il est une vraie personnalité. La personnalité n’est pas un attribut parmi d’autres, mais la manière dont se révèle la totalité de sa nature infinie et de sa volonté unifiée. La personnalité de chaque créature est conférée par le Père et maintenue dans son circuit de personnalité, et, parce que Dieu est personnel, l’homme peut communier avec lui, l’aimer et devenir son ami.","sections":[{"h":"Dieu infini et personnel","items":[{"q":"Dieu est à la fois infini et personnel, il est une personnalité infinie.","r":"1:5.1"},{"x":"Dieu transcende de loin tout concept de personnalité que l’homme puisse saisir, mais il ne peut être rien de moins qu’une personnalité éternelle, vraie, bonne et belle.","r":["1:5.2"]},{"x":"Sans Dieu et sa personnalité centrale, il n’y aurait de personnalité nulle part dans le vaste univers.","r":["1:5.7"]},{"x":"La personnalité n’est pas un attribut de Dieu, mais la totalité de sa nature infinie coordonnée et de sa volonté divine unifiée, la révélation de Dieu à l’univers des univers.","r":["1:5.13"]},{"x":"Dieu est plus que pouvoir, énergie, modèle ou présence ; il est une personnalité qui exerce une volonté souveraine, éprouve la conscience de soi de la divinité et révèle à ses enfants l’amour d’un père.","r":["3:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Idées fausses sur la personnalité","items":[{"q":"La personnalité humaine est l’ombre-image projetée dans l’espace-temps par la personnalité du divin Créateur.","r":"1:6.1"},{"x":"La personnalité n’exige pas de corps matériel ; à cause de cette erreur, le matérialisme nie la personnalité des morts, et le panthéisme celle d’un Dieu sans corps.","r":["1:5.12"]},{"x":"Nier la personnalité de la Source-Centre Première ne laisse que les deux dilemmes philosophiques du matérialisme et du panthéisme.","r":["1:5.11"]},{"x":"La raison, la sagesse et l’expérience religieuse impliquent la personnalité de Dieu, mais ne la prouvent pas ; ce concept est venu à l’humanité principalement par la révélation.","r":["1:5.10"]},{"q":"Pour la science, Dieu est une cause, pour la philosophie, il est une idée et, pour la religion, il est une personne, précisément le Père céleste et aimant.","r":"1:6.2"},{"x":"L’homme considère l’infini à partir du fini, et Dieu considère le fini à partir de l’infini ; ainsi le concept de la personnalité divine s’améliore à mesure que s’améliore la compréhension humaine de la personnalité humaine.","r":["1:6.3"]}]},{"h":"Le dispensateur de la personnalité","items":[{"x":"Le Père est le dispensateur et le conservateur de toute personnalité, du plus humble mortel au plus haut créateur, et la destinée de toute personnalité finie qui choisit sa volonté.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"x":"Le mental, l’esprit ou l’énergie physique seuls ne sont pas la personnalité ; la personnalité est la dotation que le Père confère exclusivement aux systèmes vivants de matière, de mental et d’esprit.","r":["5:6.3","5:6.4"]},{"q":"La personnalité n’est pas non plus un aboutissement progressif.","r":"5:6.3"},{"x":"De même que toute gravité est reliée à l’Ile du Paradis, tout mental à l’Acteur Conjoint et tout esprit au Fils Éternel, de même toute personnalité est reliée au circuit de personnalité du Père.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"Indépendamment de la mission des Ajusteurs, le Père est personnellement conscient des personnalités de tous les niveaux d’existence consciente de soi et en contact avec elles.","r":["5:6.10"]}]},{"h":"Le respect du libre arbitre","items":[{"x":"En conférant la personnalité à une créature, le Père lui confère aussi une liberté relative à l’égard de la réponse servile à la causalité antécédente.","r":["5:6.9"]},{"x":"Après avoir pourvu à la croissance de l’âme, le Père se retire, et il a décrété comme loi absolue la souveraineté de la volonté mortelle en ce qui concerne la survie éternelle.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure","r":"5:6.12"}]},{"h":"La communion avec un Dieu personnel","items":[{"x":"Entre choses impersonnelles, il n’y a qu’interaction ; une communion comme celle d’un père et d’un fils n’est possible que si tous deux sont des personnalités.","r":["1:7.1"]},{"q":"L’homme ne réalise pas son union avec Dieu comme une goutte d’eau pourrait trouver son unité avec l’océan.","r":"1:7.2"},{"x":"La vérité et la beauté peuvent se concevoir en dehors de la personnalité, mais la bonté divine ne se comprend qu’en relation avec la personnalité, et seule une personnalité peut aimer et être aimée.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"Parce que Dieu peut connaitre et être connu, aimer et être aimé, l’homme aussi peut être connu comme l’ami de Dieu.","r":["1:5.8"]},{"x":"Jésus a pleinement réalisé le potentiel de la personnalité spirituelle dans l’expérience humaine ; c’est pourquoi sa vie est la révélation la plus pratique de la personnalité de Dieu.","r":["1:6.8"]},{"x":"Si l’homme ne parvient pas à voir l’amour d’un Dieu personnel, le royaume de Dieu ne devient qu’un royaume du bien.","r":["2:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Personnalité","Libre arbitre","Attributs de Dieu","Amour","Effusion de Jésus"]},{"n":69,"t":"Peur et inquiétude","en":"Fear and Worry","sum":"Fear was a powerful emotion that bound primitive man into society and prepared the first soil of religion, but unreasoned fear and worry now become poisons that hinder the progress of the soul. Revealed religion and the Thought Adjuster seek to change the fear of God into love and trust, and Jesus taught that foresight and prudence are permitted but that worry and anxiety should be abandoned for trust in the Father. His peace is a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid.","sections":[{"h":"Fear in Evolution","items":[{"x":"Early man lived in constant fear of bad luck, and that fear had a paralyzing power.","r":["86:1.3","86:1.4"]},{"x":"If hunger and love drew men together, vanity and ghost fear held primitive society together.","r":["68:3.4","68:3.1"]},{"x":"It was not the sanctity of life but the fear aroused by the shock of death that fostered primitive religion.","r":["86:3.1","87:1.1"]},{"x":"The false fears of primitive religion prepared the soil of the mind, and the Adjusters have ever since been transforming fear into the love of God.","r":["86:7.6"]},{"x":"Evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion leads them to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1","101:0.1"]}]},{"h":"A Poison to the Soul","items":[{"q":"La peur irraisonnée est une fraude intellectuelle maitresse pratiquée sur l’âme mortelle en évolution.","r":"48:7.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion, like physical poisons, greatly hinder the spiritual progress of the soul.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"The emotion in man that angels find hardest to understand is the inheritance of animal fear that throws even faith into panic.","r":["113:2.5"]},{"q":"Fear is man's chief enslaver and pride his great weakness","r":"142:0.2"},{"q":"Hate is the shadow of fear; revenge the mask of cowardice.","r":"145:3.4"},{"q":"Le découragement, les soucis et l’indolence sont des preuves positives de l’immaturité morale.","r":"160:1.6"}]},{"h":"The Worry-Free Life Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not forbid prudent foresight for the future, but he opposed worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.3"]},{"x":"Anxiety cannot add a cubit to one's stature or a day to one's life, so trust the Father who feeds even the ravens.","r":["165:5.2"]},{"x":"He counseled not to be overanxious about needs but to spread them before the Father with prayer and thanksgiving.","r":["146:2.16"]},{"x":"To Martha, troubled about many things, he said that the small things of life must give way to the greater things of the kingdom.","r":["162:8.3"]},{"x":"People spend much time crying in fear like lost children, though in fact they are not far from safety.","r":["132:6.1"]},{"x":"Returning from rest in the hills, the apostles realized that many pressing problems were the products of exaggerated fear and anxiety.","r":["143:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Overcome Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus told a fear-ridden young man to make his mind not a slave of fear but a courageous ally in solving problems.","r":["130:6.3"]},{"x":"When the indwelling spirit is freed from the fetters of fear, the consciousness of being a child of God overcomes the fear of men.","r":["130:6.3","130:6.4"]},{"q":"Les Ajusteurs de Pensée aimeraient changer vos sentiments de crainte en convictions d’amour et de confiance, mais ils ne peuvent le faire arbitrairement et mécaniquement ; c’est à vous que cela incombe.","r":"108:5.8"},{"x":"The anxiety arising from the fear of being alone in the universe should be dissolved by the contemplation of faith in the Father and the rest of worship.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"x":"Happy and effective people are motivated not by fear of wrongdoing but by love of right doing.","r":["140:4.6","140:5.6"]},{"x":"Mere belief may not overcome doubt and fear, but living faith always triumphs over doubting.","r":["102:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Peace Without Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus knew no fear; he faced the realities of life without fear and was always cheerful and glad.","r":["100:7.4","100:7.12"]},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is not passive calm but a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid amid trials and persecutions.","r":["140:5.18"]},{"q":"Let not your heart be troubled, neither let it be fearful. I have overcome the world, and in me you shall all triumph through faith.","r":"181:1.5"},{"x":"On the morontia worlds ascenders learn to accept challenges without complaint and to face difficulties and uncertainties without fear.","r":["48:6.35"]},{"x":"Teachers are exhorted to proclaim the love of God that casts out all fear.","r":["48:6.8"]}]}],"see":["Foi","Joie et bonheur","Adversité et épreuves","Ajusteur de Pensée","Amour","Religion institutionnelle"]},{"n":74,"t":"Philosophie","en":"Philosophy","sum":"Philosophy is the effort of the human mind to weave the facts revealed by science and the values experienced by religion into one coherent view of the universe; it is the domain of wisdom. Its body is founded on material facts, while its soul and energy come from spiritual insight. The highest attainable philosophy rests on the reason of science, the faith of religion, and the truth insight of revelation, and the philosophic quest does not end even on Paradise.","sections":[{"h":"Wisdom Seeking Unity","items":[{"q":"Dans l’expérience humaine, c’est par la philosophie que l’on trouve le plus facilement l’unité.","r":"102:2.6"},{"x":"The body of philosophic thought must be founded on material facts, but its soul and energy is mortal spiritual insight.","r":["102:2.6"]},{"x":"Philosophy arose from the effort to organize the separate findings of science and religion into a reasoned and unified attitude toward the universe.","r":["103:6.9"]},{"x":"Science is the domain of knowledge, religion the sphere of the faith experience, and philosophy the realm of wisdom.","r":["101:5.2"]},{"x":"Science is satisfied with a First Cause, religion with a supreme personality, and philosophy with unity.","r":["102:3.15"]},{"q":"La philosophie est sa tentative pour unifier l’expérience humaine.","r":"196:3.30"}]},{"h":"The Place and Limits of Philosophy","items":[{"x":"In science the self observes the material world, philosophy observes this observation, and religion experiences the reality that observes it all.","r":["112:2.12"]},{"q":"La philosophie est inévitablement suprascientifique. L’homme est un fait matériel de la nature, mais sa vie est un phénomène qui en transcende les niveaux matériels, en ce sens qu’elle déploie les attributs contrôlants du mental et les qualités créatives de l’esprit.","r":"195:7.9"},{"x":"Philosophy inclined to matter becomes naturalism, overweighted toward spirit becomes mysticism, and leaning on metaphysics ends in skepticism and confusion.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"Philosophy should not project reality only by straight-line logic but should allow for the elliptic symmetry of reality and the curvature of relation concepts.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"A philosophy useful to both science and religion avoids the extremes of materialism and pantheism and recognizes the reality of personality, the changeless in the midst of change.","r":["103:8.6"]}]},{"h":"The Highest Philosophy","items":[{"q":"La philosophie la plus élevée que l’homme mortel puisse atteindre doit être logiquement basée sur la raison de la science, la foi de la religion et la clairvoyance de la vérité fournie par la révélation.","r":"103:6.15"},{"x":"Philosophy clarified by revelation can function adequately even in the absence of the morontia mota and despite the failure of metaphysics.","r":["103:6.9","103:8.6"]},{"x":"True philosophy grows out of the wisdom that seeks to correlate the quantitative observations of science with the qualitative observations of religion.","r":["133:5.4"]},{"x":"The lower planes of the morontia mota join directly with the highest levels of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"x":"The ideal human state is one in which wisdom, faith, and experience work together, meaningfully fusing philosophy, religion, and science into one.","r":["98:2.12"]}]},{"h":"The Formation of a Philosophy of Religion","items":[{"x":"An individual's philosophy of religion is formed from many factors, including inner experience, environment, temperament, education, and social conditions.","r":["101:7.1"]},{"q":"Moral cowards never achieve high planes of philosophic thinking","r":"101:7.2"},{"x":"The philosophy of religion evolves through four levels, from conformity to tradition to fearless and sincere thinking and living.","r":["101:7.4"]},{"x":"A sound philosophy of religion distinguishes material and spiritual realities while recognizing their unity in intellectual striving and social service.","r":["101:7.5"]},{"x":"An effective philosophy of living weaves together cosmic insight and emotional reactions to the environment.","r":["140:4.8"]}]},{"h":"Philosophy in History and the Eternal Quest","items":[{"q":"En Grèce, la croyance était subordonnée à la pensée. En Palestine, la pensée était maintenue asservie à la croyance.","r":"98:2.8"},{"x":"The Greek philosophers achieved lofty ethical systems, but their concept of God dissolved in a pantheistic haze and failed to satisfy the masses' longing for salvation.","r":["98:2.9","98:2.10"]},{"x":"Religion has long endured without philosophy, but philosophy wholly unconnected with religion has seldom endured long.","r":["98:2.12"]},{"x":"Even on Paradise endless mysteries remain for philosophy to solve, and the exhilaration of philosophy is a satisfaction second only to worship.","r":["27:6.1"]},{"x":"The masters of philosophy on Paradise delight in leading ascenders in the thrilling quest of solving universe problems.","r":["27:6.2","27:6.5"]}]}],"see":["Sagesse","Science et religion","Révélation","Vérité","Réalité","Morontia"]},{"n":30,"t":"Porteurs de Vie","en":"Life Carriers","sum":"Les Porteurs de Vie sont des Fils de l’univers local créés conjointement par le Fils Créateur, l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers et l’un des Anciens des Jours ; ils conçoivent la vie des créatures, l’implantent sur les planètes et favorisent son évolution. L’étincelle de vie est donnée par leur intermédiaire, mais son facteur essentiel vient de l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers, et leurs manipulations cessent dès qu’apparaissent des êtres dotés de volonté. Urantia est un monde de modification de la vie, et sa vie a été formulée à nouveau sur la planète même.","sections":[{"h":"Origine et organisation","items":[{"x":"Les Porteurs de Vie sont la progéniture du Fils Créateur, de l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers et d’un Ancien des Jours désigné ; ils sont le seul groupe de vie intelligente de l’univers local à la création duquel participent les chefs du superunivers.","r":["36:1.1"]},{"q":"Ils sont chargés d’élaborer la vie des créatures et de la porter aux sphères planétaires.","r":"36:0.1"},{"x":"Après avoir créé trois ordres de fils, dont les Melchizédeks, le Fils et l’Esprit de l’univers local coopèrent avec le niveau suivant de Dieu le Septuple pour produire les Porteurs de Vie.","r":["35:0.7"]},{"x":"Cent millions ont été créés dans Nébadon, dirigés par le trio déterminant la vie que forment Gabriel, le Père Melchizédek et Nambia, le Porteur de Vie premier-né.","r":["36:1.2"]},{"x":"Ils se répartissent en trois groupes : Porteurs de Vie seniors, assistants et gardiens ; le corps envoyé sur une planète comprend habituellement cent seniors, cent assistants et mille gardiens.","r":["36:1.3","36:3.2"]},{"x":"Ils peuvent fonctionner sur trois niveaux : le niveau physique de l’électrochimie, le niveau intermédiaire de l’existence quasi morontielle et le niveau semi-spirituel.","r":["65:1.2","65:1.3","65:1.5"]}]},{"h":"La conception et l’implantation de la vie","items":[{"q":"La vie n’apparait pas spontanément dans les univers ; sur les planètes stériles, il faut qu’elle soit instaurée par les Porteurs de Vie.","r":"36:3.1"},{"x":"Sur les sept mondes des Porteurs de Vie du circuit de Salvington, ils étudient la planification de la vie, sa conservation, l’évolution, la vie associée au mental, entre autres ; les modèles de vie originaux sont fournis par le Fils Créateur.","r":["36:2.1","36:2.12"]},{"q":"L’étincelle vitale — le mystère de la vie — est conférée par l’entremise des Porteurs de Vie, mais ne vient pas d’eux.","r":"36:3.4"},{"x":"Ils formulent le plasma vital, mais l’étincelle d’énergie qui anime le corps et présage le mental vient de l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers.","r":["36:3.4"]},{"x":"En transmettant la vie, ils ne transmettent rien de leur nature personnelle ; en tant que présences catalytiques vivantes, ils ne font qu’amorcer les révolutions essentielles de la matière.","r":["36:3.5"]},{"q":"Les Fils de Dieu peuvent construire les formes de vie, mais c’est l’Esprit de Dieu qui fournit réellement l’étincelle vitale.","r":"36:6.4"}]},{"h":"Le soutien de l’évolution et ses limites","items":[{"x":"Environ un demi-million d’années du temps planétaire est accordé pour établir la vie sur un nouveau monde ; une fois cette période écoulée, rien de nouveau ne peut être ajouté.","r":["36:3.6"]},{"x":"Jusqu’à l’apparition d’êtres moraux, ils peuvent manipuler l’environnement pour favoriser l’évolution, mais il ne leur est pas permis d’intervenir mécaniquement ou arbitrairement dans le processus évolutionnaire.","r":["36:3.7","65:3.2"]},{"q":"C’est pourquoi l’évolution — sur Urantia ou ailleurs — est toujours intentionnelle et jamais accidentelle.","r":"65:0.7"},{"x":"Lorsque des êtres dotés de volonté apparaissent, leur œuvre prend fin, et ils doivent soit quitter la planète, soit prêter des serments de renoncement pour ne plus influencer l’évolution.","r":["36:3.8","65:1.8"]},{"x":"Deux Porteurs de Vie seniors et douze gardiens demeurent encore aujourd’hui sur Urantia en tant que conseillers, liés par des serments de renoncement.","r":["36:3.9"]},{"x":"Comme on ne peut pas faire se déployer la vie plus vite que le développement physique de la planète, les Porteurs de Vie doivent attendre l’évolution géologique.","r":["58:1.2","65:8.2"]}]},{"h":"L’expérience de la vie sur Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia est une planète décimale, un monde de modification de la vie, où les Porteurs de Vie ont tenté de modifier et d’améliorer les modèles de vie standard.","r":["58:0.1","65:4.1"]},{"q":"La vie sur Urantia est unique et a son origine sur cette planète.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"Comme le protoplasme d’Urantia fut conçu pour ne fonctionner que dans une solution saline, l’implantation attendit que les eaux de la mer soient devenues suffisamment salées.","r":["58:1.3"]},{"x":"Il y a cinq-cent-cinquante millions d’années, le corps des Porteurs de Vie revint et fit trois implantations de vie marine dans les criques tropicales abritées de la mer centrale, entre les continents en voie de séparation.","r":["58:4.2","58:4.4"]},{"x":"La formule chimique de la cicatrisation des plaies fut choisie après plus d’un demi-million d’expériences, ce qui montre que la vie humaine fut planifiée intelligemment.","r":["65:4.3","65:4.4"]},{"x":"Urantia est la seule planète de Satania où une volonté de type humain soit apparue dans une race antérieure aux races de couleur.","r":["65:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Vie, mental et esprit","items":[{"x":"Les sept esprits-mentaux adjuvats accompagnent toujours les Porteurs de Vie sur une nouvelle planète, et leur foyer central se trouve sur le monde-siège des Porteurs de Vie.","r":["36:5.4","36:2.10"]},{"q":"life springs only from life.","r":"36:6.2"},{"x":"Les formes de vie expérimentales qu’ils organisent sur les mondes de Salvington sont toujours dépourvues de capacité de reproduction.","r":["36:6.3"]},{"x":"Ils savent que la vie découle du Père, par le Fils et par l’Esprit, mais eux-mêmes ne comprennent pas pleinement la nature et la source de l’étincelle qui active la vie.","r":["36:6.7"]},{"x":"Lorsque l’univers sera ancré dans la lumière et la vie, ils espèrent atteindre un quatrième stade d’existence, entièrement spirituel.","r":["65:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Évolution","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Urantia","Melchizédeks","Fils Créateur Micaël"]},{"n":52,"t":"Prière","en":"Prayer","sum":"Prayer is a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit, the breath of the soul in the communion of sonship with God. Beginning as primitive petitions for material things, prayer gradually evolved into ethical and spiritual communion. Prayer does not change God but changes the one who prays, and it is truest when it seeks values, not things, and growth, not gratification. Jesus lived a life dedicated in prayer to the Father's will.","sections":[{"h":"What Prayer Is","items":[{"q":"Prayer is entirely a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit","r":"144:2.2"},{"x":"Prayer is the communion of sonship and the expression of fellowship; the ideal prayer is spiritual communion leading to intelligent worship.","r":["144:2.2"]},{"x":"Prayer is the breath of the soul, leading one to strive persistently to ascertain the Father's will.","r":["144:2.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is the process of exchanging the human will for the divine will, part of the divine plan for making over what is into what ought to be.","r":["144:4.9"]},{"x":"True prayer is the sincere and trusting communication of the creature's spiritual nature with the omnipresent spirit of the Creator.","r":["91:8.4"]},{"q":"« La prière est le souffle de l’âme et devrait vous inciter à persévérer dans vos tentatives pour mieux connaitre la volonté du Père.","r":"144:2.3"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Prayer","items":[{"x":"Primitive man prayed for material blessings such as food and rain; this was a perversion of prayer, yet it also stimulated social and ethical effort.","r":["91:1.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is a monologue only in the most primitive minds; it soon becomes a dialogue and broadens into group worship.","r":["91:1.4"]},{"x":"Magic was an attempt to adjust Deity to conditions; prayer is an effort to adjust the personality to the will of Deity.","r":["91:8.2"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice, offering material things in place of the will, diminishes the efficacy of true prayer.","r":["91:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Principles of True Prayer","items":[{"x":"Selfish and materialistic prayer is incompatible with ethical religion founded on unselfish love.","r":["91:4.1"]},{"q":"La prière ne doit jamais être prostituée au point de devenir un substitut à l’action.","r":"91:4.2"},{"x":"Do not be so lazy as to ask God to solve problems for you; ask for wisdom and strength while you face them.","r":["91:6.5"]},{"q":"Ne priez que pour des valeurs, non pour des choses ; pour la croissance, et non pour la satisfaction.","r":"91:8.13"},{"x":"God answers the attitude of the soul, not words, and he answers prayer with an enlarged revelation of truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["91:8.11","91:8.12"]},{"x":"Effective prayer requires courageously facing reality, sincere effort, choosing and carrying out the divine will, and living faith.","r":["91:9.2","91:9.5","91:9.8"]}]},{"h":"What Prayer Changes","items":[{"x":"Prayer does not change God, but great and lasting changes take place in the one who prays in faith.","r":["91:4.5"]},{"q":"La prière ne change pas l’attitude divine envers l’homme, mais elle change l’attitude de l’homme envers le Père invariant.","r":"146:2.8"},{"x":"As a bird must spread its wings to ride rising air currents, prayer lifts one up on the spiritual currents of the universe.","r":["91:8.9"]},{"x":"The quickest way to overcome the habit of criticizing a friend is to pray for him every day.","r":["91:5.3"]},{"x":"Prayer offered sincerely in faith, even a foolish petition, never fails to enlarge the soul's capacity for spiritual receptivity.","r":["144:4.2"]},{"q":"Rappelez-vous que, même si la prière ne change pas Dieu, elle effectue très souvent des changements importants et durables chez celui qui prie avec foi et dans une expectative confiante.","r":"91:4.5"}]},{"h":"Prayer as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to doing the Father's will, every petition is answered, because the prayer is in accord with that will.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus prayed more for the spiritual progress of his brothers than for himself, and he urged prayer especially for enemies and persecutors.","r":["146:2.10","146:2.11"]},{"x":"One should be able to talk with the Father as a son not only in times of distress but also when the soul is at peace.","r":["146:2.12"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that after praying one should wait in silence for a time, giving the indwelling spirit opportunity to speak to the soul.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus usually prayed in the plural rather than the singular, and he prayed for himself only in the great crises of his earth life.","r":["144:4.6"]},{"x":"For Jesus prayer was not a religious duty but a sincere expression of spiritual attitude and constant communion with God.","r":["196:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Adoration","Volonté de Dieu","Foi","Filiation avec Dieu","Expérience religieuse","Religion personnelle"]},{"n":100,"t":"Quête de la perfection","en":"Quest for Perfection","sum":"The Father's command, \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect,\" is an invitation calling every creature of time and space to the long and fascinating ascent toward Paradise. Urantia mortals cannot attain perfection in the infinite sense, but it is entirely possible for them to reach divine perfection on their own level. This journey begins with the hunger for perfection that the Adjuster awakens, passes through Havona to the Father bearing a perfection of purpose forged by faith, and continues beyond into the finaliter career.","sections":[{"h":"The Command to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universe have embarked on the eternal adventure of attaining God the Father, the long, long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"The effort to achieve the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and the highest ambition of every struggling creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Mortals cannot be perfect in the sense of infinity, but it is entirely possible for them, from their starting point, to reach the divine goal God has set.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Cette recherche sublime du Dieu des univers est l’aventure suprême des habitants de tous les mondes du temps et de l’espace.","r":"1:0.6"},{"x":"The Eternal Son, together with the Father, broadcast this command to all creation, and it has motivated every survival plan and bestowal plan.","r":["7:5.1"]}]},{"h":"The Hunger for Perfection","items":[{"x":"The indwelling Adjuster unfailingly arouses in man's soul a searching hunger for perfection, which can be satisfied only by communion with God.","r":["102:1.6"]},{"q":"L’âme assoiffée de l’homme refuse d’être satisfaite tant qu’elle n’est pas parvenue à la réalisation personnelle du Dieu vivant.","r":"102:1.6"},{"x":"The names of Andon and Fonta, the first parents of mankind, mean the first creatures to show the longing for human perfection.","r":["63:0.3"]},{"x":"Spiritual progress rests on the recognition of spiritual poverty, the hunger for perfection, the desire to be like God, and the purpose to do the Father's will.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic tension arising as all creatures and Creators together pursue divine perfection is resolved in the Supreme Being.","r":["116:7.6"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of an Imperfect World","items":[{"x":"Courage requires an environment of hardship, altruism of inequality, and hope of uncertainty.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.8"]},{"x":"Faith grows where more can always be believed than known, and loyalty amid the possibility of disloyalty.","r":["3:5.9","3:5.12"]},{"x":"Had the Father made all mortals perfect from the start, he would have deprived them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"x":"The perfection that creatures of time finally attain is a true personal possession gained through personal effort.","r":["32:3.9"]}]},{"h":"Perfection of Purpose and Faith","items":[{"x":"On arriving in Havona the pilgrim brings only one perfection, perfection of purpose.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"x":"Faith has won perfection of purpose, and now the pilgrim must develop perfection of understanding.","r":["26:4.14"]},{"q":"L’aptitude à comprendre est le passeport des mortels pour le Paradis.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Long before reaching Havona, ascenders have learned to feast upon uncertainty and to fatten upon disappointment.","r":["26:5.3"]},{"q":"\"In liaison with God, nothing—absolutely nothing—is impossible.\"","r":"26:5.3"}]},{"h":"Havona and Attaining the Father","items":[{"x":"After the brief test on Urantia, the morontia stages of the mansion worlds and the local universe, and spiritual training in the superuniverse, the pilgrim goes to Havona.","r":["14:5.1"]},{"x":"In the circuits of Havona ascenders progress inward, coming to comprehend in turn God the Supreme, the Infinite Spirit, and the Eternal Son.","r":["26:6.2","26:8.1"]},{"x":"Those who fail in Deity attainment are comforted and try again; their disappointment differs only in magnitude from many experiences in rising from chaos to glory.","r":["26:10.2"]},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father is the passport to eternity, and it forever demonstrates the justice of the command to be perfect.","r":["26:9.2","26:9.3"]},{"q":"L’épreuve du temps est presque passée ; la course pour l’éternité est presque terminée.","r":"26:9.3"}]},{"h":"The Endless Journey","items":[{"q":"Nous autres d’Uversa, nous ne connaissons pas la « destinée finalitaire » des mortels ascendants du temps.","r":"31:3.2"},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded only as spirits of the sixth stage, suggesting that yet another stage lies before them.","r":["31:3.3"]},{"x":"Even the splendid development of worlds settled in light and life is only the first stage of an endless ascending career.","r":["55:6.7"]},{"x":"Though his body came from the dust, man, if he truly wills it, will become a child of God the Supreme and a divine son of the Paradise Father.","r":["112:7.19"]}]}],"see":["Ascension des mortels","Havona","Corps de la Finalité","Croissance","Foi","Père Universel"]},{"n":80,"t":"Races","en":"Races","sum":"Mankind on Urantia began nearly a million years ago with Andon and Fonta, and about five hundred thousand years ago the six colored races, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and indigo, appeared all at once in one Sangik family. The violet race of Adam and Eve was later added, forming the Andites, and no pure races remain today. The races differ in mental outlook and capacity, yet all races have the same standing before heaven and are indwelt by the same spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Andon and Fonta","items":[{"x":"Urantia was registered as an inhabited world when the twins, the first two human beings, were eleven years old.","r":["63:0.1"]},{"q":"« Le mental humain est apparu sur la 606 de Satania, et les parents de cette nouvelle race seront appelés Andon et Fonta.","r":"63:0.2"},{"x":"Mankind has a history of nearly a million years; the Andonites avoided the forests and made progress in open lands and higher latitudes.","r":["64:0.2","64:1.3"]},{"x":"Again and again in Urantia's history superior stocks have mixed with inferior stocks and deteriorated.","r":["64:1.7","64:1.8"]}]},{"h":"The Emergence of the Six Sangik Races","items":[{"x":"About five hundred thousand years ago, in the highlands of northwestern India, a Sangik family produced unusually intelligent children.","r":["64:5.1","64:5.2"]},{"q":"Parmi ces dix-neuf enfants, cinq étaient rouges, deux orangés, quatre jaunes, deux verts, quatre bleus et deux indigo.","r":"64:5.3"},{"x":"On an average planet the races appear one after another beginning with the red, but on Urantia the six races came from one family at the same time.","r":["64:6.1"]},{"x":"The red, yellow, and blue are primary races and the orange, green, and indigo secondary, and their intellectual and spiritual gifts overlap.","r":["51:4.3","82:6.2"]},{"x":"Differentiation into the various colored races gives mankind desirable variation that could not be obtained otherwise.","r":["51:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Histories of the Races","items":[{"x":"Driven out of Asia by the yellow man, the red man crossed to North America about eighty-five thousand years ago, where Onamonalonton for a time restored peace.","r":["64:6.4","64:6.5","64:6.7"]},{"x":"The yellow race first achieved settled agriculture and social cooperation and, under Singlangton's leadership, worshiped \"One Truth.\"","r":["64:6.14","64:6.15"]},{"x":"The orange and green races, after endless strife, were absorbed into other races and disappeared.","r":["64:6.13","64:6.20"]},{"x":"The blue man invented the spear and laid the foundations of the modern arts; the so-called white race is mainly descended from him.","r":["64:6.21","64:6.24"]},{"x":"The violet race of Adam and Eve spread out from the second garden and blended with the Nodites and Sangik races to become the Andites.","r":["78:0.1","78:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Racial Diversity and Blending","items":[{"x":"Diversity stimulates natural selection and healthy competition, and differences among races foster tolerance and altruism.","r":["64:6.31","64:6.33","64:6.34"]},{"q":"L’homogénéité de la race humaine n’est pas désirable avant que les peuples d’un monde en évolution aient atteint des niveaux relativement élevés de développement spirituel.","r":"64:6.35"},{"q":"Il n’y a pas, aujourd’hui, de races pures dans le monde.","r":"82:6.1"},{"x":"The blending of superior and dissimilar stocks produces new and vigorous strains, and the dangers of race mixture have been much exaggerated.","r":["82:6.5","82:6.8"]},{"x":"Most objection to race mixture rests on social and cultural prejudice rather than on biology.","r":["82:6.7","82:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Equal Standing Before Heaven","items":[{"q":"En dépit de leur retard, les peuples indigo ont exactement le même statut devant les pouvoirs célestes que n’importe quelle autre race terrestre.","r":"64:6.27"},{"q":"Le mental peut différer d’une race à l’autre, mais toute l’humanité est habitée par le même esprit éternel et divin.","r":"155:6.8"},{"x":"Human unity and brotherhood can be achieved only through the religion of the spirit, which is personal experience, not through religions of authority.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus commanded that the gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man be wisely carried to all nations and races.","r":["191:4.4"]},{"x":"Pentecost wiped out all religious discrimination based on race, culture, caste, or sex.","r":["194:3.14"]}]}],"see":["Évolution","Adam et Ève","Urantia","Civilisation","Fraternité des hommes","Caligastia"]},{"n":98,"t":"Réalité","en":"Reality","sum":"In The Urantia Book reality is the totality of all existence, originating in the infinite volition of the Universal Father and differentiated and actualized on various universe levels. Reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal, and its totality is infinity, which no finite mind can fully grasp. Man recognizes fact, meaning, and value through science, philosophy, and religion, and spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality originates in and by the infinite volition of the Universal Father and is differentiated and actualized on various universe levels.","r":["0:4.1"]},{"x":"Universe philosophers attribute absolute primal causation in infinity to the Universal Father functioning as the I AM.","r":["105:1.1"]},{"q":"Le JE SUIS est l’Infini ; le JE SUIS est aussi l’infinité.","r":"105:1.3"},{"x":"All absolute reality, the three Deities, the Isle of Paradise, and the three Absolutes, is from eternity and without beginning.","r":["105:2.1"]},{"x":"The primal differentiation of reality is into the deified and the undeified, the Deity Absolute and the Unqualified Absolute, whose tension is resolved by the Universal Absolute.","r":["0:4.5"]}]},{"h":"The Differentiation of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality appears as undeified reality, deified reality, and the interassociated reality between the two.","r":["0:4.2","0:4.3","0:4.4"]},{"x":"From the viewpoint of time and space, reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal.","r":["0:4.7","0:4.8","0:4.10"]},{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The grand universe and the emerging master universe consist of many levels of reality beginning with the incomplete finite, and Urantia mortals are on its first level.","r":["106:0.2","106:0.3"]},{"x":"On absolute and eternal levels potential reality is as meaningful as actual reality; only to time-bound creatures do the two seem so different.","r":["118:1.10"]}]},{"h":"The Limits of the Finite Mind","items":[{"x":"Even to high intelligences infinity is only partially comprehensible, and the finality of reality only relatively so.","r":["105:0.1"]},{"q":"reality totality is infinity and therefore can never be fully comprehended by any mind that is subinfinite in concept capacity.","r":"105:0.2"},{"x":"Concepts of reality inevitably suffer serious distortion when translated to the level of mortal comprehension.","r":["105:0.3"]},{"x":"The mortal mind can hardly comprehend seven levels of relative cosmic reality, but it can grasp much of the three functioning levels of finite reality.","r":["12:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Fact, Meaning, and Value","items":[{"q":"Il n’y a que trois éléments dans la réalité universelle : le fait, l’idée et la relation.","r":"196:3.2"},{"x":"We call these three realities thing, meaning, and value, and science, philosophy, and religion respectively recognize them.","r":["196:3.2"]},{"x":"The three insights inherent in cosmic mind, causation, duty, and worship, make possible the recognition of scientific, moral, and spiritual reality.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Physical certainty lies in the logic of science, moral certainty in the wisdom of philosophy, and spiritual certainty in the truth of genuine religious experience.","r":["196:3.5"]},{"x":"In the final analysis matter vanishes from the senses and mind too disappears, but spirit insight still recognizes spiritual reality and supreme value.","r":["112:2.11"]}]},{"h":"Spirit, the Basic Reality","items":[{"q":"L’esprit est la réalité personnelle fondamentale dans les univers, et la personnalité est fondamentale pour toute expérience progressive avec la réalité spirituelle.","r":"12:9.1"},{"x":"Because God is spirit, changeless spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience, beyond the experiential variables of mind and matter.","r":["12:8.14"]},{"x":"It is an error to regard matter as basic reality and mind and spirit as rooted in matter.","r":["8:2.3"]},{"q":"The spirit is the creative reality","r":"42:12.14"},{"x":"The physical is the time-space reflection of spirit reality; matter is the skeleton of morontia, and both are shadows of spirit reality.","r":["42:12.14","189:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Reality and God","items":[{"x":"The soul is a new morontia reality born in experience, with the indwelling spirit as father and the material mind as mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"q":"La compréhension progressive de la réalité équivaut à s’approcher de Dieu.","r":"196:3.3"},{"x":"To experience total reality is the full realization of God, the finality of the God-knowing experience.","r":["196:3.3"]},{"x":"Ascending man advances at once inward toward the experience of God and outward toward the understanding of energy.","r":["103:7.3"]}]}],"see":["Les trois Absolus","Père Universel","Être Suprême","Expérience","Science et religion","Philosophie"]},{"n":76,"t":"Rébellion de Lucifer","en":"Lucifer Rebellion","sum":"The Lucifer rebellion was the revolt launched some two hundred thousand years ago by Lucifer, sovereign of the system of Satania, together with his first assistant, Satan. It began with a \"Declaration of Liberty\" that denied the reality of the Father, the sovereignty of Michael, and the ascension plan. Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined it, and Urantia was among their worlds. The rebellion sprang from self-contemplation and pride; the universe rulers waited long so that every being could make a full choice, and Michael's bestowal virtually ended the rebellion.","sections":[{"h":"Lucifer and the Origin of the Rebellion","items":[{"x":"Lucifer was not an ascendant being but a brilliant Son created in the local universe, and he ruled Satania with its 607 inhabited worlds.","r":["53:1.1","53:1.2"]},{"q":"La contemplation de soi est vraiment désastreuse, même pour les personnalités exaltées du monde céleste.","r":"53:1.3"},{"x":"No special conditions in Satania favored rebellion; the idea of revolt originated in Lucifer's own mind.","r":["53:2.2","53:2.3"]},{"x":"In a pride that led to self-deception, he at some point became disloyal, and evil turned into deliberate sin.","r":["53:2.5"]},{"x":"On Urantia Lucifer entrusted his cause to his first assistant, Satan, and Caligastia took his side here.","r":["53:1.4","53:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Lucifer Manifesto","items":[{"x":"Lucifer claimed that the Universal Father did not really exist and was a myth invented by the Sons to maintain their rule.","r":["53:3.2"]},{"x":"He demanded self-government for the local systems and attacked the sovereignty of Michael and the interference of the Ancients of Days as tyranny.","r":["53:3.3","53:3.4"]},{"x":"He denounced the plan of long training for ascending mortals as a waste of time and energy.","r":["53:3.6"]},{"q":"L’affirmation de soi fut le cri de guerre de la rébellion de Lucifer.","r":"53:4.2"},{"x":"Lucifer pointed to the merciful delays of justice as proof that the government of the Sons was incompetent.","r":["53:4.5"]}]},{"h":"War in Heaven and Its Losses","items":[{"x":"Michael, not yet having completed his bestowals, chose noninterference, and Gabriel led the loyal hosts.","r":["53:5.1","53:5.4"]},{"x":"The war in heaven was not a physical conflict, but it was far more deadly because eternal life was at stake.","r":["53:5.6","53:5.7"]},{"x":"Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined the rebellion; only on Panoptia did the people refuse to follow their prince and stand with Michael.","r":["53:7.1"]},{"x":"The angelic orders suffered the greatest losses, yet no being of Paradise origin and none of the Trinitized Sons went astray.","r":["53:7.5","53:7.6","53:7.8"]},{"q":"it is recorded to the glory of the wisdom of the ascension scheme that not a single member of the Satania ascendant citizenship resident on Jerusem participated in the Lucifer rebellion.","r":"53:7.10"}]},{"h":"True and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"The greatest confusion left by the Lucifer rebellion came from the failure to distinguish true liberty from false liberty.","r":["54:1.1"]},{"q":"La vraie liberté est le fruit de la maitrise de soi ; la fausse liberté est la prétention de s’affirmer soi-même.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty becomes self-destroying when it is divorced from justice, fairness, forbearance, moral obligation, and spiritual values.","r":["54:1.3","54:1.4"]},{"x":"Lucifer's folly lay in attempting to short-circuit time in an experiential universe.","r":["54:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom of Delay and the End of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"La justice suprême est dominée par un amour de Père, et c’est pourquoi la justice ne détruira jamais ce que la miséricorde peut sauver.","r":"54:5.3"},{"x":"It was advised that an arbitrary suppression would have led at least three times as many beings astray.","r":["54:5.12"]},{"x":"Michael offered the rebels forgiveness and restoration to service if they repented, but none of the leaders accepted.","r":["53:9.1"]},{"x":"Michael's bestowal ended the rebellion throughout Satania, and Lucifer was afterward detained by the Ancients of Days.","r":["53:8.3","53:9.2"]},{"q":"faith is an effective armor against sin and iniquity.","r":"53:8.8"},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousand times the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]}]}],"see":["Caligastia","Libre arbitre","Péché","Mal","Fils Créateur Micaël","Constellations et systèmes locaux"]},{"n":56,"t":"Religion institutionnelle","en":"Institutional Religion","sum":"Institutional religion is the church and religious organization formed as individual religious experiences gather socially. It is natural for religious groups to arise when people share their faith, and such groups have practical value in fostering worship, education, and fellowship. But the more religion is institutionalized, the weaker its power for good and the greater the dangers of dogmatism, sectarianism, and alliance with secular power. The Urantia Book regards the church's displacement of Jesus' spiritual kingdom as a tragedy.","sections":[{"h":"Why Religion Becomes Social","items":[{"x":"Religion is the personal experience of knowing God as Father, but it leads to recognizing men as brothers, and so it has a social side.","r":["99:5.1"]},{"x":"When people share their religious beliefs, some form of religious group with common goals inevitably arises.","r":["99:5.7"]},{"x":"The purpose of the religious group is to dramatize loyalty, enlarge the attractions of truth, beauty, and goodness, and foster fellowship, the home, religious education, and group worship.","r":["99:6.2"]},{"x":"Prayer sooner or later becomes a technique for institutionalizing every religion, giving rise to secondary agencies such as priests, scriptures, and rituals.","r":["91:5.6"]},{"q":"Ce sont les buts plutôt que les crédos qui devraient unir les religionistes.","r":"99:5.7"}]},{"h":"Dangers of Institutionalization","items":[{"q":"Le sectarisme est une maladie de la religion institutionnelle, et le dogmatisme est un esclavage de la nature spirituelle.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"Il vaut bien mieux avoir une religion sans Église qu’une Église sans religion.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"Mais, à mesure que la religion se conforme à des institutions, son pouvoir de faire du bien s’amenuise, tandis que ses possibilités de faire du mal s’accroissent considérablement.","r":"99:6.3"},{"x":"The dangers of formalized religion include fixation of beliefs, fossilization of truth, diversion from the service of God to the service of the church, and oppressive authority.","r":["99:6.3"]},{"q":"La religion officielle freine les hommes dans leurs activités spirituelles personnelles au lieu de les libérer pour un service plus élevé de bâtisseurs du royaume.","r":"99:6.4"}]},{"h":"Institutional Religion and Society","items":[{"x":"Institutionalized religion has become part of the social order that must be reconstructed, and so it cannot lead the coming social reconstruction.","r":["99:2.1","99:2.2"]},{"x":"Religionists should take part in social and political life as individuals, not as groups; a religious group acting politically becomes a party or an economic organization.","r":["99:2.3","99:3.15"]},{"x":"Early Christianity was free from all civil and economic entanglements, but later institutional Christianity became part of the structure of Western civilization.","r":["99:3.1"]},{"x":"To be free from secular alliances, religion needs a critical philosophy, political and economic independence, loving fellowship, and a scientific attitude.","r":["99:3.9","99:3.10","99:3.11","99:3.14"]},{"x":"Religious peace will not come until all religions renounce ecclesiastical authority and claims of spiritual sovereignty; God alone is spiritual sovereign.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"Religionists, as a group, must never concern themselves with anything but religion","r":"99:3.15"}]},{"h":"The Religion of Authority","items":[{"x":"The religion of traditional authority offers an easy refuge to fearful souls, but at the price of spiritual and religious liberty.","r":["155:5.9","155:6.5"]},{"x":"The religions of authority divide people by demanding uniformity of belief, while the religion of the spirit requires only unity of experience.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"True religion is not slavish belief in threats of punishment or in promises of mystical rewards.","r":["99:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus did not ask people to recite formulated creeds; he asked them to gather and share a supper in remembrance of his life.","r":["99:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Church and the Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural and desirable; the trouble was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7"]},{"x":"A formal, institutionalized church came to take the place of the kingdom brotherhood of spirit-led individuals.","r":["170:5.9"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean kingdom fellowship; the one is spiritual, the other mainly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"The present church is the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, a cocoon carrying the kingdom through the material age.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"x":"A church that worships the living God, affirms the brotherhood of man, and removes the pressure of creeds holds great hope.","r":["103:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Religion personnelle","Royaume des cieux","Expérience religieuse","Fraternité des hommes","Gouvernement et société","Enseignements de Jésus"]},{"n":55,"t":"Religion personnelle","en":"Personal Religion","sum":"Personal religion is the \"religion of the spirit,\" in which each person discovers and experiences God within his own soul, unlike the \"religion of the mind,\" which leans on tradition and ecclesiastical authority. It cannot be received, borrowed, or learned from others; it grows with loyalty to supreme values. Jesus proclaimed this religion of living personal experience beyond the religion of authority, and its fruits appear in love and service.","sections":[{"h":"Religion of the Mind and Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"There is the primitive religion of fear, the religion of civilization based on traditional authority, and the religion of revelation validated in human experience.","r":["155:5.3","155:5.4","155:5.5"]},{"q":"Jésus exposa clairement la grande différence entre la religion du mental et la religion de l’esprit ; alors que la première est soutenue par l’autorité ecclésiastique, la seconde est entièrement fondée sur l’expérience humaine.","r":"155:5.6"},{"x":"The religion of authority offers an easy refuge to fearful and uncertain souls, but it demands only passive, intellectual assent.","r":["155:5.9"]},{"q":"La religion de l’esprit signifie effort, lutte, conflit, foi, détermination, amour, loyauté et progrès.","r":"155:5.11"},{"x":"The religion of the mind ties one to the past, but the religion of the spirit, through progressive revelation, ever beckons to higher attainment.","r":["155:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Discovering God for Oneself","items":[{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God for itself within itself and to live that as personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"x":"It is good to revere the God-knowing leaders of the past, but not at the cost of sacrificing one's own experience of knowing God.","r":["155:6.7"]},{"x":"Do not seek the word of God only in ancient records; the one born of the spirit discerns the word of God wherever it comes from.","r":["155:6.12"]},{"x":"Once one begins to find God in one's soul, one soon finds him in the souls of others and in all creation.","r":["155:6.13"]},{"x":"The religion of the apostles was to be not a theological refuge from fear but a real experience testifying that God had found and exalted them.","r":["155:6.18"]}]},{"h":"A Religion That Cannot Be Given","items":[{"q":"La religion ne peut être ni conférée, ni reçue, ni prêtée, ni apprise, ni perdue.","r":"100:1.7"},{"x":"Every child should be given the opportunity to grow his own religious experience; an adult's finished experience should not be forced upon him.","r":["100:1.3"]},{"x":"Children are permanently impressed only by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]},{"q":"La manière la plus rapide pour un têtard de devenir une grenouille est de vivre loyalement chaque instant comme un têtard.","r":"100:1.4"},{"x":"Some people are too busy to grow; the chief obstacles to growth are prejudice and ignorance.","r":["100:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Growth of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by passing on to fellows what has been received.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spirituality measures both nearness to God and usefulness to fellows, and it grows as the selfish qualities of love are eliminated.","r":["100:2.4"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, and worshipful problem solving favor religious growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over, the God-knowing person has a citadel of the spirit that is never assailed.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"q":"La spiritualité indique immédiatement votre proximité de Dieu et la mesure de votre utilité pour vos compagnons.","r":"100:2.4"}]},{"h":"Social Fruits of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"The religions of authority divide people, but the religion of the spirit binds them together in unity of experience and destiny while allowing diversity of belief.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"The unity and brotherhood of mankind can be achieved only through the religion of personal spiritual experience.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The evidence of knowing God is the fruit of the spirit borne in daily life and a life plan that stakes everything on the adventure of survival.","r":["155:6.14","155:6.15","155:6.16"]},{"x":"The religion of the kingdom is personal, but its fruits are familial and social; no one can keep it within himself alone.","r":["170:3.9","170:3.10"]},{"x":"The Father responds to the faintest flicker of faith, but those who are called must believe with body, mind, and spirit.","r":["155:6.17"]},{"q":"The religions of authority can only divide men and set them in conscientious array against each other","r":"155:6.9"}]}],"see":["Expérience religieuse","Religion institutionnelle","Foi","Royaume des cieux","Ajusteur de Pensée","Croissance"]},{"n":91,"t":"Résurrection de Jésus","en":"Resurrection of Jesus","sum":"Before dawn on Sunday, April 9, A.D. 30, Jesus came forth from the tomb, not in the flesh but as a morontia personality, just as ascenders awaken in the resurrection halls of the mansion worlds. His physical body remained in the tomb and was later dissolved at the request of the archangels. During forty days the risen Jesus appeared nineteen times to believers while experiencing the morontia career of ascending mortals, and his resurrection revealed the gift of life that assures every believer of rising after death.","sections":[{"h":"The Resurrection Morning","items":[{"q":"at two minutes past three o’clock, this Sunday morning, April 9, A.D. 30, the resurrected morontia form and personality of Jesus of Nazareth came forth from the tomb.","r":"189:1.1"},{"x":"Even after he came forth, his body of flesh lay wrapped in linen, and the stones of the tomb and Pilate's seals remained undisturbed.","r":["189:1.2"]},{"x":"Seven Paradise personalities surrounded the tomb, but no creature of this local universe took part in his awakening.","r":["189:1.4","189:1.5"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus told the morontia groups that he would tarry for a time to know more fully the career of ascending creatures and to further reveal the Father's will.","r":["189:1.10"]},{"x":"That same morning the morontia Michael directed Gabriel to begin the planetary roll call of the resurrection.","r":["189:3.1"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivors of Urantia since the days of Adam awoke in the resurrection halls of Mansonia; this was the third dispensational resurrection.","r":["189:3.2","189:3.3"]}]},{"h":"In What Body He Arose","items":[{"q":"Son corps matériel ou physique ne faisait pas partie de sa personnalité ressuscitée.","r":"189:1.7"},{"x":"He came forth from the tomb neither as a spirit nor in the form of Michael the Creator as he was before incarnation.","r":["189:1.8"]},{"x":"He came forth as a morontia personality, like the ascenders who awaken in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world.","r":["189:1.9"]},{"x":"So that the human form of the Creator would not be seen slowly decaying, the archangels took charge of his body and dissolved it by a process of accelerated time.","r":["189:2.1","189:2.3"]},{"x":"Secondary midwayers rolled away the stones of the tomb, and the guards who saw it fled in terror.","r":["189:2.4"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Appearances","items":[{"x":"Jesus appeared to believers nineteen times before his ascension.","r":["190:2.1"]},{"q":"Il n’apparut pas à ses ennemis ni à ceux qui ne pouvaient faire un usage spirituel de sa manifestation sous forme visible.","r":"190:2.1"},{"x":"At the empty tomb Mary Magdalene took Jesus for the gardener and asked where he had taken the Master.","r":["189:4.10"]},{"q":"Touch me not, Mary, for I am not as you knew me in the flesh.","r":"189:4.12"},{"x":"Human eyes could see his morontia form because of the special ministry of the transformers and the midwayers.","r":["189:4.11"]},{"x":"Jesus appeared alone to Peter, who was weighed down by the guilt of denying the Master, and enabled his faith to overcome his doubts.","r":["191:1.1","191:1.2"]},{"q":"Bénis soient, dans les âges à venir, ceux qui croiront même sans avoir vu avec les yeux de la chair ni entendu avec les oreilles de mortels. »","r":"191:5.5"}]},{"h":"Apostles Slow to Believe","items":[{"x":"The apostles had taken lightly Jesus' words about his death and resurrection and believed only when faced with undeniable experience.","r":["190:1.1"]},{"x":"When the women reported, only John among the apostles was inclined vaguely to believe in the resurrection; the others thought the Jews had moved the body.","r":["190:1.2","190:1.3"]},{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that as the Father had sent him so he sent them, to reveal divine love in their daily lives.","r":["191:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of the Resurrection","items":[{"q":"All this power which is inherent in Jesus—the endowment of life—and which enabled him to rise from the dead, is the very gift of eternal life which he bestows upon kingdom believers","r":"190:0.2"},{"x":"Mortals too will rise on the resurrection morning in morontia bodies like the one Jesus wore, bodies without circulating blood yet real.","r":["190:0.3"]},{"x":"Man is slow to realize that matter is the skeleton of morontia and that both are the reflected shadow of enduring spirit reality.","r":["189:1.3"]},{"x":"The greatest news the disciples proclaimed at Pentecost was the risen Lord, and this led Christianity to grow up around fellowship with the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:0.4"]}]},{"h":"The Ascension","items":[{"x":"The so-called ascension, when Jesus vanished on Olivet, was no different from his other disappearances from view during the forty days.","r":["193:5.3"]},{"x":"Passing through Jerusem and Edentia, he was released from the morontia state and returned to Paradise sonship and supreme sovereignty on Salvington.","r":["193:5.4"]},{"x":"It was about a quarter to eight that morning when Jesus vanished from the sight of the eleven and began his ascent to the Father to receive confirmation of his completed sovereignty over Nebadon.","r":["193:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Mort sur la croix","Morontia","Pentecôte","Survie","Mondes des maisons","Les douze apôtres"]},{"n":75,"t":"Révélation","en":"Revelation","sum":"Revelation is the direct presentation by the real spiritual world of the truth that evolutionary religion seeks by circuitous ways, and it sorts and elevates evolutionary religion. Truth is autorevelation when it comes through the Adjuster and epochal revelation when it comes through celestial beings. Urantia has had five epochal revelations; revelation keeps in touch with evolution so as not to be too far removed from the thought of its age, and it coordinates science, religion, and philosophy as one truth.","sections":[{"h":"Evolutionary and Revealed Religion","items":[{"q":"La révélation est évolutionnaire, mais toujours progressive.","r":"92:4.1"},{"q":"La religion évolutionnaire décrit les tâtonnements de l’humanité qui tourne en rond à la recherche de la vérité ; la religion révélée est cette vérité même.","r":"92:4.3"},{"x":"Revealed religion is always characterized by belief in a Deity of final values and a concept of the survival of personality after death.","r":["92:4.2"]},{"x":"To elevate evolutionary religion, revelation must present teachings not too far removed from the thought of its age.","r":["92:4.1"]},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives by fear, but revealed religion leads people to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1"]}]},{"h":"The Five Epochal Revelations","items":[{"x":"There have been only five revelations of epochal significance; the first was the Dalamatia teachings of the one hundred of Caligastia's staff.","r":["92:4.4","92:4.5"]},{"x":"The second was the Edenic teachings of Adam and Eve; though interrupted by the default of the Garden, the Sethite priests carried on part of them.","r":["92:4.6"]},{"x":"The third was the revelation of Machiventa Melchizedek of Salem, who taught trust and faith.","r":["92:4.7"]},{"x":"The fourth was Jesus of Nazareth, who revealed God as the Universal Father and taught love and service.","r":["92:4.8"]},{"x":"The fifth is the Urantia Papers, presented jointly by many beings.","r":["92:4.9"]},{"q":"Toutefois, jamais aucune révélation ne peut être complète avant d’atteindre le Père Universel.","r":"92:4.9"}]},{"h":"Truth Is Always a Revelation","items":[{"q":"La vérité est toujours une révélation. C’est une autorévélation quand elle émerge comme résultat du travail de l’Ajusteur intérieur, et c’est une révélation d’époque quand elle est présentée par le truchement d’autres intermédiaires, groupes ou personnalités célestes.","r":"101:4.3"},{"q":"The pursuit of knowledge constitutes science; the search for wisdom is philosophy; the love for God is religion; the hunger for truth is a revelation.","r":"102:3.12"},{"x":"That the First Cause of science is a Father full of mercy can be known only through revelation.","r":["4:4.7","101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"Revelation is validated only by human experience, and it confirms the harmony of the approaches of science, religion, and philosophy.","r":["101:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Methods and Limits of Revelation","items":[{"x":"The revelators give preference to the highest existing human concepts and resort to pure revelation only when there is no adequate expression.","r":["0:12.11"]},{"x":"These papers are based on more than a thousand human concepts gathered from God-knowing mortals.","r":["0:12.12"]},{"x":"The laws of revelation forbid imparting unearned or premature knowledge, so the cosmology contained in revelation soon becomes outdated.","r":["101:4.1","101:4.2"]},{"x":"Revelation is a spiritual phenomenon, but its statements on cosmology are not inspired; their value lies in reducing error and restoring lost knowledge.","r":["101:4.5","101:4.6","101:4.8"]},{"x":"Because of the isolation of rebellion, the revelation of truth was mixed with transient cosmologies, but eternal truth should not be slighted for that reason.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"What Revelation Does","items":[{"x":"Revelation compensates for the absence of the morontia viewpoint, providing a technique of unity for understanding the relationships of matter and spirit.","r":["101:2.2"]},{"q":"La vraie révélation ne dénature jamais la science ; elle ne rend ni la religion déraisonnable, ni la philosophie illogique.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Revelation compensates for the weaknesses of evolving philosophy and accomplishes what metaphysics could not.","r":["103:8.6","101:2.7"]},{"x":"Revelation liberates man for the eternal adventure and gives assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["102:3.6","102:3.9"]},{"x":"Revelation glorifies man and discloses his capacity to be a partner with God.","r":["102:3.7"]}]}],"see":["Vérité","Science et religion","Philosophie","Machiventa Melchizédek","Adam et Ève","Effusion de Jésus"]},{"n":49,"t":"Royaume des cieux","en":"Kingdom of Heaven","sum":"The kingdom of God, or kingdom of heaven, is the central concept of the gospel Jesus proclaimed; above all it is the personal spiritual experience of the heavenly Father's will ruling in the believer's heart. It is founded on the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, is entered now by faith, and bears fruit in loving service. In later times the kingdom concept was replaced by the institutional church, but the spiritual kingdom Jesus taught will yet be proclaimed again.","sections":[{"h":"\"The Kingdom Is Within You\"","items":[{"x":"Jesus used the kingdom of heaven and the kingdom of God with the same meaning, and made it the name for his bestowal mission.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"x":"To his apostles Jesus taught the kingdom as a personal experience lived in relation to one's fellows and to the heavenly Father.","r":["170:1.13"]},{"q":"Ses derniers mots, au sujet du royaume, étaient toujours : « Le royaume est en vous. »","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his followers to use \"the will of God\" in place of \"the kingdom,\" and to replace the idea of king and subjects with that of a heavenly family and liberated sons.","r":["170:2.11","170:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Foundations and Gifts of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The kingdom of heaven begins with and is centered in the truth of the fatherhood of God and the fact of the brotherhood of man.","r":["170:2.1"]},{"x":"This teaching frees man from age-old animal fears and gives him new courage and spiritual power.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom gives assurance and comfort even to the poor, and teaches the superiority of the spiritual over the material.","r":["170:2.3","170:2.5"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are barely in the kingdom; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are truly in the kingdom.","r":["141:2.2"]}]},{"h":"How One Enters","items":[{"q":"Jésus enseigna que, par la foi, le croyant entre dès maintenant dans le royaume.","r":"170:2.20"},{"x":"The two conditions for entering the kingdom are childlike faith and sincerity, and a hunger for righteousness.","r":["170:2.21","170:2.22"]},{"x":"Simple, childlike belief is the key that opens the door, but once inside there are steps of righteousness to climb.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"q":"Faith is the price you pay for entrance into the family of God","r":"170:3.3"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in so far as one forgives one's fellows, and love of neighbor is the highest ethic.","r":["170:3.4","170:3.6"]},{"q":"L’homme peut disposer effectivement du pardon de Dieu et en faire l’expérience personnelle dans la mesure exacte où il pardonne à ses semblables.","r":"170:3.4"}]},{"h":"Fruits and Stages of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The inner religion of the kingdom increasingly shows itself in practical social service; Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]},{"q":"La religion du royaume est personnelle, individuelle ; ses fruits, ses résultats, sont familiaux et sociaux.","r":"170:3.10"},{"x":"Jesus taught two phases of the kingdom: the kingdom in this world and the kingdom in heaven.","r":["170:2.18","170:2.19"]},{"x":"The kingdom has five phases: the inner experience of the individual, the brotherhood of believers, the superhuman brotherhood, a new social order, and the age of light and life.","r":["170:4.2","170:4.4","170:4.6"]},{"x":"The kingdom is not a social or economic order but a spiritual brotherhood of God-knowing individuals.","r":["99:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom and the Church","items":[{"x":"For Jesus the kingdom was the sum of individuals who had confessed faith in the fatherhood of God and dedicated themselves to doing his will.","r":["170:5.11"]},{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural, but the tragedy was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7","170:5.10"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean fellowship in the kingdom; the one is spiritual, the other chiefly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"Some day a greater John the Baptist will appear, proclaiming a return to Jesus' concept of the kingdom as the Father's will ruling in the believer's heart.","r":["170:5.19"]},{"x":"The outward church is only the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, and the teachings of Jesus will never remain fruitless.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"q":"Mais n’en doutez pas, ce même royaume des cieux, dont le Maitre enseigna l’existence dans le cœur des hommes, sera encore proclamé à cette Église chrétienne, ainsi qu’à toutes les autres religions, races et nations de la terre — et même à chaque individu.","r":"170:5.8"}]}],"see":["Volonté de Dieu","Filiation avec Dieu","Fraternité des hommes","Foi","Enseignements de Jésus","Religion institutionnelle"]},{"n":64,"t":"Sagesse","en":"Wisdom","sum":"Wisdom goes beyond knowledge to embrace facts and ideals, the relationships and meanings of things. God's wisdom exists perfectly in his infinite insight, but human wisdom evolves through experience, through trial and error, and especially through adjustment to failure. The adjutant spirit of wisdom lays its foundation, the Adjuster and the Spirit of Truth lead it toward truth, and in time thinking leads to wisdom and wisdom to worship.","sections":[{"h":"Divine Wisdom and Experiential Wisdom","items":[{"q":"Man's wisdom grows out of the trials and errors of human experience; God's wisdom consists in the unqualified perfection of his infinite universe insight","r":"4:3.4"},{"x":"Because of the discrimination of infinite wisdom, God can be both just and merciful at the same time in any situation.","r":["2:4.3","2:3.2"]},{"x":"Wisdom has a dual origin: the divine insight of perfect beings and the personal experience of evolutionary creatures.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Superuniverse administration always associates the Perfectors of Wisdom, with their divine insight, and ascendant personalities seasoned by experience.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Infinite wisdom ordains that anything be done in the best way, the right way, in the circumstances.","r":["12:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Foundation of Wisdom in Mind","items":[{"x":"The spirit of wisdom is the highest of the adjutant mind-spirits, coordinating the work of all the others.","r":["36:5.12"]},{"q":"La sagesse est l’apogée des performances intellectuelles. La sagesse est le but d’une existence purement mentale et morale.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"Animals may possess knowledge, but only man has the potential of wisdom that weaves ideas from memory.","r":["101:6.4"]},{"x":"Wisdom is consciousness in which knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]},{"q":"La clairvoyance divine ou spirituelle est un don, mais la sagesse humaine doit évoluer.","r":"101:4.2"}]},{"h":"Wisdom Distinct from Knowledge and Truth","items":[{"q":"La connaissance traite des faits ; la sagesse traite des relations ; la vérité traite des valeurs de la réalité.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Science leads to fact-consciousness, religion to value-consciousness, and philosophy, or wisdom, to the co-ordinating consciousness that embraces both.","r":["102:3.5"]},{"x":"Science classifies men and religion loves men, but wisdom does justice to differing men.","r":["102:3.7"]},{"x":"When the viewpoints of material fact and spiritual value are harmonized, wisdom interprets universe phenomena through progressive personality experience.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"Knowledge is gained by education, but the wisdom true culture requires comes only through experience; intelligence controls civilization, and wisdom directs it.","r":["81:6.13","81:6.27"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Wisdom","items":[{"q":"Le succès peut engendrer le courage et promouvoir la confiance, mais la sagesse ne provient que des expériences par lesquelles un homme s’adapte aux résultats de ses échecs.","r":"160:4.14"},{"x":"Neither the idealist who ignores facts nor the materialist without spiritual outlook is wise, but only the one who adjusts facts to ideals.","r":["160:4.14"]},{"x":"Knowledge, culture, and wisdom are different, and wisdom always dominates knowledge and glorifies culture.","r":["160:4.16"]},{"x":"Wisdom is superknowledge; when people pool their minds, they can share each other's insight and avoid prejudice and narrowness.","r":["160:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus told James that true wisdom embraces discretion as well as courage.","r":["181:2.15"]}]},{"h":"From Wisdom to Faith and Worship","items":[{"x":"Reason, wisdom, and faith are man's three highest attainments, and in the higher philosophy wisdom becomes allied to faith.","r":["103:9.6","103:9.10"]},{"x":"True wisdom counsels allowing faith to accomplish what knowledge and reason cannot.","r":["102:1.2"]},{"x":"The superphilosophic wisdom of the enlightened recognizes that to doubt God is to be untrue to the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["101:1.7"]},{"q":"Dans le temps, la pensée conduit à la sagesse, et la sagesse mène à l’adoration. Dans l’éternité, l’adoration conduit à la sagesse et la sagesse aboutit à la finalité de la pensée.","r":"112:2.13"}]}],"see":["Philosophie","Vérité","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Mental","Science et religion","Expérience"]},{"n":40,"t":"Saint-Esprit","en":"Holy Spirit","sum":"The Holy Spirit is the spirit circuit, and the personal influence, that the local universe Mother Spirit, the Divine Minister, extends throughout her universe. Proceeding from the Creative Daughter of the Paradise Infinite Spirit, it is indigenous to that local universe and bound to her personal presence on Salvington. A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is soon encircuited in it; this is the first supermind endowment man receives and the foundation for receiving the Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Spirit Circuit of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"q":"Le Saint-Esprit est le circuit spirituel de cette Fille Créative de l’Esprit Paradisiaque Infini.","r":"8:5.3"},{"x":"The Holy Spirit is a circuit indigenous to each local universe and confined to the spiritual realm of that creation, whereas the Infinite Spirit is everywhere present.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"In the sacred writings the term \"Spirit of God\" seems to refer interchangeably to the Infinite Spirit on Paradise and the Creative Spirit of the local universe.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the second is the spirit circuit of the Divine Minister, the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:4.3","15:9.13"]},{"x":"As the spirit of the Infinite Spirit and of the Universe Mother Spirit, the Holy Spirit is often regarded as the spirit of the Universe Spirit, the \"spirit of spirit\" in the threefold spirit endowment.","r":["194:2.17","194:2.11"]},{"x":"Mortals too can know the presence of the Infinite Spirit, for they actually experience his grace working through the Holy Spirit bestowed by the local universe.","r":["9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"A Presence Bound to Salvington","items":[{"q":"Le Saint-Esprit de la Divine Ministre cesserait d’être fonctionnel si sa présence personnelle était retirée de Salvington.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"The Mother Spirit never leaves the universe headquarters world, and she acts as the universe focus not only of her Holy Spirit but also of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit and the Spirit of Truth go out from the local universe headquarters and, with the ministry of the adjutant mind-spirits, reach the lower levels of material mind.","r":["56:3.3"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit \"searches all things,\" the Mother Spirit on Salvington knows mortals fully.","r":["28:5.22"]}]},{"h":"The First Supermind Endowment","items":[{"q":"Man's first supermind endowment is that of personality encircuitment in the Holy Spirit of the Universe Creative Spirit;","r":"103:0.1"},{"x":"This influence functions long before the bestowals of the divine Sons or the universal bestowal of the Adjusters, enlarging man's view of ethics, religion, and spirituality.","r":["103:0.1"]},{"q":"Le Saint-Esprit — c’est le premier don supramental, et il apparait infailliblement chez toutes les personnalités humaines de bonne foi.","r":"92:0.4"},{"x":"This ministry to a mind that craves worship and desires wisdom creates the capacity to realize human survival both as a concept and as actual experience.","r":["92:0.4"]},{"x":"A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is at once included in the spiritual circuit of the Divine Minister.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"A mind ministered by the Holy Spirit has the capacity to choose the Adjuster, and the Adjuster enters only after the preparation of the adjutants and encircuitment in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:5.4","108:2.2","110:6.13"]}]},{"h":"Inner Ministry and the Fruits of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Spiritual reason, the intelligence of the soul, is the endowment of the Holy Spirit, the gift of the Creative Spirit to man.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit works partly independently of human attitude and partly according to the co-operation of the will, sanctifying the inner life of one who fully follows its leading.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"The seed of theoretical truth is dead, the highest moral concepts without effect, unless and until the divine Spirit breathes upon the forms of truth and quickens the formulas of righteousness.","r":"34:6.6"},{"q":"L’Esprit ne contraint jamais, il ne fait que guider.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"In a life led by the spirit, the fruits of the spirit such as love, joy, and peace appear, and the kingdom of God is righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:6.13","137:8.9"]},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective as the ages pass.","r":["55:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Oneness with Other Spirit Ministries","items":[{"x":"Man possesses no separate part of the Creator Son or the Mother Spirit; these ministries do not indwell the mind as the Adjuster does.","r":["34:5.6"]},{"x":"The presence in mortals of the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster is a symmetry of spiritual endowment that qualifies them to realize sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"q":"Indépendamment de leur pluralité d’origine, toutes les influences d’esprit fonctionnent comme une seule unité.","r":"34:6.2"},{"x":"The three supermortal endowments, the Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit, are unified in human experience as the ministry of the Supreme.","r":["101:2.12","113:4.6"]},{"x":"The ascender uses spirit circuits such as the Holy Spirit but does not possess them, and these circuits convey to the Supreme the values emerging in the personality.","r":["117:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Esprit Infini","Esprits-mentaux adjuvats","Esprit de Vérité","Ajusteur de Pensée","Royaume des cieux"]},{"n":73,"t":"Science et religion","en":"Science and Religion","sum":"Science explores the world of facts and energy-matter by reason, and religion experiences values and spiritual realities by faith. They are independent domains starting from different postulates; philosophy seeks to coordinate them, and revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are one and the same. Science purifies religion by clearing away superstition, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood by which the civilization of a scientific age can live together.","sections":[{"h":"Two Different Domains","items":[{"q":"La science traite des faits. La religion ne s’occupe que des valeurs.","r":"101:5.2"},{"q":"La raison est la méthode de la science ; la foi est la méthode de la religion ; la logique est la technique que tâche d’utiliser la philosophie.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Science assumes without proof the reality of matter, motion, and life; religion assumes mind, spirit, and the Supreme.","r":["103:7.11","103:7.10"]},{"q":"Les certitudes de la science proviennent entièrement de l’intellect ; les certitudes de la religion jaillissent des fondements mêmes de la personnalité tout entière.","r":"102:1.4"},{"x":"In science the idea precedes its expression, but in religion the experience of realization precedes the expression of the idea.","r":["102:3.13"]}]},{"h":"Different Eyes for Seeing God","items":[{"x":"God is to science a cause, to philosophy an idea, and to religion a person, the loving heavenly Father.","r":["1:6.2","4:4.7"]},{"x":"The existence of God can never be proved by scientific experiment or pure logic; it is realized only in human experience.","r":["1:2.7","101:10.6"]},{"x":"Reason may reach a First Cause by studying nature, but faith is needed to transform it into a God of salvation.","r":["101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are the same Deity.","r":["101:2.7"]},{"x":"In science God is a possibility, in philosophy a probability, and in religion a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]}]},{"h":"A Relationship of Mutual Help","items":[{"q":"La science stabilise aussi la philosophie en éliminant les erreurs, et purifie en même temps la religion en détruisant les superstitions.","r":"81:6.10"},{"x":"Evolutionary religion must be continually refined by the censorship of revelation and in the crucible of true science.","r":["92:3.10","99:3.7"]},{"x":"Science enables man to control his physical environment, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood that lets people live together in the complex civilization of a scientific age.","r":["103:7.9"]},{"x":"Both science and religion need more searching and fearless self-criticism, and teachers in both fields are often too dogmatic.","r":["103:7.7"]},{"x":"Harmonizing the discoveries of science with the insights of religion requires a sincere desire to follow truth wherever it leads.","r":["103:7.5"]}]},{"h":"Coordinating Philosophy and Revelation","items":[{"x":"Science discovers the material world, religion evaluates it, and philosophy seeks to interpret meanings by coordinating both viewpoints.","r":["103:7.15"]},{"x":"Harmonizing science and religion is difficult because of ignorance of the intervening domain of morontia; the morontia viewpoint removes the difference.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Metaphysics is man's earnest but futile attempt to compensate for the absence of the morontia mota.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"True revelation never renders science unnatural, religion unreasonable, or philosophy illogical.","r":["101:2.2","102:3.15"]}]},{"h":"Beyond the Materialistic Age","items":[{"x":"The statements on physical science in revelatory papers will soon need revision, and their cosmology is not inspired.","r":["101:4.2"]},{"q":"Plus vous êtes docte en science, moins vous êtes sûr de vous ; plus vous avez de religion, plus vous êtes pénétré de certitude.","r":"102:1.3"},{"x":"Scientists unintentionally plunged mankind into a materialistic panic, but the religion of Jesus has never become bankrupt.","r":["195:6.1"]},{"x":"What science has destroyed is only childish illusions born of mistaken interpretations; true religion remains untouched.","r":["195:6.4"]},{"q":"Facts never quarrel with real spiritual faith; theories may.","r":"195:7.1"}]}],"see":["Philosophie","Révélation","Vérité","Foi","Expérience religieuse","Morontia"]},{"n":20,"t":"Sept Maitres Esprits","en":"Seven Master Spirits","sum":"Les Sept Maitres Esprits sont les personnalités primaires de l’Esprit Infini, chacun exprimant l’une des sept associations possibles des trois Déités : le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit. Depuis la périphérie du Paradis, chacun supervise l’un des sept superunivers, et ils sont la source septuple du mental cosmique et les ancêtres des directeurs de pouvoir. Les créatures de chaque superunivers portent pour toujours le caractère distinctif de son Maitre Esprit, et le Maitre Esprit Numéro Sept, qui supervise Orvonton, représente l’Être Suprême.","sections":[{"h":"Sept associations possibles","items":[{"x":"Les Sept Maitres Esprits sont les personnalités primaires de l’Esprit Infini, et, comme il n’y a que sept associations possibles inhérentes aux trois Déités, l’univers est administré en sept grandes divisions.","r":["16:0.1"]},{"x":"Chacun tient son caractère de l’une de sept ressemblances : le Père, le Fils, l’Esprit, le Père et le Fils, le Père et l’Esprit, le Fils et l’Esprit, et le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit.","r":["16:0.2","16:0.9"]},{"q":"Nous avons été conduits à parler de la triple personnalisation de la Déité comme de l’inévitabilité absolue, et à considérer l’apparition des Sept Maitres Esprits comme l’inévitabilité subabsolue.","r":"16:1.1"},{"x":"Personnalisés par le premier acte créatif de Déité de l’Esprit Infini, ils sont les distributeurs de l’Esprit Infini aux univers.","r":["9:8.2"]},{"x":"Dans leur caractère et leur nature spirituels, les Sept Esprits sont comme un seul, mais dans tous les autres aspects de leur identité ils sont nettement différents.","r":["16:0.11"]},{"q":"Les Maitres Esprits ont de nombreuses fonctions, mais leur domaine particulier à l’heure actuelle est la supervision centrale des sept superunivers.","r":"16:0.12"}]},{"h":"La voix de l’Esprit Infini","items":[{"q":"En dehors du Paradis et de Havona, l’Esprit Infini ne parle que par la voix des Sept Maitres Esprits.","r":"16:2.2"},{"x":"La présence superuniverselle de l’Esprit Infini sur n’importe quel monde est conditionnée par la nature distinctive du Maitre Esprit qui supervise ce segment.","r":["16:2.3"]},{"x":"Les attributs d’omnipotence, d’omniscience et d’omniprésence n’apparaissent que lorsqu’ils agissent ensemble ; individuellement, chacun est limité au superunivers qu’il supervise.","r":["16:2.4"]},{"x":"Lorsque les Sept Maitres Esprits se rassemblent autour de l’Acteur Conjoint, ils représentent collectivement le pouvoir, la sagesse et l’autorité fonctionnels de la Trinité dans les univers évolutionnaires.","r":["16:1.3"]},{"x":"Ils sont le troisième niveau de Dieu le Septuple ; les ascendeurs, après être passés par les Anciens des Jours, découvrent la personnalité d’un Maitre Esprit avant de poursuivre vers le Père.","r":["0:8.4","0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Le caractère distinctif des Sept","items":[{"x":"Le Maitre Esprit Numéro Un exprime directement le Père ; il est étroitement associé au chef des Ajusteurs et, au conseil, il parle toujours pour le Père.","r":["16:3.2"]},{"x":"Le Numéro Deux dépeint le Fils Éternel, le Numéro Trois l’Esprit Infini, et le Numéro Quatre la nature combinée du Père et du Fils.","r":["16:3.4","16:3.6","16:3.8"]},{"x":"Le Numéro Cinq dépeint le Père et l’Esprit et il est le conseiller des directeurs de pouvoir et des contrôleurs physiques, tandis que le Numéro Six dépeint le Fils et l’Esprit.","r":["16:3.10","16:3.12"]},{"x":"Le Maitre Esprit Numéro Sept, qui préside Orvonton, dépeint également le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit, et il a une relation personnelle et organique avec la personne spirituelle de l’Être Suprême.","r":["16:3.14","16:3.15"]},{"q":"Durant le présent âge de l’univers où l’on ne peut pas contacter la personne du Suprême, le Maitre Esprit Numéro Sept fonctionne à la place du Dieu des créatures ascendantes en matière de relations personnelles.","r":"16:3.19"}]},{"h":"La supervision superuniverselle et le mental cosmique","items":[{"x":"Chaque Maitre Esprit a son siège sur la périphérie du Paradis, en face du superunivers qu’il supervise, et c’est là que convergent les lignes radiales des frontières de ce superunivers.","r":["16:0.12"]},{"x":"Les Maitres Esprits sont en contact avec les gouvernements superuniversels par l’intermédiaire des Sept Administrateurs Suprêmes et restent en communication constante avec les Esprits Réflectifs de chaque capitale superuniverselle.","r":["17:1.2","16:3.20"]},{"q":"Il est littéralement vrai que ces Sept Esprits sont le pouvoir physique, le mental cosmique et la présence spirituelle personnalisés de la Déité trine, « les Sept Esprits de Dieu envoyés dans tout l’univers ».","r":"16:4.1"},{"x":"Ils sont la source septuple du mental cosmique et les ancêtres des directeurs de pouvoir de l’univers, et ils aident aussi matériellement les Fils Créateurs qui organisent les univers locaux.","r":["16:4.2","16:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"La substance morontielle et le mental morontiel, qui allient matière et esprit, semblent liés à des activités non révélées des Maitres Esprits.","r":["16:4.5"]},{"x":"Ils n’ont cependant rien à voir avec le don et le ministère des Ajusteurs ni avec la fonction de l’Absolu Non Qualifié.","r":["16:4.16"]},{"x":"Dans le présent âge, le potentiel mental du Suprême est confié aux Sept Maitres Esprits, et le Septième Maitre Esprit, en particulier, connait le Suprême et se trouve en contact personnel avec lui.","r":["116:1.3","116:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Un caractère imprimé sur les créatures","items":[{"x":"Chaque monde jouit de la sagesse combinée des sept Maitres Esprits, mais ne reçoit sa touche et sa coloration personnelles que d’un seul.","r":["16:5.1"]},{"x":"Un Maitre Esprit n’entre pas directement dans le mental matériel des mortels ; son influence passe par le ministère de l’Esprit Créatif de l’univers local, qui lui ressemble beaucoup.","r":["16:5.3"]},{"q":"Pendant toute l’éternité, un mortel ascendant exhibera des traits rappelant l’Esprit qui présidait son superunivers natal.","r":"16:5.5"},{"x":"C’est pourquoi même le Corps de la Finalité, lorsqu’il représente une relation complète avec la création évolutionnaire, rassemble un groupe de sept finalitaires, un de chaque superunivers.","r":["16:5.5"]},{"x":"Sur le septième circuit de Havona, l’ascendeur doit saisir l’identité du Maitre Esprit de son superunivers avant de pouvoir avancer au sixième circuit.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"Il y a sept grandes avenues vers le Père Universel, et chaque ascension s’accomplit par la divinité de l’un des Sept Maitres Esprits.","r":["117:6.15"]}]}],"see":["Esprit Infini","Mental cosmique","Les sept superunivers","Dieu le Septuple","Être Suprême","Anciens des Jours"]},{"n":14,"t":"Les sept superunivers","en":"The Seven Superuniverses","sum":"Les sept superunivers sont les créations qui évoluent dans le temps et l’espace, formées en divisant en sept segments le premier niveau d’espace au-delà de Havona. Chaque superunivers contient environ mille milliards de mondes habitables, il est gouverné par trois Anciens des Jours à partir d’un monde-siège architectural et il est supervisé du Paradis par l’un des Sept Maitres Esprits. Orvonton, le septième superunivers, auquel appartient Urantia, est connu comme une démonstration universelle d’amour et de miséricorde.","sections":[{"h":"La roue gigantesque","items":[{"x":"Pour ce qui concerne la Trinité du Paradis, il n’y a que sept univers habités hors de Havona, et ils ont juridiction sur le premier niveau d’espace au-delà de Havona.","r":["15:0.1"]},{"q":"the hub being the eternal Isle of Paradise, the seven spokes the radiations of the Seven Master Spirits, the rim the outer regions of the grand universe.","r":"15:0.1"},{"x":"Le plan septuple d’organisation des superunivers fut établi au début de la matérialisation de la création universelle, et le système administratif actuel existe presque depuis l’éternité.","r":["15:0.2"]},{"x":"Les sept superunivers tournent dans le sens inverse des aiguilles d’une montre autour du Paradis et de Havona, en suivant une énorme trajectoire elliptique.","r":["15:1.2","15:3.14"]},{"x":"Urantia ne plonge pas aveuglément dans un espace inconnu ; elle suit la trajectoire ordonnée et prédéterminée du niveau d’espace superuniversel.","r":["15:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Unités d’organisation","items":[{"q":"Only the Universal Father knows the location and actual number of inhabited worlds in space","r":"15:2.1"},{"x":"Environ mille mondes habitables forment un système, cent systèmes une constellation et cent constellations un univers local.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4","15:2.5"]},{"x":"Cent univers locaux forment un secteur mineur, cent secteurs mineurs un secteur majeur et dix secteurs majeurs un superunivers, qui contient environ mille milliards de planètes habitables.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]},{"x":"On prévoit environ sept-mille milliards de mondes habitables pour l’ensemble du grand univers, mais ces chiffres ne sont que des approximations.","r":["15:2.9","15:2.25"]},{"x":"Les secteurs mineurs sont gouvernés par trois Récents des Jours, les secteurs majeurs par trois Perfections des Jours et les superunivers par trois Anciens des Jours.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Orvonton et notre place","items":[{"x":"Presque toutes les étoiles visibles à l’œil nu depuis Urantia appartiennent à Orvonton, le septième superunivers, et la Voie lactée est le noyau central d’Orvonton.","r":["15:3.1"]},{"x":"Le centre de rotation de notre secteur mineur se situe dans le nuage stellaire du Sagittaire, et tous les secteurs d’Orvonton tournent autour d’Uversa, son siège.","r":["15:3.5","15:3.7"]},{"x":"Urantia est le 606e monde du système de Satania et appartient à Orvonton par l’intermédiaire de Satania, Norlatiadek, Nébadon, Ensa et Splandon.","r":["15:14.5","15:14.6","15:14.7"]},{"q":"Votre planète est un membre d’un cosmos immense. Vous appartenez à une famille à peu près infinie de mondes, mais votre sphère est administrée avec tout autant de précision et entretenue avec tout autant d’amour que si elle était le seul monde habité existant.","r":"15:14.9"}]},{"h":"Formation physique et contrôle de l’énergie","items":[{"x":"Les organisateurs de force du Paradis sont des initiateurs de nébuleuses : ils mobilisent les forces de l’espace pour mettre en mouvement les vastes roues mères qui donnent naissance aux soleils et aux systèmes.","r":["15:4.4"]},{"x":"L’énergie est distribuée universellement, et non par nébuleuses, de sorte que chaque univers local détient exactement un cent-millième de l’énergie totale de son superunivers.","r":["15:4.6"]},{"x":"Tous les corps spatiaux, excepté les sphères architecturales, sont d’origine évolutionnaire, et notre système solaire se compose de planètes nées d’un processus d’explosion gravitationnelle.","r":["15:5.5","15:6.7"]},{"x":"La lumière est une matière réelle qui a du poids, comme le montrent les queues des comètes, dirigées à l’opposé du soleil.","r":["15:6.13"]},{"q":"Les nébuleuses peuvent se disperser, les soleils se consumer, les systèmes disparaitre et les planètes périr, mais les univers ne s’épuisent pas.","r":"15:8.10"}]},{"h":"Le gouvernement superuniversel","items":[{"x":"Les sièges des superunivers sont des mondes architecturaux spécialement construits qui donnent une lumière sans chaleur et se trouvent près du centre astronomique de chaque superunivers.","r":["15:7.1"]},{"q":"En réalité, tous les mondes-sièges sont paradisiaques.","r":"15:7.3"},{"x":"L’exécutif du gouvernement superuniversel se compose des Anciens des Jours, des Perfecteurs de Sagesse, des Conseillers Divins et des Censeurs Universels, ainsi que des mortels ascendants glorifiés : les Messagers Puissants, les Élevés en Autorité et les Dépourvus de Nom et de Nombre.","r":["15:10.3","15:10.12"]},{"x":"Chaque superunivers est supervisé par l’un des Maitres Esprits du Paradis par l’intermédiaire des Esprits Réflectifs stationnés dans sa capitale.","r":["9:8.3","116:4.4"]},{"x":"Les Fils de l’univers local peuvent décréter la survie des mortels, mais les verdicts exécutifs concernant la vie et la mort éternelles ne sont rendus que par les Anciens des Jours.","r":["15:12.2"]},{"x":"L’assemblée délibérante d’Uversa se compose de représentants élus parmi les diplômés ascendants qualifiés pour Havona, et elle n’a jamais été en désaccord avec l’exécutif.","r":["15:11.2","15:11.3"]}]},{"h":"Admission dans la confédération et dessein","items":[{"x":"Un univers local ne peut entrer dans la confédération superuniverselle qu’après avoir atteint la stabilité physique et la loyauté spirituelle envers son Fils Souverain.","r":["15:9.16","15:9.17"]},{"x":"Nébadon n’appartient même pas encore à l’ordre physique ancré du superunivers, mais le gouvernement superuniversel souhaite ardemment sa pleine admission et l’y aide.","r":["15:9.18"]},{"x":"Les superunivers sont isolés les uns des autres et ne connaissent leurs affaires mutuelles que par la chambre de compensation du Paradis, isolement qui durera jusqu’à ce que la souveraineté de l’Être Suprême soit factualisée.","r":["15:10.23"]},{"x":"Chacun des sept desseins majeurs de l’évolution superuniverselle s’exprime le plus pleinement dans un superunivers.","r":["15:14.1"]},{"q":"Orvonton est, dans l’univers, une démonstration d’amour et de miséricorde.","r":"15:14.2"},{"x":"Dans Orvonton, les desseins des six autres superunivers sont en train d’être reliés entre eux, et l’on conjecture que Dieu le Suprême gouvernera un jour, depuis Uversa, les sept superunivers parachevés.","r":["15:14.3","117:7.16"]}]}],"see":["Anciens des Jours","Sept Maitres Esprits","Univers local de Nébadon","Grand univers et maitre univers","Havona","Être Suprême"]},{"n":27,"t":"Séraphins","en":"Seraphim","sum":"Les séraphins sont des anges créés par l’Esprit-Mère de l’univers local, et, avec les chérubins et les sanobins, ils forment le corps des esprits tutélaires de l’univers local. Bien que dépourvus de corps matériel, ce sont des êtres spirituels dotés d’une personnalité individuelle, qui comprennent et aiment les êtres humains. Répartis en sept ordres, des séraphins suprêmes aux séraphins de l’avenir, ils participent à presque toutes les tâches de l’univers local : administration, éducation, transport, archives et supervision planétaire. Ils sont eux-mêmes des êtres ascendants, destinés à atteindre le Paradis en passant par Séraphington.","sections":[{"h":"Origine et nature","items":[{"x":"Les séraphins sont créés par projection de l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers, 41 472 à la fois, et, comme Nébadon est encore en formation, ils continuent d’être créés périodiquement.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"De même que les supernaphins servent l’univers central et les seconaphins les superunivers, de même, dans l’univers local, les séraphins, avec les chérubins et les sanobins, forment les armées angéliques.","r":["38:0.2"]},{"q":"Les anges n’ont pas de corps matériels, mais sont des êtres bien précis et distincts les uns des autres. Ils sont de nature et d’origine spirituelles.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"Ils sont pleinement conscients des luttes morales et des difficultés spirituelles des humains, ils apprécient la musique, l’art et le véritable humour, et ils aiment les êtres humains.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Bien qu’ils ne soient pas des créatures sexuées, ils sont profondément affectueux ; ils vivent en couples d’êtres négatifs et positifs et accomplissent la plupart de leurs missions deux par deux.","r":["38:2.2","38:4.3"]},{"q":"Les anges ne jugent pas l’humanité, et les mortels individuels ne devraient pas non plus condamner d’avance leurs compagnons.","r":"38:2.4"},{"x":"Il est bon d’aimer les anges, mais il ne faut pas les adorer ; ils sont les compagnons de service de l’homme dans l’adoration de Dieu.","r":["38:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Formation et organisation","items":[{"x":"Ils passent leur premier millénaire comme observateurs dans les écoles de Salvington et le deuxième sur les mondes séraphiques, puis ils traversent la constellation et le système avant d’être nommés esprits tutélaires du temps.","r":["38:5.1","38:5.3"]},{"q":"Their work in the universe is without bounds and limitations","r":"38:5.4"},{"x":"À partir de groupes de douze couples, ils sont organisés en compagnies, bataillons, unités, légions, armées et armées angéliques, chacune douze fois plus grande que la précédente, et les armées sont commandées par des Brillantes Étoiles du Soir et d’autres.","r":["38:6.1","38:6.2"]},{"x":"Les « plus de douze légions d’anges » dont Jésus parla à Gethsémani désignent précisément ces légions de séraphins.","r":["38:6.1"]},{"x":"Depuis l’effusion de Micaël sur Urantia, les séraphins et tous les ordres de l’univers local sont passés sous la souveraineté du Maitre Fils.","r":["38:6.3"]},{"x":"Les chérubins et les sanobins, de même origine que les séraphins, sont l’ordre le plus humble des anges ; travaillant par couples, ils sont les fidèles auxiliaires des séraphins.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]}]},{"h":"Les sept ordres et leur œuvre","items":[{"x":"Les séraphins révélés se répartissent en sept ordres : suprêmes, supérieurs, superviseurs, administrateurs, auxiliaires planétaires, ministres de transition et séraphins de l’avenir.","r":["39:0.1","39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"q":"Mercy is the keynote of seraphic service and angelic ministry.","r":"39:2.5"},{"x":"Les séraphins de transport enséraphinent les ascendeurs et les portent de monde en monde ; l’être ainsi enveloppé dort pendant un temps déterminé et s’éveille à destination.","r":["39:2.10","39:2.12"]},{"x":"Les architectes sociaux, parmi les séraphins superviseurs, favorisent les véritables contacts sociaux et aident à constituer des groupes de travail efficaces et harmonieux.","r":["39:3.4","39:3.5"]},{"x":"Les conseillers moraux, parmi les séraphins administrateurs, enseignent l’interaction de la liberté et de la loyauté, et présentent la vie mortelle comme le premier maillon d’une longue chaine ininterrompue.","r":["39:4.10","39:4.13"]},{"q":"Les clefs du royaume des cieux sont la sincérité, plus de sincérité et encore plus de sincérité.","r":"39:4.14"},{"x":"Les ministres de transition favorisent le progrès morontiel des survivants sur les mondes des maisons et comptent parmi les séraphins qui se rapprochent le plus des êtres humains.","r":["48:6.1","48:6.34"]}]},{"h":"Le ministère angélique sur la planète","items":[{"x":"Même après l’échec du régime adamique, les esprits de fraternité, les âmes de paix et les esprits de confiance, parmi les auxiliaires planétaires, poursuivent leur œuvre sur Urantia.","r":["39:5.4","39:5.5","39:5.8"]},{"x":"L’idée que les anges ont des ailes provient en grande partie de traditions fondées sur d’anciennes observations de séraphins se préparant au transport.","r":["39:5.12"]},{"x":"Avec l’effusion de l’Esprit de Vérité vinrent les douze légions de maitres séraphins de supervision planétaire, qui s’occupent des époques, du progrès, de la religion, des nations, des races, de l’éducation, de la santé, du foyer, de l’industrie, des distractions et d’autres domaines encore.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.4"]},{"x":"Tandis que les anges du progrès favorisent de nouvelles avancées, les gardiens religieux transmettent à la génération suivante les valeurs immortelles contenues dans des formes plus anciennes, et ainsi ils s’équilibrent les uns les autres.","r":["114:6.6","114:6.7"]},{"q":"Aucun de ces groupes angéliques n’exerce de contrôle direct ou arbitraire sur les domaines de leur affectation.","r":"114:6.18"}]},{"h":"La destinée des séraphins","items":[{"x":"Les séraphins peuvent atteindre le Paradis par plusieurs voies, entre autres l’accomplissement parfait d’un service spécialisé, la convocation à Séraphington et la garde de mortels évolutionnaires.","r":["39:8.2","39:8.3","39:8.4"]},{"x":"Les anges ne sont pas sûrs de leur avenir éternel avant d’atteindre Séraphington, et l’on ne connait aucun ange ayant atteint Séraphington qui se soit jamais égaré.","r":["39:8.9"]},{"x":"Les chérubins et les sanobins peuvent, eux aussi, renaitre en séraphins complets après un long service et des étreintes répétées de l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers.","r":["38:8.6"]},{"x":"Beaucoup de voies s’ouvrent aux séraphins parachevés, mais ce qu’ils désirent le plus, c’est servir comme assistants d’effusion des Fils du Paradis incarnés.","r":["39:9.3"]},{"q":"Dans toute l’ascension morontielle et l’ascension spirituelle subséquente, votre fraternité avec les séraphins sera idéale et votre camaraderie magnifique.","r":"38:2.6"}]}],"see":["Armées angéliques","Gardiens séraphiques","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Médians","Mondes des maisons","Morontia"]},{"n":63,"t":"Service","en":"Service","sum":"Service is one way in which divinity is revealed on the personal level: the Son serves mankind, and the Infinite Spirit and his children possess by nature the urge to minister. For man, service is the social fruit of true religion, the inner experience of loving God flowing out as loving service to one's fellows. Jesus showed by washing feet that the one who serves is great, and the path of ascension leads on into endless universe service.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Divine Service","items":[{"x":"On personality levels creatures can comprehend divinity as love, mercy, and ministry.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"q":"Dieu le Père aime les hommes. Dieu le Fils sert les hommes.","r":"3:6.8"},{"x":"Ministry to mind is the essence of the Infinite Spirit, and all his spirit offspring share the divine urge to serve.","r":["8:4.1","8:4.2"]},{"x":"The family of the Infinite Spirit is forever devoted to ministering the love of God and the mercy of the Son, becoming a living ladder by which mortals ascend.","r":["9:8.25"]},{"x":"The attributes of mercy and service displayed by the descending Sons derive from the Eternal Son.","r":["7:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Fruit of True Religion","items":[{"q":"La religion n’est pas une technique pour obtenir une paix mentale statique et sereine ; c’est une impulsion destinée à organiser l’âme pour un service dynamique.","r":"100:3.1"},{"x":"One who has found God seeks out and serves less enlightened fellows, not to boast but out of overflowing goodness.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"q":"La marque intellectuelle particulière de la religion est la certitude ; sa caractéristique philosophique est la cohérence ; ses fruits sociaux sont l’amour et le service.","r":"102:7.5"},{"x":"Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics and service as the effect; inner religion shows itself in practical social service.","r":["170:3.8","170:3.9"]},{"x":"Religion becoming a personal experience is not dangerous so long as it does not lose the motive of unselfish social service.","r":["99:4.7"]},{"x":"Contact with the Adjuster is fostered by meditation, but it occurs more often in loving service to one's fellows.","r":["91:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Way of Service Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"At the Last Supper, before apostles quarreling over places, Jesus knelt like a servant and washed the feet of all twelve, even Judas.","r":["179:3.1","179:3.7"]},{"q":"Que celui qui veut être grand devienne le cadet et que celui qui veut être chef devienne celui qui sert.","r":"179:3.9"},{"x":"The lesson of the foot washing was that the secret of greatness in the spiritual kingdom differs from the methods of power in the material world.","r":["179:3.8"]},{"q":"My kingdom is founded on love, proclaimed in mercy, and established by unselfish service.","r":"155:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus asked not for sacrifice but for loyalty; service rendered by a friend for a friend cannot be called sacrifice.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"Even a small loving service, like a cup of cold water given to a thirsty soul, is always recorded by the Father's messengers.","r":["159:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Service in Society and Civilization","items":[{"q":"Dans l’économie, la recherche du profit se situe, par rapport à la recherche du service, à la même place relative que la peur par rapport à l’amour dans la religion.","r":"71:6.2"},{"x":"The profit motive should not be abolished suddenly but gradually transformed into unselfish motives.","r":["71:6.2"]},{"x":"Apart from parental instinct, altruism does not arise spontaneously, so an unselfish social order requires the impulses of reason, morality, and religion.","r":["16:9.7"]},{"x":"True parents engage in continuous service-ministry that their children, as they grow, will come to recognize and appreciate.","r":["84:7.26"]},{"x":"The social service and intellectual fellowship of believers are precious, but as by-products of inner transformation they cannot replace the proclamation of the gospel.","r":["178:1.11"]}]},{"h":"Service That Continues into Eternity","items":[{"x":"On the fourth mansion world ascenders first experience a social order based on the love of mutual service rather than selfish conquest.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"x":"What the Father and the Sons bestow on us we bestow in turn on our fellows and the Supreme; the experience of love, joy, and service is mutual.","r":["56:8.3"]},{"x":"Entry into the Mortal Corps of the Finality is the beginning of eternal service to the Paradise Trinity.","r":["27:7.8","27:7.10"]},{"x":"In the present universe age the finaliters return to the universes of time and serve in one superuniverse after another.","r":["31:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Amour","Fraternité des hommes","Expérience religieuse","Corps de la Finalité","Enseignements de Jésus","Esprit Infini"]},{"n":42,"t":"Survie","en":"Survival","sum":"Survival means that the mortal personality, beyond the death of the flesh, awakens again in the morontia worlds and continues the eternal ascent. The Urantia Book teaches that survival is a gift of God, but a gift that man must desire and choose for himself. What survives is the soul built together with the Adjuster, and the key to it is not knowledge or doctrine but the sincere determination to find God and be like him, and a living faith.","sections":[{"h":"Survival Is a Chosen Gift","items":[{"q":"survival is a gift of the Gods which must be desired by the creatures of time.","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Human identity is real only in so far as the personality chooses to become a continuing universe phenomenon, and that path must be pursued by free will.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"Personality is destined for a divine goal, but man must choose for himself whether he will be present where that goal is attained.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"The capacity to reject survival did not arise with the Lucifer rebellion; it is an endowment of choice that mortals have always possessed.","r":["54:6.9"]},{"q":"The energy system must continue, it has no choice; but man has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":"112:5.3"}]},{"h":"What Survives","items":[{"x":"The reality that survives the death of the material body and mind is the soul, the morontia self born of man and the Adjuster together.","r":["112:5.12"]},{"x":"After death the Adjuster goes to Divinington bearing the memory transcript of the life, and the soul is held by the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"x":"The surviving self evolves only by transferring the seat of identity from the material body to the immortal morontia soul.","r":["112:2.20"]},{"x":"Memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain, but memories of relationships between personalities have cosmic value and remain.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"Man survives mortal death by the identification of his identity with the indwelling spark of divinity.","r":["132:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Survival","items":[{"q":"Le secret de la survie est enveloppé dans le suprême désir des hommes d’être semblables à Dieu, et dans la bonne volonté correspondante de faire et d’être tout ce qui est essentiel pour satisfaire finalement ce désir dominant.","r":"110:3.2"},{"x":"Success or failure in survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"Seule la résistance consciente à la gouverne de l’Ajusteur peut empêcher la survie de l’âme immortelle en évolution.","r":"110:3.5"},{"x":"Ignorance, confusion, or fearful doubt alone cannot prevent the survival of the God-knowing soul.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God is the secret of survival and of perfection in survival.","r":["111:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Faith and the Assurance of Survival","items":[{"x":"Religious experience leads at last to a sure consciousness of God and an undoubted assurance of the survival of the believing personality.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that once one has established himself by faith as a son of God, there is nothing more to worry about regarding the certainty of survival.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus said that survival depends first on being born of the spirit that seeks truth and God.","r":["193:2.2"]},{"q":"Faith in the survival of supreme values is the core of religion;","r":"111:3.5"},{"x":"The faith-activated soul cannot stop, because it has the task of finding God, and once it reaches the goal it can never end.","r":["132:3.7"]}]},{"h":"Merciful Adjudication and the Orders of Survival","items":[{"x":"Every will creature is sure to experience one genuine opportunity to make an unquestioned final choice.","r":["112:5.9"]},{"x":"Those who, through no fault of their own, have not mastered the circles on earth are given extended probation if they have the will to survive.","r":["112:5.6"]},{"x":"When a verdict is in doubt, the universe government always decides in favor of the individual.","r":["112:5.7"]},{"x":"Survivors reach the mansion worlds in several orders, among them dispensational group roll calls, individual ascensions, and probationary dependents.","r":["49:6.4","49:6.8","49:6.11"]},{"x":"Those who attained the third circle or higher and received personal guardians may be repersonalized on the mansion worlds on the third day after death.","r":["49:6.9","112:4.12"]},{"q":"Nous préférons assumer le risque d’une rébellion dans un système plutôt que de courir le risque de priver un seul individu, se débattant dans n’importe quel monde évolutionnaire, de la joie éternelle de poursuivre la carrière ascendante.","r":"112:5.8"}]}],"see":["Mort","Âme","Ajusteur de Pensée","Mondes des maisons","Libre arbitre","Foi"]},{"n":97,"t":"Temps et espace","en":"Time and Space","sum":"In The Urantia Book time and space are the conjoined mechanism of the master universe, provided so that finite creatures can coexist with the Infinite. Space is a bestowal of Paradise that alternately expands and contracts as if breathing, and time arises from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence. Paradise has neither time nor space, and the maturing personality, by unifying past and future in the present, gradually transcends the limitations of time and participates in eternal purposes.","sections":[{"h":"A Device for Finite Creatures","items":[{"q":"Le temps et l’espace sont un mécanisme conjoint du maitre univers.","r":"118:9.1"},{"x":"Time and space insulate finite creatures from the absolute levels, and without them no mortal could exist.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"Time and space are inseparably bound together only within the time-space creations of the seven superuniverses.","r":["12:5.3","65:8.1"]},{"q":"The grand universe is mechanism as well as organism, mechanical and living","r":"118:9.4"}]},{"h":"Space","items":[{"x":"Space is a bestowal of Paradise, yet it is neither infinite nor absolute, and we do not know its absolute limits.","r":["12:5.2","11:7.4"]},{"q":"L’espace n’existe sur aucune des surfaces du Paradis.","r":"11:7.1"},{"x":"Between pervaded and unpervaded space lie the relatively quiet midspace zones that separate them.","r":["11:7.2","11:7.3"]},{"x":"All space alternately contracts and expands as if breathing; when universe space expands, reservoir space contracts.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.2"]},{"x":"Space is not empty; it is the nonabsolute reality nearest to the absolute that man knows.","r":["130:7.6","118:3.5"]},{"x":"Space may be thought of as a property of bodies, so that when a body moves it carries its space with it.","r":["118:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Time","items":[{"x":"Time too is an indirect bestowal of Paradise, arising from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence.","r":["12:5.1"]},{"q":"Le temps est le courant du flot des évènements temporels perçu consciemment par les créatures.","r":"130:7.4"},{"x":"Time is perceived on three levels: duration perceived by mind, motion toward God perceived by spirit, and the unique awareness of presence held by personality.","r":["12:5.6","12:5.9"]},{"x":"As man progresses inwardly, the sequence of events is increasingly seen as one related whole.","r":["130:7.5"]},{"x":"For an individual creature the standard of time is the length of its own life, and to those not bound by time evolution is not so long a process.","r":["65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Time and Maturity","items":[{"x":"In any intelligence there is a direct relation between the degree of maturity and the unit of time consciousness.","r":["118:1.3"]},{"q":"Patience is exercised by those mortals whose time units are short","r":"118:1.6"},{"x":"True maturity transcends patience by a forbearance born of real understanding.","r":["118:1.6"]},{"x":"To mature is to live more intensely in the present while transcending its limits by embracing past experience and future values.","r":["118:1.5","118:1.7"]},{"x":"A spirit-indwelt person has forward-looking insight, and only a progressive, forward-looking attitude is personally real.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Truth and Eternity","items":[{"q":"Things are time conditioned, but truth is timeless.","r":"118:3.2"},{"x":"The more truth we know, the better we can understand the past and comprehend the future.","r":["118:3.2"]},{"x":"In the evolving universes eternity is temporal everlastingness, the everlasting now.","r":["118:1.1"]},{"x":"On infinite and absolute levels the present moment contains all of the past and all of the future.","r":["118:1.9"]},{"x":"Eternity cannot be comprehended by the finite minds of time, but it is better thought of as an endless circle than as a straight line.","r":["32:5.4","32:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Personality Transcending Time","items":[{"x":"Mortal personality can become eternal by choosing to do the Father's will and becoming one with the indwelling spirit.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"To God as an absolute, an ascending mortal who has made the eternal decision is already a Paradise finaliter.","r":["118:1.10"]},{"x":"Paradise pilgrims become unconscious as they pass through the midspace zones in crossing from time to eternity.","r":["12:5.4"]},{"x":"As spiritual values are recognized, personality is gradually freed from the limitations of time and transcends the bounds of space.","r":["65:8.6"]}]}],"see":["Paradis","Grand univers et maitre univers","Réalité","Être Suprême","Expérience","Quête de la perfection"]},{"n":6,"t":"Trinité du Paradis","en":"Paradise Trinity","sum":"La Trinité du Paradis est l’union indivisible de Déité de trois personnes coordonnées : le Père, le Fils et l’Esprit. La Trinité n’est pas elle-même une personnalité, mais elle est une réalité vraie et absolue dont les fonctions sont plus que la somme des attributs des trois personnes. Elle administre la justice et exerce le supercontrôle de la totalité dans les univers, et elle est le seul fait inévitable de l’univers, celui qui libère le Père de l’absolutisme de la personnalité pour qu’il puisse se donner sans réserve.","sections":[{"h":"La seule union inévitable","items":[{"x":"La Trinité unit l’expression de la volonté personnelle infinie de Dieu à l’absoluité de la Déité, et elle libère le Père des limitations de l’absolutisme de la personnalité.","r":["10:0.1"]},{"q":"we can discover only one inescapable inevitability in universe affairs, and that is the Paradise Trinity.","r":"10:0.3"},{"x":"Le Père a transmis à ses Fils tout le pouvoir et toute l’autorité qui peuvent être délégués ; la personnalité divine n’est pas égocentrique et prend plaisir à partager.","r":["10:1.2","10:1.3"]},{"x":"En conférant la personnalité absolue au Fils, le Père est devenu le Père du Fils, et le Père et le Fils ont ensemble conféré une personnalité conjointe à l’Esprit Infini.","r":["10:1.4","10:2.2"]}]},{"h":"Trois personnes, une Déité","items":[{"q":"Bien qu’il n’existe qu’une seule Déité, il y a trois personnalisations positives et divines de la Déité.","r":"10:3.1"},{"x":"Chacun des trois est original, aucun n’est la copie d’un autre, et pourtant tous sont unis.","r":["10:2.6"]},{"x":"Seul le Fils Éternel fait l’expérience à la fois de la filiation envers le Père et de la paternité envers l’Esprit, et il connait ainsi la plénitude de la relation de personnalité divine.","r":["10:2.7"]},{"q":"God speaks through the Son and, with the Son, acts through the Infinite Spirit","r":"10:3.3"},{"x":"La paternité n’est pas réelle sans la filiation, et le Père n’a jamais existé seul, sans le Fils et l’Esprit.","r":["10:3.5"]},{"x":"Hors de Havona, le Père agit par les Fils Créateurs, la gravité, le Fils, le Créateur Conjoint, le circuit de personnalité et les Ajusteurs, et en tant que Déité totale il n’agit que dans la Trinité.","r":["10:3.9","10:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Une vraie réalité, non une personnalité","items":[{"x":"La Trinité est une association de personnes infinies qui agissent dans une capacité impersonnelle, mais non contraire à la personnalité, comparable à une société qui agit selon la volonté personnelle de ses membres.","r":["10:4.3"]},{"q":"La Trinité est une réalité de Déité qui dépasse la somme de ses parties, elle est issue de la conjonction des trois Déités Paradisiaques.","r":"104:2.4"},{"x":"Les trois Déités, en tant qu’individus, peuvent coopérer comme elles le veulent, mais une telle coopération n’est pas la Trinité.","r":["10:4.4"]},{"x":"De même que le potentiel d’un groupe dépasse la somme des attributs de ses membres, les fonctions de la Trinité sont plus que la simple somme des attributs des trois Déités.","r":["10:5.2"]},{"x":"Il existe de nombreuses triunités existentielles, mais une seule Trinité existentielle ; la Trinité n’est pas une association fonctionnelle, mais une Déité indivise.","r":["104:3.15","104:3.16"]}]},{"h":"La justice et le supercontrôle cosmique","items":[{"x":"La loi émane du Père, l’administration de la loi spirituelle revient au Fils, la révélation de la loi à l’Esprit, et la justice, qui est l’application de la loi, appartient à la Trinité.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"La justice n’est jamais une attitude personnelle, elle est toujours une fonction plurale.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Les Fils stationnaires de la Trinité, tels que les Anciens des Jours, administrent les jugements des superunivers sur la base des témoignages présentés par les personnalités de l’Esprit Infini.","r":["10:6.4","10:6.17"]},{"x":"La justice est la pensée collective de la droiture, et la miséricorde en est l’expression personnelle ; pleinement comprises, la justice de la Trinité et l’amour du Père coïncident.","r":["10:6.18"]},{"x":"À l’égard du fini, la Trinité agit en tant que Trinité de Suprématie, et à l’égard de l’absonite, en tant que Trinité d’Ultimité.","r":["10:5.4","10:5.5"]},{"x":"Même les catastrophes et les changements inexplicables de la vie peuvent être tissés en un dessin significatif grâce aux fonctions du Suprême et au supercontrôle de la Trinité.","r":["10:7.5"]}]},{"h":"La compréhension humaine de la Trinité","items":[{"x":"Les concepts de déité trine de la religion évolutionnaire sont nés d’associations naturelles, telles que les phalanges d’un doigt ou un tabouret à trois pieds, et il faut les distinguer du concept révélé de la Trinité.","r":["104:0.1","104:0.3"]},{"q":"Une vraie conception trinitaire ne consiste pas simplement à grouper ensemble trois dieux séparés.","r":"104:1.7"},{"x":"Sur Urantia, la Trinité a été présentée successivement par l’état-major de Caligastia, par Adam et Ève et par Machiventa Melchizédek.","r":["104:1.1","104:1.2","104:1.3"]},{"x":"Le concept chrétien de la Trinité, bien qu’erroné quant aux faits, était pratiquement vrai en ce qui concerne les relations spirituelles.","r":["104:1.13"]},{"x":"Une Déité personnelle exige une relation avec d’autres personnalités égales ; un concept de Déité sans une telle relation se réduit facilement à un absolu panthéiste.","r":["104:2.2"]},{"x":"La reconnaissance du concept de Trinité rend possible une certaine compréhension de l’interrelation de l’amour et de la loi dans les créations du temps et de l’espace.","r":["104:2.3"]}]}],"see":["Père Universel","Fils Éternel","Esprit Infini","Les trois Absolus","Être Suprême","Justice"]},{"n":10,"t":"Les trois Absolus","en":"The Three Absolutes","sum":"Les trois Absolus sont les Absolus de potentialité : l’Absolu de Déité, l’Absolu Non Qualifié et l’Absolu Universel. L’Absolu de Déité est la totalité de tout potentiel de Déité ; l’Absolu Non Qualifié est la finalité de la réalité non déifiée et de tout potentiel impersonnel ; et l’Absolu Universel unifie et coordonne les deux. Ils existent éternellement en même temps que la différenciation de la réalité opérée par le libre arbitre du Père, et ils sont le fondement cosmique qui rend possible la coexistence des univers et des personnalités finis avec l’Infini.","sections":[{"h":"La différenciation de la réalité et les trois Absolus","items":[{"x":"La réalité infinie totale existe en sept Absolus coordonnés, dont trois sont l’Absolu de Déité, l’Absolu Universel et l’Absolu Non Qualifié.","r":["0:3.1","104:3.5"]},{"x":"L’Absolu Universel résout la tension primordiale apparue lorsque le Père, par son libre arbitre, a divisé la réalité en déifiée et non déifiée.","r":["0:3.21","0:4.5"]},{"x":"Lors de la création de Havona, le Père a séparé sa présence du potentiel infini, et ce potentiel est caché dans l’Absolu Non Qualifié et englobé par l’Absolu de Déité.","r":["0:11.1"]},{"q":"En dernière analyse et en compréhension finale, les trois ne sont qu’un Absolu.","r":"0:11.15"},{"x":"Sur les niveaux subinfinis, les trois Absolus existent séparément, mais dans l’infinité ils paraissent ne faire qu’un.","r":["56:9.1"]}]},{"h":"L’Absolu de Déité","items":[{"x":"L’Absolu de Déité représente les possibilités causales et potentiellement personnelles de la réalité universelle, la totalité de tout potentiel de Déité.","r":["105:3.6"]},{"q":"L’Absolu de Déité qualifie l’absolu et rend absolu le qualifié — il est l’initiateur de la destinée.","r":"105:3.6"},{"x":"L’Absolu de Déité ne semble jamais réagir de manière subabsolue à une situation quelconque, mais paraît toujours réagir en fonction du bien-être de toute la création et de toute l’éternité future.","r":["0:11.5"]},{"x":"Les valeurs spirituelles existentielles trouvent leur origine et leur destinée dans la triunité du Père Universel, du Fils-Esprit et de l’Absolu de Déité.","r":["104:4.20","104:4.21"]},{"x":"Le Fils Éternel domine les valeurs spirituelles actuelles, tandis que l’Absolu de Déité semble imprégner le vaste domaine des valeurs spirituelles encore potentielles.","r":["7:1.10"]},{"x":"Dieu l’Absolu existe actuellement en tant qu’Absolu de Déité, et l’on postule qu’il pourrait se personnaliser expérientiellement par la fonction de la Trinité Absolue.","r":["0:2.18","106:6.6"]},{"q":"J’aime et j’adore Dieu le Père ; je respecte et j’honore l’Absolu de Déité.","r":"10:8.5"}]},{"h":"L’Absolu Non Qualifié","items":[{"x":"L’Absolu Non Qualifié est non personnel et non divin, et ni les faits, ni la vérité, ni l’expérience, ni la révélation ne peuvent pénétrer sa nature.","r":["0:11.7"]},{"q":"The Unqualified Absolute is a positive universe overcontrol in infinity","r":"0:11.8"},{"x":"Ce n’est pas une influence vague, comme un concept panthéiste ou l’hypothèse de l’éther de l’ancienne science, mais une présence effective qui imprègne le grand univers et l’espace au-delà.","r":["0:11.8","0:11.9"]},{"x":"L’Absolu Non Qualifié est coordonné avec le Paradis, et dans tout l’espace sa présence seule est au repos.","r":["105:3.4","105:3.7"]},{"x":"La puissance d’espace, l’énergie qui ne réagit pas encore à la gravité du Paradis, dérive de l’Absolu Non Qualifié.","r":["0:6.5"]}]},{"h":"L’Absolu Universel","items":[{"x":"L’Absolu Universel unifie le déifié et le non-déifié et met en corrélation l’absolu et le relatif.","r":["105:3.8"]},{"q":"The finite can coexist in the cosmos along with the Infinite","r":"0:11.13"},{"x":"Cela est possible parce que l’Absolu Universel égalise les tensions entre le temps et l’éternité, le fini et l’infini, l’homme et Dieu.","r":["0:11.13"]},{"x":"La différence de potentiel infini entre l’Absolu Non Qualifié et l’Absolu de Déité rend possible l’existence des univers matériels et des personnalités finies dans le temps.","r":["0:11.12"]},{"x":"On pense que la présence imprévisible qui fonctionne à côté des circuits mentaux dérive en partie de la fonction de l’Absolu Universel.","r":["9:6.8"]}]},{"h":"La triunité de potentialité et la destinée","items":[{"x":"L’association des trois Absolus n’est pas une trinité, mais la triunité de potentialité, puisque tous trois ne sont pas Déité.","r":["104:5.7","106:5.4"]},{"x":"La triunité de potentialité met en corrélation toutes les réalités énergétiques latentes, spirituelles, mentales et cosmiques, et elle est infinie en potentialité.","r":["104:5.11"]},{"x":"Les potentiels peuvent en partie ne pas se réaliser dans le temps, mais ils n’échouent pas dans leur totalité, et la volonté de Dieu finit par prévaloir.","r":["115:3.13"]},{"x":"Au sein des trois Absolus subsistent toujours des possibilités inconnues qu’aucun développement expérientiel ne pourra jamais épuiser.","r":["106:7.1"]},{"q":"La recherche de Dieu n’a pas de fin !","r":"106:7.5"},{"x":"Les Absolus ne sont pas une déité impersonnelle panthéiste ; en tout ce qui concerne la personnalité de l’univers, ils sont strictement limités par la Trinité et dominés par la Déité.","r":["0:11.16"]}]}],"see":["Trinité du Paradis","Père Universel","Paradis","Dieu l’Ultime","Réalité","Énergie et matière"]},{"n":15,"t":"Univers local de Nébadon","en":"Local Universe of Nebadon","sum":"Nébadon est l’univers local, organisé et gouverné par le Fils Créateur Micaël et l’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers, auquel appartient Urantia. Destiné à comprendre cent constellations et dix-mille systèmes, il est une création relativement jeune d’Orvonton ; depuis sa capitale, Salvington, Micaël gouverne en tant que représentant du Père et du Fils, tandis que Gabriel en est le chef exécutif. L’univers local est évolutionnaire, et les créatures atteignent la perfection en montant pas à pas depuis le bas.","sections":[{"h":"Un univers local en évolution","items":[{"x":"Un univers local est l’ouvrage d’un Fils Créateur de l’ordre des Micaëls ; il se compose de cent constellations, dont chacune contient cent systèmes.","r":["32:0.1"]},{"x":"Tous les univers du temps et de l’espace sont évolutionnaires, et les plans des Fils Créateurs suivent toujours la voie du développement progressif des créatures.","r":["32:0.2"]},{"x":"Un univers local est conçu par les Architectes du Maitre Univers au Paradis, et le Fils Créateur ne commence à l’organiser qu’après que les directeurs de pouvoir ont mobilisé les énergies de l’espace.","r":["32:0.4","32:1.2"]},{"x":"Nébadon s’étend aussi loin que s’étend la présence spatiale de l’Esprit-Mère de Salvington ; au-delà, on est hors de Nébadon.","r":["41:0.1"]},{"q":"Excepté dans l’univers central, la perfection est un aboutissement progressif.","r":"32:3.3"}]},{"h":"Organisation et notre place","items":[{"x":"La première création physique achevée dans Nébadon fut le monde-siège, Salvington, suivi de cent sièges de constellation et de dix-mille sièges de système.","r":["32:2.3"]},{"x":"Salvington est situé au centre exact d’énergie-masse de l’univers local.","r":["32:2.4"]},{"x":"Au dernier recensement, Nébadon comptait 3 840 101 planètes habitées, et l’organisation de demeures planétaires se poursuit.","r":["32:2.9"]},{"x":"Nébadon se trouve vers le bord d’Orvonton, et Satania, à son tour, aux confins de Nébadon.","r":["32:2.11"]},{"x":"Nébadon est le quatre-vingt-quatrième univers du secteur mineur d’Ensa, et Salvington en est la capitale.","r":["15:14.6"]}]},{"h":"Micaël, le Fils Souverain","items":[{"x":"Micaël de Nébadon est la 611 121e personnalisation d’un concept originel issu du Père et du Fils Éternel ; il n’est pas lui-même le Fils Éternel du Paradis.","r":["33:1.1","33:1.2"]},{"q":"À toutes fins pratiques, le Fils Souverain est Dieu pour notre univers et tous ses mondes habités.","r":"33:1.4"},{"x":"Ayant achevé ses sept effusions en tant que créature, Micaël gouverne Nébadon en souverain d’une miséricorde compréhensive.","r":["119:0.4","119:0.7"]},{"x":"Son pouvoir n’est limité que par les circuits de gravité du Paradis et par les Anciens des Jours, qui se réservent le verdict final concernant l’extinction de la personnalité.","r":["33:2.2"]},{"x":"Dans l’administration de l’univers local, le Père n’agit que par le Fils Créateur, mais il est intimement présent dans les mortels en tant qu’Ajusteur intérieur.","r":["33:0.1","32:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Le gouvernement conjoint du Fils et de l’Esprit","items":[{"x":"L’Esprit-Mère de l’Univers crée et gouverne l’univers avec Micaël, et le Fils accorde à l’Esprit un statut coordonné et une autorité égale en toutes choses.","r":["33:3.2","33:3.3"]},{"x":"Lorsque Micaël revint de son effusion sur Urantia, l’Esprit de l’Univers reconnut publiquement pour la première fois sa subordination au Fils.","r":["33:3.5"]},{"x":"Le Fils proclama alors, dans la « Proclamation d’Égalité », que l’Esprit lui est égal dans tous les attributs de personnalité, un idéal élevé pour la famille et le mariage.","r":["33:3.6"]},{"q":"Le Fils et l’Esprit président maintenant l’univers, comme un père et une mère veillent sur leur famille de fils et de filles, et pourvoient à leurs besoins.","r":"33:3.7"},{"x":"Face à la rébellion, seul le Fils agit en sauveur, mais aucun Fils ne pourrait réussir sans la coopération incessante de la Divine Ministre.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Administration et tribunaux","items":[{"x":"Gabriel, la Radieuse Étoile du Matin, né de la première création conjointe du Fils et de l’Esprit, est le chef exécutif de Nébadon.","r":["32:2.6","33:4.5"]},{"x":"Emmanuel de Salvington, l’ambassadeur de la Trinité, est la seule personnalité de Nébadon qui ne reconnaisse pas sa subordination à Micaël, et il ne donne conseil que lorsqu’on le lui demande.","r":["33:5.1","33:5.2"]},{"x":"Les systèmes s’occupent principalement des problèmes biologiques, les constellations de l’unité et de la stabilité sociales, et les chefs de l’univers du statut spirituel des royaumes.","r":["33:6.3"]},{"x":"Micaël ne s’occupe que de création, de soutien et de ministère ; les créateurs ne siègent jamais pour juger leurs propres créatures.","r":["33:7.1"]},{"q":"Vous vivez dans un univers bien ordonné, et tôt ou tard vous pouvez être surs d’être traités avec justice, et même avec miséricorde.","r":"33:7.8"}]},{"h":"L’ascension et le dessein des créatures","items":[{"q":"C’est un fait, quiconque a vu un Fils Créateur a vu le Père.","r":"32:3.6"},{"x":"Plus une créature est bas sur l’échelle de la vie, plus il lui est difficile de reconnaitre le Père dans le Fils Créateur, mais s’attacher fermement à la vérité de la présence du Père dans ses Fils est la sauvegarde la plus sure.","r":["32:3.6"]},{"x":"L’origine évolutionnaire animale n’est pas une flétrissure ; ceux qui gravissent l’échelle de la vie depuis le bas acquièrent un plus grand honneur et une expérience plus complète.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"L’univers local est le point de départ de la véritable évolution, où des personnalités imparfaites cocréent leur propre avenir et où les créateurs eux-mêmes évoluent.","r":["116:4.8"]},{"x":"Dans le mental de Dieu existe un plan éternel d’opportunité infinie et de vie sans fin qui embrasse chaque créature.","r":["32:5.7"]},{"q":"Le but de l’éternité est en avant !","r":"32:5.8"}]}],"see":["Fils Créateur Micaël","Esprit-Mère de l’univers local","Constellations et systèmes locaux","Les sept superunivers","Effusion de Jésus","Urantia"]},{"n":95,"t":"Urantia","en":"Urantia","sum":"Urantia is the universe name of the earth on which we live, the 606th inhabited world of the system of Satania, in the constellation of Norlatiadek, in the local universe of Nebadon. Urantia is a life-modification world where the Life Carriers formulated an original life, and an isolated world spiritually quarantined through Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default. Yet it is also known throughout the universe as the \"World of the Cross,\" where Michael, the Creator Son, made his final bestowal.","sections":[{"h":"Its Place in the Universe","items":[{"q":"Your world is called Urantia, and it is number 606 in the planetary group, or system, of Satania.","r":"15:14.5"},{"x":"Urantia belongs to Norlatiadek, one of the one hundred constellations of the local universe of Nebadon, which is part of the superuniverse of Orvonton.","r":["43:0.1","0:0.5"]},{"x":"Satania is an unfinished system with only 619 inhabited worlds, and the number 606 means that this was the 606th world in it on which human beings appeared.","r":["49:0.3"]},{"x":"Urantia reached its present size about a billion years ago and was entered under this name in the physical registry of Nebadon.","r":["57:8.1"]}]},{"h":"A Life-Modification World","items":[{"x":"Urantia originated from your sun, which is one of the many offspring of the Andronover nebula.","r":["57:1.1"]},{"x":"There are only sixty-one life-modification planets like Urantia in all Satania, and Urantia was a decimal planet on which the life designs could be modified.","r":["58:0.1","58:1.1"]},{"q":"La vie sur Urantia est unique et a son origine sur cette planète.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"The ancient inland seas were the cradle of evolution, recording the history of life on pages of stone.","r":["57:8.26"]},{"x":"Man can live in comfort thanks to more than forty seemingly accidental protective factors, such as the ozone layer.","r":["58:2.4"]},{"x":"Urantia was officially recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago, and its first parents were Andon and Fonta.","r":["62:7.7","63:0.2"]}]},{"h":"An Isolated World","items":[{"q":"Une partie, une très grande partie des difficultés éprouvées par les mortels d’Urantia pour comprendre Dieu provient des conséquences profondes de la rébellion de Lucifer et de la trahison de Caligastia.","r":"4:3.3"},{"x":"Since Caligastia's betrayal, Urantia has been one of the isolated worlds of Norlatiadek, with a Most High observer stationed on it.","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers regret that Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default greatly hindered their efforts to improve intelligent life.","r":["65:5.1"]},{"x":"The planet's spiritual isolation had no effect on the presence and function of the spirit-gravity circuit of the Eternal Son.","r":["7:1.7"]},{"x":"Urantia is still under partial spiritual quarantine, so the reflective seraphim cannot function freely.","r":["28:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Opportunity of Isolation","items":[{"q":"Mais l’isolement de ces sphères offre à leurs races une occasion unique d’exercer leur foi et de développer une qualité particulière de confiance dans la sécurité cosmique, qui ne dépend ni de la vue ni d’aucune autre considération matérielle.","r":"50:7.1"},{"x":"Mortals from worlds quarantined because of rebellion may turn out in the end to be extremely fortunate.","r":["50:7.1"]},{"x":"Though Urantia mortals differ in opportunity and endowment, their spiritual endowment is equal, since all enjoy the same indwelling divine spirit.","r":["5:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The World of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where Michael completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"Il est de fait que, sur d’autres planètes habitées voisines, on appelle Urantia le « Monde de la Croix ».","r":"188:4.1"},{"x":"On completing his Urantia bestowal Michael received the title Planetary Prince of Urantia and sought to set right the confusion left by Caligastia's betrayal.","r":["120:2.3"]},{"x":"The life lived on Urantia was intended as an inspiration not only to this planet but to beings on all the worlds of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Future of Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps on the way to light and life are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"x":"When that time comes, Machiventa Melchizedek, the vicegerent Planetary Prince, will take the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even if Urantia is restored to the system circuits, difficulties will remain for a time because all of Satania is isolated.","r":["46:8.2"]},{"q":"Jésus de Nazareth, en tant qu’homme parmi les hommes, atteignit personnellement le statut de lumière et de vie sur Urantia, il y a plus de dix-neuf-cents ans.","r":"55:11.7"}]}],"see":["Univers local de Nébadon","Constellations et systèmes locaux","Évolution","Rébellion de Lucifer","Caligastia","Effusion de Jésus"]},{"n":57,"t":"Vérité","en":"Truth","sum":"Truth is a spirit-discerned living reality that goes beyond knowledge, which deals with facts, and wisdom, which deals with relationships, to deal with reality values. God is the first truth, and all truth issues from him. Truth cannot be confined in words or creeds but is defined only by living, and static truth is dead truth. The Spirit of Truth enables people to realize this living, growing truth, and truth is unified with beauty and goodness in God.","sections":[{"h":"What Truth Is","items":[{"q":"La vérité ne peut se définir par des mots, mais seulement en la vivant.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Knowledge originates in science, wisdom in philosophy, and truth in the religious experience of spiritual living; truth deals with reality values.","r":["132:3.2"]},{"x":"Knowledge is demonstrable, but truth is experienced; knowledge is a possession of the mind, truth an experience of the soul.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"God is the first truth and the last fact, so all truth takes origin in him.","r":["102:6.6"]},{"x":"Truth is always a revelation: autorevelation when it comes through the work of the Adjuster, epochal revelation when presented by celestial agencies.","r":["101:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"Physical facts are uniform, but truth is a living and flexible factor in the philosophy of the universe.","r":["2:7.2"]},{"x":"Truth cannot be imprisoned in formulas, codes, or creeds; when one attempts to formulate it, it speedily dies.","r":["180:5.2"]},{"q":"La vérité statique est une vérité morte, et seule la vérité morte peut être considérée comme une théorie.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Truth is unshaken by shocks and free from all temporal fluctuations, yet it is never formalized and is always vital.","r":["118:3.3"]},{"x":"It is folly to regard the past as the only source of truth, for truth lives always in the present and finds new expression in each generation.","r":["79:8.8"]},{"q":"La vérité est relative et s’amplifie ; elle vit toujours dans le présent, parvenant à de nouvelles expressions dans chaque génération d’hommes — et même dans chaque vie humaine.","r":"79:8.8"}]},{"h":"The Way to Know Truth","items":[{"x":"Truth cannot become man's possession without faith, for a person's thoughts and ideals can never rise higher than his faith.","r":["132:3.5"]},{"q":"Revealed truth, personally discovered truth, is the supreme delight of the human soul","r":"132:3.4"},{"x":"Fearing the unknown, man tends to fixate science, formalize philosophy, and dogmatize truth.","r":["132:3.3"]},{"x":"There is never conflict between true knowledge and truth; conflict arises between knowledge and human beliefs colored by prejudice and fear.","r":["132:3.4"]},{"x":"The more one knows truth and the more one becomes truth, the more one can understand the past and grasp the future.","r":["118:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit of Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or law of truth but the conviction of true meanings on real spirit levels, a living and growing teacher.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"x":"The God-knowing person lifts wisdom to the level of living truth, but the spiritually unprogressive soul drags living truth down to dead wisdom.","r":["180:5.4"]},{"x":"Even the golden rule remains a mere ethical rule without the insight of the Spirit of Truth; its meaning is realized only by living it.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.11"]},{"x":"Truth, the understanding of cosmic relationships and spiritual values, is best attained through the ministry of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"q":"La vérité divine est une réalité vivante discernée par l’esprit.","r":"180:5.2"}]},{"h":"Truth, Beauty, and Goodness","items":[{"q":"La vérité est belle parce qu’elle est à la fois complète et symétrique.","r":"2:7.4"},{"x":"Because truth can be acted upon and lived, happiness follows the recognition of truth, while disappointment and sorrow follow error.","r":["2:7.6"]},{"x":"All truth, whether material, philosophic, or spiritual, is both beautiful and good.","r":["2:7.11"]},{"x":"Truth is coherent, beauty attractive, and goodness stabilizing; when these are harmonized, they become a high love.","r":["2:7.12"]},{"x":"Truth is the basis of science and philosophy and the intellectual foundation of religion.","r":["56:10.10"]}]}],"see":["Beauté","Bonté","Esprit de Vérité","Sagesse","Foi","Révélation"]},{"n":50,"t":"Volonté de Dieu","en":"Will of God","sum":"The will of God is the eternal purpose of the First Source and Center, and in the life of the individual it is partnership with the way and choice of God. The Urantia Book regards doing the will of God as the secret of survival and of perfection, and says that it is not a surrender of will but its consecration and expansion. Throughout his life Jesus lived \"not my will but yours\" and became the example of that way.","sections":[{"h":"What the Will of God Is","items":[{"x":"The will of God is the purpose of the First Source and Center, personalized in the Eternal Son and shown in universe action in the Infinite Spirit.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"q":"La volonté de Dieu est la voie de Dieu, et cette voie est une association avec le choix de Dieu devant chaque alternative potentielle.","r":"130:2.7"},{"x":"Doing the will of God is therefore the experience of becoming more and more like God, the source of all that is good, beautiful, and true.","r":["130:2.7"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God reveals a willingness to share one's inner life with God, and sharing is a divine thing.","r":["111:5.1"]},{"x":"In his mind Jesus unified all the attributes of God in \"the will of the Father in heaven.\"","r":["196:0.2"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of a Dedicated Will","items":[{"x":"The loving dedication of the human will to doing the Father's will is the highest and the only truly valuable gift man can offer God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"x":"God requires no coerced worship or slavish service; man must of himself love and worship God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"Such a creature choice is not a surrender of will. It is a consecration of will, an expansion of will, a glorification of will, a perfecting of will","r":"111:5.5"},{"x":"This choice lies less in the negation \"not my will but yours\" than in the positive affirmation \"it is my will that your will be done.\"","r":["111:5.6"]},{"x":"God too first consented to entrust a fragment of himself to the human will and to dwell within it.","r":["111:5.3","111:5.4"]},{"q":"The affectionate dedication of the human will to the doing of the Father's will is man's choicest gift to God","r":"1:1.2"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of a Life That Does His Will","items":[{"x":"The imitation of God is the key to perfection, and doing his will is the secret of survival and perfection.","r":["111:5.2"]},{"x":"Peace in this life, survival after death, perfection in the next life, and service in eternity are already achieved in spirit when one chooses to submit the will to the Father's will.","r":["111:5.4"]},{"x":"By choosing to do the Father's will, the mortal personality may become one with the indwelling spirit and so become eternal.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"A life that lives the Father's will is founded on truth, sensitive to beauty, governed by goodness, and shown outwardly in loving service.","r":["106:9.12"]},{"x":"In many cases the Thought Adjuster is dispatched at the very moment a person quietly resolves to do the Father's will.","r":["108:2.10"]},{"q":"L’imitation de Dieu est la clef de la perfection. Le secret de la survie et de la perfection dans la survie est de faire sa volonté.","r":"111:5.2"}]},{"h":"The Adventure of Finding and Doing His Will","items":[{"q":"N’oubliez jamais que la seule aventure plus satisfaisante et plus passionnante que la tentative de découvrir la volonté du Dieu vivant, c’est l’expérience suprême de tâcher honnêtement de faire cette volonté divine.","r":"155:6.11"},{"x":"The will of God can be done in any occupation, and for those who are spirit led there is no division between holy and secular callings.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to the Father's will, prayer comes into harmony with that will, and every petition is answered.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice impairs the efficacy of true prayer by offering material things instead of one's own will.","r":["91:2.4"]},{"x":"The will of God does not prevail from moment to moment, but viewed over a whole lifetime it becomes ever clearer in the fruits of those who are led by the spirit.","r":["12:7.7"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, the Example of a Life Lived in the Father's Will","items":[{"q":"\"Regardless of who I am and what power I may or may not wield, I always have been, and always will be, subject to the will of my Paradise Father.\"","r":"128:7.2"},{"x":"In every situation of life the mind of Jesus held to \"not my will but yours,\" and this consecration is the true passport to divine attainment.","r":["109:6.5"]},{"x":"The great task of Michael's bestowal was to reveal God to the creatures of flesh by living a life that did the Father's will.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"By dedicating his will to doing the divine will, Jesus made the greatest offering man can make to God.","r":["196:0.10"]},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his disciples to use \"the will of God\" in place of the word \"kingdom.\"","r":["170:2.11"]}]}],"see":["Libre arbitre","Royaume des cieux","Prière","Adoration","Caractère de Jésus","Être Suprême"]}];
